)\n([1a6fe9f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/1a6fe9fbf37acee03ef26074dc6f24910ad570da))\n\n\n### Dependencies\n\n* **plugin:** bump @types/node from 25.4.0 to 26.1.1 in /plugin\n([#546](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/546))\n([caa2659](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/caa26595153ffb24e2cadcfeca7572c0d45bb1e3))\n* **plugin:** upgrade TypeScript to 7 (supersedes\n[#547](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/547))\n([#611](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/611))\n([081551e](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/081551e91846221b0ba3582f3ef255a5b1e25647))\n\n\n### Documentation\n\n* OSS-side fixes from the 2026-07-26 product-coordination audit\n([#625](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/625))\n([71debfd](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/71debfd8fb6db2b36e46322c987a8e57aef63597))\n</details>\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with [Release\nPlease](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please). See\n[documentation](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please#release-please).\n\nSigned-off-by: release-please[bot] <release-please[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: caura-deploy-bot[bot] <265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-26T21:26:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6d4e8cc9258e805802b8e89dc0600dad3b0ec6dd","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/6d4e8cc9258e805802b8e89dc0600dad3b0ec6dd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6d4e8cc9258e805802b8e89dc0600dad3b0ec6dd/comments","author":{"login":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","id":265395343,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOD9Gcjw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229147182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/caura-deploy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"71debfd8fb6db2b36e46322c987a8e57aef63597","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/71debfd8fb6db2b36e46322c987a8e57aef63597","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/71debfd8fb6db2b36e46322c987a8e57aef63597"}]},{"sha":"71debfd8fb6db2b36e46322c987a8e57aef63597","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDcxZGViZmQ4ZmI2ZGIyYjM2ZTQ2MzIyYzk4N2E4ZTU3YWVmNjM1OTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-26T21:08:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-26T21:08:10Z"},"message":"docs: OSS-side fixes from the 2026-07-26 product-coordination audit (#625)\n\n## Summary\n\nExecutes all remaining OSS-side work from the 2026-07-26\nproduct-coordination audit (enterprise-side fixes landed in the\nenterprise repo's #914). One commit per task, all DCO-signed.\n\n- **Canonical SKILL.md** (`static/skills/memclaw/SKILL.md`): documents\nthe Interviewer (§3 — reflective server-side synthesis; realtime writes\nstay mandatory) and the Skill Factory (§8 — `staged` is governance not\nan error, `forge/`/`agent/` `doc_id` provenance, push delivery). Five\nnew content-invariant pins in `tests/test_direct_mcp_skill.py`. Once\nmerged, the enterprise nightly `sync-tools-json.yml` carries these\nsections to `memclaw.net/docs/agents.md` via its pin-bump PR — no manual\nstep.\n- **core-operations docstring**: `app.py` no longer claims \"this\nscaffold registers nothing\" — it names the nine registered cron jobs\n(six daily lifecycle ticks, daily/weekly agent digests, hourly\ninterviewer-schedule), each verified against its `scheduler.register`\ncall.\n- **README**: new **MemClaw Broker** section (identity headers,\n`broker:<install>` namespace, frozen v1 wire contract + oasdiff gate\nfrom #620); agent-digests bullet (`agent_digest.enabled`, `GET\n/api/v1/reports*`); a deployment-topology table stating exactly what\n`docker compose up` starts (db, redis, core-storage-api, core-api; `tei`\nonly with `--profile embed-local`) vs what is managed-only (core-worker,\nplatform tier, Pub/Sub); clarifies the `core-worker` backfill variant\nisn't in the stock compose stack.\n- **Plugin SKILL.md variant**: ports both notes, with the Interviewer\nexplicitly distinguished from the plugin's `MEMCLAW_AUTO_WRITE_TURNS`\nauto-write layer (both are floors, not substitutes); adds a mirroring\ncontent-invariant test to `plugin/src/tool-definitions.test.ts`.\n- **Component registry** (P2): `docs/component-registry.yaml` (4\nservices, 9 cron ticks, 5 event-topic families, Forge external-scheduler\nrequirement) + `tests/test_component_registry.py`, an AST-based two-way\ndrift gate between `scheduler.register(...)` calls and the registry —\nF5-class drift now fails a test.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `python3 -m pytest tests/test_direct_mcp_skill.py -q` → 10 passed\n- `python3 -m pytest tests/test_component_registry.py -q` → 3 passed\n- `cd plugin && npm test` → 378 passed, 0 failed\n- Full root suite: 3964 passed; 5 failures are local-env only (missing\n`google-cloud-pubsub`, stray `.claude/worktrees` copies) — none touch\nthis diff\n- `ruff check` / `ruff format --check` clean on the touched Python\nfiles; no `core-api`/`core-storage-api` src changes, so CI ruff/mypy\nsurfaces are untouched\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c232b09bae5d808eafe62e9b3ef3cfef9bb5de0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/c232b09bae5d808eafe62e9b3ef3cfef9bb5de0e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/71debfd8fb6db2b36e46322c987a8e57aef63597","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZnc6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEk0QADpqfn0P4yZU1faDzUKboKIe\nTNHiQR1xwLizO3/Hqz1ao4kD2J/bJqZ2LDIWBG6Bv0/JCYzfbUdUGKFRV8KXziiX\nji4YckVTngFaA8o6szq6XoYHkWS84Zm584nt4TgiEkFMmRiV5CNhFT5roD7d2Ltq\nIjA8bwvEk1Gbb3ykhL5o9EqLK4khCcdcUmXy8lMKZj1FrmpWx+OtI54kleQ9YV5C\nor/DiI+SDf0gWIKO6GXTQ9CXNrudzDmglu+3hSot5yFHjOm2zX5kvRDz0+DrKQUD\ni3VKtPsJsF1MGt24IWdUy/O6xID+arP1cnE4Detk7+wIeLRL2JjL9CuaXAfmmcCO\nYnWymdiTni5pQp8MYg/0v6CmvirFj8ty+FVnld