ed-local`) vs what is managed-only (core-worker,\nplatform tier, Pub/Sub); clarifies the `core-worker` backfill variant\nisn't in the stock compose stack.\n- **Plugin SKILL.md variant**: ports both notes, with the Interviewer\nexplicitly distinguished from the plugin's `MEMCLAW_AUTO_WRITE_TURNS`\nauto-write layer (both are floors, not substitutes); adds a mirroring\ncontent-invariant test to `plugin/src/tool-definitions.test.ts`.\n- **Component registry** (P2): `docs/component-registry.yaml` (4\nservices, 9 cron ticks, 5 event-topic families, Forge external-scheduler\nrequirement) + `tests/test_component_registry.py`, an AST-based two-way\ndrift gate between `scheduler.register(...)` calls and the registry —\nF5-class drift now fails a test.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `python3 -m pytest tests/test_direct_mcp_skill.py -q` → 10 passed\n- `python3 -m pytest tests/test_component_registry.py -q` → 3 passed\n- `cd plugin && npm test` → 378 passed, 0 failed\n- Full root suite: 3964 passed; 5 failures are local-env only (missing\n`google-cloud-pubsub`, stray `.claude/worktrees` copies) — none touch\nthis diff\n- `ruff check` / `ruff format --check` clean on the touched Python\nfiles; no `core-api`/`core-storage-api` src changes, so CI ruff/mypy\nsurfaces are untouched\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-26T21:08:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/71debfd8fb6db2b36e46322c987a8e57aef63597","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/71debfd8fb6db2b36e46322c987a8e57aef63597","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/71debfd8fb6db2b36e46322c987a8e57aef63597/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1df326f47fc6c05e76d474c03c8d4b20be4760ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1df326f47fc6c05e76d474c03c8d4b20be4760ac","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1df326f47fc6c05e76d474c03c8d4b20be4760ac"}]},{"sha":"1df326f47fc6c05e76d474c03c8d4b20be4760ac","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDFkZjMyNmY0N2ZjNmMwNWU3NmQ0NzRjMDNjOGQ0YjIwYmU0NzYwYWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-26T19:20:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-26T19:20:20Z"},"message":"feat(agent-digest): stop over-filtering agents — floor, episode-fallback, subagent rollup (#624)\n\nGrounded in the eToro over-filtering finding: active agents were\ninvisible in the digest because their work is **enrichment-classified as\n`episode`** (which we excluded wholesale) and/or **split across many\nsubagents** (e.g. `cmoclaw` + ~40 `cmoclaw-*`). Core-api side (PR 1 of\n2; UI PR follows).\n\n## Fixes\n1. **Durable floor 3→1** (default; removed the day/week special-case) —\na single decision/fact is worth surfacing. Configurable via\n`min_activity_threshold`.\n2. **Durable-first, episode-fallback** (`report_corpus` split into\n`passes_noise_filter` + `is_cohesive`). `generate_for_org` **reuses the\nalready-fetched rows** (no extra query): an agent with `< floor` durable\nrows is summarized from its non-noise **episodes** (ranked by recall)\nwith status `activity`. Same LLM budget; in-memory partition.\n3. **Count-only \"listed\" tail** — active families past `top_n` (or below\nthe summarize floors) get a no-LLM row, so no active agent is invisible.\n4. **Subagent rollup** — `resolve_parent` derives the parent from id\nconventions (`agent:<p>:subagent:<uuid>` and `<parent>-<task>`,\nlongest-prefix, transitive; `owner_ref` is unpopulated in prod).\nSubagents roll into the parent family; the parent row carries\n`source_count` = family total + a `subagents[]` list (`{agent_id,\nfleet_id, source_count}`) for the collapsed UI + child deeplinks.\n**Migration 032** adds the `subagents` JSONB column.\n\n`source_count` now means the family's **meaningful-writes total** (the\nbar value). New statuses: `activity`, `listed`.\n\n## Config (`agent_digest`)\n`min_activity_threshold=1`, `event_floor=1`, `listed_max=25`.\n\n## Tests\n- `report_corpus`: `resolve_parent` (both conventions, boundary guard,\ntransitive) + filter split.\n- generator: floor→summarize/list, episode-only→`activity`, cmoclaw\nrollup (both id forms), active-beyond-top_n→`listed`.\n- storage: `subagents` round-trip + empty default; migration head→032.\n- 23 core-api + 13 storage tests green; ruff + mypy clean (both\npackages).\n\nCost: no new queries; LLM spend unchanged/lower (one call per family,\n`top_n`-bounded). Depends on nothing; the enterprise UI PR (collapsed\nsubagent group + `activity`/`listed` rendering + child deeplinks)\nfollows.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e5f3716ac0aa73a41cb2326a57f785ac906c0f12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/e5f3716ac0aa73a41cb2326a57f785ac906c0f12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/1df326f47fc6c05e76d474c03c8d4b20be4760ac","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZl30CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAg3AQADZXgTFfWcMlRAcUcH0XlXsM\nP3njUVymEIPf5AmrErD5pfaPG/W+dvcEVN/AU9Tt8tbNI7JqN3HO7lptrlmJCTLL\nyTCrSaIzPX3MizDJJBSjWiZGaF7p43Kb/Zl5D4YEYlF27GpLBMVOODBpEm9vE7LU\n30k2GT7vUVPPapbh0zYbjerPMZsp/S3QcQsakdbYwZJ70sV1o2DtJRRuGtLIbbMs\nKO1RAlAZ6jrC3SUgxzwTDpejIuhr2KWpjxLpvlV0hhrdR7l7ap6ewPdx7Vx6QRza\nkl9W0L4Ip/dopfo0Ck2XH0TXq5MBFXdcrETHuVMDiXz6xA5FMNe9McDQ7CnTlynB\nn5WdZ8GpuCkpm/up9al+ybfGv8STcK2TD4ER2SQ1dRNcb4gB0tLrU5C80mvYJmnS\nZ1BqYRy2FbxqZiShKers71gPLAMud9UJuc0Ys+vV0ZjKYPuGe26lV7eSNj6PhgkL\nKYd/bstRai7iM+pJjDohWhuRw2wJP4IBQk0nG8FowVqyyzp1Zd9i0/j6at6FVtiD\n82+Fgt4ISufaMwWtSkmTpFywzqMXCn95rIAz1KekDcNePHQEZjCoAyavTv5+0y+v\ndW6eWQAu4hDUFcShX8NTbqpjlsLXDtTfT6WcG54YCJ93W02ElEecGzGE+38WYUsa\n9r5OM5bCM7W+UylZo4y8\n=7u/4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e5f3716ac0aa73a41cb2326a57f785ac906c0f12\nparent 1d084739c6ff0a78d22cda99a414c5fc7b1d3c43\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1785093620 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785093620 +0300\n\nfeat(agent-digest): stop over-filtering agents — floor, episode-fallback, subagent rollup (#624)\n\nGrounded in the eToro over-filtering finding: active agents were\ninvisible in the digest because their work is **enrichment-classified as\n`episode`** (which we excluded wholesale) and/or **split across many\nsubagents** (e.g. `cmoclaw` + ~40 `cmoclaw-*`). Core-api side (PR 1 of\n2; UI PR follows).\n\n## Fixes\n1. **Durable floor 3→1** (default; removed the day/week special-case) —\na single decision/fact is worth surfacing. Configurable via\n`min_activity_threshold`.\n2. **Durable-first, episode-fallback** (`report_corpus` split into\n`passes_noise_filter` + `is_cohesive`). `generate_for_org` **reuses the\nalready-fetched rows** (no extra query): an agent with `< floor` durable\nrows is summarized from its non-noise **episodes** (ranked by recall)\nwith status `activity`. Same LLM budget; in-memory partition.\n3. **Count-only \"listed\" tail** — active families past `top_n` (or below\nthe summarize floors) get a no-LLM row, so no active agent is invisible.\n4. **Subagent rollup** — `resolve_parent` derives the parent from id\nconventions (`agent:<p>:subagent:<uuid>` and `<parent>-<task>`,\nlongest-prefix, transitive; `owner_ref` is unpopulated in prod).\nSubagents roll into the parent family; the parent row carries\n`source_count` = family total + a `subagents[]` list (`{agent_id,\nfleet_id, source_count}`) for the collapsed UI + child deeplinks.\n**Migration 032** adds the `subagents` JSONB column.\n\n`source_count` now means the family's **meaningful-writes total** (the\nbar value). New statuses: `activity`, `listed`.\n\n## Config (`agent_digest`)\n`min_activity_threshold=1`, `event_floor=1`, `listed_max=25`.\n\n## Tests\n- `report_corpus`: `resolve_parent` (both conventions, boundary guard,\ntransitive) + filter split.\n- generator: floor→summarize/list, episode-only→`activity`, cmoclaw\nrollup (both id forms), active-beyond-top_n→`listed`.\n- storage: `subagents` round-trip + empty default; migration head→032.\n- 23 core-api + 13 storage tests green; ruff + mypy clean (both\npackages).\n\nCost: no new queries; LLM spend unchanged/lower (one call per family,\n`top_n`-bounded). Depends on nothing; the enterprise UI PR (collapsed\nsubagent group + `activity`/`listed` rendering + child deeplinks)\nfollows.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-26T19:20:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1df326f47fc6c05e76d474c03c8d4b20be4760ac","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1df326f47fc6c05e76d474c03c8d4b20be4760ac","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1df326f47fc6c05e76d474c03c8d4b20be4760ac/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1d084739c6ff0a78d22cda99a414c5fc7b1d3c43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1d084739c6ff0a78d22cda99a414c5fc7b1d3c43","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1d084739c6ff0a78d22cda99a414c5fc7b1d3c43"}]},{"sha":"1d084739c6ff0a78d22cda99a414c5fc7b1d3c43","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDFkMDg0NzM5YzZmZjBhNzhkMjJjZGE5OWE0MTRjNWZjN2IxZDNjNDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-26T07:13:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-26T07:13:30Z"},"message":"ci(core-api): freeze v1 broker OpenAPI baseline + oasdiff gate (Gate C Phase 1) (#620)\n\n## What\n**Freeze the v1 broker↔cloud OpenAPI contract for core-api** and enforce\nit on every PR with an `oasdiff` breaking-change gate. Phase 1\n(Deliverables A+B) of the broker API-versioning RFC\n(`docs/design/broker-cloud-api-versioning.md`, enterprise repo).\n\n## Why\nv1 was a *label*, not an enforced contract — breaking changes shipped\ninside `/v1` and silently broke installed brokers (the Phase-0\nincident). This commits the broker-facing contract as an artifact and\nfails CI on any breaking change to it, so a break must ship a new `/vN`.\n\n## Contents\n- **`core-api/scripts/gen_broker_openapi.py`** — imports `core_api.app`\noffline, filters `paths` to the 4 broker endpoints (`POST\n/api/v1/memories/bulk`, `POST /api/v1/search`, `GET /api/v1/health`,\n`GET /api/v1/version`; a missing path is a hard error), keeps only the\ntransitively-reachable schemas + referenced security schemes,\n**normalizes `info` to a frozen contract version (`v1`)** decoupled from\nthe rolling package semver (so releases don't churn the baseline), and\nemits deterministic JSON. `--check` fails if the committed baseline is\nstale.\n- **`core-api/openapi.broker.json`** — the frozen v1 baseline (4 paths,\n14 schemas, `APIKeyHeader`).\n- **`ci.yml`** — stale-baseline guard + `oasdiff breaking --fail-on ERR`\nvs `main`'s baseline (pinned `tufin/oasdiff:v1.26.0`; `--fail-on ERR`\nrequired — plain `oasdiff breaking` exits 0 even on breaks). First-merge\nbootstrap skips the diff when main has no baseline yet.\n- **`core-api/scripts/README.md`** — regeneration + contract-bump rules.\n\n## Validation\n`--check` clean and deterministic (byte-identical across runs); **proof\nthe gate bites**: a synthetic required field on `BulkMemoryCreate` →\n`oasdiff` reports `new-required-request-property`, exit 1 — then\nreverted. `ruff` clean on the script.\n\nRegenerate after an intentional broker contract change: `python\ncore-api/scripts/gen_broker_openapi.py`.\n\nGate C / Phase 1. Companion to the enterprise auth/audit gate (#889) and\nthe Phase-0 fixes.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"28cd6c678bedda7544ea699bc9e77cd91e9d0d33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/28cd6c678bedda7544ea699bc9e77cd91e9d0d33"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/1d084739c6ff0a78d22cda99a414c5fc7b1d3c43","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZbOaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGVIQAAVE93QV5TfD/8VP9vh50C6q\n3g7J7EnaJAAni1Q4/KhC5o83qT6psclMHX9VdThCHQNC2yTFeH1+L316SbIcnOST\nbOD0t0IJ20j8Ck75EgT2Rea2vxP/EpFoj60jmNPsugx1h4qeNuJtArpOyA7/SMhs\nOJFETINajoGWsdwEa1vJXwaOLt2dxS9Z/Lc1j8BaNX5xJ83RMOQtGVSNYJB2PN9w\nMSmuStuwnfSjivEvxB0RSk9UsxvFU424n62iZvpjzPvETd8mcGIou8JQaklXXcio\n1wCVllr2/l5ygLhd8jEepPpFVlS+O7Rq2sVSqmNG+xdapMuRsLm6T3iIvjkn7v3f\nq6dzBSY49pYTMEuRWFUAB4cPZ96uL/DTzb+DVOQAAUOUjvMrFfxnz/XRqICz8S14\nQ6K0zC01xxuVAIdcmqs5ag97LkiKJsnp3lbTtwZMVZozFY4L6SSY+Bzu0PQWGz+l\nbNqR/XNc2UKwPBPYEsmZ347ZJMVcA4bWmEmL1OYVlO9qx5YIjgdEBQgQJmANvVP0\nerStju18GUFWfNKBRCfrYaI5drtAQ9vqpUe2XB4pgkrarZZtgpbD7BFCQbte81VR\nYn4+qy0aUEyq8GMs0jtopSswrcYX0DPZDTPL2Pd9+1NM3miv3QOh5O7XtfA0afKD\nIozVieS2Adyo2jL+Pi1I\n=ieX7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 28cd6c678bedda7544ea699bc9e77cd91e9d0d33\nparent 5d80392d2b914a7eda3c546466d0c90d9d693eff\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1785050010 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785050010 +0300\n\nci(core-api): freeze v1 broker OpenAPI baseline + oasdiff gate (Gate C Phase 1) (#620)\n\n## What\n**Freeze the v1 broker↔cloud OpenAPI contract for core-api** and enforce\nit on every PR with an `oasdiff` breaking-change gate. Phase 1\n(Deliverables A+B) of the broker API-versioning RFC\n(`docs/design/broker-cloud-api-versioning.md`, enterprise repo).\n\n## Why\nv1 was a *label*, not an enforced contract — breaking changes shipped\ninside `/v1` and silently broke installed brokers (the Phase-0\nincident). This commits the broker-facing contract as an artifact and\nfails CI on any breaking change to it, so a break must ship a new `/vN`.\n\n## Contents\n- **`core-api/scripts/gen_broker_openapi.py`** — imports `core_api.app`\noffline, filters `paths` to the 4 broker endpoints (`POST\n/api/v1/memories/bulk`, `POST /api/v1/search`, `GET /api/v1/health`,\n`GET /api/v1/version`; a missing path is a hard error), keeps only the\ntransitively-reachable schemas + referenced security schemes,\n**normalizes `info` to a frozen contract version (`v1`)** decoupled from\nthe rolling package semver (so releases don't churn the baseline), and\nemits deterministic JSON. `--check` fails if the committed baseline is\nstale.\n- **`core-api/openapi.broker.json`** — the frozen v1 baseline (4 paths,\n14 schemas, `APIKeyHeader`).\n- **`ci.yml`** — stale-baseline guard + `oasdiff breaking --fail-on ERR`\nvs `main`'s baseline (pinned `tufin/oasdiff:v1.26.0`; `--fail-on ERR`\nrequired — plain `oasdiff breaking` exits 0 even on breaks). First-merge\nbootstrap skips the diff when main has no baseline yet.\n- **`core-api/scripts/README.md`** — regeneration + contract-bump rules.\n\n## Validation\n`--check` clean and deterministic (byte-identical across runs); **proof\nthe gate bites**: a synthetic required field on `BulkMemoryCreate` →\n`oasdiff` reports `new-required-request-property`, exit 1 — then\nreverted. `ruff` clean on the script.\n\nRegenerate after an intentional broker contract change: `python\ncore-api/scripts/gen_broker_openapi.py`.\n\nGate C / Phase 1. Companion to the enterprise auth/audit gate (#889) and\nthe Phase-0 fixes.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-26T07:13:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1d084739c6ff0a78d22cda99a414c5fc7b1d3c43","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1d084739c6ff0a78d22cda99a414c5fc7b1d3c43","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1d084739c6ff0a78d22cda99a414c5fc7b1d3c43/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5d80392d2b914a7eda3c546466d0c90d9d693eff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5d80392d2b914a7eda3c546466d0c90d9d693eff","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5d80392d2b914a7eda3c546466d0c90d9d693eff"}]},{"sha":"5d80392d2b914a7eda3c546466d0c90d9d693eff","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDVkODAzOTJkMmI5MTRhN2VkYTNjNTQ2NDY2ZDBjOTBkOWQ2OTNlZmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-26T06:34:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-26T06:34:15Z"},"message":"fix(core-api): bulk unknown memory_type → per-item 207 (stacked on #619) (#621)\n\n## What\nCompletes bulk **additive-tolerance** for `BulkMemoryItem`: an unknown\n`memory_type` on one item now surfaces as a per-item `status=\"error\"`\n(207) row instead of 422-ing the whole batch. Follow-up to #619\n(content/weight/status), which deferred `memory_type` because it\nrequired an enum→str change.\n\n> **Stacked on #619** (`CAURA-000-coreapi-bulk-oversized-207`) — base is\nthat branch so the diff shows only the memory_type delta. **Merge after\n#619.**\n\n## Change\n- `BulkMemoryItem.memory_type`: `MemoryType | None` → `str | None`\n(single-write `MemoryCreate`/`MemoryUpdate` keep the typed enum — they\nstill hard-reject).\n- `create_memories_bulk`: new `memory_type_errors` validating against\nthe **full `MEMORY_TYPES`** vocabulary the enum accepted; it joins the\naggregated per-item error row and is excluded from `valid_indices`.\n- Valid types — including reserved/deprecated-but-known ones — flow\ndownstream **unchanged** (deprecated folding, defaulting, storage):\n`MemoryType` is a `str`-Enum, so valid values compare and persist\nidentically to before.\n\n## Tests\n- Integration: mixed batch with a bad `memory_type` **and a valid\nexplicit one** → 207, bad row errored, valid items (explicit + default\ntype) created.\n- Schema: `BulkMemoryItem` now accepts an unknown `memory_type`;\n`MemoryCreate` still rejects it (scope guard).\n- Full `test_bulk_write.py` + `test_bulk_atomicity.py` pass (47), plus\nthe deprecated-type (`test_caura702_*`) and bulk-caller\n(ingest/mcp/broker-write) regression modules (65). `ruff`/`mypy` clean\non `core-api/src`.\n\nGate C / Phase 0; T0.2 core-api. Closes the `memory_type` follow-up from\n#619.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d083cddf5de71e4f793827375e59d5b420421076","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/d083cddf5de71e4f793827375e59d5b420421076"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/5d80392d2b914a7eda3c546466d0c90d9d693eff","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZapnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqioQAAC2goMzmkFglUuLyQhaDrS4\nqJdYODxErvMDkNECJAZq0nmjz4HqBvtaz3UJGrmNqwYxP3R1WF2ICYtGDuRCts5u\naIBtLGfzhMtQ5HvArdR8F1BbRtcvEWgu3SC7RxnuTchEqLY7boE1YhmziXzGU98u\nv4Tqvgkewtuc7RyTPyByf8w1xGBXjGb5WvCjD6llNuRNVtJEFIpO+u4GTRCeHW9K\nB7hv0Ny1geDCm8cQf3AXh5yyKo8nSdYwnj8ZmYa7GZnIGONsRR6Zco97GXkAcgS2\ne8zeuBVqYEj8YFQNqUXtuUftjRFsvv2Y4dKcee2B45/fj+4Dm9yeWQ8z+/yKZHRm\nUhHrcKdxJEqoaqCPh1spayPgKeCmabukT7OeRteLrZN4frY8Lu975Nyi1ZM1kBTf\nYy0hyT9obtoMIF+W7TFBaIoKTLyye8jg7vJm1uWrA9ZM22NdQ5dGA0cixrRNIzoK\nNYcEt8u1fIi6QcMeAUXZBlMUhTpLYkxjNifw4cfX1UjP5AMQYtKa1Caa46N/YmOC\np9aW8T8ELiyopDmDA0sZQ9dMr4swhW5XVwISSuM/8Jn2Fw7uinKJj1yioCrFfu/+\nFeTFZ315ODFMxnb79BDrlcNld/HBd8+QgG+6iWBHpSXf7Rk+N4+DNxpkeCfrhp7b\nksRg8fEWroGICNsnpc36\n=ixq7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d083cddf5de71e4f793827375e59d5b420421076\nparent ebc4bbb2ea00d2cd8a8c33d1e08564fa116ff0d4\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1785047655 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785047655 +0300\n\nfix(core-api): bulk unknown memory_type → per-item 207 (stacked on #619) (#621)\n\n## What\nCompletes bulk **additive-tolerance** for `BulkMemoryItem`: an unknown\n`memory_type` on one item now surfaces as a per-item `status=\"error\"`\n(207) row instead of 422-ing the whole batch. Follow-up to #619\n(content/weight/status), which deferred `memory_type` because it\nrequired an enum→str change.\n\n> **Stacked on #619** (`CAURA-000-coreapi-bulk-oversized-207`) — base is\nthat branch so the diff shows only the memory_type delta. **Merge after\n#619.**\n\n## Change\n- `BulkMemoryItem.memory_type`: `MemoryType | None` → `str | None`\n(single-write `MemoryCreate`/`MemoryUpdate` keep the typed enum — they\nstill hard-reject).\n- `create_memories_bulk`: new `memory_type_errors` validating against\nthe **full `MEMORY_TYPES`** vocabulary the enum accepted; it joins the\naggregated per-item error row and is excluded from `valid_indices`.\n- Valid types — including reserved/deprecated-but-known ones — flow\ndownstream **unchanged** (deprecated folding, defaulting, storage):\n`MemoryType` is a `str`-Enum, so valid values compare and persist\nidentically to before.\n\n## Tests\n- Integration: mixed batch with a bad `memory_type` **and a valid\nexplicit one** → 207, bad row errored, valid items (explicit + default\ntype) created.\n- Schema: `BulkMemoryItem` now accepts an unknown `memory_type`;\n`MemoryCreate` still rejects it (scope guard).\n- Full `test_bulk_write.py` + `test_bulk_atomicity.py` pass (47), plus\nthe deprecated-type (`test_caura702_*`) and bulk-caller\n(ingest/mcp/broker-write) regression modules (65). `ruff`/`mypy` clean\non `core-api/src`.\n\nGate C / Phase 0; T0.2 core-api. Closes the `memory_type` follow-up from\n#619.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-26T06:34:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5d80392d2b914a7eda3c546466d0c90d9d693eff","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5d80392d2b914a7eda3c546466d0c90d9d693eff","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5d80392d2b914a7eda3c546466d0c90d9d693eff/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ebc4bbb2ea00d2cd8a8c33d1e08564fa116ff0d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ebc4bbb2ea00d2cd8a8c33d1e08564fa116ff0d4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ebc4bbb2ea00d2cd8a8c33d1e08564fa116ff0d4"}]},{"sha":"ebc4bbb2ea00d2cd8a8c33d1e08564fa116ff0d4","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGViYzRiYmIyZWEwMGQyY2Q4YThjMzNkMWUwODU2NGZhMTE2ZmYwZDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-25T21:05:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-25T21:05:09Z"},"message":"fix(interviewer): preserve exact figures in synthesis + document list-limit cap (#623)\n\nTwo fixes surfaced by the Interviewer staging rollout rehearsal\n(OpenClaw push path, validated end-to-end on `memclaw.dev`).\n\n## 1. Synthesis preserves exact figures + whole decisions (substantive)\nThe staging quality eval ran realistic work windows through the live\n**Gemini flash-lite** synthesis and scored the output against known\nground truth. It was strong on type-mapping, faithfulness (0\nhallucinations), and negative-outcome discipline — but had one\nconsistent weakness:\n- **dropped exact numbers** (`recall@10 0.87 vs 0.83, index -33%` →\n\"better recall\"), and\n- **flattened compound/conditional decisions** (`migrate to X after the\nY fix; keep Z as fallback` → \"migrate to X\").\n\nFix: strengthen `_REPORT_SCHEMA_INSTRUCTION` in `interview_service.py`\nto require preserving figures **verbatim** (metrics, thresholds, counts,\ndurations, versions, names) and keeping each decision **whole**\n(conditions, sequencing, alternatives). **Prompt-only — no model\nchange** (flash-lite stays; it's cheap, fast, and faithful, just needed\nsteering). Adds a unit test pinning the new instructions.\n\n## 2. Document the list-limit cap (minor)\n`GET /api/v1/memories?limit=1000` returns **422** (cap is\n`MAX_LIST_LIMIT=500`), which is easy to mistake for an empty result if\nthe error body isn't parsed. Document the cap + 422 behaviour in the\nOpenAPI `limit` param description on both list endpoints. **Behaviour\nunchanged** — the memories endpoint is deliberately strict (`le=`),\nunlike the clamp-style `skills_inbox` endpoint; I kept that choice and\nmade it discoverable rather than silently changing it.\n\n## Verification\n`tests/test_api_interview.py` 22/22 pass (incl. the new\n`test_build_prompt_demands_verbatim_figures_and_whole_decisions`); ruff\nclean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2cab937791e9bc28278306195ed8bf7333ddc7a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/2cab937791e9bc28278306195ed8bf7333ddc7a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/ebc4bbb2ea00d2cd8a8c33d1e08564fa116ff0d4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZSUFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfHoQAAdXHo6GVzF6y+6KxHiGGaE/\nBUP8elqnXjayo9W12lLyaImetGRDz3nyiLGKIrglEWFoRC9RkejUO4Ql604sY4gS\ngNHZ9x4Ycet+s+H0Vf5+SL2bLgOn1x+oB8FLq+efgV4UcQBicdMmPPL6XBwpl5//\nEo11Du59jvkmRZbmHANuGWNKSCZyGa+ptaETBNvjXoNmamTzDXMyBiDe3NOAwHrq\nSO/k72K7yOetw4oH+QRCFnQcfj32UEjnazPjYj1cpbkwTvVGS58njFm21SX5GFLA\n7gbul/yYv1RPSEF3XppDDiY8cm2hwAb1yCKQaQPGRYGJ1EE4TpOnMcd+wocuW8Sr\nJ3ede3g6OTlFFvhQdGVIHI0OdeKVXKQMigvtWgCguzB1eYhfwcVFk+PoSDoTmsco\n2/7X8BTj3ekzOBk5MIKmkoUFmzBDLS1HNLWuShUWGdTpHw9B+9OElkYlgOGvbzjg\n3EHtl0+ZFU2iQ0sD3zEUd5NErA1hPjOhOV88lHuRHgdIZ6Nye0T+NdHuQTgC2Bjn\nkdAEhiM6b8tA2K76a2K3oeEETTx/kaiyKVaxhbPE6aB9lRQeELPR8HueDH0xiWFP\nW7BfLop1Pd79jXBO4wW9KjbQb6RvSn4otyzgVkXXhwALMHc1O9NaNxXp20sFm06S\nTp7xQy6n77wHGOmOB10B\n=R67+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2cab937791e9bc28278306195ed8bf7333ddc7a6\nparent c721c6d1fef76fad1330da5b127ec76cf23ea9ca\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1785013509 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785013509 +0300\n\nfix(interviewer): preserve exact figures in synthesis + document list-limit cap (#623)\n\nTwo fixes surfaced by the Interviewer staging rollout rehearsal\n(OpenClaw push path, validated end-to-end on `memclaw.dev`).\n\n## 1. Synthesis preserves exact figures + whole decisions (substantive)\nThe staging quality eval ran realistic work windows through the live\n**Gemini flash-lite** synthesis and scored the output against known\nground truth. It was strong on type-mapping, faithfulness (0\nhallucinations), and negative-outcome discipline — but had one\nconsistent weakness:\n- **dropped exact numbers** (`recall@10 0.87 vs 0.83, index -33%` →\n\"better recall\"), and\n- **flattened compound/conditional decisions** (`migrate to X after the\nY fix; keep Z as fallback` → \"migrate to X\").\n\nFix: strengthen `_REPORT_SCHEMA_INSTRUCTION` in `interview_service.py`\nto require preserving figures **verbatim** (metrics, thresholds, counts,\ndurations, versions, names) and keeping each decision **whole**\n(conditions, sequencing, alternatives). **Prompt-only — no model\nchange** (flash-lite stays; it's cheap, fast, and faithful, just needed\nsteering). Adds a unit test pinning the new instructions.\n\n## 2. Document the list-limit cap (minor)\n`GET /api/v1/memories?limit=1000` returns **422** (cap is\n`MAX_LIST_LIMIT=500`), which is easy to mistake for an empty result if\nthe error body isn't parsed. Document the cap + 422 behaviour in the\nOpenAPI `limit` param description on both list endpoints. **Behaviour\nunchanged** — the memories endpoint is deliberately strict (`le=`),\nunlike the clamp-style `skills_inbox` endpoint; I kept that choice and\nmade it discoverable rather than silently changing it.\n\n## Verification\n`tests/test_api_interview.py` 22/22 pass (incl. the new\n`test_build_prompt_demands_verbatim_figures_and_whole_decisions`); ruff\nclean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-25T21:05:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ebc4bbb2ea00d2cd8a8c33d1e08564fa116ff0d4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ebc4bbb2ea00d2cd8a8c33d1e08564fa116ff0d4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ebc4bbb2ea00d2cd8a8c33d1e08564fa116ff0d4/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c721c6d1fef76fad1330da5b127ec76cf23ea9ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c721c6d1fef76fad1330da5b127ec76cf23ea9ca","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/c721c6d1fef76fad1330da5b127ec76cf23ea9ca"}]},{"sha":"c721c6d1fef76fad1330da5b127ec76cf23ea9ca","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGM3MjFjNmQxZmVmNzZmYWQxMzMwZGE1YjEyN2VjNzZjZjIzZWE5Y2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-25T20:42:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-25T20:42:46Z"},"message":"feat(search): unified relevance-dominant ranking formula behind score_formula flag (#622)\n\n## What\nA per-tenant **`score_formula`** flag (default **0 = legacy**, no\nbehaviour change). When **1**, `memory_scored_search` computes a\n**unified, relevance-dominant** score instead of the legacy\nmultiplicative boost stack.\n\n## The unified formula (`score_formula = 1`)\n```\nscore = ( similarity                                        # relevance, dominant ∈ [0,1]\n        + 0.10 · recency_gate · (freshness − freshness_floor)   # recency, GATED to temporal queries\n        + 0.10 · (date_range_boost − 1.0)                        # date-window nudge (0 off-query)\n        + 0.10 · (entity_boost − 1.0)                            # entity/graph nudge (0 when absent)\n        − 0.20 · (1.0 − currency_factor) )                       # staleness penalty (0 when current)\n        × status_penalty                                         # hard conflicted/outdated demotion\n```\n`recency_gate = 1` iff the query is temporal (`temporal_window` set),\nelse 0.\n\nVs legacy: **similarity dominates**; boosts are **additive + bounded**\n(reorder within a relevance band, never override a real gap);\n**freshness gated to temporal queries**; drops the `0.15·weight` floor\n(A46) and popularity `recall_boost` (A41).\n\n## Why\nLongMemEval failure analysis + offline calibration: relevance-dominant\nordering beats the boost stack on every category (incl. temporal),\nbecause the multiplicative boosts demote strong matches. Full rationale:\n`docs/ranking/unified-ranking-formula.md`.\n\n## Scope / safety\n- **Off by default → zero behaviour change.** Flip per tenant via\n`default_search_profile.score_formula`.\n- Weights are a **first cut, uncalibrated** — tune via the offline\nharness before considering default-on.\n- Enables an A/B on the benchmark by flipping the flag between runs (no\nrunner change).\n\n## Tests\n- core-api plumbing (default legacy, validate/clamp, resolve threading).\n- storage integration (real pgvector): the unified formula ranks a\nstrong match above a boost-inflated low-similarity row; legacy does the\nopposite. No regression on existing `/scored-search` tests.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"3e281f2b7b106fd33bb3149df7169df69d6ebf30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/3e281f2b7b106fd33bb3149df7169df69d6ebf30"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/c721c6d1fef76fad1330da5b127ec76cf23ea9ca","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZR/GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt4UQAFbk3IBo505+tnL3Tix4BsA2\nx0OmdZy3k5Q+2MAXjXTFZ+XJixRxEBSCtiV1e2b9kMSJuqEQhcdwfW/Z4paQZrvY\nYuhZgcTEIZWUrQEMk0CfDU4hrOLBOcRjDYbgl54jRHEJQp64Vq2wr+X7MbVvc0cb\nBA+Rw99iJAOBvWNayQ6KMR4VinjvACjpOztQ5xkoU+FSU60iBeKHyjN5KPlsD/HJ\nBwhaAQnFVCQwBO/wYV6Im1Wm7EbmEy/UNozEcgzaRlPVqdbKp7KxugjtKlFBQI7S\n8TW+nQva8KM+1tjONaK4TtYrwTdXchDviBaTViczUoXK6YQp4q8wpXdi4ngOnSX/\nfkeEP99pbnN9G0Bs31RZuV2hKErGQr5cdvyNO3DNlUHgrGIFnBr9kVOo/4s9XiNX\ngmr9vmBR4CIssIJFGwk7T8ydiCUPmr6S2ygdSv08Ko0KkgSobJnLeDZaB/uDAi7N\nTW+tzPCgvJXT/s0Cm3rcVb3EtLw7bMFbu+VIrO7lUf++F3MPkv6ue5ntUTj15a4H\nnyG6jEmrmwJbjGkhx7bZj1OpyNy4sFqYX5kgBm3+LdcVvaRpGj4/YOa9yumGXlF5\n1Gq8m0DjeSUaMoqVZwiNhk8e6Qal20AKes1sBunEQveRr1nH3jFzksVxnDXno+At\nGT1z47nxyEp3dlNJO9gS\n=2f/i\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3e281f2b7b106fd33bb3149df7169df69d6ebf30\nparent 36e8212406ece9308fb025ea69e13b81120977b2\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1785012166 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785012166 +0300\n\nfeat(search): unified relevance-dominant ranking formula behind score_formula flag (#622)\n\n## What\nA per-tenant **`score_formula`** flag (default **0 = legacy**, no\nbehaviour change). When **1**, `memory_scored_search` computes a\n**unified, relevance-dominant** score instead of the legacy\nmultiplicative boost stack.\n\n## The unified formula (`score_formula = 1`)\n```\nscore = ( similarity                                        # relevance, dominant ∈ [0,1]\n        + 0.10 · recency_gate · (freshness − freshness_floor)   # recency, GATED to temporal queries\n        + 0.10 · (date_range_boost − 1.0)                        # date-window nudge (0 off-query)\n        + 0.10 · (entity_boost − 1.0)                            # entity/graph nudge (0 when absent)\n        − 0.20 · (1.0 − currency_factor) )                       # staleness penalty (0 when current)\n        × status_penalty                                         # hard conflicted/outdated demotion\n```\n`recency_gate = 1` iff the query is temporal (`temporal_window` set),\nelse 0.\n\nVs legacy: **similarity dominates**; boosts are **additive + bounded**\n(reorder within a relevance band, never override a real gap);\n**freshness gated to temporal queries**; drops the `0.15·weight` floor\n(A46) and popularity `recall_boost` (A41).\n\n## Why\nLongMemEval failure analysis + offline calibration: relevance-dominant\nordering beats the boost stack on every category (incl. temporal),\nbecause the multiplicative boosts demote strong matches. Full rationale:\n`docs/ranking/unified-ranking-formula.md`.\n\n## Scope / safety\n- **Off by default → zero behaviour change.** Flip per tenant via\n`default_search_profile.score_formula`.\n- Weights are a **first cut, uncalibrated** — tune via the offline\nharness before considering default-on.\n- Enables an A/B on the benchmark by flipping the flag between runs (no\nrunner change).\n\n## Tests\n- core-api plumbing (default legacy, validate/clamp, resolve threading).\n- storage integration (real pgvector): the unified formula ranks a\nstrong match above a boost-inflated low-similarity row; legacy does the\nopposite. No regression on existing `/scored-search` tests.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-25T20:42:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c721c6d1fef76fad1330da5b127ec76cf23ea9ca","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/c721c6d1fef76fad1330da5b127ec76cf23ea9ca","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c721c6d1fef76fad1330da5b127ec76cf23ea9ca/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"36e8212406ece9308fb025ea69e13b81120977b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/36e8212406ece9308fb025ea69e13b81120977b2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/36e8212406ece9308fb025ea69e13b81120977b2"}]},{"sha":"36e8212406ece9308fb025ea69e13b81120977b2","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDM2ZTgyMTI0MDZlY2U5MzA4ZmIwMjVlYTY5ZTEzYjgxMTIwOTc3YjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-24T22:05:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-24T22:05:47Z"},"message":"fix(core-api): bulk write reports oversized items per-item (207), not whole-batch 422 (#619)\n\n## What\nMake the core-api bulk memory-write endpoint (`POST\n/api/v1/memories/bulk`) report an oversized item as a **per-item\n`status=\"error\"` (207 multi-status)** instead of rejecting the **entire\nbatch with 422**.\n\n## Why\n`BulkMemoryItem.content` carried a schema-level\n`max_length=MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH` (10 000), so FastAPI validated the whole\nbody before the handler ran and **one** oversized item 422'd **all**\nitems. The broker↔cloud API-versioning RFC\n(`docs/design/broker-cloud-api-versioning.md`, enterprise repo) requires\nthis to be additive-tolerant: valid items must still be written, the\noversized one surfaced as a typed per-item error.\n\n## Change\n- Remove `max_length` from `BulkMemoryItem.content` **only**\n(`MemoryCreate.content` and `MemoryUpdate.content` keep it —\nsingle-write still hard-rejects). `min_length=1` stays (an empty item is\na malformed request, not a per-item business error).\n- Enforce the cap per-item in `create_memories_bulk`: an oversized item\nis excluded from embed/enrich/dedup/write and recorded as\n`BulkItemResult(status=\"error\", error=\"content exceeds maximum length of\n10000 characters\")` — the **same shape** as the existing short-content\nand governance-drop paths. `_bulk_response` then yields 207 for a mix,\n200 for all-valid (unchanged). Length is measured on the raw string,\nmatching the old `max_length` semantics.\n\n## Tests\n- Mixed batch (1 oversized + 2 valid) → `created=2, errors=1`, HTTP\n**207**, oversized row `status=\"error\"` with `id=null`.\n- All-valid batch (incl. one at exactly 10 000 chars) → HTTP **200**.\n- Schema now accepts oversized bulk content; `MemoryCreate` still\nrejects it (scope guard).\n\n`ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, `mypy` clean; bulk test modules + a\nregression sweep of every `create_memories_bulk` caller pass locally.\n\nGate C / Phase 0; **T0.2 core-api side** — complements the broker\ncontent cap ([memclawd\n#92](https://github.com/caura-ai/memclawd/pull/92)) and the gateway body\nlimit (enterprise #888).\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"95b686db864f27d7af8dfc2125c232bca457c54e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/95b686db864f27d7af8dfc2125c232bca457c54e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/36e8212406ece9308fb025ea69e13b81120977b2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqY+G7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADxoQAE5Ck1sJcKJavP0e8f/3CZov\nK3cP2Wmk7Xx9S/YNCcrwAmpwMJzjnwjHDBWClP9VxswjjQNVoTp/w55GQl5KrBSl\nvBrRwbp86sRcNygWLlZ82fH5A6WtihPDb/lFjSkH5HDqqK4zW3AH102gDfoeJm6p\nrplCWPeYQdDq4S559EtcqjkiKOiNAqMzos43ueY/Qy3eVGsLHMfMigCyzw6aud38\nlSuS3VhnvhXWTk7vUHvPcJ1ywTrWE28Q13lTQRpieWhWNdl1XLccEEM8Abl02ei3\nLF8KCf3GFHX7MdwMaMYwfEAuB92yO+4/+4h5ylun1OwIh/XcSRkaPGuyHZuS53cU\nKklnepeBTT/4j3/npdPdTLZEHKok4f2l5ejsf8vrrj99u9QphGkyJaO+nqjzIQSJ\n1a12cPOZxrhXrPnI1EBXbQrZbZVd9Stjj6N4JLyoq81RHb8UTmhxxRWQ2jVeHAG2\n19zxunFmU1C8vrwVeHnG0I03oCL8wvhbThf0H91tEjhGohHb/ctqqyGieVpVsyt4\nb77v5RbLljiPNxT83I6OlW12R/cqJCs3bJKw/8yNT/TVxpev41ac8mWsu3kfh80v\ny24jNfpEJt5UJaHYP9flORDnBAg8Nc5+rRjeYJ5D3XHkeQNv8jcqzRkwbIrUCMCe\nohLQ1y7jsXObct7rSn/J\n=rbNx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 95b686db864f27d7af8dfc2125c232bca457c54e\nparent 1a6fe9fbf37acee03ef26074dc6f24910ad570da\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1784930747 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784930747 +0300\n\nfix(core-api): bulk write reports oversized items per-item (207), not whole-batch 422 (#619)\n\n## What\nMake the core-api bulk memory-write endpoint (`POST\n/api/v1/memories/bulk`) report an oversized item as a **per-item\n`status=\"error\"` (207 multi-status)** instead of rejecting the **entire\nbatch with 422**.\n\n## Why\n`BulkMemoryItem.content` carried a schema-level\n`max_length=MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH` (10 000), so FastAPI validated the whole\nbody before the handler ran and **one** oversized item 422'd **all**\nitems. The broker↔cloud API-versioning RFC\n(`docs/design/broker-cloud-api-versioning.md`, enterprise repo) requires\nthis to be additive-tolerant: valid items must still be written, the\noversized one surfaced as a typed per-item error.\n\n## Change\n- Remove `max_length` from `BulkMemoryItem.content` **only**\n(`MemoryCreate.content` and `MemoryUpdate.content` keep it —\nsingle-write still hard-rejects). `min_length=1` stays (an empty item is\na malformed request, not a per-item business error).\n- Enforce the cap per-item in `create_memories_bulk`: an oversized item\nis excluded from embed/enrich/dedup/write and recorded as\n`BulkItemResult(status=\"error\", error=\"content exceeds maximum length of\n10000 characters\")` — the **same shape** as the existing short-content\nand governance-drop paths. `_bulk_response` then yields 207 for a mix,\n200 for all-valid (unchanged). Length is measured on the raw string,\nmatching the old `max_length` semantics.\n\n## Tests\n- Mixed batch (1 oversized + 2 valid) → `created=2, errors=1`, HTTP\n**207**, oversized row `status=\"error\"` with `id=null`.\n- All-valid batch (incl. one at exactly 10 000 chars) → HTTP **200**.\n- Schema now accepts oversized bulk content; `MemoryCreate` still\nrejects it (scope guard).\n\n`ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, `mypy` clean; bulk test modules + a\nregression sweep of every `create_memories_bulk` caller pass locally.\n\nGate C / Phase 0; **T0.2 core-api side** — complements the broker\ncontent cap ([memclawd\n#92](https://github.com/caura-ai/memclawd/pull/92)) and the gateway body\nlimit (enterprise #888).\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-24T22:05:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/36e8212406ece9308fb025ea69e13b81120977b2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/36e8212406ece9308fb025ea69e13b81120977b2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/36e8212406ece9308fb025ea69e13b81120977b2/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1a6fe9fbf37acee03ef26074dc6f24910ad570da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1a6fe9fbf37acee03ef26074dc6f24910ad570da","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1a6fe9fbf37acee03ef26074dc6f24910ad570da"}]},{"sha":"1a6fe9fbf37acee03ef26074dc6f24910ad570da","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDFhNmZlOWZiZjM3YWNlZTAzZWYyNjA3NGRjNmYyNDkxMGFkNTcwZGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-23T09:01:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T09:01:07Z"},"message":"fix(mcp): allow own-fleet list/stats reads at trust 1 (#617)\n\n## Problem\n\nA client reported that `elisheva-claude` (trust 1, RND fleet) was\nrejected with `FORBIDDEN: trust_level=1 < required 2` when trying to see\nother RND agents' memories.\n\nPer the product spec, **trust level 1 = read/write within its own\nfleet**; level 2 *adds* cross-fleet reads. But `memclaw_list` and\n`memclaw_stats` gated **every** non-agent scope at trust ≥ 2:\n\n```python\nmin_level = 1 if scope == \"agent\" else 2\n```\n\nThis charged a **same-fleet** read as if it were **cross-fleet**,\ncontradicting the spec. It also diverged from the platform's other read\nsurfaces, which already implement the spec:\n- `memclaw_recall` — auto-scopes a constrained agent to its own fleet,\ngates only cross-fleet via `enforce_fleet_read`\n([mcp_server.py:678](../blob/main/core-api/src/core_api/mcp_server.py))\n- REST `GET /memories` + `POST /search` — allow own-fleet at any trust,\nrequire L2 only for a different fleet\n\n## Fix\n\nResolve the trust floor by the **target fleet**, not the scope string\n(`_resolve_read_fleet_gate`, shared by both tools):\n\n| scope | target | min trust |\n|---|---|---|\n| `agent` | own memories | 1 |\n| `fleet` | own fleet | 1 |\n| `fleet` | different fleet | 2 |\n| `all` | tenant-wide | 2 |\n\n**Security detail:** a constrained caller (trust < 2) that omits\n`fleet_id` on `scope='fleet'` is **pinned to its home fleet**.\n`memory_list_by_filters` / `memory_stats_breakdown` only apply the fleet\nfilter when `fleet_id` is set, and their visibility predicate returns\n`scope_team` rows across *all* fleets — so without the pin,\n`scope='fleet'` with no `fleet_id` would fan out to other fleets' shared\nrows at L1. This mirrors the existing `memclaw_recall` guard. Unknown\nagents soft-pass at L1 (read ergonomics), consistent with\n`require_trust` / `recall`. The `scope_agent` visibility predicate is\nunchanged, so no private rows are exposed.\n\n## Deliberately out of scope\n\n`insights` and `evolve` share the same flat gate but are **not** touched\n— investigation found each needs a separate change first:\n- **`insights`** `scope='fleet'` read has **no `scope_agent` exclusion**\n— lowering it would let a trust-1 agent read peers' *private* rows via\nsynthesis.\n- **`evolve`** `scope='fleet'` **mutates peers' memories** (weights +\ngenerated rules), not a read.\n\n## Verification\n\nNo local Postgres/Docker, so the DB-backed suite wasn't run here.\nVerified:\n- `_resolve_read_fleet_gate` logic across all 7 scope/fleet/trust cases\n- End-to-end handler behavior with stubs: own-fleet allowed + `fleet_id`\npinned; cross-fleet blocked; `scope=agent`/`all` skip the lookup\n- Baselines regenerated with the canonical producers (list/stats\ndescriptions only); `tools/list` = 4885 cl100k tokens (ceiling 5200)\n- New/updated unit tests: split `list` fleet test into own-allowed vs\ncross-blocked, 7 helper tests, `get_agent` stubs added to the two\ncross-tenant audit tests\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4f76831d7a21dda35bc27ccf5aa21c5546859b72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/4f76831d7a21dda35bc27ccf5aa21c5546859b72"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/1a6fe9fbf37acee03ef26074dc6f24910ad570da","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYdhTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApfYQAHD+6J32uqSyzGrn2U/MOhmh\nuAlLLu/8xAGuXIeoSYvWdSceoq8Y8Mrg4OSfs1whws93WpIP0Y3fVMV3b08yyPOM\nVF2M5uWzH5y4Nb8h/sL4Gn+hKrf+1aUUfO9Pn4Ef5aOa7qKQ3zvCYwQ7Dy/kqCi5\n9fLRc2MKua8F+kmjTysBUJh+WZ4Mwe3xpityrG0dk/XqJl9YHEUUrhMYDE8jlCSo\nXImthdOLhYexqRTRiS3c8+f/MFE10dV0gNSFv5ve+EV/dUwFCy9ZUoj9u2MDZClm\nSvuJDPSaSptObcvkS9y8xpEPOdPBh8YZberU7ItKVs6yNOd+rvU1Y8o16Pot7x75\nElwxpDnvk4PkkEThw1dDw2v+gbOGwK7iWblCJvPDVpUDBehl9VktQO0TzMTqBowV\nyWGNS6iPBPNjWFi6GPxXaZrRw2tDmq6yCRdn98PORmTih4/P7zPavdr92VIh9BP3\nDF52fkKqxHzMmkCSHx4u2Z1J1bOxDR3LNxxw0LEFA1AtO2L3Dc76s/6PXn2hHEYO\nsGvAgB/ZwBll3h2UzYllQuQXS4SzVqIFOMbdbodlqrqs1kEVBGm8sieqZZYfLcNl\nkKLs/QQHiI8hGHQJO8fv2haPJ8f/RI+zKOunrZQKWfi+sw3nINgXcjPchhBWf8NY\nEMH/j2v7TI5Kg6jrXz0e\n=aT0r\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4f76831d7a21dda35bc27ccf5aa21c5546859b72\nparent fa8ed57287d35d1c43d8f14e15e9d30d035a88e2\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1784797267 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784797267 +0300\n\nfix(mcp): allow own-fleet list/stats reads at trust 1 (#617)\n\n## Problem\n\nA client reported that `elisheva-claude` (trust 1, RND fleet) was\nrejected with `FORBIDDEN: trust_level=1 < required 2` when trying to see\nother RND agents' memories.\n\nPer the product spec, **trust level 1 = read/write within its own\nfleet**; level 2 *adds* cross-fleet reads. But `memclaw_list` and\n`memclaw_stats` gated **every** non-agent scope at trust ≥ 2:\n\n```python\nmin_level = 1 if scope == \"agent\" else 2\n```\n\nThis charged a **same-fleet** read as if it were **cross-fleet**,\ncontradicting the spec. It also diverged from the platform's other read\nsurfaces, which already implement the spec:\n- `memclaw_recall` — auto-scopes a constrained agent to its own fleet,\ngates only cross-fleet via `enforce_fleet_read`\n([mcp_server.py:678](../blob/main/core-api/src/core_api/mcp_server.py))\n- REST `GET /memories` + `POST /search` — allow own-fleet at any trust,\nrequire L2 only for a different fleet\n\n## Fix\n\nResolve the trust floor by the **target fleet**, not the scope string\n(`_resolve_read_fleet_gate`, shared by both tools):\n\n| scope | target | min trust |\n|---|---|---|\n| `agent` | own memories | 1 |\n| `fleet` | own fleet | 1 |\n| `fleet` | different fleet | 2 |\n| `all` | tenant-wide | 2 |\n\n**Security detail:** a constrained caller (trust < 2) that omits\n`fleet_id` on `scope='fleet'` is **pinned to its home fleet**.\n`memory_list_by_filters` / `memory_stats_breakdown` only apply the fleet\nfilter when `fleet_id` is set, and their visibility predicate returns\n`scope_team` rows across *all* fleets — so without the pin,\n`scope='fleet'` with no `fleet_id` would fan out to other fleets' shared\nrows at L1. This mirrors the existing `memclaw_recall` guard. Unknown\nagents soft-pass at L1 (read ergonomics), consistent with\n`require_trust` / `recall`. The `scope_agent` visibility predicate is\nunchanged, so no private rows are exposed.\n\n## Deliberately out of scope\n\n`insights` and `evolve` share the same flat gate but are **not** touched\n— investigation found each needs a separate change first:\n- **`insights`** `scope='fleet'` read has **no `scope_agent` exclusion**\n— lowering it would let a trust-1 agent read peers' *private* rows via\nsynthesis.\n- **`evolve`** `scope='fleet'` **mutates peers' memories** (weights +\ngenerated rules), not a read.\n\n## Verification\n\nNo local Postgres/Docker, so the DB-backed suite wasn't run here.\nVerified:\n- `_resolve_read_fleet_gate` logic across all 7 scope/fleet/trust cases\n- End-to-end handler behavior with stubs: own-fleet allowed + `fleet_id`\npinned; cross-fleet blocked; `scope=agent`/`all` skip the lookup\n- Baselines regenerated with the canonical producers (list/stats\ndescriptions only); `tools/list` = 4885 cl100k tokens (ceiling 5200)\n- New/updated unit tests: split `list` fleet test into own-allowed vs\ncross-blocked, 7 helper tests, `get_agent` stubs added to the two\ncross-tenant audit tests\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-23T09:01:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1a6fe9fbf37acee03ef26074dc6f24910ad570da","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1a6fe9fbf37acee03ef26074dc6f24910ad570da","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1a6fe9fbf37acee03ef26074dc6f24910ad570da/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fa8ed57287d35d1c43d8f14e15e9d30d035a88e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fa8ed57287d35d1c43d8f14e15e9d30d035a88e2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/fa8ed57287d35d1c43d8f14e15e9d30d035a88e2"}]},{"sha":"fa8ed57287d35d1c43d8f14e15e9d30d035a88e2","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGZhOGVkNTcyODdkMzVkMWM0M2Q4ZjE0ZTE1ZTlkMzBkMDM1YTg4ZTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-23T06:58:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-23T06:58:39Z"},"message":"chore(search): rename raw_fts -> raw_keyword_rank for clarity (#618)\n\n## What\nRename the local variable `raw_fts` → `raw_keyword_rank` in\n`memory_scored_search` (core-storage-api `postgres_service.py`).\n\n## Why\n`raw_fts` is the raw, unbounded `ts_rank_cd` cover-density keyword rank\n*before* it's squashed to `[0,1)` as `fts_score`. The new name says what\nit is.\n\n## Scope\n- Local variable only (2 lines); the built-in `ts_rank_cd(...)` call is\nuntouched.\n- **No behaviour change**, no logic change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"0d1d3fa8f2fa7702b9d3e8802f8e1aa75b2b9508","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/0d1d3fa8f2fa7702b9d3e8802f8e1aa75b2b9508"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/fa8ed57287d35d1c43d8f14e15e9d30d035a88e2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYbufCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtl0QACkZAXzXHuodbFmBmcPJY9o0\nciSbaFaQF2NTdCTviM2EMA6R682NlTP1oXZlH7dwc6Rk+cRv60//UXvQdPkGWTYf\nHpEk7G2z4zOQR5APk+1pigoaReTdYFtiAWDPXhcC42pVO05IBtL56XRmWfCtLqMK\ntD0Gv8o2VIsYfVpQ5XIynOrkH7YX5UALyZR6ZruPxeq+R0MFjyX5gLRwA9MKc4H2\nC+FDrD6G0ZS4bvbYS7DNHkcZAY5PGRxd7dT7JKzGyam8u/d73B2eipkxPMFadJS6\nf6XWovXD4vXXv3rr4BVLg1uyc9FbdyFPrGjewNaxWI0R9tTwVjfPZleY8DBlXZln\nlSmAE482MNIJz12fJA4VxaSqWB8WpPoI8YiPbS2cNBhoGgXh4YKaeRmsgwPYdWvu\njDzsEnOUL/H71MykyCkOs5pNLNlKudpthaaf2n3NYJp7OdCNsh8XpjbJvvmeUbMd\n2uiUp7ynGELGvFSG0bWMmZX4CDYAX9xAcBGjZQapgW4LrBw0303moc8xTElA+mna\n37BiT2ueTYJ427nB3y9Q2FhF5Jl7ou1uHH3j+FS6/cHWSBqR2aJNQ8xnCesW7GcI\nPKWSCteIA3myKdcZZ5BIQzxS3L0LydIWoAYISraigP2dBePrR9w1TsBhOUNOMg+o\nwXI4ibO5vyu5JILhEdOb\n=IHMT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0d1d3fa8f2fa7702b9d3e8802f8e1aa75b2b9508\nparent ed7945b12b950418034f0fa761f700e86d8866e1\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1784789919 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784789919 +0300\n\nchore(search): rename raw_fts -> raw_keyword_rank for clarity (#618)\n\n## What\nRename the local variable `raw_fts` → `raw_keyword_rank` in\n`memory_scored_search` (core-storage-api `postgres_service.py`).\n\n## Why\n`raw_fts` is the raw, unbounded `ts_rank_cd` cover-density keyword rank\n*before* it's squashed to `[0,1)` as `fts_score`. The new name says what\nit is.\n\n## Scope\n- Local variable only (2 lines); the built-in `ts_rank_cd(...)` call is\nuntouched.\n- **No behaviour change**, no logic change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-23T06:58:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fa8ed57287d35d1c43d8f14e15e9d30d035a88e2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/fa8ed57287d35d1c43d8f14e15e9d30d035a88e2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fa8ed57287d35d1c43d8f14e15e9d30d035a88e2/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ed7945b12b950418034f0fa761f700e86d8866e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ed7945b12b950418034f0fa761f700e86d8866e1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ed7945b12b950418034f0fa761f700e86d8866e1"}]},{"sha":"ed7945b12b950418034f0fa761f700e86d8866e1","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGVkNzk0NWIxMmI5NTA0MTgwMzRmMGZhNzYxZjcwMGU4NmQ4ODY2ZTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"eyal-bl","email":"eyal.b@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-22T08:11:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-22T08:11:55Z"},"message":"CAURA-703 feat(write): record memory_type provenance in metadata (#586)\n\n## What\n\nAdds a `metadata.memory_type_agent_set` boolean recording **who chose a\nmemory's type**:\n- `true` — the calling agent supplied `memory_type` explicitly.\n- `false` — the enrichment classifier, the default fallback, or the\ningest extractor chose it.\n\nThis was previously unrecoverable: nothing persisted the distinction\n(the `agent_provided_fields` snapshot lives only in the transient enrich\nevent and is discarded). It's set **synchronously at write time** — **no\nworker change, no DB migration** (plain JSONB key).\n\n## Why\n\nWe needed to answer, per memory, \"did the agent hand-pick this type or\ndid the system?\" — e.g. to audit classification quality and to tell\nagent-authored types apart from auto-classified ones. Binary was chosen\nover a multi-value source because it's fully known at write time (never\nchanges), so it avoids any async/worker coupling; the finer\nclassifier-vs-heuristic-vs-default split remains derivable from\n`metadata.llm_ms`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`merge_enrichment_fields`** (single write, fast + strong): capture\nthe flag from the raw agent value **before** the CAURA-701 deprecation\ndemotion, so an agent who supplied a now-deprecated type (`semantic` →\ncoerced to `fact`) still counts as agent-set.\n- **`create_memories_bulk`**:\n`metadata.setdefault(\"memory_type_agent_set\", item.memory_type is not\nNone)` — honours an ingest pre-stamp, else infers from the item.\n- **`ingest_service`**: pre-stamp `False` — ingested types come from the\nextraction LLM's `suggested_type`, not the calling agent.\n\n## Not in scope\n- Historical backfill (unrecoverable; absent key = legacy/unknown).\n- The bulk/ingest `semantic → fact` demotion gap (separate PR,\nCAURA-702).\n\n## Tests\n- Merge-step unit tests: agent-set wins & flagged `true`;\nclassifier-fill → `false`; deprecated-demote still `true`; default\nfallback → `false`.\n- Ingest: each committed fact is stamped `memory_type_agent_set =\nfalse`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Eyal Blyachman <eyal.b@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e81f82456126476726e03c3713cfa4014cf81102","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/e81f82456126476726e03c3713cfa4014cf81102"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/ed7945b12b950418034f0fa761f700e86d8866e1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYHtLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPFIQAHYEW9aShHWPx7eP/0yW7GiJ\naE7qP8AF8Z8xQSS/ZM/lqb1ZQ5muXdx+6rplgbcYtQxrzSQq6ngx7OZMpsB6g3Zv\n++YaKkluJQYsXaGbbhpQvpRrVhqycbZbeNZzUqjX8FPqr1RyK4NmKEaxq6Fjaenf\nWCA/QgBiLwsPyG5VfP34RUL1OM53kmWNvaNfA8TITFCgXcPIYnprc5wStMlxWvc+\ntYIu4Snx2oDO2AREqfyCbgiij4r91e9+kEX3jUAgum7ORm62Hl1s8Y/YDwTkn76M\nytmWuQlh5aXa2QvjxhI9OT9pFXPZFiA+j2zymfxkJ9YYhU4Z8MF3s5rUBoo7PSrH\npI3AKnB0xEI/o5CagciFeWpLFA1OdezcxQqbLkgQz3AO4tHLSHpYRnBMecp0RqbN\niPf+rmhh3X9b2R8DvHB2EzNJAEpMhkj1Q8sQDi7nnmzRht9MK12HJvICZOvKJRHK\n5mwp3A+11deAkjO8TPNwK83kiwxLLkbwGSWYBm6xSq/yHjxG8mE605fs/oqnyxeA\nYqAG4dBnIrZ8Yi9pV4xjOWA3c0VvOliRk8kDBky9kdP2ubl/d8pQMNpAiPlxepQa\nP0wZbw72CQJeO3pXX9SGr205Nw10PP6L5NqPB6H833Tqnvq+SCjRZKVnGcrZKXXO\n7EMGR7BTnFTjZpLNECxu\n=zKYh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e81f82456126476726e03c3713cfa4014cf81102\nparent cad8287ea842d50a1d7911e07f477b984bd5e9f5\nauthor eyal-bl <eyal.b@caura.ai> 1784707915 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784707915 +0300\n\nCAURA-703 feat(write): record memory_type provenance in metadata (#586)\n\n## What\n\nAdds a `metadata.memory_type_agent_set` boolean recording **who chose a\nmemory's type**:\n- `true` — the calling agent supplied `memory_type` explicitly.\n- `false` — the enrichment classifier, the default fallback, or the\ningest extractor chose it.\n\nThis was previously unrecoverable: nothing persisted the distinction\n(the `agent_provided_fields` snapshot lives only in the transient enrich\nevent and is discarded). It's set **synchronously at write time** — **no\nworker change, no DB migration** (plain JSONB key).\n\n## Why\n\nWe needed to answer, per memory, \"did the agent hand-pick this type or\ndid the system?\" — e.g. to audit classification quality and to tell\nagent-authored types apart from auto-classified ones. Binary was chosen\nover a multi-value source because it's fully known at write time (never\nchanges), so it avoids any async/worker coupling; the finer\nclassifier-vs-heuristic-vs-default split remains derivable from\n`metadata.llm_ms`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`merge_enrichment_fields`** (single write, fast + strong): capture\nthe flag from the raw agent value **before** the CAURA-701 deprecation\ndemotion, so an agent who supplied a now-deprecated type (`semantic` →\ncoerced to `fact`) still counts as agent-set.\n- **`create_memories_bulk`**:\n`metadata.setdefault(\"memory_type_agent_set\", item.memory_type is not\nNone)` — honours an ingest pre-stamp, else infers from the item.\n- **`ingest_service`**: pre-stamp `False` — ingested types come from the\nextraction LLM's `suggested_type`, not the calling agent.\n\n## Not in scope\n- Historical backfill (unrecoverable; absent key = legacy/unknown).\n- The bulk/ingest `semantic → fact` demotion gap (separate PR,\nCAURA-702).\n\n## Tests\n- Merge-step unit tests: agent-set wins & flagged `true`;\nclassifier-fill → `false`; deprecated-demote still `true`; default\nfallback → `false`.\n- Ingest: each committed fact is stamped `memory_type_agent_set =\nfalse`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Eyal Blyachman <eyal.b@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-22T08:11:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ed7945b12b950418034f0fa761f700e86d8866e1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ed7945b12b950418034f0fa761f700e86d8866e1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ed7945b12b950418034f0fa761f700e86d8866e1/comments","author":{"login":"eyal-bl","id":262085605,"node_id":"U_kgDOD58b5Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262085605?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl","html_url":"https://github.com/eyal-bl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cad8287ea842d50a1d7911e07f477b984bd5e9f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/cad8287ea842d50a1d7911e07f477b984bd5e9f5","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/cad8287ea842d50a1d7911e07f477b984bd5e9f5"}]},{"sha":"cad8287ea842d50a1d7911e07f477b984bd5e9f5","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGNhZDgyODdlYTg0MmQ1MGExZDc5MTFlMDdmNDc3Yjk4NGJkNWU5ZjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-21T23:08:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T23:08:36Z"},"message":"fix(common): guard ddtrace call in the structlog processor (#615)\n\n## What\nWraps the `_dd_tracer.get_log_correlation_context()` call in\n`common/structlog_config.py` (`_add_dd_trace_context`) in a\n`try/except`, returning the unmodified `event_dict` on failure.\n\n## Why\nThis processor runs on **every** log call. If ddtrace raises (tracer\nshutdown, forked-process re-init, internal bug), the exception currently\npropagates through the structlog chain — dropping the very log line that\nwould explain the failure, and in FastAPI potentially surfacing as an\nunhandled 500. Logging infrastructure must be resilient to a tracer-side\nfault.\n\nSurfaced by the `caura-memclaw-enterprise` `claude-review` when the\n`common/` re-vendor brought this file over (identical-policy vendored\nfile — fixing it here at the OSS source so the fix re-vendors\ndownstream).\n\nVerified locally: a tracer stub that raises no longer breaks the chain\n(returns `event_dict` unmodified); `ruff check`/`format` clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1607177f52d29fa61a07ec4ff2181c8bb100ae18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/1607177f52d29fa61a07ec4ff2181c8bb100ae18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/cad8287ea842d50a1d7911e07f477b984bd5e9f5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX/v0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqCAQAJv0s3PCrhAHlB6dGdePVCxW\nyUPO8jR27C4zinhxdSF+fVn/YbJ31eBjCtgmNyQMshoIwD02xZ9VhzEmSVsxe3uX\nvzRo+C0UggBu2fAgccoEaxEOp03wpcjEdtHLgeRxGGO0YVLltmD4CeDubmnCsufx\nExCxKXrc0j5SiySAahCatnvUQ1B/ij73LQZS7Fg7RbQaHgXMtYAyCre7tnf7Al+b\nnnuloK58t7GqiFffE0WjGy9xYssOuciB6lQ6zOjAaaMbxXikEC4XkO+nuNhqMK+D\nakyMWI4ieS3sAqwXHSY0UjpltPyuMJXj49qDqQI9Y+iTdV//1VK7ro8/CLE1bCpC\n8jhHQpPyoc/oXuaSOLgUZGn8AtYcS3ipK/J4OrFrP6dVZ3T58IhbJYmRLc44ovXB\nWh8Zeiy62uQ6Y3dLKdS2TBrAedfAaFbRxtmgqwsSeUAcxsuTuuizq3gTxBC+nijY\nsX2YjvNNHC4rxa2aiGFnNGJ4KlAhxvg9vO17bhvTUVBIGO0R3Ykx4JvpavVFwOKQ\nqpqDPws7Zf0toecFExULbdGQhrlBygNtTwJ60Bkk1r2Er1VwE9x+K3BmvZSY8ME9\nTK7J+r26Be3GVHweNrWBm5tzSr7f3Y09rQIBxLU2/uHoHX5AJvriOuadT9tWz1qC\nQKGvpWD1NL30rL+igSwp\n=BaQc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1607177f52d29fa61a07ec4ff2181c8bb100ae18\nparent dbd074282bb90e11d6c1a7ca771582ee4cc9c57b\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1784675316 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784675316 +0300\n\nfix(common): guard ddtrace call in the structlog processor (#615)\n\n## What\nWraps the `_dd_tracer.get_log_correlation_context()` call in\n`common/structlog_config.py` (`_add_dd_trace_context`) in a\n`try/except`, returning the unmodified `event_dict` on failure.\n\n## Why\nThis processor runs on **every** log call. If ddtrace raises (tracer\nshutdown, forked-process re-init, internal bug), the exception currently\npropagates through the structlog chain — dropping the very log line that\nwould explain the failure, and in FastAPI potentially surfacing as an\nunhandled 500. Logging infrastructure must be resilient to a tracer-side\nfault.\n\nSurfaced by the `caura-memclaw-enterprise` `claude-review` when the\n`common/` re-vendor brought this file over (identical-policy vendored\nfile — fixing it here at the OSS source so the fix re-vendors\ndownstream).\n\nVerified locally: a tracer stub that raises no longer breaks the chain\n(returns `event_dict` unmodified); `ruff check`/`format` clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T23:08:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/cad8287ea842d50a1d7911e07f477b984bd5e9f5","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/cad8287ea842d50a1d7911e07f477b984bd5e9f5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/cad8287ea842d50a1d7911e07f477b984bd5e9f5/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dbd074282bb90e11d6c1a7ca771582ee4cc9c57b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/dbd074282bb90e11d6c1a7ca771582ee4cc9c57b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/dbd074282bb90e11d6c1a7ca771582ee4cc9c57b"}]},{"sha":"dbd074282bb90e11d6c1a7ca771582ee4cc9c57b","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGRiZDA3NDI4MmJiOTBlMTFkNmMxYTdjYTc3MTU4MmVlNGNjOWM1N2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-21T20:24:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T20:24:16Z"},"message":"fix(logging): correlate structlog output with Datadog APM traces (#614)\n\n## Problem\n\n`DD_LOGS_INJECTION=true` is set on the deployed services, but ddtrace's\nlog injection patches the **stdlib** `logging.LogRecord` only. Our\nstructlog pipeline uses `PrintLoggerFactory` (writes straight to stdout,\nbypassing stdlib), so injection never fires — `dd.trace_id` /\n`dd.span_id` never reach the emitted JSON, and Datadog can't correlate a\nlog line to its APM trace. Surfaced during the caura-test-automation APM\nreview (caura-test-automation#208) and deferred there as a pre-existing,\nfleet-wide issue.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd a `_add_dd_trace_context` structlog processor that reads the active\nspan directly via ddtrace's public\n`tracer.get_log_correlation_context()` helper (verified against ddtrace\n4.11.1 — its keys are already `dd.trace_id`/`dd.span_id`) and injects\nthe IDs into the event dict. Placed in `_base_processors()` right after\n`merge_contextvars`, so it runs on **both** the native structlog chain\nand the stdlib-bridge `foreign_pre_chain`.\n\n- **Guarded import:** `ddtrace` is the optional `datadog` extra, so it's\nimported `try/except ImportError` at module top; the processor no-ops\nwhen absent (OSS / on-prem / local) — those imports and log calls are\nunaffected.\n- **No-op without an active span** (`trace_id == \"0\"`), so ambient\n(non-request) logs aren't stamped with a null trace.\n- `DD_LOGS_INJECTION` stays `true` — it still covers third-party libs\nthat log via stdlib directly.\n\n## Tests\nThree new cases in `tests/test_logging.py` (no ddtrace → no-op; active\nspan → IDs injected; no active span → skipped). Full file: **35 passed**\nlocally. `ruff format --check --isolated` (the vendored-file gate)\npasses.\n\n## Rollout\n- This file is **vendored `policy=identical`** into\n`caura-memclaw-enterprise` — the re-vendor bot syncs it after merge (no\nmanual enterprise PR).\n- `caura-ops` and `caura-test-automation` carry their own copies of this\nconfig; they get the same fix in their own repos (separate PRs).\n- **Verify after deploy:** a log line emitted inside a traced request\nshould show `dd.trace_id` matching the trace in APM. If Datadog doesn't\nauto-link, the remaining step is a Trace ID Remapper on the log pipeline\n(DD-side config, not code).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"e2fd2c4a3b4ac25e5210b567d77d608d6a4c9eed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/e2fd2c4a3b4ac25e5210b567d77d608d6a4c9eed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/dbd074282bb90e11d6c1a7ca771582ee4cc9c57b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX9VwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfXQQAAI65qmDYyMmN3uxK4tfUPZ7\nnEp2BgvPQF5L8TRWYxHbGgG1RHdTbAhDHWsTG7pv4AIBPcbPt5DyCkwEZD6+xszJ\nPI64j6d2OU3rysHY9T2qGRpcEZxBUTdRVXcCGKqjXXEx0zIXADerx+MyetZmQSnW\nnP96pZLm67B50JzogTOUSyOcZ67QPnBJ1IT7IiQBaHN7xZABNOAKSPc1K3BIsGtv\nwahxLbBpu+6Q5fAuXIbY5Fy4yo/YxhtAQBbGEl44mMLO5YAlRV9gRQ8GPRArUAy9\nK5TqZOvwVcCT2WfqMfW0qfJLp2/td09J4V8QfhbnzllJeAdH2qFZvQfShMZpmYPT\nL+33zFdeYrcz6BdZdI78YyB/i3pESlEAIje7z/V8I1U7WLI4jZe1MOalLXBfWoMU\nNDEYHSM3P+tTeqbhUVRIDWJqqtmoE3Qhp5Ep6eb+/mOam36qxzOHWCcqMydzEZ6o\nC/Zc0CtwtOv5cursp0XxnzwvTqA8SFqPZB1NeMhBAAcyN0VZt6TR7FU6FVJg9neL\nGh7RPJ1PlKblqqJbXjnmR6us/GL2E+OssIs9w/JjU/B3SD7xZ2Msz4Ugb0YBd69S\n85A1ENQCs8XfSlpQMxd6fQYryXgBbnKsDhyZSziLCVDuX+saqeo/BLYJgVSJyE40\nVO2MpzereeN9SwDP/Ghs\n=ziIL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e2fd2c4a3b4ac25e5210b567d77d608d6a4c9eed\nparent 62c21e7c9fd09efc07789c2cd6910a80dfd362a4\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1784665456 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784665456 +0300\n\nfix(logging): correlate structlog output with Datadog APM traces (#614)\n\n## Problem\n\n`DD_LOGS_INJECTION=true` is set on the deployed services, but ddtrace's\nlog injection patches the **stdlib** `logging.LogRecord` only. Our\nstructlog pipeline uses `PrintLoggerFactory` (writes straight to stdout,\nbypassing stdlib), so injection never fires — `dd.trace_id` /\n`dd.span_id` never reach the emitted JSON, and Datadog can't correlate a\nlog line to its APM trace. Surfaced during the caura-test-automation APM\nreview (caura-test-automation#208) and deferred there as a pre-existing,\nfleet-wide issue.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd a `_add_dd_trace_context` structlog processor that reads the active\nspan directly via ddtrace's public\n`tracer.get_log_correlation_context()` helper (verified against ddtrace\n4.11.1 — its keys are already `dd.trace_id`/`dd.span_id`) and injects\nthe IDs into the event dict. Placed in `_base_processors()` right after\n`merge_contextvars`, so it runs on **both** the native structlog chain\nand the stdlib-bridge `foreign_pre_chain`.\n\n- **Guarded import:** `ddtrace` is the optional `datadog` extra, so it's\nimported `try/except ImportError` at module top; the processor no-ops\nwhen absent (OSS / on-prem / local) — those imports and log calls are\nunaffected.\n- **No-op without an active span** (`trace_id == \"0\"`), so ambient\n(non-request) logs aren't stamped with a null trace.\n- `DD_LOGS_INJECTION` stays `true` — it still covers third-party libs\nthat log via stdlib directly.\n\n## Tests\nThree new cases in `tests/test_logging.py` (no ddtrace → no-op; active\nspan → IDs injected; no active span → skipped). Full file: **35 passed**\nlocally. `ruff format --check --isolated` (the vendored-file gate)\npasses.\n\n## Rollout\n- This file is **vendored `policy=identical`** into\n`caura-memclaw-enterprise` — the re-vendor bot syncs it after merge (no\nmanual enterprise PR).\n- `caura-ops` and `caura-test-automation` carry their own copies of this\nconfig; they get the same fix in their own repos (separate PRs).\n- **Verify after deploy:** a log line emitted inside a traced request\nshould show `dd.trace_id` matching the trace in APM. If Datadog doesn't\nauto-link, the remaining step is a Trace ID Remapper on the log pipeline\n(DD-side config, not code).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T20:24:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/dbd074282bb90e11d6c1a7ca771582ee4cc9c57b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/dbd074282bb90e11d6c1a7ca771582ee4cc9c57b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/dbd074282bb90e11d6c1a7ca771582ee4cc9c57b/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"62c21e7c9fd09efc07789c2cd6910a80dfd362a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/62c21e7c9fd09efc07789c2cd6910a80dfd362a4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/62c21e7c9fd09efc07789c2cd6910a80dfd362a4"}]},{"sha":"62c21e7c9fd09efc07789c2cd6910a80dfd362a4","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDYyYzIxZTdjOWZkMDllZmMwNzc4OWMyY2Q2OTEwYTgwZGZkMzYyYTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-21T17:11:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T17:11:57Z"},"message":"docs(readme): document the Interviewer feature (#613)\n\nAdds a README section for the Interviewer — MemClaw's third\nmemory-ingestion path, alongside realtime writes and ingestion.\n\n## What\nA grounded **The Interviewer** section (after Skill Factory), covering:\n- **Motivation** — `memclaw_write` captures what an agent *chose* to\nrecord; the Interviewer captures what it *did*, from the durable trail\nthe harness already keeps. Never re-runs the agent, so it can't\nconfabulate.\n- **What it writes** — the six report sections mapped onto the\nmemory-type enum (`worked_on→episode`, `decisions→decision`,\n`outcomes→outcome`, `blockers→task`, `open_questions→fact`,\n`preferences_learned→preference`).\n- **Two capture families** — OpenClaw plugin-buffer\n(`MEMCLAW_INTERVIEWER=true`) and the `memclaw-interviewer` disk-parser\nCLI (Claude Code + Cursor shipped; Hermes/others planned).\n- **Crash-safety** — deterministic attempt id then watermark advance\n(never a gap, never a duplicate).\n- **Privacy** — default-deny allowlist + local scrub + server mask.\n\nOpt-in per tenant, off by default. Full setup/protocol lives in the\nenterprise docs (separate PR).\n\n## Grounding\nEvery claim pulled from shipped source: `routes/interview.py`,\n`services/interview_service.py`, the plugin buffer, and the\n`clients/python` CLI.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8096cf2ed7b215db085693fba66ef1044d20cca0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/8096cf2ed7b215db085693fba66ef1044d20cca0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/62c21e7c9fd09efc07789c2cd6910a80dfd362a4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX6hdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO3kQAJnu37uTm7uXtHV5yxnChWQB\ngELcZgA433JJieJJWPqcpzmfy3IX12iiJRpPmF2gNFKztipN8Wj6404G1rt992UL\nsI3ER8P2bqMX+QzyivTlmfOqMQqSy/RMH7zHGUXPttdnc/8msbgVIgNWpLQC5tDY\n8pGWbO8riBVvS4iEczBn+NLjN74PNzO31L74D2Y2+Wds9XGyc5uG9n11xxPdXE5Y\nt4iE6v3B6Y+GAwsvIiJDbZ8tHmwfceDrlaHM0R/14IqncVBSh4gvwjGP5VStUDak\n1hW6noUktceASLed4jBucubVvN2/cBXQ04W+BP5IMD/fpJu9GThLtcp4/5v/8xqG\nd4GchUsWuBBE3Roc66HGYJik6p8PkqB6XtAcAi5KRgRxUYcd1snHt2FvHeAH1L4G\nCD+BQs9zazVlwjrCNycdDp/+MqHBD+j1Sqgx9zsYaT6KrqNjPsKWj5EnVpp/9Dvv\nFlbljpU9tM8trUzE4f++NsDVqJOkuETBfdKpuCwQCf5CRx8HyejzXhSCEVnwgT2V\nu2SuBeyPivx5C/rTx3wuYJ1m65uoWgz2xFJLLXGwZIqAuIAzcFFK/AICJzOZi3dC\nMJeZ3CAT/cjzoL4Qpmj01sLT0yAPRXVhBAchONltN0Oko81yEp7CNXmL/vvMWKOM\nG8Ae2kwLWhpwWmRT4L1i\n=+T9+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8096cf2ed7b215db085693fba66ef1044d20cca0\nparent efe2ff1504956a5ea89b1e9aa9df27c2703f3b55\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1784653917 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784653917 +0300\n\ndocs(readme): document the Interviewer feature (#613)\n\nAdds a README section for the Interviewer — MemClaw's third\nmemory-ingestion path, alongside realtime writes and ingestion.\n\n## What\nA grounded **The Interviewer** section (after Skill Factory), covering:\n- **Motivation** — `memclaw_write` captures what an agent *chose* to\nrecord; the Interviewer captures what it *did*, from the durable trail\nthe harness already keeps. Never re-runs the agent, so it can't\nconfabulate.\n- **What it writes** — the six report sections mapped onto the\nmemory-type enum (`worked_on→episode`, `decisions→decision`,\n`outcomes→outcome`, `blockers→task`, `open_questions→fact`,\n`preferences_learned→preference`).\n- **Two capture families** — OpenClaw plugin-buffer\n(`MEMCLAW_INTERVIEWER=true`) and the `memclaw-interviewer` disk-parser\nCLI (Claude Code + Cursor shipped; Hermes/others planned).\n- **Crash-safety** — deterministic attempt id then watermark advance\n(never a gap, never a duplicate).\n- **Privacy** — default-deny allowlist + local scrub + server mask.\n\nOpt-in per tenant, off by default. Full setup/protocol lives in the\nenterprise docs (separate PR).\n\n## Grounding\nEvery claim pulled from shipped source: `routes/interview.py`,\n`services/interview_service.py`, the plugin buffer, and the\n`clients/python` CLI.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T17:11:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/62c21e7c9fd09efc07789c2cd6910a80dfd362a4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/62c21e7c9fd09efc07789c2cd6910a80dfd362a4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/62c21e7c9fd09efc07789c2cd6910a80dfd362a4/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"efe2ff1504956a5ea89b1e9aa9df27c2703f3b55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/efe2ff1504956a5ea89b1e9aa9df27c2703f3b55","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/efe2ff1504956a5ea89b1e9aa9df27c2703f3b55"}]},{"sha":"efe2ff1504956a5ea89b1e9aa9df27c2703f3b55","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGVmZTJmZjE1MDQ5NTZhNWVhODliMWU5YWE5ZGYyN2MyNzAzZjNiNTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-21T13:56:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T13:56:19Z"},"message":"feat(client): memclaw-interviewer --harness cursor — Cursor adapter (Interviewer Phase 3) (#612)\n\n## What\n\nExtends the `memclaw-interviewer` disk-parser adapter (#581) to\n**Cursor** workstations. Client-only; zero server changes; version →\n0.3.0.\n\n## Substrate choice (grounded 2026-07-21)\n\nCursor has three conversation stores; this adapter rides the **JSONL\nagent-transcripts**\n(`~/.cursor/projects/<slug>/agent-transcripts/<uuid>/<uuid>.jsonl`) —\nthe layer Cursor's changelog persists *\"for tooling and hooks\"* and\ncalls *\"Claude Code-compatible JSONL\"*. The IDE `state.vscdb`\n(undocumented, has broken community parsers ~2×/year) and the CLI\n`store.db` (drifting to opaque protobuf) are deliberately out of scope.\n\n## Dialect (verified against real transcripts on disk)\n\n- `{role, message}` lines, no meta envelope; roleless `turn_ended`\nstatus lines consumed as noise\n- user text unwrapped from `<timestamp>`/`<user_query>` tags; timestamp\nparsed to ISO 8601 and inherited by replies (assistant lines carry none;\nmtime fallback)\n- trailing `[REDACTED]` thinking markers stripped; thinking-only turns\nfall under the 60-char floor\n- **no tool_result lines exist** — tool outputs excluded upstream by\nCursor\n\n## Reuse\n\nScan mechanics, windowing, watermark protocol, scrub, machine identity,\nand the failure matrix are shared unchanged. New: `--harness\n{claude-code,cursor}` (env `MEMCLAW_INTERVIEWER_HARNESS`), Cursor\ndiscovery layout (subagents excluded by construction),\n`cursor:`-namespaced node ids, and harness auto-inference from\n`transcript_path` shape so **one hook command serves both** Claude Code\n`SessionEnd` and Cursor `sessionEnd`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 65 unit tests (9 new, fixtures mirror a real transcript), ruff clean\n- Real-disk dry-run: correct window `[0..10]`, zero tag/redaction/tool\nleakage\n- Live dogfood vs local stack: window committed, watermark\n`cursor:<machine12>:<stem>` at `last_seq=10`, typed memory written,\nidempotent rerun skips via cheap line-count\n- Hook wet test: Cursor-shaped stdin payload drains the file, exit 0 on\nevery path, allowlist warn names the correct project (3 levels up)\n\n## Known accepted risks\n\n- Transcripts are append-only only since the 2026-06-29 Cursor CLI\nrelease; `--resume` can rewrite a file. The existing shrink guard\nskips-with-warning; same-length rewrites past the watermark are accepted\n(as with CC torn-tails).\n- Transcripts can be disabled in Cursor (`transcript_path: null`) — the\nhook exits 0 silently; docs to note enabling them.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8c3a35fd3de331fa41bbdaf90be8d5a4f42135ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/8c3a35fd3de331fa41bbdaf90be8d5a4f42135ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/efe2ff1504956a5ea89b1e9aa9df27c2703f3b55","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX3qDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzCsQAKpWeOVZKlKsytAmvn/IP0js\nhOT4sCJdom3yLS3A9FrFQX4N9D0ig7Jz8abMxYV0Y+lkyMv0HLfhtpHee+mPgrPQ\n2NG91H0QWIC3BZIyREpid1apzZ5NiXzFuvMWVxd1HY5l3YTmdgZUt/frB4z4/Tgy\njgc8dlrC9o6ztqLpLTJkYyBkyHMCJU5TeJv/CO2s9BBj45hxDP92YI94RXI87YMu\nhu0QA/6PT7oMSq7XmYR/5s1DwepM7deVBkjgJ8n6/RNkTFZlvuYRiNVkHGT+G7yk\nkJZGcCkEkOp5O2zZB9qg1tlyExbIYGd5A5BAeItHPi6cfFBCEm5vSDmQXkOzvXjN\nNyWJ3WtH8MaWAPTqhH7QxKA+rukv73EjfnHlkSIFGZx/oXShPzkWZ7AGnrklFVOc\n2ZY9oJ5T20JS8IqLxqEjVL1P5ybsB0yl/Ob1Ay/HZpyLijeMpYkRIAf+PlUFy7NB\nbuL2oUTaE1vUA2x8F4f1d7epJ1Qv3d77WP9B3JdzKp8U1/XHhl73sHvY7vVDWhAk\nTsHf7KbbMryRZqO4gPd4ApwlN7322bb17gM70h3Eu+zmXIsoMZyvP2FjiipQ0zb5\nDST2WlMKRR3TDaG+Us9uIOZPbJiJWExaSjeKi0NOw7LSfMJ8LFl+rEAUs+Rmh9ly\nlSEkUsaG47SLbDC+V5VA\n=nHOc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8c3a35fd3de331fa41bbdaf90be8d5a4f42135ce\nparent 5e16fb9920694401227faf95f1da1235ce9aa11f\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1784642179 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784642179 +0300\n\nfeat(client): memclaw-interviewer --harness cursor — Cursor adapter (Interviewer Phase 3) (#612)\n\n## What\n\nExtends the `memclaw-interviewer` disk-parser adapter (#581) to\n**Cursor** workstations. Client-only; zero server changes; version →\n0.3.0.\n\n## Substrate choice (grounded 2026-07-21)\n\nCursor has three conversation stores; this adapter rides the **JSONL\nagent-transcripts**\n(`~/.cursor/projects/<slug>/agent-transcripts/<uuid>/<uuid>.jsonl`) —\nthe layer Cursor's changelog persists *\"for tooling and hooks\"* and\ncalls *\"Claude Code-compatible JSONL\"*. The IDE `state.vscdb`\n(undocumented, has broken community parsers ~2×/year) and the CLI\n`store.db` (drifting to opaque protobuf) are deliberately out of scope.\n\n## Dialect (verified against real transcripts on disk)\n\n- `{role, message}` lines, no meta envelope; roleless `turn_ended`\nstatus lines consumed as noise\n- user text unwrapped from `<timestamp>`/`<user_query>` tags; timestamp\nparsed to ISO 8601 and inherited by replies (assistant lines carry none;\nmtime fallback)\n- trailing `[REDACTED]` thinking markers stripped; thinking-only turns\nfall under the 60-char floor\n- **no tool_result lines exist** — tool outputs excluded upstream by\nCursor\n\n## Reuse\n\nScan mechanics, windowing, watermark protocol, scrub, machine identity,\nand the failure matrix are shared unchanged. New: `--harness\n{claude-code,cursor}` (env `MEMCLAW_INTERVIEWER_HARNESS`), Cursor\ndiscovery layout (subagents excluded by construction),\n`cursor:`-namespaced node ids, and harness auto-inference from\n`transcript_path` shape so **one hook command serves both** Claude Code\n`SessionEnd` and Cursor `sessionEnd`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 65 unit tests (9 new, fixtures mirror a real transcript), ruff clean\n- Real-disk dry-run: correct window `[0..10]`, zero tag/redaction/tool\nleakage\n- Live dogfood vs local stack: window committed, watermark\n`cursor:<machine12>:<stem>` at `last_seq=10`, typed memory written,\nidempotent rerun skips via cheap line-count\n- Hook wet test: Cursor-shaped stdin payload drains the file, exit 0 on\nevery path, allowlist warn names the correct project (3 levels up)\n\n## Known accepted risks\n\n- Transcripts are append-only only since the 2026-06-29 Cursor CLI\nrelease; `--resume` can rewrite a file. The existing shrink guard\nskips-with-warning; same-length rewrites past the watermark are accepted\n(as with CC torn-tails).\n- Transcripts can be disabled in Cursor (`transcript_path: null`) — the\nhook exits 0 silently; docs to note enabling them.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T13:56:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/efe2ff1504956a5ea89b1e9aa9df27c2703f3b55","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/efe2ff1504956a5ea89b1e9aa9df27c2703f3b55","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/efe2ff1504956a5ea89b1e9aa9df27c2703f3b55/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5e16fb9920694401227faf95f1da1235ce9aa11f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5e16fb9920694401227faf95f1da1235ce9aa11f","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5e16fb9920694401227faf95f1da1235ce9aa11f"}]},{"sha":"5e16fb9920694401227faf95f1da1235ce9aa11f","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDVlMTZmYjk5MjA2OTQ0MDEyMjdmYWY5NWYxZGExMjM1Y2U5YWExMWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-21T12:53:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T12:53:33Z"},"message":"deps(core-api): update redis[hiredis] requirement from <9,>=5.0 to >=8.0.1,<9 in /core-api (#609)\n\nUpdates the requirements on\n[redis[hiredis]](https://github.com/redis/redis-py) to permit the latest\nversion.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/releases\">redis[hiredis]'s\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>8.0.1</h2>\n<h1>Changes</h1>\n<h2>🐛 Bug Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix Unix socket maintenance notification handling and tests (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4097\">#4097</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix async cluster node connection release on write errors (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4111\">#4111</a>)</li>\n<li>Fixed async MultiDBClient with underlying RedisCluster (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4108\">#4108</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix hiredis readiness checks for high file descriptors (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4115\">#4115</a>)</li>\n<li>fix(search): parse RESP3 FT.SEARCH responses with bytes-typed keys\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4109\">#4109</a>)</li>\n<li>Fixing pubsub's listen method to be blocking. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4119\">#4119</a>)</li>\n<li>fix(asyncio): release pooled connection when Pipeline.reset() is\ncancelled (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4123\">#4123</a>)</li>\n<li>Avoid per-check fd allocation in hiredis _socket_can_read() — use\npoll() instead of a per-call selector (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4118\">#4118</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🧰 Maintenance</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Updating PyJWT dependency. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4100\">#4100</a>)</li>\n<li>Update CI badge in README.md (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4099\">#4099</a>)</li>\n<li>Add missing url query argument parser for ssl_min_version (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4047\">#4047</a>)</li>\n<li>ci: least-privilege permissions on spellcheck (read) and\nstale-issues (job-level write for actions/stale) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4080\">#4080</a>)</li>\n<li>Bumping github-versions actions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4102\">#4102</a>)</li>\n<li>Updating lib version + supported Redis versions in README.md +\nupdating the Redis versions in CI test matrix (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4092\">#4092</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We'd like to thank all the contributors who worked on this release!\n<a href=\"https://github.com/violuke\"><code>@​violuke</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mokashang\"><code>@​mokashang</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/arpitjain099\"><code>@​arpitjain099</code></a>\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/coredumperror\"><code>@​coredumperror</code></a>\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elena-kolevska\"><code>@​elena-kolevska</code></a>\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vladvildanov\"><code>@​vladvildanov</code></a>\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/petyaslavova\"><code>@​petyaslavova</code></a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/7c0fd118c48a7a863d0a0262d858d02c001c4b73\"><code>7c0fd11</code></a>\nUpdating lib version to 8.0.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/b7a4d7d137b680737664e131598c6dab796a5a10\"><code>b7a4d7d</code></a>\nAvoid per-check fd allocation in hiredis <code>_socket_can_read()</code>\n— use <code>poll()</code> ...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/eec778ef52fd0a2b40b86d881721b1c9226257d4\"><code>eec778e</code></a>\nfix(asyncio): release pooled connection when Pipeline.reset() is\ncancelled (#...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/08e01bbf9f2ce8c950f93db918f0883cb6218e5e\"><code>08e01bb</code></a>\nFixing pubsub's listen method to be blocking. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4119\">#4119</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/3d5257a04bd54b994372ecd9ffddb7814f4a9755\"><code>3d5257a</code></a>\nfix(search): parse RESP3 FT.SEARCH responses with bytes-typed keys (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4109\">#4109</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/cce28ffa69666439cd8dfeb4dbb9fd313dd8272b\"><code>cce28ff</code></a>\nFix hiredis readiness checks for high file descriptors (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4115\">#4115</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/e20691c83042a9049dea22b72b74595263e07145\"><code>e20691c</code></a>\nFixed async MultiDBClient with underlying RedisCluster (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4108\">#4108</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/ea37fccf9aff261cd78e072f26b729e797644440\"><code>ea37fcc</code></a>\nFix async cluster node connection release on write errors (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4111\">#4111</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/f4146fa8c763fb9cb31f4e2a52f76030e9bebd77\"><code>f4146fa</code></a>\nUpdating lib version + supported Redis versions in README.md + updating\nthe R...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/d47674e48542fcac807a739f358b45e4a5e2f099\"><code>d47674e</code></a>\nBumping github-versions actions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4102\">#4102</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/compare/v5.0.0...v8.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"22b9ce85c334c8e32a25395ff4e5624d26338aeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/22b9ce85c334c8e32a25395ff4e5624d26338aeb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/5e16fb9920694401227faf95f1da1235ce9aa11f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX2vNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmcYQAKtkH2A8k4kqv4krX5SQO29l\nsMpHNrgT5G0LB0VumEs4gy+zOLrfeLXgW2sjqAQVoYjc3IOn7hMXrMCC5deVJUWg\noUjM7rK2KEd4rlLcl+7iNLJnIQHED4mBVAWBeys+WwwVfbqlfGFv1rk7O3zKC1sF\nLK+z/OuezX07aSB6JmVepumiQ92DmxLOYf7rznpdOnhuThTABLY6ygv1uAqcWiqI\nYYUf31/JNRLKNRgLnPBrbeb+WiXlT0qw3TD8W5nf+cUw1MF4+yyJh1+WB9oBCOsB\n/ZoxpvZBAihrG3D6Mgzjf3r7bJnNw3sCPJ34IQjF3VQXL8xyja9ZqNMwlBczvqLa\n32ttRCEMB5NdaH8Ae1Ukuzqwo4eydF0A2jlTIsW7NAvXXMyy9gKJnWiZ4fDU3eU8\n3xvXucaYlOXRt35FAzRcT+w8OD3n6prnQnuOUWQa26jfWUVSFVZzwHXK5RkPVDTW\nWYApb3dUh7w5hseZlJU7lr9enlhBaHRrDkrJZIoeb4UL2SBF9rkyH6LuDgAaDQkR\nYcqQHC75vtsJjrCdihPJAQ3DpaR2RmjHsQqbbBv1/lJXlzEBDEAFr29/5h0LAJxS\npIcyti9XseExNm3mEWZ2cyPN250fYwaNuOK+NAtGvRXEVUPH51HODR8wZAesc9eq\n0Op2THOhgZPzHM52irGG\n=r4p6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 22b9ce85c334c8e32a25395ff4e5624d26338aeb\nparent 3739f620e5cffda57674a4fe510a441fe16462a4\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784638413 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784638413 +0300\n\ndeps(core-api): update redis[hiredis] requirement from <9,>=5.0 to >=8.0.1,<9 in /core-api (#609)\n\nUpdates the requirements on\n[redis[hiredis]](https://github.com/redis/redis-py) to permit the latest\nversion.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/releases\">redis[hiredis]'s\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>8.0.1</h2>\n<h1>Changes</h1>\n<h2>🐛 Bug Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix Unix socket maintenance notification handling and tests (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4097\">#4097</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix async cluster node connection release on write errors (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4111\">#4111</a>)</li>\n<li>Fixed async MultiDBClient with underlying RedisCluster (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4108\">#4108</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix hiredis readiness checks for high file descriptors (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4115\">#4115</a>)</li>\n<li>fix(search): parse RESP3 FT.SEARCH responses with bytes-typed keys\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4109\">#4109</a>)</li>\n<li>Fixing pubsub's listen method to be blocking. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4119\">#4119</a>)</li>\n<li>fix(asyncio): release pooled connection when Pipeline.reset() is\ncancelled (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4123\">#4123</a>)</li>\n<li>Avoid per-check fd allocation in hiredis _socket_can_read() — use\npoll() instead of a per-call selector (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4118\">#4118</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>🧰 Maintenance</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Updating PyJWT dependency. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4100\">#4100</a>)</li>\n<li>Update CI badge in README.md (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4099\">#4099</a>)</li>\n<li>Add missing url query argument parser for ssl_min_version (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4047\">#4047</a>)</li>\n<li>ci: least-privilege permissions on spellcheck (read) and\nstale-issues (job-level write for actions/stale) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4080\">#4080</a>)</li>\n<li>Bumping github-versions actions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4102\">#4102</a>)</li>\n<li>Updating lib version + supported Redis versions in README.md +\nupdating the Redis versions in CI test matrix (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4092\">#4092</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We'd like to thank all the contributors who worked on this release!\n<a href=\"https://github.com/violuke\"><code>@​violuke</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mokashang\"><code>@​mokashang</code></a> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/arpitjain099\"><code>@​arpitjain099</code></a>\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/coredumperror\"><code>@​coredumperror</code></a>\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elena-kolevska\"><code>@​elena-kolevska</code></a>\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vladvildanov\"><code>@​vladvildanov</code></a>\n<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/petyaslavova\"><code>@​petyaslavova</code></a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/7c0fd118c48a7a863d0a0262d858d02c001c4b73\"><code>7c0fd11</code></a>\nUpdating lib version to 8.0.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/b7a4d7d137b680737664e131598c6dab796a5a10\"><code>b7a4d7d</code></a>\nAvoid per-check fd allocation in hiredis <code>_socket_can_read()</code>\n— use <code>poll()</code> ...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/eec778ef52fd0a2b40b86d881721b1c9226257d4\"><code>eec778e</code></a>\nfix(asyncio): release pooled connection when Pipeline.reset() is\ncancelled (#...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/08e01bbf9f2ce8c950f93db918f0883cb6218e5e\"><code>08e01bb</code></a>\nFixing pubsub's listen method to be blocking. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4119\">#4119</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/3d5257a04bd54b994372ecd9ffddb7814f4a9755\"><code>3d5257a</code></a>\nfix(search): parse RESP3 FT.SEARCH responses with bytes-typed keys (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4109\">#4109</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/cce28ffa69666439cd8dfeb4dbb9fd313dd8272b\"><code>cce28ff</code></a>\nFix hiredis readiness checks for high file descriptors (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4115\">#4115</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/e20691c83042a9049dea22b72b74595263e07145\"><code>e20691c</code></a>\nFixed async MultiDBClient with underlying RedisCluster (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4108\">#4108</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/ea37fccf9aff261cd78e072f26b729e797644440\"><code>ea37fcc</code></a>\nFix async cluster node connection release on write errors (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4111\">#4111</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/f4146fa8c763fb9cb31f4e2a52f76030e9bebd77\"><code>f4146fa</code></a>\nUpdating lib version + supported Redis versions in README.md + updating\nthe R...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/commit/d47674e48542fcac807a739f358b45e4a5e2f099\"><code>d47674e</code></a>\nBumping github-versions actions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4102\">#4102</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/redis/redis-py/compare/v5.0.0...v8.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T12:53:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5e16fb9920694401227faf95f1da1235ce9aa11f","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5e16fb9920694401227faf95f1da1235ce9aa11f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5e16fb9920694401227faf95f1da1235ce9aa11f/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3739f620e5cffda57674a4fe510a441fe16462a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3739f620e5cffda57674a4fe510a441fe16462a4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3739f620e5cffda57674a4fe510a441fe16462a4"}]},{"sha":"3739f620e5cffda57674a4fe510a441fe16462a4","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDM3MzlmNjIwZTVjZmZkYTU3Njc0YTRmZTUxMGE0NDFmZTE2NDYyYTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-21T12:49:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T12:49:20Z"},"message":"deps(core-api): update sentry-sdk[fastapi] requirement from <3,>=2.0 to >=2.66.0,<3 in /core-api (#608)\n\nUpdates the requirements on\n[sentry-sdk[fastapi]](https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-python) to\npermit the latest version.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/releases\">sentry-sdk[fastapi]'s\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.66.0</h2>\n<h3>New Features ✨</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>(tracing) Promote trace_lifecycle and ignore_spans to top-level\noptions by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ericapisani\"><code>@​ericapisani</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6821\">#6821</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes 🐛</h3>\n<h4>Tracing</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Skip child span creation in streaming path when no current span\n(HTTP clients) by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sentrivana\"><code>@​sentrivana</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6811\">#6811</a></li>\n<li>Skip child span creation in streaming path when no current span\n(task queues) by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sentrivana\"><code>@​sentrivana</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6814\">#6814</a></li>\n<li>Skip child span creation in streaming path when no current span\n(misc) by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sentrivana\"><code>@​sentrivana</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6815\">#6815</a></li>\n<li>Skip child span creation in streaming path when no current span\n(databases) by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sentrivana\"><code>@​sentrivana</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6808\">#6808</a></li>\n<li>Skip child span creation in streaming path when no current span (web\nframeworks) by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sentrivana\"><code>@​sentrivana</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6810\">#6810</a></li>\n<li>Skip child span creation in streaming path when no current span\n(django) by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sentrivana\"><code>@​sentrivana</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6809\">#6809</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Internal Changes 🔧</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>(logging) Fix flaky test_logging_captured_warnings by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ericapisani\"><code>@​ericapisani</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6824\">#6824</a></li>\n<li>Remove flaky no cyclic garbage test by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alexander-alderman-webb\"><code>@​alexander-alderman-webb</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6817\">#6817</a></li>\n<li>Remove Claude permission settings by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/cleptric\"><code>@​cleptric</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6806\">#6806</a></li>\n<li>Move <code>nullcontext</code> to <code>sentry_sdk.utils</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sentrivana\"><code>@​sentrivana</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6805\">#6805</a></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md\">sentry-sdk[fastapi]'s\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.66.0</h2>\n<h3>New Features ✨</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>(tracing) Promote trace_lifecycle and ignore_spans to top-level\noptions by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ericapisani\"><code>@​ericapisani</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6821\">#6821</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes 🐛</h3>\n<h4>Tracing</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Skip child span creation in streaming path when no current span\n(HTTP clients) by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sentrivana\"><code>@​sentrivana</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6811\">#6811</a></li>\n<li>Skip child span creation in streaming path when no current span\n(task queues) by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sentrivana\"><code>@​sentrivana</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6814\">#6814</a></li>\n<li>Skip child span creation in streaming path when no current span\n(misc) by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sentrivana\"><code>@​sentrivana</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6815\">#6815</a></li>\n<li>Skip child span creation in streaming path when no current span\n(databases) by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sentrivana\"><code>@​sentrivana</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6808\">#6808</a></li>\n<li>Skip child span creation in streaming path when no current span (web\nframeworks) by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sentrivana\"><code>@​sentrivana</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6810\">#6810</a></li>\n<li>Skip child span creation in streaming path when no current span\n(django) by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sentrivana\"><code>@​sentrivana</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6809\">#6809</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Internal Changes 🔧</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>(logging) Fix flaky test_logging_captured_warnings by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ericapisani\"><code>@​ericapisani</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6824\">#6824</a></li>\n<li>Remove flaky no cyclic garbage test by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alexander-alderman-webb\"><code>@​alexander-alderman-webb</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6817\">#6817</a></li>\n<li>Remove Claude permission settings by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/cleptric\"><code>@​cleptric</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6806\">#6806</a></li>\n<li>Move <code>nullcontext</code> to <code>sentry_sdk.utils</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sentrivana\"><code>@​sentrivana</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6805\">#6805</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.65.0</h2>\n<h3>New Features ✨</h3>\n<h4>Huey</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Set <code>messaging.destination.name</code> on consumer spans by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alexander-alderman-webb\"><code>@​alexander-alderman-webb</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6779\">#6779</a></li>\n<li>Set <code>messaging.destination.name</code> on producer spans by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alexander-alderman-webb\"><code>@​alexander-alderman-webb</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6778\">#6778</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Other</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>(arq) Set <code>messaging.destination.name</code> on consumer spans\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alexander-alderman-webb\"><code>@​alexander-alderman-webb</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6767\">#6767</a></li>\n<li>(dramatiq) Set <code>messaging.destination.name</code> on consumer\nspans by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alexander-alderman-webb\"><code>@​alexander-alderman-webb</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6776\">#6776</a></li>\n<li>(rq) Set <code>messaging.destination.name</code> on consumer spans\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alexander-alderman-webb\"><code>@​alexander-alderman-webb</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6774\">#6774</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes 🐛</h3>\n<h4>Tracing</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Take first sentry-trace header in case multiple are supplied by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sl0thentr0py\"><code>@​sl0thentr0py</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6722\">#6722</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Other</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>(django) Avoid <code>ValueError</code> in async middleware\n<code>process_*</code> hooks by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/r0ro\"><code>@​r0ro</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6698\">#6698</a></li>\n<li>(scope) Drop None user attribute values in set_user by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ericapisani\"><code>@​ericapisani</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6692\">#6692</a></li>\n<li>(starlette) Don't overwrite user set during request in\nAuthenticationMiddleware by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ericapisani\"><code>@​ericapisani</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/pull/6760\">#6760</a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/commit/5179f60b025693f381d6d93cd69817f32931825b\"><code>5179f60</code></a>\nupdate changelog with docs link</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/commit/e4bcb59e5a87772b1a9dee6189889a2dcee8d776\"><code>e4bcb59</code></a>\nrelease: 2.66.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/commit/5ba869c03908edde69b2c6526bdd5f03a37bfef4\"><code>5ba869c</code></a>\nfix(tracing): Skip child span creation in streaming path when no current\nspan...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/commit/efddaab9211769982e0c1874e2fb77b0db88b4cd\"><code>efddaab</code></a>\nfix(tracing): Skip child span creation in streaming path when no current\nspan...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/commit/b199a9eea34d7107d81714ca2d1c759f3a6e7e0e\"><code>b199a9e</code></a>\nfix(tracing): Skip child span creation in streaming path when no current\nspan...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-python/commit/d695a6eb6ab6a81251d1abec12b61456b786a566\"><code>d695a6e</code></a>\nfix(tracing): Skip child span creation in str