 <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/releases\">fastapi's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.139.2</h2>\n<h3>Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>🐛 Refactor router route building to make it thread-safe, mainly\nrelevant for tests running in parallel threads (uncommon). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16013\">#16013</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>0.139.1</h2>\n<h3>Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>🐛 Fix frontend fallback support for doted paths like\n<code>/users/john.doe</code>. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16011\">#16011</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Docs</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>📝 Fix topic repository list not being displayed and\n<code>skip_users</code> not being applied. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15995\">#15995</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Translations</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for tr (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16005\">#16005</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for zh-hant (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15996\">#15996</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for fr (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16006\">#16006</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for de (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15999\">#15999</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for ko (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16004\">#16004</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for zh (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16001\">#16001</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for uk (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16003\">#16003</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for ja (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15998\">#15998</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for pt (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16000\">#16000</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for es (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15997\">#15997</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for ru (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16002\">#16002</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for hi (add-missing). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15990\">#15990</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for hi (add-missing). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15925\">#15925</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for hi (add-missing). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15797\">#15797</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update <code>llm-prompt.md</code> for Hindi. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15810\">#15810</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Fix language-specific translation prompt for Russian language. PR\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15924\">#15924</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Internal</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>⬆ Bump the python-packages group across 1 directory with 6 updates.\nPR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15981\">#15981</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/apps/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot[bot]</code></a>.</li>\n<li>⬆ Bump typing-extensions from 4.15.0 to 4.16.0. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15982\">#15982</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/apps/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot[bot]</code></a>.</li>\n<li>⬆ Bump the github-actions group across 1 directory with 4 updates.\nPR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15983\">#15983</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/apps/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot[bot]</code></a>.</li>\n<li>⬆ Bump pre-commit hooks. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15985\">#15985</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>👷 Use <code>FASTAPI_LATEST_CHANGES</code> token in\n<code>bump-pre-commit-hooks</code> workflow. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15984\">#15984</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n<li>👷 Add GH workflow to bump pre-commit hook versions. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15873\">#15873</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🔧 Set Dependabot schedule interval to &quot;monthly&quot;. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15874\">#15874</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n<li>⬆ Bump CodSpeedHQ/action from 4.17.6 to 4.18.1 in the github-actions\ngroup. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15950\">#15950</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/apps/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot[bot]</code></a>.</li>\n<li>⬆ Bump the python-packages group with 8 updates. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15952\">#15952</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/apps/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot[bot]</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🔧 Update sponsors: add TutorCruncher. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15947\">#15947</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>👷 Fix notify translations checkout target. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15933\">#15933</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>👷 Fix latest-changes checkout target. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15932\">#15932</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🔧 Update sponsors: remove RapidProxy. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15929\">#15929</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>⬆️ Update issue-manager to 0.8.1. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15928\">#15928</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>⬆️ Update latest-changes to 0.6.1. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15926\">#15926</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/866b7a3d0ce1025a3811f23aea4846d01a2b16a8\"><code>866b7a3</code></a>\n🔖 Release version 0.139.2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16014\">#16014</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/7b3effea754619f0c305af576be23a51865292a3\"><code>7b3effe</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/7fe315c21afb8a57a2b559772e0f7ced7e5d071a\"><code>7fe315c</code></a>\n🐛 Refactor router route building to make it thread-safe, mainly relevant\nfor ...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/c48e67b1ce9c03fc9bd4b1ac72350e51ad5a6e8a\"><code>c48e67b</code></a>\n🔖 Release version 0.139.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16012\">#16012</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/2acc4fbf155caf016e3bd2602c0d2ec52723e635\"><code>2acc4fb</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/eb75fd078e83aed935016bcdf0705cd58bbf0d0e\"><code>eb75fd0</code></a>\n🐛 Fix frontend fallback support for doted paths like\n<code>/users/john.doe</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16011\">#16011</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/9b8410bdc9fa1fd679ea7e65b926535c7045ab87\"><code>9b8410b</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/e24d44cce4092a33b64e9536e96e7608a7dcb9b8\"><code>e24d44c</code></a>\n📝 Fix topic repository list not being displayed and\n<code>skip_users</code> not being ap...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/93b78f8646dea4543cc4d938f7e29b8547749a99\"><code>93b78f8</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/b959b443577c5f2b870cdef13219b98aa32f8943\"><code>b959b44</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/compare/0.137.0...0.139.2\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `pydantic-settings` from 2.14.1 to 2.14.2\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/releases\">pydantic-settings's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.14.2</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<p>This is a security patch release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Prevent <code>NestedSecretsSettingsSource</code> from following\nsymlinks outside <code>secrets_dir</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hramezani\"><code>@​hramezani</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/889\">pydantic/pydantic-settings#889</a></li>\n<li>Prepare release 2.14.2 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hramezani\"><code>@​hramezani</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/890\">pydantic/pydantic-settings#890</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Security</h3>\n<p>Fixes <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/security/advisories/GHSA-4xgf-cpjx-pc3j\">GHSA-4xgf-cpjx-pc3j</a>:\n<code>NestedSecretsSettingsSource</code> with\n<code>secrets_nested_subdir=True</code> could follow a symbolic link\ninside <code>secrets_dir</code> pointing outside it, reading out-of-tree\nfiles into settings values and bypassing the\n<code>secrets_dir_max_size</code> cap. Affected versions: <code>&gt;=\n2.12.0, &lt; 2.14.2</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/compare/v2.14.1...v2.14.2\">https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/compare/v2.14.1...v2.14.2</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commit/d703bd717e5e07439fa89da2245eee6139413e9e\"><code>d703bd7</code></a>\nPrepare release 2.14.2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/890\">#890</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/compare/v2.14.1...v2.14.2\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `ddtrace` from 4.10.6 to 4.11.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/releases\">ddtrace's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>4.11.1</h2>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>bootstrap: keep <code>yaml</code>/<code>_yaml</code> loaded during\nmodule cleanup, fixing an issue that broke PyYAML consumers such as\nAirflow.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<ul>\n<li>Code Security (IAST): fixes an issue where taint tracking could\nabort the Python process when old-style <code>%</code> string formatting\nhandled tainted text containing literal IAST evidence marker\ndelimiters.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<ul>\n<li>Code Security (IAST): Resolve a weak-hash false positive reported on\nddtrace's own code when IAST and the live debugger (Symbol Database) are\nboth enabled.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<ul>\n<li>LLM Observability: This fix resolves an issue where annotating a\nspan with a metric key containing a dot (e.g.\n<code>anomaly.query_count</code>) prevented the span from being\ningested. Dots in metric keys are now replaced with underscores.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<ul>\n<li>LLM Observability: This fixes an issue where cache write input\ntokens were not captured by the OpenAI integration when using newer\nmodels that include cache write token charges.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.11.0</h2>\n<h3>Upgrade Notes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>flask: Requests served under a non-empty WSGI\n<code>SCRIPT_NAME</code> now expose the client-hit resource on a new\n<code>flask.resource.full</code> tag (e.g. <code>GET\n/api/v2/users</code>). The span <code>resource</code> and\n<code>flask.url_rule</code> tag are unchanged. The tag is only set when\nits value would differ from <code>span.resource</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<ul>\n<li>flask: API endpoint discovery now reports every HTTP method the\nframework serves — including Werkzeug's auto-added <code>HEAD</code> for\nany <code>GET</code> route and Flask's auto-handled <code>OPTIONS</code>\nfor every route — not just the methods listed in\n<code>methods=[...]</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<ul>\n<li>LLM Observability: when APM and LLMObs are both enabled, the APM\ntrace writer now uses the <code>v0.4</code> trace API version\n(<code>v0.5</code> cannot carry the LLMObs span data). Setting\n<code>DD_TRACE_API_VERSION=v0.5</code> with LLMObs enabled logs a\nwarning and downgrades to <code>v0.4</code>. No user action is\nrequired.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>New Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>tracing: collect the <code>x-datadog-endpoint-scan</code> and\n<code>x-datadog-security-test</code> HTTP request headers on service\nentry spans unconditionally as\n<code>http.request.headers.x-datadog-endpoint-scan</code> and\n<code>http.request.headers.x-datadog-security-test</code> tags. These\nmarkers identify Datadog-originated endpoint scans and security tests so\nthe API inventory pipeline can distinguish scan/test traffic from real\nuser traffic. The headers are tagged regardless of\n<code>DD_TRACE_HEADER_TAGS</code> configuration or AppSec enablement,\nand are not propagated to downstream services.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<ul>\n<li>Database Monitoring (DBM) propagation supports\n<code>dynamic_service</code> as a new\n<code>DD_DBM_PROPAGATION_MODE</code> value. Set\n<code>DD_DBM_PROPAGATION_MODE=dynamic_service</code> to inject DBM\nservice metadata and the SQL base hash without injecting trace\ncontext.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<ul>\n<li>ai_guard: add AI Guard evaluation support to the Anthropic SDK\nMessages instrumentation. Both non-streaming and streaming requests and\nnon-streaming responses are evaluated through the configured AI Guard\nclient (covering <code>Messages.create</code> /\n<code>Messages.stream</code> and their async and Beta variants), and\nevaluation is automatically skipped when a framework integration\n(LangChain) is already evaluating the same call.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<ul>\n<li>aiokafka: Adds <code>kafka.partition</code> and\n<code>kafka.message_offset</code> tags to the producer span once the\nbroker acknowledges the send. The partition reflects the partition the\nbroker actually assigned to the message, which may differ from the\npartition the caller requested. Mirrors the behavior added to the Java\ntracer in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-java/issues/11107\">DataDog/dd-trace-java#11107</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/823648d32ed5d2ab843be193a3abcc4d63feb1f7\"><code>823648d</code></a>\nci: pin build_base_venvs memory to prevent cold-cache OOM [backport\n4.11]</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/e3b793ae95fc6e5f288b84b9f953a864ff08ca7f\"><code>e3b793a</code></a>\nchore(ci): disable release benchmarks on the 4.11 branch (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/issues/19111\">#19111</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/8a1b5a4034d1304c2da15f9af4a2bb5210a1d7ee\"><code>8a1b5a4</code></a>\nfix(bootstrap): do not unload yaml/_yaml during module cleanup [backport\n4.11...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/0bc889a4ac4dc3b444147598196185ae580be724\"><code>0bc889a</code></a>\nchore: bump pyproject to 4.11.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/issues/19049\">#19049</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/7d5f0d392456b4fd100d9afe05e52242ea911547\"><code>7d5f0d3</code></a>\nfix(llmobs): capture openai cache write input tokens [backport 4.11] (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/issues/19021\">#19021</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/bc60e33f2314a5f74f9fe0c37dc8cfc25403932c\"><code>bc60e33</code></a>\nfix(iast): avoid weak-hash false positive from symbol_db git-blob hash\n[backp...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/a7ea26e60d3cedadb41cdcaf2bc35dc41610d5e2\"><code>a7ea26e</code></a>\nfix(iast): handle literal evidence markers in modulo propagation\n[backport 4....</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/ee0fdfbbf3b8f3a86b8768a91b7ccd818ef82c77\"><code>ee0fdfb</code></a>\nfix(llmobs): sanitize dots in metric keys [backport 4.11] (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/issues/19022\">#19022</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/f21e814527fbba092ae300efc3733dc49e6ee579\"><code>f21e814</code></a>\nchore(native): upgrade libdatadog to v35.0.0 [backport 4.11] (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/issues/19029\">#19029</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/0b6e17bcc67641ea319e336640d6a88ab9a91fab\"><code>0b6e17b</code></a>\nchore: bump pyproject to 4.11.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/issues/18977\">#18977</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/compare/v4.10.6...v4.11.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `mypy` from 2.1.0 to 2.3.0\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python/mypy/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md\">mypy's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>Mypy Release Notes</h1>\n<h2>Next Release</h2>\n<h3>Packaging changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>No longer provide mypyc-accelerated wheels for macOS x86_64\n[mypyc-wheels <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python/mypy/issues/119\">#119</a>](<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/mypyc/mypy_mypyc-wheels/pull/119\">mypyc/mypy_mypyc-wheels#119</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Mypy 2.3</h2>\n<p>We've just uploaded mypy 2.3.0 to the Python Package Index (<a\nhref=\"https://pypi.org/project/mypy/\">PyPI</a>).\nMypy is a static type checker for Python. This release includes new\nfeatures, performance\nimprovements and bug fixes. You can install it as follows:</p>\n<pre><code>python3 -m pip install -U mypy\n</code></pre>\n<p>You can read the full documentation for this release on <a\nhref=\"http://mypy.readthedocs.io\">Read the Docs</a>.</p>\n<h3>The Upcoming Switch to the New Native Parser</h3>\n<p>We are planning to enable the new native parser\n(<code>--native-parser</code>) by\ndefault soon. We recommend that you test the native parser in your\nprojects and report\nany issues in the <a href=\"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues\">mypy\nissue tracker</a>.</p>\n<h3>Mypyc Free-threading Memory Safety</h3>\n<p>Free-threaded Python builds that don't have the GIL require\nadditional synchronization\nprimitives or lock-free algorithms to ensure memory safety when there\nare race conditions\n(for example, when a thread reads a list item while another thread\nwrites the same list\nitem concurrently). This release greatly improves memory safety of free\nthreading.</p>\n<p>List operations are now memory-safe on free threaded Python builds,\neven in the presence of\nrace conditions. This has some performance cost. For list-heavy\nworkloads, using\n<code>librt.vecs.vec</code> instead of list is often significantly\nfaster, but note that <code>vec</code> is not\n(and likely won't be) fully memory safe, and the user is expected to\navoid race conditions.\nThe newly introduced <code>librt.threading.Lock</code> helps with this.\nUsing variable-length tuples\ncan also be more efficient than lists, since tuples are immutable and\ndon't require\nexpensive synchronization to ensure memory safety.</p>\n<p>Instance attribute access is also (mostly) memory safe now on\nfree-threaded builds in\nthe presence of race conditions. We are planning to fix the remaining\nunsafe cases in a\nfuture release.</p>\n<p>Full list of changes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Make attribute access memory safe on free-threaded builds (Jukka\nLehtosalo, PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python/mypy/pull/21705\">21705</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix unsafe borrowing of instance attributes with free-threading\n(Jukka Lehtosalo, PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python/mypy/pull/21688\">21688</a>)</li>\n<li>Make list get/set item more memory safe on free-threaded builds\n(Jukka Lehtosalo, PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python/mypy/pull/21683\">21683</a>)</li>\n<li>Don't borrow list items on free-threaded builds (Jukka Lehtosalo, PR\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python/mypy/pull/21679\">21679</a>)</li>\n<li>Make multiple assignment from list memory-safe on free-threaded\nbuilds (Jukka Lehtosalo, PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python/mypy/pull/21684\">21684</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python/mypy/commit/8aabf8435357eaffceca7237f371e293b8168e54\"><code>8aabf84</code></a>\nDrop +dev from version</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python/mypy/commit/4d8ad2ab5e86c99581b73775f2c00b9b8265b589\"><code>4d8ad2a</code></a>\nUpdate changelog for 2.3 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python/mypy/issues/21728\">#21728</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python/mypy/commit/2c2154672040c52e481f423854d104e6cf172585\"><code>2c21546</code></a>\n[mypyc] Update documentation of race conditions under free threading (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python/mypy/issues/21726\">#21726</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python/mypy/commit/a9f62a3cf98a58a7a2607b7c81695802b39f5edc\"><code>a9f62a3</code></a>\n[mypyc] Make attribute access memory safe on free-threaded builds (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python/mypy/issues/21705\">#21705</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python/mypy/commit/0faa413ebf7c924a864ef5dabd70303d898e7766\"><code>0faa413</code></a>\nUse <code>PYODIDE</code> environment variable for Emscripten\ncross-compilation detection...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python/mypy/commit/3d75cdb09f0928fa8b83e5ef03572ed878ac8d09\"><code>3d75cdb</code></a>\n[mypyc] Borrow final attributes more aggressively (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python/mypy/issues/21702\">#21702</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python/mypy/commit/24c237d85b48f618e655ffff1dc0f19089d9b599\"><code>24c237d</code></a>\n[mypyc] Improve documentation of Final (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python/mypy/issues/21713\">#21713</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python/mypy/commit/b5be217392b9b2771d1764066b9d600bf93ce7a8\"><code>b5be217</code></a>\n[mypyc] Update free threading Python compatibility docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python/mypy/issues/21711\">#21711</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python/mypy/commit/cbcb51add3094ec91b29cdd4c624943bf251b63f\"><code>cbcb51a</code></a>\nNarrow for frozendict membership check (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python/mypy/issues/21709\">#21709</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python/mypy/commit/af2bc0f3cc7f2f129f0c11294158d0c292692c3d\"><code>af2bc0f</code></a>\nSync typeshed (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python/mypy/issues/21707\">#21707</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python/mypy/compare/v2.1.0...v2.3.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `ruff` from 0.15.17 to 0.15.22\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/releases\">ruff's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.15.22</h2>\n<h2>Release Notes</h2>\n<p>Released on 2026-07-16.</p>\n<h3>Preview features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[<code>pycodestyle</code>] Add an autofix for <code>E402</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/22212\">#22212</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>refurb</code>] Allow subclassing builtins in stub files\n(<code>FURB189</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26812\">#26812</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>ruff</code>] Add rule to replace <code>noqa</code> comments\nwith <code>ruff:ignore</code> (<code>RUF105</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26423\">#26423</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>ruff</code>] Add rule to use human-readable names in\n<code>ruff:ignore</code> comments (<code>RUF106</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26682\">#26682</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>ruff</code>] Add rule to use human-readable names in\nconfiguration selectors (<code>RUF201</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26772\">#26772</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[<code>flake8-pyi</code>] Fix false positive in <code>__all__</code>\n(<code>PYI053</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26872\">#26872</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Rule changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[<code>pylint</code>] Ignore mutable type updates in\n<code>redefined-loop-name</code> (<code>PLW2901</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/25733\">#25733</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Performance</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Avoid redundant lexer token bookkeeping (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26765\">#26765</a>)</li>\n<li>Avoid redundant pending-indentation writes (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26774\">#26774</a>)</li>\n<li>Avoid unnecessary identifier lookahead (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26525\">#26525</a>)</li>\n<li>Reuse parser scratch buffers (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26798\">#26798</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Document argfile support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26803\">#26803</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>flake8-datetimez</code>] Clarify naming guidance for\n<code>datetime.today</code> (<code>DTZ002</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26658\">#26658</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>pycodestyle</code>] Document <code>E731</code> fix safety (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26847\">#26847</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>ruff</code>] Clarify intentional async contexts for\n<code>unused-async</code> (<code>RUF029</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26641\">#26641</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Contributors</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/dwego\"><code>@​dwego</code></a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/MichaReiser\"><code>@​MichaReiser</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Joosboy\"><code>@​Joosboy</code></a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KaufmanDmitriy\"><code>@​KaufmanDmitriy</code></a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/PeterJCLaw\"><code>@​PeterJCLaw</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/ntBre\"><code>@​ntBre</code></a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/charliermarsh\"><code>@​charliermarsh</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Install ruff 0.15.22</h2>\n<h3>Install prebuilt binaries via shell script</h3>\n<pre lang=\"sh\"><code>&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">ruff's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.15.22</h2>\n<p>Released on 2026-07-16.</p>\n<h3>Preview features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[<code>pycodestyle</code>] Add an autofix for <code>E402</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/22212\">#22212</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>refurb</code>] Allow subclassing builtins in stub files\n(<code>FURB189</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26812\">#26812</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>ruff</code>] Add rule to replace <code>noqa</code> comments\nwith <code>ruff:ignore</code> (<code>RUF105</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26423\">#26423</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>ruff</code>] Add rule to use human-readable names in\n<code>ruff:ignore</code> comments (<code>RUF106</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26682\">#26682</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>ruff</code>] Add rule to use human-readable names in\nconfiguration selectors (<code>RUF201</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26772\">#26772</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[<code>flake8-pyi</code>] Fix false positive in <code>__all__</code>\n(<code>PYI053</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26872\">#26872</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Rule changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[<code>pylint</code>] Ignore mutable type updates in\n<code>redefined-loop-name</code> (<code>PLW2901</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/25733\">#25733</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Performance</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Avoid redundant lexer token bookkeeping (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26765\">#26765</a>)</li>\n<li>Avoid redundant pending-indentation writes (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26774\">#26774</a>)</li>\n<li>Avoid unnecessary identifier lookahead (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26525\">#26525</a>)</li>\n<li>Reuse parser scratch buffers (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26798\">#26798</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Document argfile support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26803\">#26803</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>flake8-datetimez</code>] Clarify naming guidance for\n<code>datetime.today</code> (<code>DTZ002</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26658\">#26658</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>pycodestyle</code>] Document <code>E731</code> fix safety (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26847\">#26847</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>ruff</code>] Clarify intentional async contexts for\n<code>unused-async</code> (<code>RUF029</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26641\">#26641</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Contributors</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/dwego\"><code>@​dwego</code></a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/MichaReiser\"><code>@​MichaReiser</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Joosboy\"><code>@​Joosboy</code></a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KaufmanDmitriy\"><code>@​KaufmanDmitriy</code></a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/PeterJCLaw\"><code>@​PeterJCLaw</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/ntBre\"><code>@​ntBre</code></a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/charliermarsh\"><code>@​charliermarsh</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>0.15.21</h2>\n<p>Released on 2026-07-09.</p>\n<h3>Preview features</h3>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/0177a7e0d2c4a3805afa1960f106d72878766cbc\"><code>0177a7e</code></a>\nBump 0.15.22 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/26884\">#26884</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/fe8ba85a55b76d838e6058d813b64468b5f81eca\"><code>fe8ba85</code></a>\n[<code>pycodestyle</code>] Document <code>E731</code> fix safety (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/26847\">#26847</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/f3cf7c81fa35f8b819a719303bf1789714f1c780\"><code>f3cf7c8</code></a>\n[<code>ruff</code>] Add <code>rule-codes-in-selectors</code>\n(<code>RUF201</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/26772\">#26772</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/d244fd75e9036e61be4896b823fe760d7aa632a3\"><code>d244fd7</code></a>\nDocument argfile support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/26803\">#26803</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/f23975849a0db64a2851029c68fc054799d5e7da\"><code>f239758</code></a>\n[<code>flake8-pyi</code>] Fix false positive in <code>__all__</code>\n(<code>PYI053</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/26872\">#26872</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/54acbcde56d76bc47b0b3dfe61e57fbaadd2c06b\"><code>54acbcd</code></a>\n[ty] Support <code>TypeVarTuple</code> and <code>Unpack</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/25240\">#25240</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/87fc38cacd7e2bd906674c6dc5b8be97aa3a5bc3\"><code>87fc38c</code></a>\n[ty] Parallelize subtype hierarchy search (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/26875\">#26875</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/e454f91fa63bd745d874ead751ad15d9f521195a\"><code>e454f91</code></a>\n[ty] Share interned query keys across Salsa queries (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/26794\">#26794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/6f361a74a232ad283cc6e5e5d3a62109802aab65\"><code>6f361a7</code></a>\n[ty] only collect expected types for files open in the editor (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/25546\">#25546</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/6d6b2b37686da8b1ee56e54fd99831f1f5fa0381\"><code>6d6b2b3</code></a>\n[ty] Avoid allocations during Salsa interned lookups (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/26877\">#26877</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/compare/0.15.17...0.15.22\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `pytest` from 9.1.0 to 9.1.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/releases\">pytest's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>9.1.1</h2>\n<h1>pytest 9.1.1 (2026-06-19)</h1>\n<h2>Bug fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/14220\">#14220</a>:\nFixed a logic bug in <code>pytest.RaisesGroup</code> which would might\ncause it to display incorrect &quot;It matches <!-- raw HTML omitted\n-->FooError()<!-- raw HTML omitted --> which was paired with <!-- raw\nHTML omitted -->BarError<!-- raw HTML omitted -->&quot; messages.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/14591\">#14591</a>:\nFixed a regression in pytest 9.1.0 which caused overriding a\nparametrized fixture with an indirect <!-- raw HTML omitted --><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytest\"><code>@​pytest</code></a>.mark.parametrize<!--\nraw HTML omitted --> to fail with &quot;duplicate parametrization of\n'&lt;fixture name&gt;'&quot;.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/14606\">#14606</a>:\nFixed <code>list-item</code> typing errors from mypy in\n<code>@pytest.mark.parametrize &lt;pytest.mark.parametrize\nref&gt;</code> <code>argvalues</code> parameter.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/14608\">#14608</a>:\nFixed a regression in pytest 9.1.0 where <code>conftest.py</code> files\nlocated in <code>&lt;invocation dir&gt;/test*</code> were no longer\nloaded as initial conftests when invoked without arguments.\nThis could cause certain hooks (like <code>pytest_addoption</code>) in\nthese files to not fire.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/commit/cf470ec0bf7eb89cd97dd56df4859eae5db46447\"><code>cf470ec</code></a>\nPrepare release version 9.1.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/commit/e0c8ce6cc5db1f08363be6f152c32e6838df2690\"><code>e0c8ce6</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/14625\">#14625</a>\nfrom pytest-dev/patchback/backports/9.1.x/a07c31a97...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/commit/1b82d1694fce22385ee7a4287917fbafbaf2e757\"><code>1b82d16</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/14624\">#14624</a>\nfrom pytest-dev/patchback/backports/9.1.x/b375b79ec...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/commit/501c4bc784da3b08bfcaa64858eba5d15dc59e53\"><code>501c4bc</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/14596\">#14596</a>\nfrom bluetech/doc-classmethod</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/commit/b61f588e36e9377c3d1d3f06bece1da0fc31d9ca\"><code>b61f588</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/14622\">#14622</a>\nfrom chrisburr/fix-14608-initial-conftest-test-subdir</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/commit/9a567e009f4d2da3ce1721c6db3109cb5744d40a\"><code>9a567e0</code></a>\n[automated] Update plugin list (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/14617\">#14617</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/14618\">#14618</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/commit/ef8b2993e5b48639e4a3d97d0525df9760781384\"><code>ef8b299</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/14620\">#14620</a>\nfrom pytest-dev/patchback/backports/9.1.x/680f9f3ed...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/commit/66abd0784d4cb7c1ba44ab9a8896506cd4985acc\"><code>66abd07</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/14220\">#14220</a>\nfrom bysiber/fix-stale-iexp-raisesgroup</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/commit/79fbf93b666cac5f27c9dad047943d47b766c8d5\"><code>79fbf93</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/14612\">#14612</a>\nfrom pytest-dev/patchback/backports/9.1.x/974ed48b6...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/commit/0d312eb876177e9f1c04262b54060a41034ebf5c\"><code>0d312eb</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/14611\">#14611</a>\nfrom bluetech/parametrize-argvalues-typing</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/compare/9.1.0...9.1.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> major version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's major version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's major version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> minor version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's minor version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's minor version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name>` will close this group update PR\nand stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency\n(unless you unignore this specific dependency or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name>` will remove all of the ignore\nconditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name> <ignore condition>` will\nremove the ignore condition of the specified dependency and ignore\nconditions\n\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T09:30:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2d40ecfb74f5fe5b72e81df431d5eb36e606bcee","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2d40ecfb74f5fe5b72e81df431d5eb36e606bcee","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2d40ecfb74f5fe5b72e81df431d5eb36e606bcee/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"39b8d090481a7221d2f9a77e4f8439066fc2de02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/39b8d090481a7221d2f9a77e4f8439066fc2de02","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/39b8d090481a7221d2f9a77e4f8439066fc2de02"}]},{"sha":"39b8d090481a7221d2f9a77e4f8439066fc2de02","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDM5YjhkMDkwNDgxYTcyMjFkMmY5YTc3ZTRmODQzOTA2NmZjMmRlMDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-21T09:27:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T09:27:01Z"},"message":"deps(actions): bump the actions group with 8 updates (#591)\n\nBumps the actions group with 8 updates:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [github/codeql-action/init](https://github.com/github/codeql-action) |\n`4.36.2` | `4.37.1` |\n|\n[github/codeql-action/analyze](https://github.com/github/codeql-action)\n| `4.36.2` | `4.37.1` |\n|\n[docker/setup-qemu-action](https://github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action)\n| `4.0.0` | `4.2.0` |\n|\n[docker/setup-buildx-action](https://github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action)\n| `4.0.0` | `4.2.0` |\n| [docker/login-action](https://github.com/docker/login-action) |\n`4.1.0` | `4.4.0` |\n| [docker/metadata-action](https://github.com/docker/metadata-action) |\n`6.0.0` | `6.2.0` |\n|\n[docker/build-push-action](https://github.com/docker/build-push-action)\n| `7.1.0` | `7.3.0` |\n|\n[actions/create-github-app-token](https://github.com/actions/create-github-app-token)\n| `3.1.1` | `3.2.0` |\n\nUpdates `github/codeql-action/init` from 4.36.2 to 4.37.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases\">github/codeql-action/init's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v4.37.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Upcoming breaking change</em>: Add a deprecation warning for\ncustomers using CodeQL version 2.20.6 and earlier. These versions of\nCodeQL were discontinued on 1 July 2026 alongside GitHub Enterprise\nServer 3.16, and will be unsupported by the next minor release of the\nCodeQL Action. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3956\">#3956</a></li>\n<li>Update default CodeQL bundle version to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases/tag/codeql-bundle-v2.26.1\">2.26.1</a>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/4019\">#4019</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.37.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update default CodeQL bundle version to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases/tag/codeql-bundle-v2.26.0\">2.26.0</a>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3995\">#3995</a></li>\n<li>In addition to the existing input format, the\n<code>config-file</code> input for the <code>codeql-action/init</code>\nstep will soon support a new <code>[owner/]repo[@ref][:path]</code>\nformat. All components except the repository name are optional. If\nomitted, <code>owner</code> defaults to the same owner as the repository\nthe analysis is running for, <code>ref</code> to <code>main</code>, and\n<code>path</code> to <code>.github/codeql-action.yaml</code>. Support\nfor this format ships in this version of the CodeQL Action, but will\nonly be enabled over the coming weeks. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3973\">#3973</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.36.3</h2>\n<p>No user facing changes.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">github/codeql-action/init's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>CodeQL Action Changelog</h1>\n<p>See the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases\">releases\npage</a> for the relevant changes to the CodeQL CLI and language\npacks.</p>\n<h2>[UNRELEASED]</h2>\n<p>No user facing changes.</p>\n<h2>4.37.1 - 16 Jul 2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Upcoming breaking change</em>: Add a deprecation warning for\ncustomers using CodeQL version 2.20.6 and earlier. These versions of\nCodeQL were discontinued on 1 July 2026 alongside GitHub Enterprise\nServer 3.16, and will be unsupported by the next minor release of the\nCodeQL Action. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3956\">#3956</a></li>\n<li>Update default CodeQL bundle version to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases/tag/codeql-bundle-v2.26.1\">2.26.1</a>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/4019\">#4019</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.37.0 - 08 Jul 2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update default CodeQL bundle version to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases/tag/codeql-bundle-v2.26.0\">2.26.0</a>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3995\">#3995</a></li>\n<li>In addition to the existing input format, the\n<code>config-file</code> input for the <code>codeql-action/init</code>\nstep will soon support a new <code>[owner/]repo[@ref][:path]</code>\nformat. All components except the repository name are optional. If\nomitted, <code>owner</code> defaults to the same owner as the repository\nthe analysis is running for, <code>ref</code> to <code>main</code>, and\n<code>path</code> to <code>.github/codeql-action.yaml</code>. Support\nfor this format ships in this version of the CodeQL Action, but will\nonly be enabled over the coming weeks. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3973\">#3973</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.36.3 - 01 Jul 2026</h2>\n<p>No user facing changes.</p>\n<h2>4.36.2 - 04 Jun 2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Cache CodeQL CLI version information across Actions steps. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3943\">#3943</a></li>\n<li>Reduce requests while waiting for analysis processing by using\nexponential backoff when polling SARIF processing status. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3937\">#3937</a></li>\n<li>Update default CodeQL bundle version to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases/tag/codeql-bundle-v2.25.6\">2.25.6</a>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3948\">#3948</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.36.1 - 02 Jun 2026</h2>\n<p>No user facing changes.</p>\n<h2>4.36.0 - 22 May 2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Breaking change</em>: Bump the minimum required CodeQL bundle\nversion to 2.19.4. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3894\">#3894</a></li>\n<li>Add support for SHA-256 Git object IDs. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3893\">#3893</a></li>\n<li>Update default CodeQL bundle version to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases/tag/codeql-bundle-v2.25.5\">2.25.5</a>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3926\">#3926</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.35.5 - 15 May 2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>We have improved how the JavaScript bundles for the CodeQL Action\nare generated to avoid duplication across bundles and reduce the size of\nthe repository by around 70%. This should have no effect on the runtime\nbehaviour of the CodeQL Action. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3899\">#3899</a></li>\n<li>For performance and accuracy reasons, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/roadmap/issues/1158\">improved\nincremental analysis</a> will now only be enabled on a pull request when\ndiff-informed analysis is also enabled for that run. If diff-informed\nanalysis is unavailable (for example, because the PR diff ranges could\nnot be computed), the action will fall back to a full analysis. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3791\">#3791</a></li>\n<li>If multiple inputs are provided for the GitHub-internal\n<code>analysis-kinds</code> input, only <code>code-scanning</code> will\nbe enabled. The <code>analysis-kinds</code> input is experimental, for\nGitHub-internal use only, and may change without notice at any time. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3892\">#3892</a></li>\n<li>Added an experimental change which, when running a Code Scanning\nanalysis for a PR with <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/roadmap/issues/1158\">improved\nincremental analysis</a> enabled, prefers CodeQL CLI versions that have\na cached overlay-base database for the configured languages. This speeds\nup analysis for a repository when there is not yet a cached overlay-base\ndatabase for the latest CLI version. We expect to roll this change out\nto everyone in May. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3880\">#3880</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.35.4 - 07 May 2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update default CodeQL bundle version to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases/tag/codeql-bundle-v2.25.4\">2.25.4</a>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3881\">#3881</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.35.3 - 01 May 2026</h2>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/7188fc363630916deb702c7fdcf4e481b751f97a\"><code>7188fc3</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/issues/4020\">#4020</a>\nfrom github/update-v4.37.1-9e7c07009</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/c8b5f69be686908c3dfd844428137d56fe80c936\"><code>c8b5f69</code></a>\nUpdate changelog for v4.37.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/9e7c070092090e89e8b3d62f977d4456e0732cd7\"><code>9e7c070</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/issues/4014\">#4014</a>\nfrom github/mbg/explicit-remote-prefix</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/3492b7e9ab96e28b1d8b971345d30e929c6f8fee\"><code>3492b7e</code></a>\nChange <code>REMOTE_PATH_PREFIX</code> to <code>remote=</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/3654baa924bc6456db54002581cb7c1c877548c4\"><code>3654baa</code></a>\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into\nmbg/explicit-remote-prefix</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/2d682ac05f1b3588aaff3814826bede39b9ba6bb\"><code>2d682ac</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/issues/4017\">#4017</a>\nfrom github/dependabot/github_actions/dot-github/wor...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/23f6a50753a88efd9b7ae8687b29f6bdb65f6250\"><code>23f6a50</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/issues/4009\">#4009</a>\nfrom github/mbg/action-state/additions</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/1ee3c75d1988ab8621f01ebb165115c38d56df91\"><code>1ee3c75</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/issues/4018\">#4018</a>\nfrom github/dependabot/github_actions/dot-github/wor...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/e053684dc500899b0b5520edc8549ac0f1ed730b\"><code>e053684</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/issues/4015\">#4015</a>\nfrom github/dependabot/npm_and_yarn/npm-minor-fd2e83...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/6803c5671d2f87a83ed96e151c441b1cb3bdc66a\"><code>6803c56</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/issues/4019\">#4019</a>\nfrom github/update-bundle/codeql-bundle-v2.26.1</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/compare/8aad20d150bbac5944a9f9d289da16a4b0d87c1e...7188fc363630916deb702c7fdcf4e481b751f97a\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `github/codeql-action/analyze` from 4.36.2 to 4.37.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases\">github/codeql-action/analyze's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v4.37.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Upcoming breaking change</em>: Add a deprecation warning for\ncustomers using CodeQL version 2.20.6 and earlier. These versions of\nCodeQL were discontinued on 1 July 2026 alongside GitHub Enterprise\nServer 3.16, and will be unsupported by the next minor release of the\nCodeQL Action. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3956\">#3956</a></li>\n<li>Update default CodeQL bundle version to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases/tag/codeql-bundle-v2.26.1\">2.26.1</a>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/4019\">#4019</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.37.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update default CodeQL bundle version to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases/tag/codeql-bundle-v2.26.0\">2.26.0</a>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3995\">#3995</a></li>\n<li>In addition to the existing input format, the\n<code>config-file</code> input for the <code>codeql-action/init</code>\nstep will soon support a new <code>[owner/]repo[@ref][:path]</code>\nformat. All components except the repository name are optional. If\nomitted, <code>owner</code> defaults to the same owner as the repository\nthe analysis is running for, <code>ref</code> to <code>main</code>, and\n<code>path</code> to <code>.github/codeql-action.yaml</code>. Support\nfor this format ships in this version of the CodeQL Action, but will\nonly be enabled over the coming weeks. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3973\">#3973</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.36.3</h2>\n<p>No user facing changes.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">github/codeql-action/analyze's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>CodeQL Action Changelog</h1>\n<p>See the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases\">releases\npage</a> for the relevant changes to the CodeQL CLI and language\npacks.</p>\n<h2>[UNRELEASED]</h2>\n<p>No user facing changes.</p>\n<h2>4.37.1 - 16 Jul 2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Upcoming breaking change</em>: Add a deprecation warning for\ncustomers using CodeQL version 2.20.6 and earlier. These versions of\nCodeQL were discontinued on 1 July 2026 alongside GitHub Enterprise\nServer 3.16, and will be unsupported by the next minor release of the\nCodeQL Action. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3956\">#3956</a></li>\n<li>Update default CodeQL bundle version to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases/tag/codeql-bundle-v2.26.1\">2.26.1</a>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/4019\">#4019</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.37.0 - 08 Jul 2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update default CodeQL bundle version to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases/tag/codeql-bundle-v2.26.0\">2.26.0</a>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3995\">#3995</a></li>\n<li>In addition to the existing input format, the\n<code>config-file</code> input for the <code>codeql-action/init</code>\nstep will soon support a new <code>[owner/]repo[@ref][:path]</code>\nformat. All components except the repository name are optional. If\nomitted, <code>owner</code> defaults to the same owner as the repository\nthe analysis is running for, <code>ref</code> to <code>main</code>, and\n<code>path</code> to <code>.github/codeql-action.yaml</code>. Support\nfor this format ships in this version of the CodeQL Action, but will\nonly be enabled over the coming weeks. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3973\">#3973</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.36.3 - 01 Jul 2026</h2>\n<p>No user facing changes.</p>\n<h2>4.36.2 - 04 Jun 2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Cache CodeQL CLI version information across Actions steps. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3943\">#3943</a></li>\n<li>Reduce requests while waiting for analysis processing by using\nexponential backoff when polling SARIF processing status. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3937\">#3937</a></li>\n<li>Update default CodeQL bundle version to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases/tag/codeql-bundle-v2.25.6\">2.25.6</a>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3948\">#3948</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.36.1 - 02 Jun 2026</h2>\n<p>No user facing changes.</p>\n<h2>4.36.0 - 22 May 2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Breaking change</em>: Bump the minimum required CodeQL bundle\nversion to 2.19.4. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3894\">#3894</a></li>\n<li>Add support for SHA-256 Git object IDs. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3893\">#3893</a></li>\n<li>Update default CodeQL bundle version to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases/tag/codeql-bundle-v2.25.5\">2.25.5</a>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3926\">#3926</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.35.5 - 15 May 2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>We have improved how the JavaScript bundles for the CodeQL Action\nare generated to avoid duplication across bundles and reduce the size of\nthe repository by around 70%. This should have no effect on the runtime\nbehaviour of the CodeQL Action. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3899\">#3899</a></li>\n<li>For performance and accuracy reasons, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/roadmap/issues/1158\">improved\nincremental analysis</a> will now only be enabled on a pull request when\ndiff-informed analysis is also enabled for that run. If diff-informed\nanalysis is unavailable (for example, because the PR diff ranges could\nnot be computed), the action will fall back to a full analysis. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3791\">#3791</a></li>\n<li>If multiple inputs are provided for the GitHub-internal\n<code>analysis-kinds</code> input, only <code>code-scanning</code> will\nbe enabled. The <code>analysis-kinds</code> input is experimental, for\nGitHub-internal use only, and may change without notice at any time. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3892\">#3892</a></li>\n<li>Added an experimental change which, when running a Code Scanning\nanalysis for a PR with <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/roadmap/issues/1158\">improved\nincremental analysis</a> enabled, prefers CodeQL CLI versions that have\na cached overlay-base database for the configured languages. This speeds\nup analysis for a repository when there is not yet a cached overlay-base\ndatabase for the latest CLI version. We expect to roll this change out\nto everyone in May. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3880\">#3880</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.35.4 - 07 May 2026</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update default CodeQL bundle version to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases/tag/codeql-bundle-v2.25.4\">2.25.4</a>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/3881\">#3881</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.35.3 - 01 May 2026</h2>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/7188fc363630916deb702c7fdcf4e481b751f97a\"><code>7188fc3</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/issues/4020\">#4020</a>\nfrom github/update-v4.37.1-9e7c07009</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/c8b5f69be686908c3dfd844428137d56fe80c936\"><code>c8b5f69</code></a>\nUpdate changelog for v4.37.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/9e7c070092090e89e8b3d62f977d4456e0732cd7\"><code>9e7c070</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/issues/4014\">#4014</a>\nfrom github/mbg/explicit-remote-prefix</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/3492b7e9ab96e28b1d8b971345d30e929c6f8fee\"><code>3492b7e</code></a>\nChange <code>REMOTE_PATH_PREFIX</code> to <code>remote=</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/3654baa924bc6456db54002581cb7c1c877548c4\"><code>3654baa</code></a>\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into\nmbg/explicit-remote-prefix</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/2d682ac05f1b3588aaff3814826bede39b9ba6bb\"><code>2d682ac</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/issues/4017\">#4017</a>\nfrom github/dependabot/github_actions/dot-github/wor...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/23f6a50753a88efd9b7ae8687b29f6bdb65f6250\"><code>23f6a50</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/issues/4009\">#4009</a>\nfrom github/mbg/action-state/additions</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/1ee3c75d1988ab8621f01ebb165115c38d56df91\"><code>1ee3c75</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/issues/4018\">#4018</a>\nfrom github/dependabot/github_actions/dot-github/wor...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/e053684dc500899b0b5520edc8549ac0f1ed730b\"><code>e053684</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/issues/4015\">#4015</a>\nfrom github/dependabot/npm_and_yarn/npm-minor-fd2e83...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/commit/6803c5671d2f87a83ed96e151c441b1cb3bdc66a\"><code>6803c56</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/github/codeql-action/issues/4019\">#4019</a>\nfrom github/update-bundle/codeql-bundle-v2.26.1</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github/codeql-action/compare/8aad20d150bbac5944a9f9d289da16a4b0d87c1e...7188fc363630916deb702c7fdcf4e481b751f97a\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `docker/setup-qemu-action` from 4.0.0 to 4.2.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/releases\">docker/setup-qemu-action's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v4.2.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Preserve names in esbuild bundle by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/crazy-max\"><code>@​crazy-max</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/311\">docker/setup-qemu-action#311</a></li>\n<li>Bump <code>@​actions/core</code> from 3.0.0 to 3.0.1 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/295\">docker/setup-qemu-action#295</a></li>\n<li>Bump <code>@​docker/actions-toolkit</code> from 0.91.0 to 0.92.0 in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/315\">docker/setup-qemu-action#315</a></li>\n<li>Bump <code>@​sigstore/core</code> from 3.1.0 to 3.2.1 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/312\">docker/setup-qemu-action#312</a></li>\n<li>Bump js-yaml from 4.1.1 to 4.2.0 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/310\">docker/setup-qemu-action#310</a></li>\n<li>Bump tmp from 0.2.6 to 0.2.7 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/304\">docker/setup-qemu-action#304</a></li>\n<li>Bump undici from 6.26.0 to 6.27.0 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/308\">docker/setup-qemu-action#308</a></li>\n<li>Bump vite from 7.3.2 to 7.3.6 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/307\">docker/setup-qemu-action#307</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/compare/v4.1.0...v4.2.0\">https://github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/compare/v4.1.0...v4.2.0</a></p>\n<h2>v4.1.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add <code>reset</code> input to uninstall current emulators by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/crazy-max\"><code>@​crazy-max</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/21\">docker/setup-qemu-action#21</a></li>\n<li>Bump <code>@​docker/actions-toolkit</code> from 0.77.0 to 0.91.0 in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/250\">docker/setup-qemu-action#250</a>\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/247\">docker/setup-qemu-action#247</a></li>\n<li>Bump brace-expansion from 1.1.12 to 1.1.15 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/265\">docker/setup-qemu-action#265</a></li>\n<li>Bump fast-xml-builder from 1.0.0 to 1.2.0 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/286\">docker/setup-qemu-action#286</a></li>\n<li>Bump fast-xml-parser from 5.4.2 to 5.8.0 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/255\">docker/setup-qemu-action#255</a></li>\n<li>Bump flatted from 3.3.3 to 3.4.2 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/257\">docker/setup-qemu-action#257</a></li>\n<li>Bump glob from 10.3.15 to 10.5.0 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/254\">docker/setup-qemu-action#254</a></li>\n<li>Bump handlebars from 4.7.8 to 4.7.9 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/262\">docker/setup-qemu-action#262</a></li>\n<li>Bump lodash from 4.17.23 to 4.18.1 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/273\">docker/setup-qemu-action#273</a></li>\n<li>Bump postcss from 8.5.6 to 8.5.10 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/285\">docker/setup-qemu-action#285</a></li>\n<li>Bump tar from 6.2.1 to 7.5.15 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/287\">docker/setup-qemu-action#287</a></li>\n<li>Bump tmp from 0.2.5 to 0.2.6 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/291\">docker/setup-qemu-action#291</a></li>\n<li>Bump undici from 6.23.0 to 6.26.0 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/251\">docker/setup-qemu-action#251</a></li>\n<li>Bump vite from 7.3.1 to 7.3.2 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/pull/271\">docker/setup-qemu-action#271</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/compare/v4.0.0...v4.1.0\">https://github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/compare/v4.0.0...v4.1.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/commit/96fe6ef7f33517b61c61be40b68a1882f3264fb8\"><code>96fe6ef</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/issues/315\">#315</a>\nfrom docker/dependabot/npm_and_yarn/docker/actions-to...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/commit/31f08d3fc9186dbe4b4550696f2e32e9aa7f9465\"><code>31f08d3</code></a>\n[dependabot skip] chore: update generated content</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/commit/4e7017a474d2cf3912bb0437f7fafec6d5fb6c52\"><code>4e7017a</code></a>\nbuild(deps): bump <code>@​docker/actions-toolkit</code> from 0.91.0 to\n0.92.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/commit/0eca235293ca1939b58c082f69bdc981ccce8c94\"><code>0eca235</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/issues/314\">#314</a>\nfrom crazy-max/fix-yarn-preapprove-actions-toolkit</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/commit/ea66a4130b037e7961e14a0e5b155836e797cced\"><code>ea66a41</code></a>\nchore: allow actions-toolkit to bypass yarn age gate</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/commit/451542b03ae7946b7082a398b11c8c315a0e4e80\"><code>451542b</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/issues/308\">#308</a>\nfrom docker/dependabot/npm_and_yarn/undici-6.27.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/commit/532ae0057542ec2102e2d19e9feccf85f1f69013\"><code>532ae00</code></a>\n[dependabot skip] chore: update generated content</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/commit/b6f5af659afad3f9931b782668dee4595ae7e841\"><code>b6f5af6</code></a>\nbuild(deps): bump undici from 6.26.0 to 6.27.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/commit/cf96b86294b57480ac6d330bd177fca87eac95bc\"><code>cf96b86</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/issues/304\">#304</a>\nfrom docker/dependabot/npm_and_yarn/tmp-0.2.7</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/commit/f0ba643f78dc96bc931fb83e5dadc39628e10047\"><code>f0ba643</code></a>\n[dependabot skip] chore: update generated content</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/docker/setup-qemu-action/compare/ce360397dd3f832beb865e1373c09c0e9f86d70a...96fe6ef7f33517b61c61be40b68a1882f3264fb8\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `docker/setup-buildx-action` from 4.0.0 to 4.2.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/releases\">docker/setup-buildx-action's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v4.2.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Preserve names in esbuild bundle by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/crazy-max\"><code>@​crazy-max</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/572\">docker/setup-buildx-action#572</a></li>\n<li>Bump <code>@​actions/core</code> from 3.0.0 to 3.0.1 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/551\">docker/setup-buildx-action#551</a></li>\n<li>Bump <code>@​docker/actions-toolkit</code> from 0.90.0 to 0.92.0 in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/557\">docker/setup-buildx-action#557</a>\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/580\">docker/setup-buildx-action#580</a></li>\n<li>Bump <code>@​sigstore/core</code> from 3.1.0 to 3.2.1 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/573\">docker/setup-buildx-action#573</a></li>\n<li>Bump <code>@​sigstore/verify</code> from 3.1.0 to 3.1.1 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/576\">docker/setup-buildx-action#576</a></li>\n<li>Bump js-yaml from 4.1.1 to 5.2.0 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/562\">docker/setup-buildx-action#562</a></li>\n<li>Bump sigstore from 4.1.0 to 4.1.1 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/577\">docker/setup-buildx-action#577</a></li>\n<li>Bump tmp from 0.2.5 to 0.2.7 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/556\">docker/setup-buildx-action#556</a></li>\n<li>Bump undici from 6.25.0 to 6.27.0 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/570\">docker/setup-buildx-action#570</a></li>\n<li>Bump vite from 7.3.2 to 7.3.6 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/569\">docker/setup-buildx-action#569</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/compare/v4.1.0...v4.2.0\">https://github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/compare/v4.1.0...v4.2.0</a></p>\n<h2>v4.1.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Bump <code>@​docker/actions-toolkit</code> from 0.79.0 to 0.90.0 in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/489\">docker/setup-buildx-action#489</a></li>\n<li>Bump brace-expansion from 1.1.12 to 5.0.6 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/547\">docker/setup-buildx-action#547</a>\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/508\">docker/setup-buildx-action#508</a></li>\n<li>Bump fast-xml-builder from 1.0.0 to 1.2.0 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/540\">docker/setup-buildx-action#540</a></li>\n<li>Bump fast-xml-parser from 5.4.2 to 5.8.0 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/496\">docker/setup-buildx-action#496</a></li>\n<li>Bump flatted from 3.3.3 to 3.4.2 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/499\">docker/setup-buildx-action#499</a></li>\n<li>Bump glob from 10.3.12 to 13.0.6 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/setup-buildx-a