res</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> gpt-5.6-sol updates (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/039d1feb264a2dca7195ba5028e9fb47a5e04987\">039d1fe</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> restore beta resource accessors (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/2dfc130b8f0fdb0049e075aac21aaef29482b4e3\">2dfc130</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Chores</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>retrigger release automation (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/7b61351b014bb6ca4623ff6cce7f32f45038a92e\">7b61351</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.44.0 (2026-06-24)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.43.0...v2.44.0\">v2.43.0...v2.44.0</a></p>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>auth:</strong> prioritize first auth header (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/797e3362e222ae14e587a4543b76a54d8992d66c\">797e336</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.43.0 (2026-06-17)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.42.0...v2.43.0\">v2.42.0...v2.43.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> update OpenAPI spec or Stainless config (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/22542358490ef8f31f0d373e17f7b791b3d983ca\">2254235</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/0e6adb15adc1e74087bcb402de7a75e4fbc0aecb\"><code>0e6adb1</code></a>\nrelease: 2.46.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3501\">#3501</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/f16fbbd2bd25dc1ff150b5f78dbd15ff6bab6d91\"><code>f16fbbd</code></a>\nrelease: 2.45.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3478\">#3478</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/6d9262d5c666a1e4d47f63178db907ba3087ac5d\"><code>6d9262d</code></a>\nrelease: 2.44.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/d35627525e192b7a65b556d8a79d22079ccabdf6\"><code>d356275</code></a>\n[codex] Add AWS Bedrock provider authentication (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3398\">#3398</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/f47f9a270861ca6a6096e8ea15ef8f3e1fb089b0\"><code>f47f9a2</code></a>\nfix(auth): prioritize first auth header</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/e20b6b82c145091f0d8412a7e4a9bc5900a40462\"><code>e20b6b8</code></a>\nrelease: 2.43.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/4d354538e8c2618e228c80f1fdc332ee1f70d1f2\"><code>4d35453</code></a>\nfeat(api): update OpenAPI spec or Stainless config</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/2bba15e71817a75e9b8517e09cb244bc144b50d0\"><code>2bba15e</code></a>\nrelease: 2.42.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/1ec3e8298982d900d31b486177b5d4cecadcf035\"><code>1ec3e82</code></a>\ncodegen metadata</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/93c2eca17d2d484b95245c849b39f51c6d291478\"><code>93c2eca</code></a>\nfeat(api): manual updates</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.41.1...v2.46.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `mcp` from 1.27.2 to 1.28.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/releases\">mcp's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.28.0</h2>\n<h2>Deprecations</h2>\n<p>Two API surfaces now emit <code>DeprecationWarning</code> ahead of\ntheir removal in v2. Nothing is removed in 1.x, and the warnings fire\nonly when the deprecated API is <em>called</em> - importing the modules\nstays silent.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>WebSocket transport</strong> -\n<code>mcp.client.websocket.websocket_client</code> and\n<code>mcp.server.websocket.websocket_server</code><code>modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk#1783</code></li>\n<li><strong>Experimental tasks API</strong> -\n<code>ClientSession.experimental</code>,\n<code>Server.experimental</code>,\n<code>ServerSession.experimental</code>, and the\n<code>experimental_task_handlers=</code> kwarg on\n<code>ClientSession</code>. Tasks (SEP-1686) were removed from the MCP\nspecification and are expected to return as a separate MCP\nextension.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If your test suite runs with <code>filterwarnings =\n[&quot;error&quot;]</code> and exercises these paths, add a scoped\nignore such as <code>ignore:The experimental tasks API is\ndeprecated:DeprecationWarning</code> or <code>ignore:The WebSocket .*\ntransport is deprecated:DeprecationWarning</code>.</p>\n<p>See <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/issues/2828\">#2828</a>\nfor full details.</p>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[v1.x] Support Python 3.14 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/maxisbey\"><code>@​maxisbey</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/2769\">modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk#2769</a></li>\n<li>fix: omit null optional fields from task result payloads by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/liuzemei\"><code>@​liuzemei</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/2809\">modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk#2809</a></li>\n<li>[v1.x] Deprecate the WebSocket transport and the experimental tasks\nentry points by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/maxisbey\"><code>@​maxisbey</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/2828\">modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk#2828</a></li>\n<li>[v1.x] Add a v2 status banner to the README by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/maxisbey\"><code>@​maxisbey</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/2835\">modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk#2835</a></li>\n<li>[v1.x] Deflake the child process cleanup tests by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/maxisbey\"><code>@​maxisbey</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/2839\">modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk#2839</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/liuzemei\"><code>@​liuzemei</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/2809\">modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk#2809</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/compare/v1.27.2...v1.28.0\">https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/compare/v1.27.2...v1.28.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/777b8d06710c140e3606b0d4598e2aa48546c266\"><code>777b8d0</code></a>\n[v1.x] Support TransportSecuritySettings in the WebSocket server\ntransport (#...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/47204674fb26185c2cf45f065831f27b8e5d5c65\"><code>4720467</code></a>\n[v1.x] Set Development Status classifier to Production/Stable (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/issues/2976\">#2976</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/6df3d734265eb49bf758a5e5eb420937337184e9\"><code>6df3d73</code></a>\n[v1.x] Buffer per-request StreamableHTTP streams; store priming event\nbefore ...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/32d32908feb7b15eddeb46872774bf95869cc5f0\"><code>32d3290</code></a>\n[v1.x] Pass a list to parametrize in test_docs_examples (pytest 9.1.0\ncompat)...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/0dca751056dc87d04893d53af129fd00b56a18da\"><code>0dca751</code></a>\n[v1.x] Deflake the child process cleanup tests (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/issues/2839\">#2839</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/52258a95645c66fccbe925289c3382712b9bc68a\"><code>52258a9</code></a>\n[v1.x] Add a v2 status banner to the README (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/issues/2835\">#2835</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/b8f491724c45dbf89d6569364b58d6e8d25d7e42\"><code>b8f4917</code></a>\n[v1.x] Deprecate the WebSocket transport and the experimental tasks\nentry poi...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/2309e5ef974062748e0268c396eba73cfdb6f5e3\"><code>2309e5e</code></a>\nfix: omit null optional fields from task result payloads (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/issues/2809\">#2809</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/494eb11d36b4238226cc0551da6015e1c73f7f3b\"><code>494eb11</code></a>\n[v1.x] Support Python 3.14 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/issues/2769\">#2769</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/compare/v1.27.2...v1.28.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `croniter` from 6.2.2 to 6.2.4\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/releases\">croniter's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>6.2.4</h2>\n<h2>croniter 6.2.4</h2>\n<h3>Bugfixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix <code>expand_from_start_time</code> day-of-week low bound so\nSunday wraps correctly for stepped day-of-week ranges\n(<code>isoweekday() % 7</code> instead of <code>weekday() + 1</code>).\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/239\">#239</a>,\nthanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alhudz\"><code>@​alhudz</code></a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Packaging</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Bump pinned GitHub Actions via dependabot. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/238\">#238</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/240\">#240</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Install:</strong> <code>pip install croniter==6.2.4</code> ·\n<a href=\"https://pypi.org/project/croniter/6.2.4/\">PyPI</a></p>\n<h2>6.2.3</h2>\n<p>No release notes provided.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">croniter's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>6.2.4 (2026-07-10)</h2>\n<p>Bugfixes</p>\n<pre><code>- Fix ``expand_from_start_time`` day-of-week low bound so\nSunday wraps correctly for stepped day-of-week ranges (``isoweekday() %\n7`` instead of ``weekday() + 1``). [44e3090,\n[#239](https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/239), @alhudz]\n<p>Packaging\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bump pinned GitHub Actions via dependabot. [fd13d2e, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/240\">#240</a>;\n5cd2e46, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/238\">#238</a>]</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>6.2.3 (2026-07-02)</h2>\n<p>Features and Improvements</p>\n<pre><code>- Fix quadratic expansion of comma-separated range lists for\na large speed-up on expressions with many ranges. [1d79fc6,\n[#231](https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/231), @alhudz]\n<p>Bugfixes</p>\n<pre><code>- Reject a zero step (e.g. ``5-5/0``) in equal and reversed\ncron ranges instead of silently accepting it. [ab27767,\n[#232](https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/232), @alhudz]\n- Fix ``expand_from_start_time`` month low-bound off-by-one so stepped\nmonth ranges start on the correct month. [f329964,\n[#235](https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/235), @alhudz]\n\nPackaging\n</code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix zizmor-reported security findings in GitHub Actions workflows.\n[ed19f94, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/230\">#230</a>]</li>\n<li>Bump pinned build and CI dependencies via dependabot.</li>\n<li>Upgrade locked development and build dependencies (<code>uv lock\n--upgrade</code>).\n</code></pre></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/58534997eb4634344f00d407fb199d4d1bd057e7\"><code>5853499</code></a>\nPrepare for release 6.2.4 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/241\">#241</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/fd13d2ec447efd854806638cb5f71a2a3a90a0b5\"><code>fd13d2e</code></a>\nBump the github-actions group with 2 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/240\">#240</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/44e3090ae47ccf72e4027ed6fabf6a31eca42f85\"><code>44e3090</code></a>\nwrap sunday in expand_from_start_time day-of-week low bound (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/239\">#239</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/5cd2e4611e8ebea446a9d0edef3f9d8e1f30c0e3\"><code>5cd2e46</code></a>\nBump the github-actions group with 2 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/238\">#238</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/f1eeddd7b9057b66406d162d04879258b29601d5\"><code>f1eeddd</code></a>\nPrepare for 6.2.4 development (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/237\">#237</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/22b59e05f5ca485c45596b2a9b580fddffbf753f\"><code>22b59e0</code></a>\nPrepare for release 6.2.3 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/236\">#236</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/ab277671adc8e446e8dc7f1e939eabf024b6199e\"><code>ab27767</code></a>\nreject zero step in equal and reversed cron ranges (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/232\">#232</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/f329964223eeb29e7788b1a9d615b525148fec96\"><code>f329964</code></a>\nfix expand_from_start_time month low bound off-by-one (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/235\">#235</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/9810279c20030954e2f1ed2cf5f1d34b98c6b07f\"><code>9810279</code></a>\nBump the github-actions group with 2 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/233\">#233</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/d051aaf6342fbe9c559b9fcd99e6fb6f3bb63cb7\"><code>d051aaf</code></a>\nBump hatchling from 1.29.0 to 1.30.1 in the pip-dependencies group (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/cro…","tree":{"sha":"f079fa09ccefdfcbf82e479ce074918448de8a3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f079fa09ccefdfcbf82e479ce074918448de8a3e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/dde9cac57aa26eec49fd95410a5bedcf0ffef435","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXziDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOuEQAKMg99FE+eij8d5DZbYsyL3k\nSn15/8Kp+j5NFzJqv4o3meRAmQPV4N1I0rA+K+wH2f/g3C4H1jhYQZcazr7mkZCz\nn0BVTt58hG7eFjnyIfVjlRurHfAZ5x1gLfRYnc4cpK++WKG30cydZ2c7OjHW1IIo\nj/XV/GXC1lrCYESfKxJCMwe2eDU0h6fs/I6m4mQkSUq7SJkgnIBGtgoykjrsBLQ7\n2etb8goe2gr9FS7k2zcZ31nBXs+Pb/JYkGATX+MtRCr11BchrNGzCibHtlydheXO\nuM2G5hTIUqmSG07kSUnwaPZHAXX9d8BH4M4WZFMGxFf5QwP0GwWAPs0Ny9MTMMhl\nGw7PhMrcafAPk4wN8biLlyRZzl5KVzZQKNjb4YXdpN7Dt9nxlsga+bPRJCoak5UP\nB+9GN9Uxyogc4owBAbiViL2RwXjnOFFC8+PyjgDS19IpJwPJwDg3lzFvCoYaLWq5\nRP+0C1dTTJWgHpoROEIFB3YM9VnNEIR1l6xDLkVYWltRAiVddVZ2m40MPIGwjC2m\n/pw6cKR+oNHyzBXLW5KzIV2mUqWYXAqsbz9Bj67+XLfAZlmMjuzNPVcyRf9AFLST\n+kjnsEzyUHsyyiMtMnFcTS7pLVlq8DjmQB/mSJprw/H+wvBHiCvoCBL/+sFZPW3T\njb33KNl3uv7x3s6m9+ne\n=bDH5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f079fa09ccefdfcbf82e479ce074918448de8a3e\nparent dce9e5922119ea7d6ebdd0812ee5cc88b9f944ac\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1784625283 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784625283 +0300\n\ndeps(core-api): bump the uv-minor-patch group in /core-api with 16 updates (#605)\n\nBumps the uv-minor-patch group in /core-api with 16 updates:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [fastapi](https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi) | `0.137.0` | `0.139.2`\n|\n| [greenlet](https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet) | `3.5.1` |\n`3.5.3` |\n| [pgvector](https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector-python) | `0.4.2` |\n`0.5.0` |\n| [alembic](https://github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic) | `1.18.4` | `1.18.5`\n|\n| [pydantic-settings](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings) |\n`2.14.1` | `2.14.2` |\n|\n[google-cloud-aiplatform](https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform)\n| `1.157.0` | `1.161.0` |\n| [google-genai](https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai) | `2.8.0` |\n`2.12.1` |\n| [openai](https://github.com/openai/openai-python) | `2.41.1` |\n`2.46.0` |\n| [mcp](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk) | `1.27.2` |\n`1.28.1` |\n| [croniter](https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter) | `6.2.2` |\n`6.2.4` |\n| [ddtrace](https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py) | `4.10.6` |\n`4.11.1` |\n| [kreuzberg](https://github.com/kreuzberg-dev/kreuzberg-lts) | `4.9.9`\n| `4.10.2` |\n| [mypy](https://github.com/python/mypy) | `2.1.0` | `2.3.0` |\n| [ruff](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff) | `0.15.17` | `0.15.22` |\n| [types-croniter](https://github.com/python/typeshed) |\n`6.2.2.20260518` | `6.2.4.20260711` |\n| [pytest](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest) | `9.1.0` | `9.1.1` |\n\nUpdates `fastapi` from 0.137.0 to 0.139.2\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/releases\">fastapi's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.139.2</h2>\n<h3>Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>🐛 Refactor router route building to make it thread-safe, mainly\nrelevant for tests running in parallel threads (uncommon). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16013\">#16013</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>0.139.1</h2>\n<h3>Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>🐛 Fix frontend fallback support for doted paths like\n<code>/users/john.doe</code>. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16011\">#16011</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Docs</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>📝 Fix topic repository list not being displayed and\n<code>skip_users</code> not being applied. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15995\">#15995</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Translations</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for tr (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16005\">#16005</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for zh-hant (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15996\">#15996</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for fr (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16006\">#16006</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for de (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15999\">#15999</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for ko (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16004\">#16004</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for zh (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16001\">#16001</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for uk (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16003\">#16003</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for ja (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15998\">#15998</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for pt (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16000\">#16000</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for es (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15997\">#15997</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for ru (update-outdated). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16002\">#16002</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for hi (add-missing). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15990\">#15990</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for hi (add-missing). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15925\">#15925</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update translations for hi (add-missing). PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15797\">#15797</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Update <code>llm-prompt.md</code> for Hindi. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15810\">#15810</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🌐 Fix language-specific translation prompt for Russian language. PR\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15924\">#15924</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Internal</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>⬆ Bump the python-packages group across 1 directory with 6 updates.\nPR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15981\">#15981</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/apps/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot[bot]</code></a>.</li>\n<li>⬆ Bump typing-extensions from 4.15.0 to 4.16.0. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15982\">#15982</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/apps/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot[bot]</code></a>.</li>\n<li>⬆ Bump the github-actions group across 1 directory with 4 updates.\nPR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15983\">#15983</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/apps/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot[bot]</code></a>.</li>\n<li>⬆ Bump pre-commit hooks. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15985\">#15985</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>👷 Use <code>FASTAPI_LATEST_CHANGES</code> token in\n<code>bump-pre-commit-hooks</code> workflow. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15984\">#15984</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n<li>👷 Add GH workflow to bump pre-commit hook versions. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15873\">#15873</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🔧 Set Dependabot schedule interval to &quot;monthly&quot;. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15874\">#15874</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n<li>⬆ Bump CodSpeedHQ/action from 4.17.6 to 4.18.1 in the github-actions\ngroup. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15950\">#15950</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/apps/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot[bot]</code></a>.</li>\n<li>⬆ Bump the python-packages group with 8 updates. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15952\">#15952</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/apps/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot[bot]</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🔧 Update sponsors: add TutorCruncher. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15947\">#15947</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>👷 Fix notify translations checkout target. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15933\">#15933</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>👷 Fix latest-changes checkout target. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15932\">#15932</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🔧 Update sponsors: remove RapidProxy. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15929\">#15929</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>⬆️ Update issue-manager to 0.8.1. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15928\">#15928</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>⬆️ Update latest-changes to 0.6.1. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15926\">#15926</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/866b7a3d0ce1025a3811f23aea4846d01a2b16a8\"><code>866b7a3</code></a>\n🔖 Release version 0.139.2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16014\">#16014</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/7b3effea754619f0c305af576be23a51865292a3\"><code>7b3effe</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/7fe315c21afb8a57a2b559772e0f7ced7e5d071a\"><code>7fe315c</code></a>\n🐛 Refactor router route building to make it thread-safe, mainly relevant\nfor ...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/c48e67b1ce9c03fc9bd4b1ac72350e51ad5a6e8a\"><code>c48e67b</code></a>\n🔖 Release version 0.139.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16012\">#16012</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/2acc4fbf155caf016e3bd2602c0d2ec52723e635\"><code>2acc4fb</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/eb75fd078e83aed935016bcdf0705cd58bbf0d0e\"><code>eb75fd0</code></a>\n🐛 Fix frontend fallback support for doted paths like\n<code>/users/john.doe</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16011\">#16011</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/9b8410bdc9fa1fd679ea7e65b926535c7045ab87\"><code>9b8410b</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/e24d44cce4092a33b64e9536e96e7608a7dcb9b8\"><code>e24d44c</code></a>\n📝 Fix topic repository list not being displayed and\n<code>skip_users</code> not being ap...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/93b78f8646dea4543cc4d938f7e29b8547749a99\"><code>93b78f8</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/b959b443577c5f2b870cdef13219b98aa32f8943\"><code>b959b44</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/compare/0.137.0...0.139.2\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `greenlet` from 3.5.1 to 3.5.3\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/blob/master/CHANGES.rst\">greenlet's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>3.5.3 (2026-06-26)</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix a crash on free-threaded builds when multiple greenlets were\nholding a critical section on an object and the GIL for the thread\nwas dropped. See <code>issue 513\n&lt;https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/513&gt;</code>_.\nThanks\nto ddorian.</li>\n</ul>\n<h1>3.5.2 (2026-06-17)</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>The minimum supported version of Python 3.15 is now 3.15b2.</li>\n<li>Fix some garbage-collection related crashes on free-threaded Python\n3.15. Thanks to Kumar Aditya in <code>PR\n[#511](https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/511)\n&lt;https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/pull/511&gt;</code>_.</li>\n<li>Improve garbage collection of greenlets. This mostly applies to\nPython 3.15. Thanks to Kumar Aditya in <code>PR\n[#512](https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/512)\n&lt;https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/pull/512&gt;</code>_.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/6ee8c2c5b92fbf296c10219030d0bd3ab0ea6300\"><code>6ee8c2c</code></a>\nPreparing release 3.5.3</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/6ec0bbba46fdcbfbf5fe4a37ab744aa3835f05c6\"><code>6ec0bbb</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/514\">#514</a>\nfrom python-greenlet/issue513-preserve-crit-section</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/c03a7e6932c3b437bdf873acfc66fbaae31f1875\"><code>c03a7e6</code></a>\nPy3.13+: Preserve thread state critical_section to prevent crash on\nfree-thre...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/bc10829b9eb05d35bc0b8a09c8c6e4d54cfccc18\"><code>bc10829</code></a>\nSpeed up manylinux test runs by only running the core checks; only start\nmany...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/c2db75dca4bafa562ace9553b6e5c17af6b483e4\"><code>c2db75d</code></a>\nBack to development: 3.5.3</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/0b64e9c851ae7bd8fc9b73d98031168237ee71db\"><code>0b64e9c</code></a>\nPreparing release 3.5.2</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/3e28d276d01e74882f4cff1a4b54aed47153d617\"><code>3e28d27</code></a>\nAdd change note for <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/512\">#512</a>\n[skip ci]</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/6563c5e909a84c037c3d03e46851cd3016525a35\"><code>6563c5e</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/512\">#512</a>\nfrom kumaraditya303/ft-mem</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/ab6eff60766e8954d890eef064ee2e1dd7c8b262\"><code>ab6eff6</code></a>\nadd ignore for win 3.10</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/41f5349a0f1b69ce180c90acb9a4cf2c84d612e7\"><code>41f5349</code></a>\nrevert back to fails_leakcheck_on_py314_or_less</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/compare/3.5.1...3.5.3\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `pgvector` from 0.4.2 to 0.5.0\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector-python/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md\">pgvector's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.5.0 (2026-07-06)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Added experimental support for type hints</li>\n<li>Changed <code>vector</code> and <code>halfvec</code> types to return\nlist for Django, SQLAlchemy, SQLModel, and Peewee</li>\n<li>Changed <code>vector</code> type to return <code>Vector</code>\nobject for Psycopg 3, Psycopg 2, asyncpg, and pg8000</li>\n<li>Removed <code>utils</code> package (use top-level\n<code>pgvector</code> package instead)</li>\n<li>Removed re-exported classes (use top-level <code>pgvector</code>\npackage instead)</li>\n<li>Removed dependency on NumPy</li>\n<li>Dropped support for Python &lt; 3.10</li>\n<li>Dropped support for SQLAlchemy &lt; 2</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector-python/commit/60739dfd6cb9d674f32afa4184d43e6aff9dfbcf\"><code>60739df</code></a>\nVersion bump to 0.5.0 [skip ci]</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector-python/commit/a810f27ca93c185e81e98b05d87622d736e89568\"><code>a810f27</code></a>\nUpdated example [skip ci]</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector-python/commit/45b054c53fb174ca12ecb08157f7875bd4795356\"><code>45b054c</code></a>\nUpdated example [skip ci]</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector-python/commit/efa144252a96be79c695923d2717b0555bea8fcd\"><code>efa1442</code></a>\nUpdated examples [skip ci]</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector-python/commit/780cc73f723fd2300cd16ae7362c9ab00453ecfc\"><code>780cc73</code></a>\nUpdated example [skip ci]</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector-python/commit/9f0d6b97640486eacf858143430b40d11634a845\"><code>9f0d6b9</code></a>\nUpdated examples [skip ci]</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector-python/commit/f6e113e1ad10968473e630d001bc473b6c9a62ed\"><code>f6e113e</code></a>\nUpdated example [skip ci]</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector-python/commit/dc6877060099dcd2485e23c9facb04d3e6df3faf\"><code>dc68770</code></a>\nUpdated readme [skip ci]</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector-python/commit/0c18e0aa5de9d9a4ff1bd1ad58c8839bb5ce814c\"><code>0c18e0a</code></a>\nAddressed todo</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector-python/commit/28191fc8b9a5702cd07b2854dbf89b1e0d263100\"><code>28191fc</code></a>\nRemoved todo [skip ci]</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector-python/compare/v0.4.2...v0.5.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `alembic` from 1.18.4 to 1.18.5\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/releases\">alembic's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>1.18.5</h1>\n<p>Released: June 25, 2026</p>\n<h2>usecase</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>[usecase] [commands]</strong> Added <code>--splice</code>\nsupport to the <code>merge()</code> command. Previously, the\nmerge command would suggest using <code>--splice</code> when attempting\nto merge\nnon-head revisions, but the flag was not actually accepted by the\ncommand.\nThe <code>splice</code> parameter is now available in both the\ncommand-line\ninterface and the <code>command.merge()</code> function, matching the\nexisting\nsupport in <code>command.revision()</code>. Pull request courtesy Kadir\nCan\nOzden.</p>\n<p>References: <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/1712\">#1712</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>[usecase] [environment]</strong> Added\n<code>ScriptDirectory.get_heads.consider_depends_on</code>\nparameter to <code>ScriptDirectory.get_heads()</code>. When set to\n<code>True</code>,\nhead revisions that are also a dependency of another revision via\n<code>depends_on</code> are excluded from the result, matching the\neffective\nheads that would be present in the <code>alembic_version</code> table\nafter\nrunning all upgrades.</p>\n<p>References: <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/1806\">#1806</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>bug</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>[bug] [autogenerate]</strong> Fixed rendering of dialect\nkeyword arguments containing\n<code>~sqlalchemy.schema.Column</code> objects within sequences, such as\n<code>postgresql_include</code>. These were previously rendered using\n<code>repr()</code>,\nproducing invalid Python in the generated migration scripts.  Column\nobjects within list or tuple values are now correctly rendered as their\nstring column names.  Pull request courtesy Ajay Singh.</p>\n<p>References: <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/1258\">#1258</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>[bug] [mysql]</strong> Implemented type comparison for\n<code>ENUM</code> datatypes on MySQL, which\nchecks that the individual enum values are equivalent.  If additional\nentries are on either side, this generates a diff. Changes of order do\nnot\ngenerate a diff.  Pull request courtesy Furkan Köykıran.</p>\n<p>References: <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/1745\">#1745</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/779\">#779</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>[bug] [operations]</strong> Fixed bug where the\n<code>inline_references</code> parameter of\n<code>Operations.add_column()</code> did not include foreign key\nreferential\nactions such as <code>ON DELETE</code>, <code>ON UPDATE</code>,\n<code>DEFERRABLE</code>,\n<code>INITIALLY</code>, and <code>MATCH</code> when rendering the inline\n<code>REFERENCES</code>\nclause.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/commits\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `pydantic-settings` from 2.14.1 to 2.14.2\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/releases\">pydantic-settings's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.14.2</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<p>This is a security patch release.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Prevent <code>NestedSecretsSettingsSource</code> from following\nsymlinks outside <code>secrets_dir</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hramezani\"><code>@​hramezani</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/889\">pydantic/pydantic-settings#889</a></li>\n<li>Prepare release 2.14.2 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hramezani\"><code>@​hramezani</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/890\">pydantic/pydantic-settings#890</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Security</h3>\n<p>Fixes <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/security/advisories/GHSA-4xgf-cpjx-pc3j\">GHSA-4xgf-cpjx-pc3j</a>:\n<code>NestedSecretsSettingsSource</code> with\n<code>secrets_nested_subdir=True</code> could follow a symbolic link\ninside <code>secrets_dir</code> pointing outside it, reading out-of-tree\nfiles into settings values and bypassing the\n<code>secrets_dir_max_size</code> cap. Affected versions: <code>&gt;=\n2.12.0, &lt; 2.14.2</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/compare/v2.14.1...v2.14.2\">https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/compare/v2.14.1...v2.14.2</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commit/d703bd717e5e07439fa89da2245eee6139413e9e\"><code>d703bd7</code></a>\nPrepare release 2.14.2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/890\">#890</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/compare/v2.14.1...v2.14.2\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `google-cloud-aiplatform` from 1.157.0 to 1.161.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/releases\">google-cloud-aiplatform's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.161.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/compare/v1.160.0...v1.161.0\">1.161.0</a>\n(2026-07-14)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add FeedbackService to Agent Platform Python SDK (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f6ecd6773ab95e1e1492d91d77af1f1e019479d0\">f6ecd67</a>)</li>\n<li>Add identity_type to Reasoning Engine public protos (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/66d48376ed9e2ec65daa2200e478f9f1a54e6eea\">66d4837</a>)</li>\n<li>Add identity_type to Reasoning Engine public protos (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/66d48376ed9e2ec65daa2200e478f9f1a54e6eea\">66d4837</a>)</li>\n<li>Add support for FeedbackContext to Agent Platform Python SDK (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f5f750c572b8ce0bfce05f04c15502b10c765b83\">f5f750c</a>)</li>\n<li>Expose retrieval_queries in GroundingMetadata for the v1 API (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/66d48376ed9e2ec65daa2200e478f9f1a54e6eea\">66d4837</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - evaluate Gemini Agents API agents via\ninteraction (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/a44c5209c2b4656ce44f0c5510c543844eb27fdb\">a44c520</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - evaluate() agent parameter for interaction-id\ndatasets (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/135224cacfd13901d101f3b10be6478ffbb5c07c\">135224c</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - exponential backoff for Gemini agent\ninteraction polling (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/1f3c0748394a002abcc9642d29674bb267bc18cc\">1f3c074</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - generate_conversation_scenarios support for\nGemini Agents API agents (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/df4e67201d905829a3a5f3c2b6c1ce0819bf519f\">df4e672</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - run_inference support for Gemini Agents API\nagents (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/852c546df44c064332be67a89e4abb343517a4e1\">852c546</a>)</li>\n<li>Onboard Vertex Model Garden to GenAI Python SDK: Add\nlist_custom_model_deploy_options support (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/239bc1303157448b02d879764961e6d3bb3dc439\">239bc13</a>)</li>\n<li>Resolve Interactions API data for agent trace display in eval\nresults. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f1585179ef51fa1bf223dbeaeb8d7412aeb997fa\">f158517</a>)</li>\n<li>Support creating evaluation runs from pre-existing Interactions API\ndata (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/b430014af02c7f4657ce394f7b908bee38cfb467\">b430014</a>)</li>\n<li>Support Prompt Management in the JS GenAI Modules (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/89d2b917b47b9c0c9c4a376a7157533d7c870b53\">89d2b91</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Remove OpenTelemetry event logger setup since the Events API/SDK has\nbeen deprecated and is soon being removed entirely. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/73fde8dfee08b385e9a63eeeb48b8ed95c1bfa5f\">73fde8d</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add result_parsing_function field to LLMMetric SDK types (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/8f1a0a14e361b0bc6c82a7192438c88983862d68\">8f1a0a1</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v1.160.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/compare/v1.159.0...v1.160.0\">1.160.0</a>\n(2026-07-07)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add revision_labels, revision_expire_time, revision_ttl,\ndisable_memory_revisions, metadata, metadata_merge_strategy and\noverlap_event_count to Memory Bank IngestEvents API (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/e169af9ac0f56603be763466694b95fc2fd64e8c\">e169af9</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - add Gemini Agents API related eval types (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/c8a38a085931b01f4d6071f0ab7a64cb42851829\">c8a38a0</a>)</li>\n<li>Onboard Vertex Model Garden to GenAI Python SDK: Add\nlist_publisher_model_deploy_options support (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/ce463e6820b7a92dfb312ad6d0a8d3da8314567c\">ce463e6</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add mTLS and telemetry endpoint configurations to preview AdkApp (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/c3c1836b5aad5d3d38b961231b55b096787e983e\">c3c1836</a>)</li>\n<li>Avoid shadowing of built-in list in Python 3.14 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/195ca275c0ec94a6e1f1b73872807e4774a29a4e\">195ca27</a>)</li>\n<li>Honor explicitly passed api_endpoint when location is\n&quot;global&quot; (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f9e3c6ea96ef38c67ace5e876db269f3580a66ed\">f9e3c6e</a>),\ncloses <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/issues/6958\">#6958</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v1.159.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/compare/v1.158.0...v1.159.0\">1.159.0</a>\n(2026-06-30)</h2>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">google-cloud-aiplatform's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/compare/v1.160.0...v1.161.0\">1.161.0</a>\n(2026-07-14)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add FeedbackService to Agent Platform Python SDK (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f6ecd6773ab95e1e1492d91d77af1f1e019479d0\">f6ecd67</a>)</li>\n<li>Add identity_type to Reasoning Engine public protos (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/66d48376ed9e2ec65daa2200e478f9f1a54e6eea\">66d4837</a>)</li>\n<li>Add identity_type to Reasoning Engine public protos (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/66d48376ed9e2ec65daa2200e478f9f1a54e6eea\">66d4837</a>)</li>\n<li>Add support for FeedbackContext to Agent Platform Python SDK (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f5f750c572b8ce0bfce05f04c15502b10c765b83\">f5f750c</a>)</li>\n<li>Expose retrieval_queries in GroundingMetadata for the v1 API (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/66d48376ed9e2ec65daa2200e478f9f1a54e6eea\">66d4837</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - evaluate Gemini Agents API agents via\ninteraction (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/a44c5209c2b4656ce44f0c5510c543844eb27fdb\">a44c520</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - evaluate() agent parameter for interaction-id\ndatasets (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/135224cacfd13901d101f3b10be6478ffbb5c07c\">135224c</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - exponential backoff for Gemini agent\ninteraction polling (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/1f3c0748394a002abcc9642d29674bb267bc18cc\">1f3c074</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - generate_conversation_scenarios support for\nGemini Agents API agents (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/df4e67201d905829a3a5f3c2b6c1ce0819bf519f\">df4e672</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - run_inference support for Gemini Agents API\nagents (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/852c546df44c064332be67a89e4abb343517a4e1\">852c546</a>)</li>\n<li>Onboard Vertex Model Garden to GenAI Python SDK: Add\nlist_custom_model_deploy_options support (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/239bc1303157448b02d879764961e6d3bb3dc439\">239bc13</a>)</li>\n<li>Resolve Interactions API data for agent trace display in eval\nresults. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f1585179ef51fa1bf223dbeaeb8d7412aeb997fa\">f158517</a>)</li>\n<li>Support creating evaluation runs from pre-existing Interactions API\ndata (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/b430014af02c7f4657ce394f7b908bee38cfb467\">b430014</a>)</li>\n<li>Support Prompt Management in the JS GenAI Modules (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/89d2b917b47b9c0c9c4a376a7157533d7c870b53\">89d2b91</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Remove OpenTelemetry event logger setup since the Events API/SDK has\nbeen deprecated and is soon being removed entirely. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/73fde8dfee08b385e9a63eeeb48b8ed95c1bfa5f\">73fde8d</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add result_parsing_function field to LLMMetric SDK types (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/8f1a0a14e361b0bc6c82a7192438c88983862d68\">8f1a0a1</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/compare/v1.159.0...v1.160.0\">1.160.0</a>\n(2026-07-07)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add revision_labels, revision_expire_time, revision_ttl,\ndisable_memory_revisions, metadata, metadata_merge_strategy and\noverlap_event_count to Memory Bank IngestEvents API (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/e169af9ac0f56603be763466694b95fc2fd64e8c\">e169af9</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - add Gemini Agents API related eval types (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/c8a38a085931b01f4d6071f0ab7a64cb42851829\">c8a38a0</a>)</li>\n<li>Onboard Vertex Model Garden to GenAI Python SDK: Add\nlist_publisher_model_deploy_options support (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/ce463e6820b7a92dfb312ad6d0a8d3da8314567c\">ce463e6</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add mTLS and telemetry endpoint configurations to preview AdkApp (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/c3c1836b5aad5d3d38b961231b55b096787e983e\">c3c1836</a>)</li>\n<li>Avoid shadowing of built-in list in Python 3.14 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/195ca275c0ec94a6e1f1b73872807e4774a29a4e\">195ca27</a>)</li>\n<li>Honor explicitly passed api_endpoint when location is\n&quot;global&quot; (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f9e3c6ea96ef38c67ace5e876db269f3580a66ed\">f9e3c6e</a>),\ncloses <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/issues/6958\">#6958</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/compare/v1.158.0...v1.159.0\">1.159.0</a>\n(2026-06-30)</h2>\n<h3>⚠ BREAKING CHANGES</h3>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/3335750c877654c37d26190afa9259d177dd264e\"><code>3335750</code></a>\nchore(main): release 1.161.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/issues/6967\">#6967</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/83453b9be0a3a7e0df71625aeb1d6ae400f5ba8c\"><code>83453b9</code></a>\nchore: GenAI Client(evals) - remove experimental (non-GA) warnings</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/1f3c0748394a002abcc9642d29674bb267bc18cc\"><code>1f3c074</code></a>\nfeat: GenAI Client(evals) - exponential backoff for Gemini agent\ninteraction ...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/66d48376ed9e2ec65daa2200e478f9f1a54e6eea\"><code>66d4837</code></a>\nCopybara import of the project:</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/df4e67201d905829a3a5f3c2b6c1ce0819bf519f\"><code>df4e672</code></a>\nfeat: GenAI Client(evals) - generate_conversation_scenarios support for\nGemin...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/73fde8dfee08b385e9a63eeeb48b8ed95c1bfa5f\"><code>73fde8d</code></a>\nfix: remove OpenTelemetry event logger setup since the Events API/SDK\nhas bee...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/852c546df44c064332be67a89e4abb343517a4e1\"><code>852c546</code></a>\nfeat: GenAI Client(evals) - run_inference support for Gemini Agents API\nagents</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/239bc1303157448b02d879764961e6d3bb3dc439\"><code>239bc13</code></a>\nfeat: Onboard Vertex Model Garden to GenAI Python SDK: Add\nlist_custom_model_...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/b430014af02c7f4657ce394f7b908bee38cfb467\"><code>b430014</code></a>\nfeat: Support creating evaluation runs from pre-existing Interactions\nAPI data</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f1585179ef51fa1bf223dbeaeb8d7412aeb997fa\"><code>f158517</code></a>\nfeat: Resolve Interactions API data for agent trace display in eval\nresults.</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/compare/v1.157.0...v1.161.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `google-genai` from 2.8.0 to 2.12.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/releases\">google-genai's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.12.1</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.12.0...v2.12.1\">2.12.1</a>\n(2026-07-16)</h2>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix the normalization of Interactions inside triggers (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/be554d3f35dd4e74c49769379c82225d8b5c3032\">be554d3</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.12.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.11.0...v2.12.0\">2.12.0</a>\n(2026-07-15)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add AntigravityAgentConfig to OpenAPI schema overlays and regenerate\nSDKs. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/c68f857234ed510ed3d85b136cca8a5b7421e597\">c68f857</a>)</li>\n<li>Add trigger resource (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/0ab9525157aa04fbed46caa0955486c2a3aad11a\">0ab9525</a>)</li>\n<li>Add Triggers resource to GoogleGenAI client. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/60727fe1277c68fe7c4da3be7e369408b5463e7f\">60727fe</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>interactions:</strong> Add CodeMenderAgentConfig (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/50eca746eb6acf66e98e6381b71c122a868613f0\">50eca74</a>)</li>\n<li>Populate per-modality prompt token count in embedding responses for\ngemini-embedding-2 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/2ba0154a41654dc2e999c6242633e2b2eedaa5e7\">2ba0154</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.11.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.10.0...v2.11.0\">2.11.0</a>\n(2026-07-09)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add environment_id in network config (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/df5f13a9decc1f01f102aba1b953f2a4c6e350d6\">df5f13a</a>)</li>\n<li>Add response_format and Translation_config in GenerationConfig (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/8928da369dfad9eb77979a207b435d4ab589eca0\">8928da3</a>)</li>\n<li>Add retrieval result step and new fields to maps and search results\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/d2b19f6d1a8659af56515f537dc148fb25b5422c\">d2b19f6</a>)</li>\n<li>Add Tool.exa_ai_search for Gemini Enterprise API (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/8928da369dfad9eb77979a207b435d4ab589eca0\">8928da3</a>)</li>\n<li>Support Function declarations during Agent Creation (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/bbeb934283e64ec2232576ea8fbd30ff96e589bb\">bbeb934</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Avoid shadowing of built-in list in Python 3.14 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/5a140468953aa73eee66c879225281db0a92dede\">5a14046</a>)</li>\n<li>Event loop mismatch in GenAI SDK (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/10df4b1eeb54140ca56e011d3bc21862f6d594d0\">10df4b1</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>interactions:</strong> Accept both dict and list[dict] for\ntransform (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/8c7cee3405fa3a6f23dccf44b0bb120eeb546ae6\">8c7cee3</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add Agent Platform MCP example to readme (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/cb2a2a3a7aba32b01569ac9a1b61652e18d2728c\">cb2a2a3</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Code Refactoring</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>interactions:</strong> Remove cached_content,\npresence_penalty, and frequency_penalty; expose safety_settings and\nlabels (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/ba552f72b657a4b5893d453a500b42dfe8d659e4\">ba552f7</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.10.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.9.0...v2.10.0\">2.10.0</a>\n(2026-06-24)</h2>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">google-genai's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.12.0...v2.12.1\">2.12.1</a>\n(2026-07-16)</h2>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix the normalization of Interactions inside triggers (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/be554d3f35dd4e74c49769379c82225d8b5c3032\">be554d3</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.11.0...v2.12.0\">2.12.0</a>\n(2026-07-15)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add AntigravityAgentConfig to OpenAPI schema overlays and regenerate\nSDKs. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/c68f857234ed510ed3d85b136cca8a5b7421e597\">c68f857</a>)</li>\n<li>Add trigger resource (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/0ab9525157aa04fbed46caa0955486c2a3aad11a\">0ab9525</a>)</li>\n<li>Add Triggers resource to GoogleGenAI client. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/60727fe1277c68fe7c4da3be7e369408b5463e7f\">60727fe</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>interactions:</strong> Add CodeMenderAgentConfig (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/50eca746eb6acf66e98e6381b71c122a868613f0\">50eca74</a>)</li>\n<li>Populate per-modality prompt token count in embedding responses for\ngemini-embedding-2 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/2ba0154a41654dc2e999c6242633e2b2eedaa5e7\">2ba0154</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.10.0...v2.11.0\">2.11.0</a>\n(2026-07-09)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add environment_id in network config (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/df5f13a9decc1f01f102aba1b953f2a4c6e350d6\">df5f13a</a>)</li>\n<li>Add response_format and Translation_config in GenerationConfig (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/8928da369dfad9eb77979a207b435d4ab589eca0\">8928da3</a>)</li>\n<li>Add retrieval result step and new fields to maps and search results\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/d2b19f6d1a8659af56515f537dc148fb25b5422c\">d2b19f6</a>)</li>\n<li>Add Tool.exa_ai_search for Gemini Enterprise API (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/8928da369dfad9eb77979a207b435d4ab589eca0\">8928da3</a>)</li>\n<li>Support Function declarations during Agent Creation (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/bbeb934283e64ec2232576ea8fbd30ff96e589bb\">bbeb934</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Avoid shadowing of built-in list in Python 3.14 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/5a140468953aa73eee66c879225281db0a92dede\">5a14046</a>)</li>\n<li>Event loop mismatch in GenAI SDK (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/10df4b1eeb54140ca56e011d3bc21862f6d594d0\">10df4b1</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>interactions:</strong> Accept both dict and list[dict] for\ntransform (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/8c7cee3405fa3a6f23dccf44b0bb120eeb546ae6\">8c7cee3</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add Agent Platform MCP example to readme (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/cb2a2a3a7aba32b01569ac9a1b61652e18d2728c\">cb2a2a3</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Code Refactoring</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>interactions:</strong> Remove cached_content,\npresence_penalty, and frequency_penalty; expose safety_settings and\nlabels (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/ba552f72b657a4b5893d453a500b42dfe8d659e4\">ba552f7</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.9.0...v2.10.0\">2.10.0</a>\n(2026-06-24)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add Agent Platform MCP support to async generate_content_stream (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/a4772cce433632fbf49eb029bf601480ef58a2ab\">a4772cc</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/6debc1c88d6b1e0f60faf01ecc2868760a81af00\"><code>6debc1c</code></a>\nchore(main): release 2.12.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/python-genai/issues/2734\">#2734</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/94d59e5ae462f49c88256ed122fa7dd9712337f0\"><code>94d59e5</code></a>\nCopybara import of the project:</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/be554d3f35dd4e74c49769379c82225d8b5c3032\"><code>be554d3</code></a>\nfix: fix the normalization of Interactions inside triggers</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/939c667fa96a63d44c83e813114bb00faa1a609d\"><code>939c667</code></a>\nchore(main): release 2.12.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/python-genai/issues/2696\">#2696</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/8115b163cdb5a96bfa48f7c3f170a17af88e1129\"><code>8115b16</code></a>\nchore: internal change</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/c8750696763056122433b4b611c84063c575396a\"><code>c875069</code></a>\nfeat: Add max_total_tokens for Interaction.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/d38eaca21d244dce66e4261806b20be804824bb1\"><code>d38eaca</code></a>\nchore: defer <code>mcp</code> SDK import to first MCP usage</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/2a9350d1f3f38e13738ab1527357810aef9cea45\"><code>2a9350d</code></a>\ntest: add tests for private chat</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/c68f857234ed510ed3d85b136cca8a5b7421e597\"><code>c68f857</code></a>\nfeat: Add AntigravityAgentConfig to OpenAPI schema overlays and\nregenerate SDKs.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/60727fe1277c68fe7c4da3be7e369408b5463e7f\"><code>60727fe</code></a>\nfeat: Add Triggers resource to GoogleGenAI client.</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.8.0...v2.12.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `openai` from 2.41.1 to 2.46.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/releases\">openai's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.46.0</h2>\n<h2>2.46.0 (2026-07-17)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.45.0...v2.46.0\">v2.45.0...v2.46.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong>\n/organization/projects/{project_id}/service_accounts/{service_account_id}/api_keys&quot;\nendpoint (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/5a0094194eac9c605c8ca84d47d1c5518f8e2131\">5a00941</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> add owner_project_access to APIKeyListParams\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/f589d04bf9f377ecb1f54335ab3ab9d825b5dfee\">f589d04</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> manual updates (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/980f176e83ee5d991bf9e8e4def80d9905ade5ec\">980f176</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> manual updates (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/2eae984315580cdbf9ceb14d6cb568c581baa768\">2eae984</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> preserve generated type compatibility (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/00bd72adbe03f4b5c4b89d91b8d317f11b58bbdf\">00bd72a</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> remove beta annotation compatibility aliases\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/99dbd15ff3ad1628b94a729a6b688212d4655908\">99dbd15</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.45.0</h2>\n<h2>2.45.0 (2026-07-09)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.44.0...v2.45.0\">v2.44.0...v2.45.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> gpt-5.6-sol updates (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/039d1feb264a2dca7195ba5028e9fb47a5e04987\">039d1fe</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> restore beta resource accessors (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/2dfc130b8f0fdb0049e075aac21aaef29482b4e3\">2dfc130</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Chores</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>retrigger release automation (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/7b61351b014bb6ca4623ff6cce7f32f45038a92e\">7b61351</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.44.0</h2>\n<h2>2.44.0 (2026-06-24)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.43.0...v2.44.0\">v2.43.0...v2.44.0</a></p>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>auth:</strong> prioritize first auth header (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/797e3362e222ae14e587a4543b76a54d8992d66c\">797e336</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.43.0</h2>\n<h2>2.43.0 (2026-06-17)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.42.0...v2.43.0\">v2.42.0...v2.43.0</a></p>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">openai's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.46.0 (2026-07-17)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.45.0...v2.46.0\">v2.45.0...v2.46.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong>\n/organization/projects/{project_id}/service_accounts/{service_account_id}/api_keys&quot;\nendpoint (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/5a0094194eac9c605c8ca84d47d1c5518f8e2131\">5a00941</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> add owner_project_access to APIKeyListParams\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/f589d04bf9f377ecb1f54335ab3ab9d825b5dfee\">f589d04</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> manual updates (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/980f176e83ee5d991bf9e8e4def80d9905ade5ec\">980f176</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> manual updates (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/2eae984315580cdbf9ceb14d6cb568c581baa768\">2eae984</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> preserve generated type compatibility (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/00bd72adbe03f4b5c4b89d91b8d317f11b58bbdf\">00bd72a</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> remove beta annotation compatibility aliases\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/99dbd15ff3ad1628b94a729a6b688212d4655908\">99dbd15</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.45.0 (2026-07-09)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.44.0...v2.45.0\">v2.44.0...v2.45.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> gpt-5.6-sol updates (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/039d1feb264a2dca7195ba5028e9fb47a5e04987\">039d1fe</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> restore beta resource accessors (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/2dfc130b8f0fdb0049e075aac21aaef29482b4e3\">2dfc130</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Chores</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>retrigger release automation (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/7b61351b014bb6ca4623ff6cce7f32f45038a92e\">7b61351</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.44.0 (2026-06-24)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.43.0...v2.44.0\">v2.43.0...v2.44.0</a></p>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>auth:</strong> prioritize first auth header (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/797e3362e222ae14e587a4543b76a54d8992d66c\">797e336</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.43.0 (2026-06-17)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.42.0...v2.43.0\">v2.42.0...v2.43.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> update OpenAPI spec or Stainless config (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/22542358490ef8f31f0d373e17f7b791b3d983ca\">2254235</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/0e6adb15adc1e74087bcb402de7a75e4fbc0aecb\"><code>0e6adb1</code></a>\nrelease: 2.46.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3501\">#3501</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/f16fbbd2bd25dc1ff150b5f78dbd15ff6bab6d91\"><code>f16fbbd</code></a>\nrelease: 2.45.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3478\">#3478</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/6d9262d5c666a1e4d47f63178db907ba3087ac5d\"><code>6d9262d</code></a>\nrelease: 2.44.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/d35627525e192b7a65b556d8a79d22079ccabdf6\"><code>d356275</code></a>\n[codex] Add AWS Bedrock provider authentication (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3398\">#3398</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/f47f9a270861ca6a6096e8ea15ef8f3e1fb089b0\"><code>f47f9a2</code></a>\nfix(auth): prioritize first auth header</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/e20b6b82c145091f0d8412a7e4a9bc5900a40462\"><code>e20b6b8</code></a>\nrelease: 2.43.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/4d354538e8c2618e228c80f1fdc332ee1f70d1f2\"><code>4d35453</code></a>\nfeat(api): update OpenAPI spec or Stainless config</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/2bba15e71817a75e9b8517e09cb244bc144b50d0\"><code>2bba15e</code></a>\nrelease: 2.42.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/1ec3e8298982d900d31b486177b5d4cecadcf035\"><code>1ec3e82</code></a>\ncodegen metadata</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/93c2eca17d2d484b95245c849b39f51c6d291478\"><code>93c2eca</code></a>\nfeat(api): manual updates</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.41.1...v2.46.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `mcp` from 1.27.2 to 1.28.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/releases\">mcp's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.28.0</h2>\n<h2>Deprecations</h2>\n<p>Two API surfaces now emit <code>DeprecationWarning</code> ahead of\ntheir removal in v2. Nothing is removed in 1.x, and the warnings fire\nonly when the deprecated API is <em>called</em> - importing the modules\nstays silent.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>WebSocket transport</strong> -\n<code>mcp.client.websocket.websocket_client</code> and\n<code>mcp.server.websocket.websocket_server</code><code>modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk#1783</code></li>\n<li><strong>Experimental tasks API</strong> -\n<code>ClientSession.experimental</code>,\n<code>Server.experimental</code>,\n<code>ServerSession.experimental</code>, and the\n<code>experimental_task_handlers=</code> kwarg on\n<code>ClientSession</code>. Tasks (SEP-1686) were removed from the MCP\nspecification and are expected to return as a separate MCP\nextension.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If your test suite runs with <code>filterwarnings =\n[&quot;error&quot;]</code> and exercises these paths, add a scoped\nignore such as <code>ignore:The experimental tasks API is\ndeprecated:DeprecationWarning</code> or <code>ignore:The WebSocket .*\ntransport is deprecated:DeprecationWarning</code>.</p>\n<p>See <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/issues/2828\">#2828</a>\nfor full details.</p>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[v1.x] Support Python 3.14 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/maxisbey\"><code>@​maxisbey</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/2769\">modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk#2769</a></li>\n<li>fix: omit null optional fields from task result payloads by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/liuzemei\"><code>@​liuzemei</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/2809\">modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk#2809</a></li>\n<li>[v1.x] Deprecate the WebSocket transport and the experimental tasks\nentry points by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/maxisbey\"><code>@​maxisbey</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/2828\">modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk#2828</a></li>\n<li>[v1.x] Add a v2 status banner to the README by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/maxisbey\"><code>@​maxisbey</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/2835\">modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk#2835</a></li>\n<li>[v1.x] Deflake the child process cleanup tests by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/maxisbey\"><code>@​maxisbey</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/2839\">modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk#2839</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/liuzemei\"><code>@​liuzemei</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/2809\">modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk#2809</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/compare/v1.27.2...v1.28.0\">https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/compare/v1.27.2...v1.28.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/777b8d06710c140e3606b0d4598e2aa48546c266\"><code>777b8d0</code></a>\n[v1.x] Support TransportSecuritySettings in the WebSocket server\ntransport (#...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/47204674fb26185c2cf45f065831f27b8e5d5c65\"><code>4720467</code></a>\n[v1.x] Set Development Status classifier to Production/Stable (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/issues/2976\">#2976</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/6df3d734265eb49bf758a5e5eb420937337184e9\"><code>6df3d73</code></a>\n[v1.x] Buffer per-request StreamableHTTP streams; store priming event\nbefore ...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/32d32908feb7b15eddeb46872774bf95869cc5f0\"><code>32d3290</code></a>\n[v1.x] Pass a list to parametrize in test_docs_examples (pytest 9.1.0\ncompat)...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/0dca751056dc87d04893d53af129fd00b56a18da\"><code>0dca751</code></a>\n[v1.x] Deflake the child process cleanup tests (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/issues/2839\">#2839</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/52258a95645c66fccbe925289c3382712b9bc68a\"><code>52258a9</code></a>\n[v1.x] Add a v2 status banner to the README (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/issues/2835\">#2835</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/b8f491724c45dbf89d6569364b58d6e8d25d7e42\"><code>b8f4917</code></a>\n[v1.x] Deprecate the WebSocket transport and the experimental tasks\nentry poi...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/2309e5ef974062748e0268c396eba73cfdb6f5e3\"><code>2309e5e</code></a>\nfix: omit null optional fields from task result payloads (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/issues/2809\">#2809</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/494eb11d36b4238226cc0551da6015e1c73f7f3b\"><code>494eb11</code></a>\n[v1.x] Support Python 3.14 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/issues/2769\">#2769</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/compare/v1.27.2...v1.28.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `croniter` from 6.2.2 to 6.2.4\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/releases\">croniter's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>6.2.4</h2>\n<h2>croniter 6.2.4</h2>\n<h3>Bugfixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix <code>expand_from_start_time</code> day-of-week low bound so\nSunday wraps correctly for stepped day-of-week ranges\n(<code>isoweekday() % 7</code> instead of <code>weekday() + 1</code>).\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/239\">#239</a>,\nthanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alhudz\"><code>@​alhudz</code></a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Packaging</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Bump pinned GitHub Actions via dependabot. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/238\">#238</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/240\">#240</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Install:</strong> <code>pip install croniter==6.2.4</code> ·\n<a href=\"https://pypi.org/project/croniter/6.2.4/\">PyPI</a></p>\n<h2>6.2.3</h2>\n<p>No release notes provided.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">croniter's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>6.2.4 (2026-07-10)</h2>\n<p>Bugfixes</p>\n<pre><code>- Fix ``expand_from_start_time`` day-of-week low bound so\nSunday wraps correctly for stepped day-of-week ranges (``isoweekday() %\n7`` instead of ``weekday() + 1``). [44e3090,\n[#239](https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/239), @alhudz]\n<p>Packaging\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bump pinned GitHub Actions via dependabot. [fd13d2e, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/240\">#240</a>;\n5cd2e46, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/238\">#238</a>]</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>6.2.3 (2026-07-02)</h2>\n<p>Features and Improvements</p>\n<pre><code>- Fix quadratic expansion of comma-separated range lists for\na large speed-up on expressions with many ranges. [1d79fc6,\n[#231](https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/231), @alhudz]\n<p>Bugfixes</p>\n<pre><code>- Reject a zero step (e.g. ``5-5/0``) in equal and reversed\ncron ranges instead of silently accepting it. [ab27767,\n[#232](https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/232), @alhudz]\n- Fix ``expand_from_start_time`` month low-bound off-by-one so stepped\nmonth ranges start on the correct month. [f329964,\n[#235](https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/235), @alhudz]\n\nPackaging\n</code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix zizmor-reported security findings in GitHub Actions workflows.\n[ed19f94, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/230\">#230</a>]</li>\n<li>Bump pinned build and CI dependencies via dependabot.</li>\n<li>Upgrade locked development and build dependencies (<code>uv lock\n--upgrade</code>).\n</code></pre></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/58534997eb4634344f00d407fb199d4d1bd057e7\"><code>5853499</code></a>\nPrepare for release 6.2.4 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/241\">#241</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/fd13d2ec447efd854806638cb5f71a2a3a90a0b5\"><code>fd13d2e</code></a>\nBump the github-actions group with 2 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/240\">#240</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/44e3090ae47ccf72e4027ed6fabf6a31eca42f85\"><code>44e3090</code></a>\nwrap sunday in expand_from_start_time day-of-week low bound (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/239\">#239</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/5cd2e4611e8ebea446a9d0edef3f9d8e1f30c0e3\"><code>5cd2e46</code></a>\nBump the github-actions group with 2 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/238\">#238</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/f1eeddd7b9057b66406d162d04879258b29601d5\"><code>f1eeddd</code></a>\nPrepare for 6.2.4 development (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/237\">#237</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/22b59e05f5ca485c45596b2a9b580fddffbf753f\"><code>22b59e0</code></a>\nPrepare for release 6.2.3 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/236\">#236</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/ab277671adc8e446e8dc7f1e939eabf024b6199e\"><code>ab27767</code></a>\nreject zero step in equal and reversed cron ranges (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/232\">#232</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/f329964223eeb29e7788b1a9d615b525148fec96\"><code>f329964</code></a>\nfix expand_from_start_time month low bound off-by-one (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/235\">#235</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/9810279c20030954e2f1ed2cf5f1d34b98c6b07f\"><code>9810279</code></a>\nBump the github-actions group with 2 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/233\">#233</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/d051aaf6342fbe9c559b9fcd99e6fb6f3bb63cb7\"><code>d051aaf</code></a>\nBump hatchling from 1.29.0 to 1.30.1 in the pip-dependencies group (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/234\">#234</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/compare/6.2.2...6.2.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `ddtrace` from 4.10.6 to 4.11.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</s...\n\n_Description has been truncated_\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T09:14:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/dde9cac57aa26eec49fd95410a5bedcf0ffef435","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/dde9cac57aa26eec49fd95410a5bedcf0ffef435","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/dde9cac57aa26eec49fd95410a5bedcf0ffef435/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dce9e5922119ea7d6ebdd0812ee5cc88b9f944ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/dce9e5922119ea7d6ebdd0812ee5cc88b9f944ac","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/dce9e5922119ea7d6ebdd0812ee5cc88b9f944ac"}]},{"sha":"dce9e5922119ea7d6ebdd0812ee5cc88b9f944ac","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGRjZTllNTkyMjExOWVhN2Q2ZWJkZDA4MTJlZTVjYzg4YjlmOTQ0YWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-21T08:28:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T08:28:51Z"},"message":"feat(skills-inbox): scan findings on the card + truncated page flag (Phase B backend) (#587)\n\n## Summary\n\nBackend half of the Skills Inbox Phase B polish (pairs with an\nenterprise dashboard PR). Two **additive** list-contract changes:\n\n- **`sentinel_scan.findings`** — up to 20 well-formed `{code, severity,\nmessage, fatal, locator?}` entries mapped from `data.scan.findings`, so\nthe UI can show *why* a scan tripped (and disable Approve with a reason\nwhen `critical_count > 0`). Malformed entries are skipped without\nconsuming a capped slot; the full list stays on the doc.\n- **`truncated`** top-level response flag — `true` when more staged\ncards exist than the page returned (effective limit `min(limit,\ninbox_max_pending, 200)` cut the list, or the oversample window\nsaturated). Without it, a page of exactly N items is indistinguishable\nfrom a capped one, so no client-side \"showing first N\" heuristic can be\naccurate.\n\nBoth changes are backward-compatible (new fields only); the dashboard\nfeature-detects them, so deploy order doesn't matter.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Golden Forge-card contract updated (finding entry now rides the golden\ndoc's `warn: 1`).\n- New: findings cap at 20 with malformed-entry skip (the test caught a\nslice-before-filter bug where junk consumed a slot — fixed), legacy scan\nblocks without a `findings` key, and `truncated` across cap-cut /\noversample-saturated / partial-page cases.\n- 60 route tests green; ruff + format clean; CI-invocation mypy clean\nfor the touched file.\n- `docs/skills-inbox-api.md` updated (response example + field notes).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7da1494f0c7775611b7a4d51b6f48d8b8756e752","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/7da1494f0c7775611b7a4d51b6f48d8b8756e752"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/dce9e5922119ea7d6ebdd0812ee5cc88b9f944ac","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXy3DCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjBgQAGlJXvqRm9jL9BcvYxcLOHSN\noFdBeXhsxW+A6m0NQMn96OzyDKcvAIJRcc6vfAc94HfeUdIJoUDZI4A1PEyZcEQH\ny7ir8K2qqsp9lvwkrtg992QuZt4QXd9AO4n8DjLp1R3gW+CTzpHJpc7DIDmVtpPV\nVa7v7Ec0h6UCLwrxX5VI/6Mh0rPRTIiM2M6dHI3K9pCqGzw8M4O5+NHrKQgNd/Kj\n5W2hF/pB/uNopIYori0KSfZGNkgGygaF+J38nJvjIJPGDawTYa4Xv/ikQ+KEusYa\nMZjuob+D/8GET6QqtJGJspeqhYnp1y95i4ZVAnqjGEb0jdsbwLmMODflFCIjAD4n\nwHSpL6QIP6ZpAQ9AWor5vnUAoiUBzc/L802U7u25BRt+8ZrooqqygLflbgeQVomH\nh3t/RU3771EebMildXGy5T52wBAe+lShUVk4HB3tGhfOgLy7TWd/XqF2YPqCk1C6\nNAQ5604iUjkNMx2Nk3lNIR6MR9VZPA0L7mKMkXNSt0tYRa23L2Sa8JPj49K6LrxC\nMDjqjaHqVjkVTi8ye8HmhbTuYTpGBFF3WXDIeEyR+i7b15zZ3tEqNhzEU3JHXC54\n2Jipg3RzAfj4hOzrVVDuBaD2XAIsupUAJD1XtNIM5oozFhWTpkrljaSS3C4WBt28\nPJF2m2DbeAS0b8tY6m7B\n=NyTY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7da1494f0c7775611b7a4d51b6f48d8b8756e752\nparent 49ccc1170cfd06c576d4eea04e8e5f8868a699c8\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1784622531 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784622531 +0300\n\nfeat(skills-inbox): scan findings on the card + truncated page flag (Phase B backend) (#587)\n\n## Summary\n\nBackend half of the Skills Inbox Phase B polish (pairs with an\nenterprise dashboard PR). Two **additive** list-contract changes:\n\n- **`sentinel_scan.findings`** — up to 20 well-formed `{code, severity,\nmessage, fatal, locator?}` entries mapped from `data.scan.findings`, so\nthe UI can show *why* a scan tripped (and disable Approve with a reason\nwhen `critical_count > 0`). Malformed entries are skipped without\nconsuming a capped slot; the full list stays on the doc.\n- **`truncated`** top-level response flag — `true` when more staged\ncards exist than the page returned (effective limit `min(limit,\ninbox_max_pending, 200)` cut the list, or the oversample window\nsaturated). Without it, a page of exactly N items is indistinguishable\nfrom a capped one, so no client-side \"showing first N\" heuristic can be\naccurate.\n\nBoth changes are backward-compatible (new fields only); the dashboard\nfeature-detects them, so deploy order doesn't matter.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Golden Forge-card contract updated (finding entry now rides the golden\ndoc's `warn: 1`).\n- New: findings cap at 20 with malformed-entry skip (the test caught a\nslice-before-filter bug where junk consumed a slot — fixed), legacy scan\nblocks without a `findings` key, and `truncated` across cap-cut /\noversample-saturated / partial-page cases.\n- 60 route tests green; ruff + format clean; CI-invocation mypy clean\nfor the touched file.\n- `docs/skills-inbox-api.md` updated (response example + field notes).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T08:28:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/dce9e5922119ea7d6ebdd0812ee5cc88b9f944ac","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/dce9e5922119ea7d6ebdd0812ee5cc88b9f944ac","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/dce9e5922119ea7d6ebdd0812ee5cc88b9f944ac/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"49ccc1170cfd06c576d4eea04e8e5f8868a699c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/49ccc1170cfd06c576d4eea04e8e5f8868a699c8","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/49ccc1170cfd06c576d4eea04e8e5f8868a699c8"}]},{"sha":"49ccc1170cfd06c576d4eea04e8e5f8868a699c8","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDQ5Y2NjMTE3MGNmZDA2YzU3NmQ0ZWVhMDRlOGU1Zjg4NjhhNjk5Yzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-21T07:51:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-21T07:51:57Z"},"message":"deps: group Dependabot minor/patch bumps per ecosystem (#588)\n\n## What\n\nAdds `groups:` to every ecosystem in `.github/dependabot.yml` so weekly\n**minor/patch** bumps collapse into a **single grouped PR per\necosystem** instead of one PR per package.\n\n- **Majors stay individual** → dedicated review (e.g. a `typescript` 5→7\njump still gets its own PR).\n- **GitHub Actions** bumps are grouped together (`patterns: [\"*\"]`) —\nlow-risk.\n- Mirrors the grouping strategy already used in\n`caura-memclaw-enterprise`.\n\n## Why\n\nWe currently have **31 open individual Dependabot PRs** — a flood that's\nimpractical to review/merge, especially under strict branch protection.\nGrouping collapses future weekly runs into ~a handful of PRs.\n\nThis only changes *future* Dependabot behavior; it does not touch any\ndependency versions. Existing open PRs are unaffected until Dependabot\nnext reconciles them (a `@dependabot recreate` on the open ones will\nregroup them).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"57e0f7d473e501dfa053e7083dbcc37566051520","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/57e0f7d473e501dfa053e7083dbcc37566051520"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/49ccc1170cfd06c576d4eea04e8e5f8868a699c8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXyUdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9MIQABNMt7v0pn6inxZ4VKc2ECTK\nWWQmL2sBIZcDZAuuehMhCl+UQsC/XFglzi/dys+FQvZuiuVCHH49vJhMT1Wfx7pr\nmntJs+nkPRFJlUDkQLFymeeCLgRcNihnSo54OFjODAJ0sjJUYBTgGUjQWn36IitY\nnXe+ueYI6GTrdBKfINjg7MGiL4TI1Ce5gZX5byydRjNcRQS7AeKmMzFgZFJdbXjM\nzmnEeZktrQ35nWSYp4EKNHNHS4zudSQxfDIB6UNU7AlYHM+EebP04/+7aBa/76Jh\nLYyvs/atX6L8HMZWhsuRB+hIhGASy8Sys0hTgwLibagoXJ9NXZBninCj6DfC+FiE\nvkOJsMgbFw4SFAe5Dd73gRo8i/8GoQC7L+Jbx48J8db2dQVlt01CPiAcsAhO1v5N\nJQXGua8iWNw01m+aZbSu1aaieipSE2D54Ftq5IvGxbbvhVoethbnWFyN5vG//Jsu\nKHUmfm/KIoCLUF5SsJXinLwXsKQ4+TUkSAECtNqYrQ3BiopLVsQHsbPxjDqYWQzp\nQRMDcLoU5b5oExrHWPY5GMTi7ih7T+lBwpUYOrp19ZjQ1gI3QBQbccaVXTz7xKoj\nLF39v9J07oK3IVUSoQ8RJnt9JtLMRkL97BxnvQ6PHbH2KUtnjVF4wukxwukonAG4\n+PZ9yWfXlRUpJB9tXCbX\n=2G/q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 57e0f7d473e501dfa053e7083dbcc37566051520\nparent a4edb4e4f3ad7f0c2755c0cdbfcac0787d99c967\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1784620317 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784620317 +0300\n\ndeps: group Dependabot minor/patch bumps per ecosystem (#588)\n\n## What\n\nAdds `groups:` to every ecosystem in `.github/dependabot.yml` so weekly\n**minor/patch** bumps collapse into a **single grouped PR per\necosystem** instead of one PR per package.\n\n- **Majors stay individual** → dedicated review (e.g. a `typescript` 5→7\njump still gets its own PR).\n- **GitHub Actions** bumps are grouped together (`patterns: [\"*\"]`) —\nlow-risk.\n- Mirrors the grouping strategy already used in\n`caura-memclaw-enterprise`.\n\n## Why\n\nWe currently have **31 open individual Dependabot PRs** — a flood that's\nimpractical to review/merge, especially under strict branch protection.\nGrouping collapses future weekly runs into ~a handful of PRs.\n\nThis only changes *future* Dependabot behavior; it does not touch any\ndependency versions. Existing open PRs are unaffected until Dependabot\nnext reconciles them (a `@dependabot recreate` on the open ones will\nregroup them).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-21T07:51:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/49ccc1170cfd06c576d4eea04e8e5f8868a699c8","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/49ccc1170cfd06c576d4eea04e8e5f8868a699c8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/49ccc1170cfd06c576d4eea04e8e5f8868a699c8/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type