ra-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/572))\n([740505d](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/740505da50aa6bdc2916a1ca7aecb0a993855718))\n</details>\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with [Release\nPlease](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please). See\n[documentation](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please#release-please).\n\nSigned-off-by: release-please[bot] <release-please[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: caura-deploy-bot[bot] <265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-20T18:25:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7d69fbf4651d1f30a15281291ae015cd213819be","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/7d69fbf4651d1f30a15281291ae015cd213819be","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/7d69fbf4651d1f30a15281291ae015cd213819be/comments","author":{"login":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","id":265395343,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOD9Gcjw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229147182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/caura-deploy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bef753ccbd9f2071f52e5fd0af9613c10f54a5ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bef753ccbd9f2071f52e5fd0af9613c10f54a5ca","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/bef753ccbd9f2071f52e5fd0af9613c10f54a5ca"}]},{"sha":"bef753ccbd9f2071f52e5fd0af9613c10f54a5ca","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGJlZjc1M2NjYmQ5ZjIwNzFmNTJlNWZkMGFmOTYxM2MxMGY1NGE1Y2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-20T14:02:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-20T14:02:43Z"},"message":"feat(client): memclaw-interviewer — Claude Code disk-parser adapter (Interviewer Phase 2) (#581)\n\n## Summary\n\nPhase 2 of the Interviewer (client-priority roadmap: OpenClaw ✅\n#558/#564/#572 → **Claude Code/CLI** → Hermes): a new\n`memclaw-interviewer` console command in `memclaw-client` (0.2.0) for\nClaude Code workstations. It reads Claude Code session transcripts\n(`~/.claude/projects/*/*.jsonl`) **read-only** — Claude Code owns the\ntrail; we never modify it — and submits event windows to the existing\n`POST /api/v1/interview/submit`. **Zero server changes.**\n\n### Protocol\n- **Cursor = the server's forward-only watermark doc**\n(`interview_watermarks`), read back via the documents GET — **no local\nstate**. Crash-safety inherited from Phase 1: watermark advances only on\ncommit; deterministic attempt ids dedup retries; never a gap, never a\nduplicate.\n- **Per-file cursors, seq = raw line index.** Verified on real disk: one\n`.jsonl` can interleave MULTIPLE `sessionId`s (session resume appends to\nthe original file), so per-session cursors would fragment; line index\nstays monotonic under append-only writes. Session identity travels per\nevent (`session_id = \"<project>:<sessionId>\"`).\n- **Advance-past-noise-tail:** the final window's `cursor_to` reaches\nEOF even when the tail is filtered noise (legal — server validation only\nrequires `seqs[-1] <= cursor_to`), enabling the cheap next-run skip.\nTorn/mid-append tails are left for the next run; a shrunken file\n(append-only violated) is skipped loudly.\n\n### Parser (v1, pilot-proven signal)\nEmits real user prompts + assistant text; drops tool results\n(`type:\"user\"` lines with `tool_result` blocks / `toolUseResult`),\nmeta/compaction lines\n(`isMeta`/`isCompactSummary`/`isVisibleInTranscriptOnly`),\nthinking/`tool_use` blocks, timestamp-less metadata line types, and\nsubagent files. Local credential scrub\n(sk-/mc_/ghp_/xox/AWS/PEM/Bearer/JWT) before anything leaves the\nmachine; the server masks PII again on receipt.\n\n### Privacy: default-deny\nNo allowlist → the CLI lists discovered project dirs and exits 2 with\nguidance. `--projects <globs>` / `MEMCLAW_INTERVIEWER_PROJECTS` opt in\nper project; `--all-projects` is the explicit full opt-in. Hook mode\nsilently ignores non-allowlisted transcripts.\n\n### CLI\n- `run` — cron-able; window caps 400 events / 150k chars (sized to the\nserver's 90s synchronous interview budget: the real-LLM pilot measured\n~63s at ~200k chars); dribble gate (`--flush` to override); `--dry-run`\nis fully offline.\n- `status` — per-file server cursor vs local line count.\n- `hook` — Claude Code **SessionEnd** hook: drains that session's\ntranscript; **always exits 0** (a memory-harvest failure must never fail\na session).\n\n## Test plan\n- **40 unit tests**: parser quirks from the on-disk survey\n(multi-session files, tool_result-user lines, meta/compaction,\ntimestamp-less metadata, torn tails, block mixes, scrub), window\nmechanics (cap splits, EOF-past-noise, contiguity, sparse-seq validity),\nand a runner suite against a fake server that re-implements the server's\nseq-validation rules across 200/207/403/422/500/504 (watermark resume,\nsingle 504 dedup-safe retry, 403 abort, per-file isolation, budget caps,\nshrink guard).\n- **Real-disk dry-run** on actual transcripts from this machine:\n7,925-line file → 3 contiguous windows at ~150k chars, 1,004 events,\n**zero tool_result/meta leakage, zero unredacted credentials**.\n- **Live dogfood** against the released `:latest` images: submit →\n`committed`, watermark == EOF, memories carry `source=interviewer` +\n`node_id=cc:<machine>:<file>`; rerun → cheap \"no new lines\" skip; live\nSessionEnd hook drained a second transcript end-to-end (exit 0).\n\nPyPI publish (tag `memclaw-client-v0.2.0`) deferred until after merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"338b34da0f41a6a608eb2c115cf27835e8151c36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/338b34da0f41a6a608eb2c115cf27835e8151c36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/bef753ccbd9f2071f52e5fd0af9613c10f54a5ca","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXiqDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyacQAAKfV7DZBr9ernYoxRA9wvSR\nnB6cQEJ33D0I9JYKLOC4a6UaklPptDW1SKRcKD8ia7Sk9AhKk2vQwEA1jlxguTgB\nf05CDZ9T4LWeAiPDFi1Dut3Y+XSweWlv9KCZfeWSsF1jkyEvp2O2fZPSk2IGXunN\nrjkMhToW+EClo/CwRvzx9tV7SzSbWo+d/Kd0G5pabyCMjXYHqQRBOPeVc9A+9hv1\n1T01n4Qim5UsbrfFpEAT1P6TClS2pvYWovoq7qeSU16iX8PAE1YoEtpUZR3Cwfmo\n9tQcU/sfCpqszTiYFl0XiSv+su0wHhmHsqZMj2wgW1AOy9AsmXIbfqFuzTMc80S5\nDRrLAvXis8cJgnc+eLJWZTQSuLcFLLroVQO8ikvPEZWxXtSj45AjpZCruRoP7RTD\nox6BQmI3gBsicgvrPcuTsfCdA25rahTMGeFDnPqFMC1y/fyQ1uov+ePKlt/TiFCK\nw3aMKsdjyLp5BHutpivN8LiRxCVEtz/xIi5XiHB/LWZdVAGl4dpsX+cCPRbtiYsK\n06iFANZ7gOdUSfZsZR00/YBtCzI3z4d/EMPrAox/slp01wE1Y/3S2eeRTapYY2kq\nKqlDFAGXpE63azxX76LpiFDUfDJZ82+Tk5k2j2y74z5X8/F2wnCYqekDylVfD0Mo\npPeoi3Om9MKw98OHxuJd\n=HJal\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 338b34da0f41a6a608eb2c115cf27835e8151c36\nparent 30d9bc9fd365c7dba93183b2d1fe386a9da8ceb4\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1784556163 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784556163 +0300\n\nfeat(client): memclaw-interviewer — Claude Code disk-parser adapter (Interviewer Phase 2) (#581)\n\n## Summary\n\nPhase 2 of the Interviewer (client-priority roadmap: OpenClaw ✅\n#558/#564/#572 → **Claude Code/CLI** → Hermes): a new\n`memclaw-interviewer` console command in `memclaw-client` (0.2.0) for\nClaude Code workstations. It reads Claude Code session transcripts\n(`~/.claude/projects/*/*.jsonl`) **read-only** — Claude Code owns the\ntrail; we never modify it — and submits event windows to the existing\n`POST /api/v1/interview/submit`. **Zero server changes.**\n\n### Protocol\n- **Cursor = the server's forward-only watermark doc**\n(`interview_watermarks`), read back via the documents GET — **no local\nstate**. Crash-safety inherited from Phase 1: watermark advances only on\ncommit; deterministic attempt ids dedup retries; never a gap, never a\nduplicate.\n- **Per-file cursors, seq = raw line index.** Verified on real disk: one\n`.jsonl` can interleave MULTIPLE `sessionId`s (session resume appends to\nthe original file), so per-session cursors would fragment; line index\nstays monotonic under append-only writes. Session identity travels per\nevent (`session_id = \"<project>:<sessionId>\"`).\n- **Advance-past-noise-tail:** the final window's `cursor_to` reaches\nEOF even when the tail is filtered noise (legal — server validation only\nrequires `seqs[-1] <= cursor_to`), enabling the cheap next-run skip.\nTorn/mid-append tails are left for the next run; a shrunken file\n(append-only violated) is skipped loudly.\n\n### Parser (v1, pilot-proven signal)\nEmits real user prompts + assistant text; drops tool results\n(`type:\"user\"` lines with `tool_result` blocks / `toolUseResult`),\nmeta/compaction lines\n(`isMeta`/`isCompactSummary`/`isVisibleInTranscriptOnly`),\nthinking/`tool_use` blocks, timestamp-less metadata line types, and\nsubagent files. Local credential scrub\n(sk-/mc_/ghp_/xox/AWS/PEM/Bearer/JWT) before anything leaves the\nmachine; the server masks PII again on receipt.\n\n### Privacy: default-deny\nNo allowlist → the CLI lists discovered project dirs and exits 2 with\nguidance. `--projects <globs>` / `MEMCLAW_INTERVIEWER_PROJECTS` opt in\nper project; `--all-projects` is the explicit full opt-in. Hook mode\nsilently ignores non-allowlisted transcripts.\n\n### CLI\n- `run` — cron-able; window caps 400 events / 150k chars (sized to the\nserver's 90s synchronous interview budget: the real-LLM pilot measured\n~63s at ~200k chars); dribble gate (`--flush` to override); `--dry-run`\nis fully offline.\n- `status` — per-file server cursor vs local line count.\n- `hook` — Claude Code **SessionEnd** hook: drains that session's\ntranscript; **always exits 0** (a memory-harvest failure must never fail\na session).\n\n## Test plan\n- **40 unit tests**: parser quirks from the on-disk survey\n(multi-session files, tool_result-user lines, meta/compaction,\ntimestamp-less metadata, torn tails, block mixes, scrub), window\nmechanics (cap splits, EOF-past-noise, contiguity, sparse-seq validity),\nand a runner suite against a fake server that re-implements the server's\nseq-validation rules across 200/207/403/422/500/504 (watermark resume,\nsingle 504 dedup-safe retry, 403 abort, per-file isolation, budget caps,\nshrink guard).\n- **Real-disk dry-run** on actual transcripts from this machine:\n7,925-line file → 3 contiguous windows at ~150k chars, 1,004 events,\n**zero tool_result/meta leakage, zero unredacted credentials**.\n- **Live dogfood** against the released `:latest` images: submit →\n`committed`, watermark == EOF, memories carry `source=interviewer` +\n`node_id=cc:<machine>:<file>`; rerun → cheap \"no new lines\" skip; live\nSessionEnd hook drained a second transcript end-to-end (exit 0).\n\nPyPI publish (tag `memclaw-client-v0.2.0`) deferred until after merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-20T14:02:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bef753ccbd9f2071f52e5fd0af9613c10f54a5ca","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/bef753ccbd9f2071f52e5fd0af9613c10f54a5ca","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bef753ccbd9f2071f52e5fd0af9613c10f54a5ca/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"30d9bc9fd365c7dba93183b2d1fe386a9da8ceb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/30d9bc9fd365c7dba93183b2d1fe386a9da8ceb4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/30d9bc9fd365c7dba93183b2d1fe386a9da8ceb4"}]},{"sha":"30d9bc9fd365c7dba93183b2d1fe386a9da8ceb4","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDMwZDliYzlmZDM2NWM3ZGJhOTMxODNiMmQxZmUzODZhOWRhOGNlYjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Abhinav Jain","email":"abhinav.ajay03@gmail.com","date":"2026-07-20T12:31:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-20T12:31:54Z"},"message":"docs: fix agent install reference (#542)\n\nCloses #513\n\n## Summary\n- replace the dead ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW.md reference in AGENT-INSTALL.md\nwith existing README anchors\n- add a stable README project-structure anchor for the docs link target\n- remove the stale ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW.md mention from the PR template\n\n## Verification\n- git grep -n \"ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW\" returned no matches\n- git grep -n \"project-structure\" -- AGENT-INSTALL.md README.md\n- git diff --check\n\nSigned-off-by: Abhinav <avhinav.yt@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"a9f0719eeadffdd88545098b50a1d950064e77bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/a9f0719eeadffdd88545098b50a1d950064e77bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/30d9bc9fd365c7dba93183b2d1fe386a9da8ceb4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXhU6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwk4QAGL7Z+gp1/KtlzCj9XPUExoH\nx7lcPbF3NSH+CDeHYK7B3KAYTHKyp6Pq8BS0AIQppe0d3x1mYLjuhOAjjneVlijz\n9cIEwSf1/XA0CSqhDhKMcdxiaT6kFCu4ZMlLVlafliR5OOV0WkOl1V+5+q5JBvu2\nsLpfY0R0UKX+HlATeOs0B8lSBtuiLMbvBsP0DPZtbXWmwf31pn74ld0KgjHbJkm0\nUsNgj+9SmaNPvRE92Cvq6bEGXKyzVdfLdPxwLJFEfcd43P0gH9V2XgbB3N3G/ip1\np/OPLvYoKYytIX9lJ2p7Qj+qUxdDl3fHoGaBIoUVlOh/97yFNZQoBpUcFI8Zgnbi\nn6/v+h42mmjrJGZpEO2mSoLyG+wQbVi0CMlSZcO5m9HAZIUcn/IunKNi9APEREDe\n37FXevtAaI8Hd+n7qXkZA9uOJAIMbthWT6vSyAdjv9h8zmqHveP89ZVF/vTnjtZR\nugV1eSFqiRM5PdrOYY6v244JDjmI+a4zfetEduvcMVUCttBTPmhPjGFhS0IvQMML\noxvoNkwr7uuEAEx/0E/rLRqDJl6XGpsavsJIGQVXff9nzckCyFUTQKg8ZG6IY4Vb\n2CKeOmULd6OQXkx5CR+U7ClW7cEqm+Qk9a/SotefAmKEx3InEs62daWAUfNyU/D4\n3wQPGgMuDFeVKx1WC89a\n=60jr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a9f0719eeadffdd88545098b50a1d950064e77bb\nparent 13a256cecce7bdb55bf70501596914dd07a6abc4\nauthor Abhinav Jain <abhinav.ajay03@gmail.com> 1784550714 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784550714 +0300\n\ndocs: fix agent install reference (#542)\n\nCloses #513\n\n## Summary\n- replace the dead ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW.md reference in AGENT-INSTALL.md\nwith existing README anchors\n- add a stable README project-structure anchor for the docs link target\n- remove the stale ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW.md mention from the PR template\n\n## Verification\n- git grep -n \"ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW\" returned no matches\n- git grep -n \"project-structure\" -- AGENT-INSTALL.md README.md\n- git diff --check\n\nSigned-off-by: Abhinav <avhinav.yt@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-20T12:31:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/30d9bc9fd365c7dba93183b2d1fe386a9da8ceb4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/30d9bc9fd365c7dba93183b2d1fe386a9da8ceb4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/30d9bc9fd365c7dba93183b2d1fe386a9da8ceb4/comments","author":{"login":"Abhinav-0311","id":177344956,"node_id":"U_kgDOCpIRvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177344956?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhinav-0311","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhinav-0311","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhinav-0311/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhinav-0311/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhinav-0311/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhinav-0311/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhinav-0311/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhinav-0311/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhinav-0311/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhinav-0311/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhinav-0311/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"13a256cecce7bdb55bf70501596914dd07a6abc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/13a256cecce7bdb55bf70501596914dd07a6abc4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/13a256cecce7bdb55bf70501596914dd07a6abc4"}]},{"sha":"13a256cecce7bdb55bf70501596914dd07a6abc4","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDEzYTI1NmNlY2NlN2JkYjU1YmY3MDUwMTU5NjkxNGRkMDdhNmFiYzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Abdullah Shamil Basayev","email":"139082653+sayevvv@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-20T12:28:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-20T12:28:07Z"},"message":"docs: document TESTING=1 env var with production-danger warning (#544)\n\n<!-- Thanks for the contribution! Please fill in this template so we can\nreview quickly. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd a commented-out `TESTING=1` entry to `.env.example` with a clear\nproduction-danger warning. The variable was checked in two places in the\ncodebase but entirely absent from the example config, leaving no hint of\nits existence or risk for anyone bootstrapping from it.\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #511 \n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change that fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change that adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that changes existing behavior)\n- [x] Documentation update\n- [ ] Refactor / internal cleanup\n- [ ] Other:\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n\nDocumentation-only change — no code paths affected. Verified manually:\n1. `TESTING` now appears in `.env.example` (previously absent).\n2. The entry is fully commented out, so copying the file verbatim cannot\n   accidentally activate the test endpoints.\n3. `ruff`, `mypy`, and `pytest` are unaffected (no Python files\nchanged).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have added tests that cover my changes (or explained why none\nare needed)\n- [x] `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass\n- [x] `mypy` passes\n- [x] `pytest` passes locally\n- [ ] I have updated relevant documentation (README,\nARCHITECTURE_REVIEW, etc.)\n- [ ] I have updated `CHANGELOG.md` under the `Unreleased` section (if\nuser-facing)\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n`TESTING=1` registers the `/api/v1/testing/time-warp` router, which can\ndirectly overwrite timestamp columns in the database. It is set\nautomatically by `tests/conftest.py` and `.env.test` — developers\nrunning\n`pytest` or the containerised test stack never need to set it manually.\nThe only scenario requiring a manual set is debugging\ntemporal/crystallizer\nE2E tests against a live local Docker stack.\n\nSigned-off-by: sayevvv <shamilbasayev10@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"6c7731e0098539d89a8bbccfc48b050684444f22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/6c7731e0098539d89a8bbccfc48b050684444f22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/13a256cecce7bdb55bf70501596914dd07a6abc4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXhRXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgpwQAAPPUIeCbbs0QrNJ4A5i3dAZ\nQM8ULa7grZMZ+8NLqXb/0ytPz4cEy6iQw1V8U1xZ1vfBlkBrrBv2oV2hZTVYN8LW\nVFRWVT+MA3JNhL2T/CBo7IMKvXYlliIGJkH075btWI4+J8cGErnzpzcAtJ6ECosv\neEOjlkFar9l5G5+bblrR1NuQSC45cCAbKdKwLEaDB2fxEc5y+5v15XM1iYW2SyTH\nEhcAuWUUq4G9b8K3Z6F8P/SHBSKahNjD0xGCTWDL5hjPcP64fv8C7/Zi1p2WsYAB\n+9Gucy0y9kSQaPQpGTBG1sTV0/f5/tsQy0HtaBW8fQjIKyIFwsEfxaqnnuFbMdJd\nGr0VDPPLDTk1sT9Gv1cYAxWLBr4hPhl109pLcdEudi7EnekJdpa5S/WfmVppU0T1\nhiMOSvdCsI8Y02YpXOlgoDT4EFhmird4iwyHjMl0bftuBmvXHbBsMGg15XekRYqA\nHMQoLANLAe+6Y90rz3bcuchkNP0hP/pWjt66sfZfCT6CYuiyjT1daxwWOJvrcLaC\nWbT5YC5onfBMyusqn3rl2YoLnEJ1AHmxbopjtiacwpON4cMpOmhfeIkjEumo3j7v\nNCngj1Z0QHUzzmPnn7jHODHpRMEYAatoWgdrPDY/xyvfHJOQyod2oDaAtpab0QBw\nSBS2q5/MMCuj3BNkU+5l\n=tkh/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6c7731e0098539d89a8bbccfc48b050684444f22\nparent 5af356e826bdc85633a9fbd23d8adc6b3a5fde54\nauthor Abdullah Shamil Basayev <139082653+sayevvv@users.noreply.github.com> 1784550487 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784550487 +0300\n\ndocs: document TESTING=1 env var with production-danger warning (#544)\n\n<!-- Thanks for the contribution! Please fill in this template so we can\nreview quickly. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd a commented-out `TESTING=1` entry to `.env.example` with a clear\nproduction-danger warning. The variable was checked in two places in the\ncodebase but entirely absent from the example config, leaving no hint of\nits existence or risk for anyone bootstrapping from it.\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #511 \n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change that fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change that adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that changes existing behavior)\n- [x] Documentation update\n- [ ] Refactor / internal cleanup\n- [ ] Other:\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n\nDocumentation-only change — no code paths affected. Verified manually:\n1. `TESTING` now appears in `.env.example` (previously absent).\n2. The entry is fully commented out, so copying the file verbatim cannot\n   accidentally activate the test endpoints.\n3. `ruff`, `mypy`, and `pytest` are unaffected (no Python files\nchanged).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have added tests that cover my changes (or explained why none\nare needed)\n- [x] `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass\n- [x] `mypy` passes\n- [x] `pytest` passes locally\n- [ ] I have updated relevant documentation (README,\nARCHITECTURE_REVIEW, etc.)\n- [ ] I have updated `CHANGELOG.md` under the `Unreleased` section (if\nuser-facing)\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n`TESTING=1` registers the `/api/v1/testing/time-warp` router, which can\ndirectly overwrite timestamp columns in the database. It is set\nautomatically by `tests/conftest.py` and `.env.test` — developers\nrunning\n`pytest` or the containerised test stack never need to set it manually.\nThe only scenario requiring a manual set is debugging\ntemporal/crystallizer\nE2E tests against a live local Docker stack.\n\nSigned-off-by: sayevvv <shamilbasayev10@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-20T12:28:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/13a256cecce7bdb55bf70501596914dd07a6abc4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/13a256cecce7bdb55bf70501596914dd07a6abc4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/13a256cecce7bdb55bf70501596914dd07a6abc4/comments","author":{"login":"sayevvv","id":139082653,"node_id":"U_kgDOCEo7nQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139082653?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayevvv","html_url":"https://github.com/sayevvv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayevvv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayevvv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayevvv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayevvv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayevvv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayevvv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayevvv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayevvv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayevvv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5af356e826bdc85633a9fbd23d8adc6b3a5fde54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5af356e826bdc85633a9fbd23d8adc6b3a5fde54","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5af356e826bdc85633a9fbd23d8adc6b3a5fde54"}]},{"sha":"5af356e826bdc85633a9fbd23d8adc6b3a5fde54","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDVhZjM1NmU4MjZiZGM4NTYzM2E5ZmJkMjNkOGFkYzZiM2E1ZmRlNTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Joseph Yaksich","email":"294273268+gitcommit90@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-20T12:19:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-20T12:19:36Z"},"message":"fix(clients): raise on unexpected search() response shape (#510) (#539)\n\n## Problem\n\nOn HTTP 200, silently returned when the JSON body was not a dict with an\n`items` list (e.g. `{ \"error\": \"quota exceeded\" }`), so callers could\nnot distinguish zero hits from a malformed response.\n\nRefs: caura-ai/caura-memclaw#510\n\n## Proposed change\n\nValidate the search response shape in both Python and TypeScript clients\nand raise `MemClawAPIError` / `MemClawApiError` with status 200 when the\nbody is unexpected.\n\n## Test results\n\n- clients/python: 12 passed\n- clients/typescript: 10 passed\n\nSigned-off-by: Joseph Yaksich <294273268+gitcommit90@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"bc80cea029e1a7571a3d88dc74e1882e0762026a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/bc80cea029e1a7571a3d88dc74e1882e0762026a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/5af356e826bdc85633a9fbd23d8adc6b3a5fde54","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXhJYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlhsQABdQScEcgegyhfSEguDMb31r\nez+2pBGNpmOXdSK0S35+so9wTRDGS693JJ4HyoTJ1I4a5bHBpeiP/69gVLF6He/b\n+NrldsBovAZPDhTaqb0RKIrqlZPZjQ7C5fGzOR5DJ6gWj0Zw22FxirSIrhENyx4H\nMDdPaNJAUHf72mGZf5G58ZMGO/7GEAyLRerFxkLvmElxWZAJw9cIC6rKUuK4iDtk\nO1XCbmRg0o3hcySUXcPnr7JFnw5aGon5WEeVxbjwxvOUQa7Ln4a2DGum6nM2H/5d\nL+lZ5kf0jMv+9imuJq7aaJVzbfSVh44V5qqhVse2YqsfN1t8ayy2TuGxBijwH3cr\nPVgwR/7OEJzVYcrcy67wCDmM6rl3WzNiiuKv62n9MZ0jp6wIUaLL46Jl0dgBrfzw\nn/jl1ablhoGg4NmH36sI4obImese1jJJKBEf0wAHW7+4VeVvTfVIKHdqGE+60dT1\ne0Yw9I/CG+ESAf+jf+iqkiR2pSnhqFW+t3hmOHZhTuHHckhG2Yl8/BT7Fou/ZzzJ\npC2z4e94wY+ULPU+EOyNMJMMpEm+0DBn6txYT5igv0326CB+bDEyOvuLU2C2j7cK\ne0mD2AIDASAz9OHU/eirEl3glN2dbQvSs8BQFHw1BJjvoFgAwhuOTIn7bTMqiafS\nPVOHtdcqd6QQm6N8GgOy\n=lDnQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bc80cea029e1a7571a3d88dc74e1882e0762026a\nparent 9b92e691f7d6b459e21e166bcba6d6fecdd3b609\nauthor Joseph Yaksich <294273268+gitcommit90@users.noreply.github.com> 1784549976 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784549976 +0300\n\nfix(clients): raise on unexpected search() response shape (#510) (#539)\n\n## Problem\n\nOn HTTP 200, silently returned when the JSON body was not a dict with an\n`items` list (e.g. `{ \"error\": \"quota exceeded\" }`), so callers could\nnot distinguish zero hits from a malformed response.\n\nRefs: caura-ai/caura-memclaw#510\n\n## Proposed change\n\nValidate the search response shape in both Python and TypeScript clients\nand raise `MemClawAPIError` / `MemClawApiError` with status 200 when the\nbody is unexpected.\n\n## Test results\n\n- clients/python: 12 passed\n- clients/typescript: 10 passed\n\nSigned-off-by: Joseph Yaksich <294273268+gitcommit90@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-20T12:19:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5af356e826bdc85633a9fbd23d8adc6b3a5fde54","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5af356e826bdc85633a9fbd23d8adc6b3a5fde54","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5af356e826bdc85633a9fbd23d8adc6b3a5fde54/comments","author":{"login":"gitcommit90","id":294273268,"node_id":"U_kgDOEYpA9A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/294273268?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gitcommit90","html_url":"https://github.com/gitcommit90","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gitcommit90/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gitcommit90/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gitcommit90/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gitcommit90/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gitcommit90/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gitcommit90/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gitcommit90/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gitcommit90/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gitcommit90/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9b92e691f7d6b459e21e166bcba6d6fecdd3b609","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9b92e691f7d6b459e21e166bcba6d6fecdd3b609","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9b92e691f7d6b459e21e166bcba6d6fecdd3b609"}]},{"sha":"9b92e691f7d6b459e21e166bcba6d6fecdd3b609","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDliOTJlNjkxZjdkNmI0NTllMjFlMTY2YmNiYTZkNmZlY2RkM2I2MDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-20T12:04:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-20T12:04:42Z"},"message":"ci: fix Claude review retrigger checkout for fork PRs (#585)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe `claude-retrigger` job (fires when someone comments `@claude` on a\nPR) checked out the PR code with `ref: <PR head branch>` against the\n**base** repo. A fork PR's head branch only exists on the contributor's\nfork, not on `caura-ai/caura-memclaw`, so `actions/checkout` couldn't\nresolve it and the job exited 1 — **no review verdict was ever posted**\nfor external fork PRs. It only worked when a fork's head branch happened\nto be named `main` (which exists in the base repo). Tracked as\n`.github#111`.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe shared review script (`.github/scripts/claude_pr_review.sh`) fetches\nthe PR diff via the **GitHub API**, not from the working tree — so this\njob never actually needs the PR's code checked out.\n\n- Check out the **base repo's default branch** (trusted) instead of the\nfork's branch, and drop the now-unused `head_ref` lookup.\n- **Security:** this job runs on `issue_comment`, which — unlike fork\n`pull_request` events — **does** receive repo secrets\n(`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, a write token). Checking out base code (not fork\ncode) ensures a malicious fork PR can't have its code executed with our\nsecrets when an org member triggers a review (a \"pwn request\" avoided).\n\n## Hardening\n\n- Gate the job on `author_association` (`MEMBER`/`OWNER`) at the **job\nlevel**, so the runner never even starts for a non-member's `@claude`\ncomment. The existing step-level org-membership check stays as\ndefense-in-depth (both read the same `author_association` field, so they\ncan't drift).\n\n## Testing\n\n- YAML validated locally.\n- Full end-to-end can only be confirmed after merge, since\n`issue_comment` workflows run from the **default branch** version of the\nworkflow file.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4faf8cccb6ab19dac13069cf5c541fb0af1c5a9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/4faf8cccb6ab19dac13069cf5c541fb0af1c5a9c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/9b92e691f7d6b459e21e166bcba6d6fecdd3b609","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXg7aCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANEsQAGpcogjs21S+7rq5gdzdJL5u\nytMEzxh48oDgs7ARemXVdUnKYRPj1maglvxP4lasAOfY6QySCdHDNZkLBZdV02lT\nRt1CNWGAHrY9kPsYztO/CXblUY4bKL4OdGtcRU/YcGN6nFAc+ablgFOKgFYRDCnt\nQZzcFSlGQktexVf/lEIst/SE3dzQdBTBQ1FX6yWQCGcCLOnp2oTGlY1XRxfrYqGx\nYKTKOyhGTtjthnw2/2njQH6Q+2K7haRJH3+g3+SHDm5UHug14xfpbasimNKwL/9c\n0qJjzQy30J2rC57QEpE2FgNIgcHPXaRpFGOyzX9qsWvTB+XX//8pwtQ4OxFZrq9B\n/++8Son/V00Ld0KbeczQyrDxJ3v5LjG/WhlTK3xoPa1odRqQCE3OAQbrPLEZVdP1\npUUIFbLaOU2vMcvpYOHXHhJRLSXECKVgAQeOb836XC7C7JJ1O/6NUzxzcVjZFZ/M\nSDAvknnx6VcRqMCt42JyKk9pxc4n/lseBlZRULHiuGKLun+PT0175+J8VxOudhJ1\nJhTxhuuFY70SnGuWPYZC1h2aGM86t20b6Wc2mBIBtFiOhePTJ3HspLOG4Q5fmPcb\npTHBfgtO3y6OPaxU+uqH+1vJ0R2HOIHfrA4dhFW9AfJpFYslf+l7X7jARX98epFD\n9kxkDBd22EvA8cjBTIAB\n=AggD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4faf8cccb6ab19dac13069cf5c541fb0af1c5a9c\nparent 5680c7c5fe2d47f58536a42d846b09dc7c749884\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1784549082 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784549082 +0300\n\nci: fix Claude review retrigger checkout for fork PRs (#585)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe `claude-retrigger` job (fires when someone comments `@claude` on a\nPR) checked out the PR code with `ref: <PR head branch>` against the\n**base** repo. A fork PR's head branch only exists on the contributor's\nfork, not on `caura-ai/caura-memclaw`, so `actions/checkout` couldn't\nresolve it and the job exited 1 — **no review verdict was ever posted**\nfor external fork PRs. It only worked when a fork's head branch happened\nto be named `main` (which exists in the base repo). Tracked as\n`.github#111`.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe shared review script (`.github/scripts/claude_pr_review.sh`) fetches\nthe PR diff via the **GitHub API**, not from the working tree — so this\njob never actually needs the PR's code checked out.\n\n- Check out the **base repo's default branch** (trusted) instead of the\nfork's branch, and drop the now-unused `head_ref` lookup.\n- **Security:** this job runs on `issue_comment`, which — unlike fork\n`pull_request` events — **does** receive repo secrets\n(`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, a write token). Checking out base code (not fork\ncode) ensures a malicious fork PR can't have its code executed with our\nsecrets when an org member triggers a review (a \"pwn request\" avoided).\n\n## Hardening\n\n- Gate the job on `author_association` (`MEMBER`/`OWNER`) at the **job\nlevel**, so the runner never even starts for a non-member's `@claude`\ncomment. The existing step-level org-membership check stays as\ndefense-in-depth (both read the same `author_association` field, so they\ncan't drift).\n\n## Testing\n\n- YAML validated locally.\n- Full end-to-end can only be confirmed after merge, since\n`issue_comment` workflows run from the **default branch** version of the\nworkflow file.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-20T12:04:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9b92e691f7d6b459e21e166bcba6d6fecdd3b609","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9b92e691f7d6b459e21e166bcba6d6fecdd3b609","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9b92e691f7d6b459e21e166bcba6d6fecdd3b609/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5680c7c5fe2d47f58536a42d846b09dc7c749884","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5680c7c5fe2d47f58536a42d846b09dc7c749884","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5680c7c5fe2d47f58536a42d846b09dc7c749884"}]},{"sha":"5680c7c5fe2d47f58536a42d846b09dc7c749884","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDU2ODBjN2M1ZmUyZDQ3ZjU4NTM2YTQyZDg0NmIwOWRjN2M3NDk4ODQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-20T11:58:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-20T11:58:30Z"},"message":"feat(auth): read gateway-plumbed X-Org-Role into AuthContext (Skills Inbox A2, reader side) (#583)\n\n## Summary\n\nPart 1 of 2 of the Skills Inbox admin-identity fix (A2). Today every\ninbox action (`approve`/`edit`/`defer`/`quarantine`/`reject`) returns\n**403 for everyone on the SaaS gateway path** — `_require_inbox_admin`\nchecks `org_role == 'admin'`, but Path 4 of `get_auth_context` builds\nthe `AuthContext` from gateway headers that never carried the org role.\nOnly standalone mode (hardcoded `org_role='admin'`) works.\n\nThis PR is the **reader side**: Path 4 now reads `X-Org-Role` into\n`AuthContext.org_role`.\n\n- **Allowlisted** to the org-membership model (`admin` | `member`,\nnormalized); unknown values are dropped so `== 'admin'` gates never see\na smuggled third role.\n- **Trust boundary unchanged**: read only on the branch already gated by\n`X-Gateway-Secret` (when configured); the gateway overwrites any\nclient-supplied `X-Org-Role` via `proxy_set_header`.\n- **Deliberate non-goal**: the `MEMCLAW_API_KEY` path (Path 2) does NOT\nread the header — API-key/agent callers must not gain inbox-action\nrights from a self-asserted header.\n- **Safe to deploy first**: absent header → `org_role=None` → behavior\nidentical to today.\n\nPart 2 (enterprise repo, follows): platform-auth-api `/validate` emits\n`X-Org-Role` from the session row / JWT claim; nginx captures + forwards\nit on the `/api/v1/` and legacy `/api/` blocks.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `tests/test_org_role_plumb.py`: admin/member parse + normalization,\nunknown-role allowlist drop, absent-header no-op, Path 2 ignores the\nheader, and an end-to-end check that a gateway-shaped request opens the\nSkills Inbox admin gate (and 403s without the role / with `member`).\n- Neighboring suites green: `test_gateway_secret_gate`,\n`test_skills_inbox_routes`, `test_install_credential_auth`,\n`test_cross_tenant_auth` (89 tests).\n- `cd core-api && uv run mypy src/` (CI's invocation) clean for\n`auth.py`; ruff check + format clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b8cbe95e39bd548abdb457b97c7d377fa06189a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/b8cbe95e39bd548abdb457b97c7d377fa06189a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/5680c7c5fe2d47f58536a42d846b09dc7c749884","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXg1mCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ6cQAGDtfNMEFJuPUPsxFYPms9cu\nqYiwJRqf+CCP9a0Wt8SxusRRXdw4w6BORQZEx3mNY6ztidb6yfrx72OkvI+i/CiN\nA7oYYQxPAUB84So8XI/9UnCAH2cm+JfDklvo5tgoyID/r3lriSiwW3knKudHh3vN\n8ekBCB+fQa0LpiiJg58QAXLZ703vZ2UL3LRKzUHSa9rj7vwjO3uTbPViDC5+jptY\nV2G4KL7SzQyc6y/V6T4XSDSAcj/p2H0vLoGOV67rtyDUdv2fdYgGJD/q2mEcJ1g9\n5HipQAaPAd0ayH1BEho/jXhea2w1QxY3HPLCwD0Cq/BOEJ0FNNimFI4Y+A1WabVH\nSY2V5XuAxv2ls+OBfdGBcsub9rK8MuLUCiMKYwYwMAop1DGilDN4YtjRtX3pdJAZ\njznJ3TdSYTrOLNP0tqJzZ5AEvBKL7C3k+obtXKsAmXBG/Qp1QpXuQH9RznWjWAjA\nX1xnA23TVgeuabu4K/BQGUWrQyRxJzmq2BAunyCaBa1gltBP1B5bNgOfvpXtNdda\n80wi/qb4WHHnwlMSXIXoUAuTWSn4PYkjZ4pJ+/cuhuRxIXJWRmNWgEUBWO73QpD2\nIOfd3oIelJAqXcX0TSvDtKb5t4Pma298nF05EZ944zQZUYkXgHzj6pPz4vbtRCkz\nJWfgaHTq9m2Owsk0VABL\n=wv4C\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b8cbe95e39bd548abdb457b97c7d377fa06189a4\nparent df259cf0feb4e0126c202f6fb44d9297b8e3fb93\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1784548710 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784548710 +0300\n\nfeat(auth): read gateway-plumbed X-Org-Role into AuthContext (Skills Inbox A2, reader side) (#583)\n\n## Summary\n\nPart 1 of 2 of the Skills Inbox admin-identity fix (A2). Today every\ninbox action (`approve`/`edit`/`defer`/`quarantine`/`reject`) returns\n**403 for everyone on the SaaS gateway path** — `_require_inbox_admin`\nchecks `org_role == 'admin'`, but Path 4 of `get_auth_context` builds\nthe `AuthContext` from gateway headers that never carried the org role.\nOnly standalone mode (hardcoded `org_role='admin'`) works.\n\nThis PR is the **reader side**: Path 4 now reads `X-Org-Role` into\n`AuthContext.org_role`.\n\n- **Allowlisted** to the org-membership model (`admin` | `member`,\nnormalized); unknown values are dropped so `== 'admin'` gates never see\na smuggled third role.\n- **Trust boundary unchanged**: read only on the branch already gated by\n`X-Gateway-Secret` (when configured); the gateway overwrites any\nclient-supplied `X-Org-Role` via `proxy_set_header`.\n- **Deliberate non-goal**: the `MEMCLAW_API_KEY` path (Path 2) does NOT\nread the header — API-key/agent callers must not gain inbox-action\nrights from a self-asserted header.\n- **Safe to deploy first**: absent header → `org_role=None` → behavior\nidentical to today.\n\nPart 2 (enterprise repo, follows): platform-auth-api `/validate` emits\n`X-Org-Role` from the session row / JWT claim; nginx captures + forwards\nit on the `/api/v1/` and legacy `/api/` blocks.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `tests/test_org_role_plumb.py`: admin/member parse + normalization,\nunknown-role allowlist drop, absent-header no-op, Path 2 ignores the\nheader, and an end-to-end check that a gateway-shaped request opens the\nSkills Inbox admin gate (and 403s without the role / with `member`).\n- Neighboring suites green: `test_gateway_secret_gate`,\n`test_skills_inbox_routes`, `test_install_credential_auth`,\n`test_cross_tenant_auth` (89 tests).\n- `cd core-api && uv run mypy src/` (CI's invocation) clean for\n`auth.py`; ruff check + format clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-20T11:58:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5680c7c5fe2d47f58536a42d846b09dc7c749884","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5680c7c5fe2d47f58536a42d846b09dc7c749884","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5680c7c5fe2d47f58536a42d846b09dc7c749884/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"df259cf0feb4e0126c202f6fb44d9297b8e3fb93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/df259cf0feb4e0126c202f6fb44d9297b8e3fb93","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/df259cf0feb4e0126c202f6fb44d9297b8e3fb93"}]},{"sha":"df259cf0feb4e0126c202f6fb44d9297b8e3fb93","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGRmMjU5Y2YwZmViNGUwMTI2YzIwMmY2ZmI0NGQ5Mjk3YjhlM2ZiOTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Sowndappan S","email":"147894621+sowndappan5@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-20T11:29:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-20T11:29:22Z"},"message":"fix(mcp): add warning when top_k is capped and document search limit (#516)\n\n<!-- Thanks for the contribution! Please fill in this template so we can\nreview quickly. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR addresses the silent truncation of `top_k` results in the MCP\nserver. It updates the parameter schema description to explicitly\nmention the limit of 20, and adds a `\"warning\"` field in the JSON\nresponse payload whenever the requested `top_k` exceeds the maximum\nallowed value (`MAX_SEARCH_TOP_K`).\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #512\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] Bug fix (non-breaking change that fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change that adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that changes existing behavior)\n- [ ] Documentation update\n- [ ] Refactor / internal cleanup\n- [ ] Other:\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n\nRan the updated unit test to assert both the capped `top_k` value and\nthe warning payload:\n```powershell\npytest tests/test_mcp_recall.py -k test_recall_top_k_is_capped\n\nSigned-off-by: sowndappan5 <sowndappan610@gmail.com>\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"2332d4fde7ff3d59616dffcf682f36c03a8bceb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/2332d4fde7ff3d59616dffcf682f36c03a8bceb0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/df259cf0feb4e0126c202f6fb44d9297b8e3fb93","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXgaSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaLsQAFvFsAKmTLi6SyeH05J274cZ\n45gTPqmRSIHg6XIfacSJ6Ywu6nkmgIUGcxhYA0Bw2AWiLDMHOuTxNYlQ7SZ+EO82\nIQ8rSPTbh22QsH9PIUTS5MddyhS0Ej3rukRV+gR3RBij2cDMCXkB0koIp3nS9vOr\nIXa2L2eEIbanIUtkt6nlDyvmJ8nYjtB7DxMArh/uBMhxCY7tOnLCLi7mRscPABVT\n8jNvb4UcO+UM3eNL2Hj9ekkYIUs8Y+rA9k+ULmIHoCKtMeIayXzpXhGM3YgXsk7T\nStbWCGj087SI1ZOjhpIN+Zg+nmLfDm8o4XY8u1SfrIsVPN1OwgCN0naKmJcYUHLH\n2IABA3tWHIyYTCLt0NbkzxEkj6v+2Vv+aMfFRT+T9L1+RRXGrDKC2nRjoAx4qW2z\nn0xzD5TlerMRXhg32udmaGRB+vSNkauUjslC5jIYUi2cOdtgMcsWnYBHj8r5+B97\nVFyXAz8DYj8rta5rkZF2CD0A4EwhW5hZKXsjMCL5LqNMVX6IJvr8Csbt1g0KwYRN\nFdSi8UHgtJYjDiGeptDPydyvfhrgrdnNv3UO/8kkzcjnudCaLJjh3yXLsJB0g+CN\nMa2ZLLdsCCotHdcW4k657XYN9SKXSj6if3o9fbLihsCyF28auDXlk8DOXrWfCiFA\noNmBQRCFOnCV2zb4Y7z8\n=9utR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2332d4fde7ff3d59616dffcf682f36c03a8bceb0\nparent 3ab73b42d64248f565afa9a6543f0405356c0275\nauthor Sowndappan S <147894621+sowndappan5@users.noreply.github.com> 1784546962 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784546962 +0300\n\nfix(mcp): add warning when top_k is capped and document search limit (#516)\n\n<!-- Thanks for the contribution! Please fill in this template so we can\nreview quickly. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR addresses the silent truncation of `top_k` results in the MCP\nserver. It updates the parameter schema description to explicitly\nmention the limit of 20, and adds a `\"warning\"` field in the JSON\nresponse payload whenever the requested `top_k` exceeds the maximum\nallowed value (`MAX_SEARCH_TOP_K`).\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #512\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] Bug fix (non-breaking change that fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change that adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that changes existing behavior)\n- [ ] Documentation update\n- [ ] Refactor / internal cleanup\n- [ ] Other:\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n\nRan the updated unit test to assert both the capped `top_k` value and\nthe warning payload:\n```powershell\npytest tests/test_mcp_recall.py -k test_recall_top_k_is_capped\n\nSigned-off-by: sowndappan5 <sowndappan610@gmail.com>\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-07-20T11:29:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/df259cf0feb4e0126c202f6fb44d9297b8e3fb93","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/df259cf0feb4e0126c202f6fb44d9297b8e3fb93","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/df259cf0feb4e0126c202f6fb44d9297b8e3fb93/comments","author":{"login":"sowndappan5","id":147894621,"node_id":"U_kgDOCNCxXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/147894621?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sowndappan5","html_url":"https://github.com/sowndappan5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sowndappan5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sowndappan5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sowndappan5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sowndappan5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sowndappan5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sowndappan5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sowndappan5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sowndappan5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sowndappan5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3ab73b42d64248f565afa9a6543f0405356c0275","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3ab73b42d64248f565afa9a6543f0405356c0275","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3ab73b42d64248f565afa9a6543f0405356c0275"}]},{"sha":"3ab73b42d64248f565afa9a6543f0405356c0275","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDNhYjczYjQyZDY0MjQ4ZjU2NWFmYTlhNjU0M2YwNDA1MzU2YzAyNzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-20T10:34:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-20T10:34:16Z"},"message":"fix(skills-inbox): converge the inbox card contract with the dashboard UI (A1) (#582)\n\nPhase A1 of the Skills Inbox GA plan: make the OSS backend serve the\ncard contract the enterprise dashboard's Skill Factory page\n(`app/(dashboard)/skill-factory/`) already consumes, and fix the defects\nfound while grounding it.\n\n## What changed\n\n**Bug fixes**\n- **`evidence` 500**: Forge writes `evidence` as a free-text rationale\nstring (`forge_service.py`), but `InboxCard.evidence` was typed `dict` —\nthe first Forge-minted staged card failed response validation and 500'd\nthe entire `GET /api/v1/skills-inbox`. Now `str | dict | None`, with a\nregression test covering string / dict / absent.\n- **Trailing-slash 307**: the list route was only registered at\n`/skills-inbox/`; the dashboard calls the bare path, and Starlette's\nredirect answers with a Location built from the internal upstream host\nbehind the gateway. The route now answers both spellings directly (bare\npath is the canonical schema entry).\n- **Bodyless `defer` 422**: every `DeferRequest` field is optional, but\nthe body envelope itself was required — a plain `POST …/defer` (curl\noperators, the documented contract) 422'd. Body is now optional.\n\n**Card contract convergence** (all additive; flat\n`scan_state`/`scan_critical`/`scan_warn` and `origin` are kept for\nexisting consumers)\n- `content` — the SKILL.md body. The list is the only inbox read surface\n(no per-slug GET) and the UI's Edit form pre-fills from it; without it a\nUI edit would silently blank the content.\n- `updated_at` — bumped by every inbox transition; the UI sorts/labels\nwith it.\n- `sentinel_scan: { status, critical_count, warning_count }` — nested\nscan verdict in the shape `normalizeInboxCard` reads.\n- `forge_evidence: { cluster_size, distinct_agents }` — only on\n`source=forge` cards (for hand-authored docs `origin` describes the\nwriter, not a cluster).\n- `cites` — memory-ID provenance, so the drawer can link a skill back to\nits source memories (Phase B needs no second backend PR).\n\n**Tests** — first dedicated coverage for the inbox routes (54 tests,\nunit-marked, no DB): golden Forge-card contract test (doubles as the\nshared fixture the frontend can assert against), the evidence-string\nregression, no-redirect on the bare path, admin-only actions vs\nmember-readable list, `SKILLS_FACTORY_DISABLED` gate, per-action status\nmatrices, 422 body validation, and the TOCTOU 409 guards (approve\ncontent-hash drift, reject-vs-approve race refusing the poison write,\nedit-vs-approve race).\n\n**Docs** — `docs/skills-inbox-api.md` response example + field notes\nupdated for the enriched shape; defer documented as body-optional.\n\n## Not in this PR (per plan)\n- A2: plumbing `X-Org-Role` through auth-api → gateway → core-api\n(enterprise repo + a small core-api reader) — without it, SaaS dashboard\nactions still 403.\n- A3: enterprise frontend repairs (flag-name copy bug, deferred chip,\nlimit heuristic).\n\n## Testing\n- `pytest tests/test_skills_inbox_routes.py` — 54 passed.\n- `pytest tests/test_skill_lifecycle_transitions.py\ntests/test_sentinel_scanner.py tests/test_route_authz_gaps.py\ntests/test_mcp_doc.py` — 181 passed.\n- `ruff check` / `ruff format --check` clean on both files; `mypy`\nreports no issues in `skills_inbox.py`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"587290a32979595f228f9c3b9b06cbde3d31cf70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/587290a32979595f228f9c3b9b06cbde3d31cf70"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/3ab73b42d64248f565afa9a6543f0405356c0275","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXfmoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbYsQAEVF8b5YUnxULJ7dcqUckWIo\nP7M8v6MdWAE7VNbH773CknMCEOAGGmaLeVDYGq8jHCzzyFIZTb8SV+r6k04RFm1a\n/XDxbPlNvIkTEMpDCSxPz5gqrfi40NE3KpZouahO/IG2ApVgLP5gYPU39r+8ZnYB\nsgTWKFRGdrWRcGQuqGMzNZTWPOGJ77Q7WqZkPPuvDmcf3FI3ThwmatMDyEZKtGUb\n7oeXNe47Fe4swdebq0BFAoDcoFL6A8nIJS7jCCj88NGWllNmcGD7ETMYAjdBjrKY\nK8mF8Cr3Tj95CcKX11sk3+tcZCcKsp7f8eBWkIIDqLZ3TlEA8a91j1h3pqUFX0XC\nUzZkCxiHOjEHBwnYA4OBNglI3cd3WEQZu/KlMDQdWa1LSDlAndPOfaBqBwkQ0sGO\nVW3tjFqFCxDsGadUMwXNkx5bAOkd4zsxISkT4Wohalc2BUyeIWbHOvX2hr04yE6w\nZXLPTDKY+mlGsgqtBjm/zM1kvsvFvnqWvMD37Ou8PeMKqu7zdUGny+UyaJpoRIx+\nFj0xGN5c1fGGYrsGylXNUtNPNuq8axLNOW8UxXhoxJvTNRYWVzVPfdosxwuUkYs/\nIlRzdmYRdDkZQq1ZhatrHo6w0FyhV+qXHbGX2hWuTaEEKesQzQVpADDi+UaZoPGX\npmOc1h8vDe2tXB0KIdQk\n=DNjR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 587290a32979595f228f9c3b9b06cbde3d31cf70\nparent 5918ed8cb11e8316b8cc1d4d3b91fe92d64173ff\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1784543656 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784543656 +0300\n\nfix(skills-inbox): converge the inbox card contract with the dashboard UI (A1) (#582)\n\nPhase A1 of the Skills Inbox GA plan: make the OSS backend serve the\ncard contract the enterprise dashboard's Skill Factory page\n(`app/(dashboard)/skill-factory/`) already consumes, and fix the defects\nfound while grounding it.\n\n## What changed\n\n**Bug fixes**\n- **`evidence` 500**: Forge writes `evidence` as a free-text rationale\nstring (`forge_service.py`), but `InboxCard.evidence` was typed `dict` —\nthe first Forge-minted staged card failed response validation and 500'd\nthe entire `GET /api/v1/skills-inbox`. Now `str | dict | None`, with a\nregression test covering string / dict / absent.\n- **Trailing-slash 307**: the list route was only registered at\n`/skills-inbox/`; the dashboard calls the bare path, and Starlette's\nredirect answers with a Location built from the internal upstream host\nbehind the gateway. The route now answers both spellings directly (bare\npath is the canonical schema entry).\n- **Bodyless `defer` 422**: every `DeferRequest` field is optional, but\nthe body envelope itself was required — a plain `POST …/defer` (curl\noperators, the documented contract) 422'd. Body is now optional.\n\n**Card contract convergence** (all additive; flat\n`scan_state`/`scan_critical`/`scan_warn` and `origin` are kept for\nexisting consumers)\n- `content` — the SKILL.md body. The list is the only inbox read surface\n(no per-slug GET) and the UI's Edit form pre-fills from it; without it a\nUI edit would silently blank the content.\n- `updated_at` — bumped by every inbox transition; the UI sorts/labels\nwith it.\n- `sentinel_scan: { status, critical_count, warning_count }` — nested\nscan verdict in the shape `normalizeInboxCard` reads.\n- `forge_evidence: { cluster_size, distinct_agents }` — only on\n`source=forge` cards (for hand-authored docs `origin` describes the\nwriter, not a cluster).\n- `cites` — memory-ID provenance, so the drawer can link a skill back to\nits source memories (Phase B needs no second backend PR).\n\n**Tests** — first dedicated coverage for the inbox routes (54 tests,\nunit-marked, no DB): golden Forge-card contract test (doubles as the\nshared fixture the frontend can assert against), the evidence-string\nregression, no-redirect on the bare path, admin-only actions vs\nmember-readable list, `SKILLS_FACTORY_DISABLED` gate, per-action status\nmatrices, 422 body validation, and the TOCTOU 409 guards (approve\ncontent-hash drift, reject-vs-approve race refusing the poison write,\nedit-vs-approve race).\n\n**Docs** — `docs/skills-inbox-api.md` response example + field notes\nupdated for the enriched shape; defer documented as body-optional.\n\n## Not in this PR (per plan)\n- A2: plumbing `X-Org-Role` through auth-api → gateway → core-api\n(enterprise repo + a small core-api reader) — without it, SaaS dashboard\nactions still 403.\n- A3: enterprise frontend repairs (flag-name copy bug, deferred chip,\nlimit heuristic).\n\n## Testing\n- `pytest tests/test_skills_inbox_routes.py` — 54 passed.\n- `pytest tests/test_skill_lifecycle_transitions.py\ntests/test_sentinel_scanner.py tests/test_route_authz_gaps.py\ntests/test_mcp_doc.py` — 181 passed.\n- `ruff check` / `ruff format --check` clean on both files; `mypy`\nreports no issues in `skills_inbox.py`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-20T10:34:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3ab73b42d64248f565afa9a6543f0405356c0275","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3ab73b42d64248f565afa9a6543f0405356c0275","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3ab73b42d64248f565afa9a6543f0405356c0275/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5918ed8cb11e8316b8cc1d4d3b91fe92d64173ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5918ed8cb11e8316b8cc1d4d3b91fe92d64173ff","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5918ed8cb11e8316b8cc1d4d3b91fe92d64173ff"}]},{"sha":"5918ed8cb11e8316b8cc1d4d3b91fe92d64173ff","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDU5MThlZDhjYjExZTgzMTZiOGNjMWQ0ZDNiOTFmZTkyZDY0MTczZmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-19T21:39:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-19T21:39:49Z"},"message":"fix(ci): publish semver image tags for component-prefixed release tags (#580)\n\n## Summary\n\nFound during the Interviewer real-LLM pilot: pulling\n`ghcr.io/caura-ai/caura-memclaw-core-api:2.22.0` (and `:v2.22.0`, and\n`:2.21.0`) fails — **no version tag has been published since\nrelease-please component prefixes began; every release ships only\n`:latest`.**\n\nVerified in the `backend: v2.22.0` publish run logs — the metadata step\ncomputed exactly one tag per image (`:latest`, `image.version=latest`):\n`docker/metadata-action`'s `type=semver` patterns can't parse\n`backend-v2.22.0` and drop silently.\n\nConsequences until now: no version pinning (`MEMCLAW_VERSION`), no\nrollback-by-tag, README's documented pins broken. Also found: the\nworkflow has no component gate, so **`plugin-v*` releases rebuilt the\nbackend images** from their checkout and re-pushed `:latest` outside any\nbackend release.\n\n## Changes\n\n1. **Resolve step strips the `backend-` prefix** → parser sees `vX.Y.Z`\n→ publishes `X.Y.Z`, `X.Y`, `X` (+`latest` on release).\n2. **Job gated to backend releases** (`workflow_dispatch` unaffected) —\nplugin releases no longer touch backend images.\n3. **Tag-shape validation now runs on both event types** — a future\ntag-scheme change fails the run loudly instead of silently publishing\nlatest-only again (exactly this incident's failure mode).\n4. **Adds `v{{version}}` alias tags** (`vX.Y.Z`) so the README's\nv-prefixed pin examples work as documented, alongside bare semver.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- YAML parses; strip + validation regex exercised against all three real\ntag shapes (`backend-v2.22.0` ✓, `backend-v2.23.0-rc.1` ✓,\n`plugin-v2.15.0` → gated/rejected).\n- End-to-end validation: the next backend release (release-please #576\nis open) should publish `2.X.Y` / `v2.X.Y` / `2.X` / `2` / `latest`.\nSuggest merging this before #576 so that release exercises it; if\nneeded, `workflow_dispatch` re-publish of `v2.22.0` also works as\nrecovery.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9635f3bb9a3de85f2cbd53e59cc10af27ee4e2ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/9635f3bb9a3de85f2cbd53e59cc10af27ee4e2ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/5918ed8cb11e8316b8cc1d4d3b91fe92d64173ff","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXUQlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2bYQAKtRAOLUJX3qpUYRY5yftQDL\nZ7sjXZ23dgB3T66WLqmr2vF9qA4D9PnzvmePY9CbY5ncv2508erRSGU3zHnMoE50\na7E1WKMMqv/UdueyDKUNAO5m2dNc96QyY0HJvfFr5LtRArEBIsTkLMtcLZ+qacoD\nu2lg4UNDeQhqephIYM2XdB6kgONKjFvijI/OveMd/EvnSdDpAUQPG3Z79xQIlOEW\nPxLLhluo/0OVna40omUHbyqnqZOi23WXVDcSUC/w/w7orhTAh43gZLuHiGcBONdK\ng/Mh6ky/xrV01Mkax4L68D1bzUggi7ivim2DI/o9NVy8XpG6mqqwoDgRh6e0aU7X\nVQibkZTj6lt6GwdSXuq8vvsqLHXgL0KLXiy1raoEzer5XNxjgtBKgkeXsz3yAQmJ\nbS3n4Iqx3xqpMr/03L6izSY1kamd4tAYa+NpFEbeisQ7oY/kAE2vmoz7p1gCNYXy\nD8DEQhzPAPOERXNxb5LYmpe4lfjm8t+/5VDeHKWDXvfA1CpWHstN2AaEdlh5iZZl\nynExndbrqNo48bZc+nOqV9HDGtBoQ4lFs2uil3q8M2uXtY6NVCqhBNsDe6KKybtH\n5IUtz4vXaq3rftx/wsQ/Xzxx7NTQoVrK4bB4oOr8M/+5RlXJmTdWeKnrglFExTaH\nuRmCdaGrcSoajNtz8mN9\n=sJU6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9635f3bb9a3de85f2cbd53e59cc10af27ee4e2ea\nparent fd597c723e5ec2c93544ed9804710a96c1778d7c\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1784497189 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784497189 +0300\n\nfix(ci): publish semver image tags for component-prefixed release tags (#580)\n\n## Summary\n\nFound during the Interviewer real-LLM pilot: pulling\n`ghcr.io/caura-ai/caura-memclaw-core-api:2.22.0` (and `:v2.22.0`, and\n`:2.21.0`) fails — **no version tag has been published since\nrelease-please component prefixes began; every release ships only\n`:latest`.**\n\nVerified in the `backend: v2.22.0` publish run logs — the metadata step\ncomputed exactly one tag per image (`:latest`, `image.version=latest`):\n`docker/metadata-action`'s `type=semver` patterns can't parse\n`backend-v2.22.0` and drop silently.\n\nConsequences until now: no version pinning (`MEMCLAW_VERSION`), no\nrollback-by-tag, README's documented pins broken. Also found: the\nworkflow has no component gate, so **`plugin-v*` releases rebuilt the\nbackend images** from their checkout and re-pushed `:latest` outside any\nbackend release.\n\n## Changes\n\n1. **Resolve step strips the `backend-` prefix** → parser sees `vX.Y.Z`\n→ publishes `X.Y.Z`, `X.Y`, `X` (+`latest` on release).\n2. **Job gated to backend releases** (`workflow_dispatch` unaffected) —\nplugin releases no longer touch backend images.\n3. **Tag-shape validation now runs on both event types** — a future\ntag-scheme change fails the run loudly instead of silently publishing\nlatest-only again (exactly this incident's failure mode).\n4. **Adds `v{{version}}` alias tags** (`vX.Y.Z`) so the README's\nv-prefixed pin examples work as documented, alongside bare semver.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- YAML parses; strip + validation regex exercised against all three real\ntag shapes (`backend-v2.22.0` ✓, `backend-v2.23.0-rc.1` ✓,\n`plugin-v2.15.0` → gated/rejected).\n- End-to-end validation: the next backend release (release-please #576\nis open) should publish `2.X.Y` / `v2.X.Y` / `2.X` / `2` / `latest`.\nSuggest merging this before #576 so that release exercises it; if\nneeded, `workflow_dispatch` re-publish of `v2.22.0` also works as\nrecovery.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-19T21:39:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5918ed8cb11e8316b8cc1d4d3b91fe92d64173ff","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5918ed8cb11e8316b8cc1d4d3b91fe92d64173ff","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5918ed8cb11e8316b8cc1d4d3b91fe92d64173ff/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fd597c723e5ec2c93544ed9804710a96c1778d7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fd597c723e5ec2c93544ed9804710a96c1778d7c","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/fd597c723e5ec2c93544ed9804710a96c1778d7c"}]},{"sha":"fd597c723e5ec2c93544ed9804710a96c1778d7c","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGZkNTk3YzcyM2U1ZWMyYzkzNTQ0ZWQ5ODA0NzEwYTk2YzE3NzhkN2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-19T15:54:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-19T15:54:39Z"},"message":"feat(memories): list filters — created_after/before + exclude_memory_types (#573)\n\nBackend enabling-work for the **Prism agent deeplink** from the Agent\nActivity report (frontend PR to follow). Adds two filters to the `GET\n/api/v1/memories` list path so a link can open Prism pre-filtered to an\nagent's *durable* memories within the digest window.\n\n## Changes\n- **`created_after` / `created_before`** (date window): core-api\n`list_memories` now accepts + forwards them. The core-storage\n`/memories/list` route and `memory_list_by_filters` service already\nsupported them — this just closes the core-api gap.\n- **`exclude_memory_types`** (list): new end-to-end — core-api query\nparam → storage `/memories/list` body → `memory_list_by_filters` `WHERE\nmemory_type NOT IN (...)`. Lets the deeplink request \"durable\" =\nnon-`episode`.\n\n## Contract\n```\nGET /api/v1/memories?agent_id=<a>&fleet_id=<f>&created_after=<ISO>&created_before=<ISO>&exclude_memory_types=episode\n```\n(`exclude_memory_types` repeats for multiple:\n`&exclude_memory_types=episode&exclude_memory_types=...`)\n\n## Tests\nIntegration test: three memories (in-window `decision`, in-window\n`episode`, out-of-window `decision`) → list with\n`exclude_memory_types=[episode]` + the window returns **only** the\nin-window `decision`. Passes against pgvector. ruff + mypy clean (both\npackages).\n\nFrontend PR (Prism URL hydration + report deeplink) depends on this;\ndeploy this first (unknown params are harmless-ignored if the frontend\nsomehow lands earlier).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b6bb52bd35f16e37df95d4a56b65c952a377fe2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/5b6bb52bd35f16e37df95d4a56b65c952a377fe2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/fd597c723e5ec2c93544ed9804710a96c1778d7c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXPM/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfkIQADz1zT25hksxwP1L6mTz4Jct\n53onoPhoBdTb5tT17UqyaVm9/qzL0d/hbN94kde1p1X/SUtUH9QxD9U2qR4g53Gc\n/lA05XmuTFjLKRCN76O2CJn9aWYke/MIrOxinalBvwyg4SXdyEbzUKGLNHE46xV5\nZZr/tUYT5Wk58kSfhxDOchCV1O0PPBVJlcIYTn9FcbSBUrp1rwrlA3QMcoSfTeE7\njma9WeqJ7WoZPwnoxYE37sh1rEklhFbTkwnxDXbqViCO0GT7yxJLn90I+86GVD08\nKBqnQfClmYeLWa70+h8ErGHq+43VxSmTVFcR4Z2hAOeInj0Sae0zSm1Gll4RRT5N\nZtj3MKo0c7yUki+z4GD4iPBBnwJHHE2RQ1dVJWGKasnIAasrN4PmoQgrZ6GeVLj6\nldR91VApAm/HFWyg6kE1b7Gp4BksVzr0Fxmj+fw45OjB+khz2xbWuoTmVGEwfmtJ\nauobjv+89U4uSwEJ+wCbehsxQfcQ/g0ui1/x/eN/LdqQGtWcsbkmURHxYxTjtLFW\niQzaJ+OgV9Utw+GUzVXGH8LVs25SnJJEI1TWs465CCZVUK8P7BBS+l7cKKj0/Ijf\nptZvgQIm5Veg6/keOau96+M82mM45IB3Um2yO87zD1p4ibELBpuss/pqHOiSZ2Fy\nVYVexbdUAsXvZttPi7Df\n=GX7i\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5b6bb52bd35f16e37df95d4a56b65c952a377fe2\nparent 6625bd10fb55de4de14048684d7677b0557a9294\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1784476479 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784476479 +0300\n\nfeat(memories): list filters — created_after/before + exclude_memory_types (#573)\n\nBackend enabling-work for the **Prism agent deeplink** from the Agent\nActivity report (frontend PR to follow). Adds two filters to the `GET\n/api/v1/memories` list path so a link can open Prism pre-filtered to an\nagent's *durable* memories within the digest window.\n\n## Changes\n- **`created_after` / `created_before`** (date window): core-api\n`list_memories` now accepts + forwards them. The core-storage\n`/memories/list` route and `memory_list_by_filters` service already\nsupported them — this just closes the core-api gap.\n- **`exclude_memory_types`** (list): new end-to-end — core-api query\nparam → storage `/memories/list` body → `memory_list_by_filters` `WHERE\nmemory_type NOT IN (...)`. Lets the deeplink request \"durable\" =\nnon-`episode`.\n\n## Contract\n```\nGET /api/v1/memories?agent_id=<a>&fleet_id=<f>&created_after=<ISO>&created_before=<ISO>&exclude_memory_types=episode\n```\n(`exclude_memory_types` repeats for multiple:\n`&exclude_memory_types=episode&exclude_memory_types=...`)\n\n## Tests\nIntegration test: three memories (in-window `decision`, in-window\n`episode`, out-of-window `decision`) → list with\n`exclude_memory_types=[episode]` + the window returns **only** the\nin-window `decision`. Passes against pgvector. ruff + mypy clean (both\npackages).\n\nFrontend PR (Prism URL hydration + report deeplink) depends on this;\ndeploy this first (unknown params are harmless-ignored if the frontend\nsomehow lands earlier).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-19T15:54:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fd597c723e5ec2c93544ed9804710a96c1778d7c","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/fd597c723e5ec2c93544ed9804710a96c1778d7c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/fd597c723e5ec2c93544ed9804710a96c1778d7c/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6625bd10fb55de4de14048684d7677b0557a9294","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6625bd10fb55de4de14048684d7677b0557a9294","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/6625bd10fb55de4de14048684d7677b0557a9294"}]},{"sha":"6625bd10fb55de4de14048684d7677b0557a9294","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDY2MjViZDEwZmI1NWRlNGRlMTQwNDg2ODRkNzY3N2IwNTU3YTkyOTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-19T15:46:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-19T15:46:56Z"},"message":"docs: Skills Inbox REST API reference (Skill Factory GA prep) (#578)\n\n## Summary\n\n- New [`docs/skills-inbox-api.md`](docs/skills-inbox-api.md):\noperator-facing reference for the Skills Inbox REST API — auth (session\ncookie + CSRF for browsers, Bearer JWT for scripts, admin required for\nactions), base path, Forge-slug path-encoding rules (`{slug:path}` —\nencode per segment, keep raw slashes), `GET /api/v1/skills-inbox` list\nshape, the five `POST …/{slug}/<action>` endpoints (approve / defer /\nedit / quarantine / reject), a status/action matrix, an operator triage\nwalkthrough, and error codes.\n- README Skill Factory section: the governance bullet now names the REST\nsurface explicitly, and the deep-dives sentence links the new doc\nalongside `mcp-skill-delivery.md` and `operator-forge-cron.md`.\n\nThe doc is grounded in the actual implementation\n(`core-api/src/core_api/routes/skills_inbox.py`). Where the\nimplementation differs from the earlier draft spec, the doc follows the\ncode:\n\n- `GET /` lists **staged only** (candidate/quarantined docs don't\nappear), and is readable by any tenant member — only the five actions\nare admin-gated.\n- `defer` keeps the doc `staged` and stamps `deferred_at` (sorts to the\nbottom); it does not demote to `candidate`.\n- `reject` is allowed from staged/candidate/quarantined.\n- Wrong-status actions return **409** (404 is reserved for a missing\ndoc).\n- The card shape is flat (`scan_state`/`scan_critical`/`scan_warn`,\nevidence under `origin.cluster_size`/`origin.distinct_agents`), matching\n`InboxCard`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Docs-only change; verified endpoint paths, payloads, status codes, and\ndefaults against `routes/skills_inbox.py` and the router mount in\n`core_api/app.py` (`prefix=/api/v1`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0a212400cc932c3291c39b4664c4f6d377ae5bb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/0a212400cc932c3291c39b4664c4f6d377ae5bb9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/6625bd10fb55de4de14048684d7677b0557a9294","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXPFwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFS4QAKlPTK32OLyxj8QHDr9h/Wc5\n8GlSGvBhlOdUSwpNLXbJzp4v1+mdAME/tAdL3LLIOLwxqM4vd3//+1WmEZx4fWUL\niyTa3JRriouypr9jsPEiRy8CgARtFvT3Xi13SpI/GgT9r2nvu/pfY4uTY07YSIYL\nPxf9l1ZLOVPBtEitkS9d2ePRpLbjCtteGWeMwLiiR3UV5tP86PNQpWdCIRVPzmAo\nqzPgzJlE4EESX4HmnJio3DIkuhy3N9wPXA/OhN1u2t0O0nouqGStLdO9PSPoI7ws\nuWqkvqCQXcTPzBYG+pAm32qjcQ4WjdPM/UmCrqfZTzYoKnqqxCVMXSscMGSmsJOd\nwipTDt4VIrO4ifjSHhg9z8fTegbSzRxfRql8C6AG2njb2alNmm/SBDtTTIQ3Futy\nxMpxLnowoA/mqcW2Zm9XStGUOss9cKS0gO5CY4jNfs/o1tKs+anI9WZd8xTaLpKl\ni320R2SeYv88ET1fIPeDIVeZOIaDS4CEWDKVlb3ps1vlDRjbDZwfbXIwk+WRyred\nPEITFxYZLjzZwNnV33L1l8ghqjeGqiMJ4G70LlAfERCiblEAdcRMhx5o5Rrc+vRf\nC/y9+DSWYVDK+RiDGW8Bf16qrt6EDYyAZtfOVHVtAE+z/Ut2fbA5ZcBmrbvsL199\nyO2Kx1D0UWeX00mb4GiW\n=zMpe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0a212400cc932c3291c39b4664c4f6d377ae5bb9\nparent 740505da50aa6bdc2916a1ca7aecb0a993855718\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1784476016 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784476016 +0300\n\ndocs: Skills Inbox REST API reference (Skill Factory GA prep) (#578)\n\n## Summary\n\n- New [`docs/skills-inbox-api.md`](docs/skills-inbox-api.md):\noperator-facing reference for the Skills Inbox REST API — auth (session\ncookie + CSRF for browsers, Bearer JWT for scripts, admin required for\nactions), base path, Forge-slug path-encoding rules (`{slug:path}` —\nencode per segment, keep raw slashes), `GET /api/v1/skills-inbox` list\nshape, the five `POST …/{slug}/<action>` endpoints (approve / defer /\nedit / quarantine / reject), a status/action matrix, an operator triage\nwalkthrough, and error codes.\n- README Skill Factory section: the governance bullet now names the REST\nsurface explicitly, and the deep-dives sentence links the new doc\nalongside `mcp-skill-delivery.md` and `operator-forge-cron.md`.\n\nThe doc is grounded in the actual implementation\n(`core-api/src/core_api/routes/skills_inbox.py`). Where the\nimplementation differs from the earlier draft spec, the doc follows the\ncode:\n\n- `GET /` lists **staged only** (candidate/quarantined docs don't\nappear), and is readable by any tenant member — only the five actions\nare admin-gated.\n- `defer` keeps the doc `staged` and stamps `deferred_at` (sorts to the\nbottom); it does not demote to `candidate`.\n- `reject` is allowed from staged/candidate/quarantined.\n- Wrong-status actions return **409** (404 is reserved for a missing\ndoc).\n- The card shape is flat (`scan_state`/`scan_critical`/`scan_warn`,\nevidence under `origin.cluster_size`/`origin.distinct_agents`), matching\n`InboxCard`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Docs-only change; verified endpoint paths, payloads, status codes, and\ndefaults against `routes/skills_inbox.py` and the router mount in\n`core_api/app.py` (`prefix=/api/v1`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-19T15:46:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6625bd10fb55de4de14048684d7677b0557a9294","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/6625bd10fb55de4de14048684d7677b0557a9294","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6625bd10fb55de4de14048684d7677b0557a9294/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"740505da50aa6bdc2916a1ca7aecb0a993855718","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/740505da50aa6bdc2916a1ca7aecb0a993855718","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/740505da50aa6bdc2916a1ca7aecb0a993855718"}]},{"sha":"740505da50aa6bdc2916a1ca7aecb0a993855718","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDc0MDUwNWRhNTBhYTZiZGMyOTE2YTFjYTdhZWNiMGE5OTM4NTU3MTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-19T15:20:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-19T15:20:08Z"},"message":"fix(interview): latency budgets for realistic submit windows (real-LLM pilot finding) (#572)\n\n## Summary\n\nFirst real-LLM pilot of the Interviewer (released images + OpenAI\nproviders, 400-event replay of a real working session) found that **both\ndefault request budgets kill any realistic window** — the interview runs\nsynchronously server-side and measured ~63s:\n\n1. plugin `apiCall` 15s default → client abort;\n2. core-api blanket 45s middleware → `504 request timeout`.\n\nEvery failure was safe (no prune, buffer intact — the invariants held\nunder real fire), but the feature could never complete a full window.\n\n## Fix\n\n- **Plugin:** `INTERVIEW_SUBMIT_TIMEOUT_MS` (300s) passed as the submit\n`AbortSignal` (the `BUILD_TIMEOUT_MS` pattern).\n- **Server:** `/interview/submit` added to `_TIMEOUT_OPT_OUT_PATHS`,\nroute enforces its own `interview_request_timeout_seconds` (300s\ndefault) via `asyncio.wait_for` — exactly the bulk-write pattern, and\nfor the same reason. 504 is retry-safe end-to-end.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- New route test: slow interview + tiny budget → 504 with \"window not\nconsumed\"; full interview suite 21/21.\n- Plugin suite 377/377; ruff + mypy clean at CI scope.\n- Validated live on the pilot VM: with both budgets, 400 events → 63s →\n68 typed memories committed, watermark 399, buffer pruned.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"95457a0ad07523dc4ddbe73ebace36f7def4c059","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/95457a0ad07523dc4ddbe73ebace36f7def4c059"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/740505da50aa6bdc2916a1ca7aecb0a993855718","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXOsoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlB4QAERJ6sIlxeposgAqtgVSlAJL\n/MxLD65QPL2xFtdsuEwvPN64L7wXul5TqOmssi4V3KJ9CjnVNMb9lb4ZRqXp636C\nz03qv/yPA+X2Fo4Kp/DmitPksIB0G9L1ubKdvseHQr2fLBSYqai0jdKoRbaGibhQ\n4PTpZcgwWsKgQr0lO6c7t99B00dkPMj5i3etWCwdItZdcaAF2dxmN3LlxWTOoaOL\nUNTFa8yPnsg+XZXjdmqIgEDPt9Uju7xfqV6hx5Z5RRbApn7jljYchdJQE34+tijr\nacysbeAjMWIPCmaF6K33Sm5igL9QnCK/V8F86Et2iTeQSm4aoKRa6rvk1fy+rARI\nV3vRWK8EStXQiOYmb8z93QnujtMZE7HqcjkMjTXf6OIVKYhM+whB4HGacQmZqwbt\nN8m4LJs9QIxN1MQ0VncXDQ6G4eDDrWF4C5cS00YAeR9EnErkYsGmrxQFDc8hxSnJ\nZYNa/mWoOkQd4oQ6nALsgxVsiKV6Yp2B2VTu2gFNGW8/KqWsc7XVKeWyp5oNdETv\nsmpEWayVx9HQ8EzpKLTZqxpaI/yye5rnScIawJTZbxo5bhq2OtqUqaN76UQjaYjp\ndVJWc7hBGlbn7hD80bAEDlmLwMXrNm5pSRYivc8dGzvdbc5qakuy9nxKfdcNXScN\n/iM8VoE9DOJMyKrT21wr\n=aPUU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 95457a0ad07523dc4ddbe73ebace36f7def4c059\nparent 1ce740ab97aa292c37cf935f3010bc47edd2fd0f\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1784474408 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784474408 +0300\n\nfix(interview): latency budgets for realistic submit windows (real-LLM pilot finding) (#572)\n\n## Summary\n\nFirst real-LLM pilot of the Interviewer (released images + OpenAI\nproviders, 400-event replay of a real working session) found that **both\ndefault request budgets kill any realistic window** — the interview runs\nsynchronously server-side and measured ~63s:\n\n1. plugin `apiCall` 15s default → client abort;\n2. core-api blanket 45s middleware → `504 request timeout`.\n\nEvery failure was safe (no prune, buffer intact — the invariants held\nunder real fire), but the feature could never complete a full window.\n\n## Fix\n\n- **Plugin:** `INTERVIEW_SUBMIT_TIMEOUT_MS` (300s) passed as the submit\n`AbortSignal` (the `BUILD_TIMEOUT_MS` pattern).\n- **Server:** `/interview/submit` added to `_TIMEOUT_OPT_OUT_PATHS`,\nroute enforces its own `interview_request_timeout_seconds` (300s\ndefault) via `asyncio.wait_for` — exactly the bulk-write pattern, and\nfor the same reason. 504 is retry-safe end-to-end.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- New route test: slow interview + tiny budget → 504 with \"window not\nconsumed\"; full interview suite 21/21.\n- Plugin suite 377/377; ruff + mypy clean at CI scope.\n- Validated live on the pilot VM: with both budgets, 400 events → 63s →\n68 typed memories committed, watermark 399, buffer pruned.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-19T15:20:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/740505da50aa6bdc2916a1ca7aecb0a993855718","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/740505da50aa6bdc2916a1ca7aecb0a993855718","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/740505da50aa6bdc2916a1ca7aecb0a993855718/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1ce740ab97aa292c37cf935f3010bc47edd2fd0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1ce740ab97aa292c37cf935f3010bc47edd2fd0f","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1ce740ab97aa292c37cf935f3010bc47edd2fd0f"}]},{"sha":"1ce740ab97aa292c37cf935f3010bc47edd2fd0f","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDFjZTc0MGFiOTdhYTI5MmMzN2NmOTM1ZjMwMTBiYzQ3ZWRkMmZkMGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-19T14:15:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-19T14:15:18Z"},"message":"feat(search): cosine-dominant candidate pool selection (A49), off by default (#579)\n\n## What\n\nAdds an opt-in **per-tenant** knob `candidate_pool_size` (default **0 =\noff**). When `>0`, the first-stage candidate pool is selected by\nsemantic relevance (`similarity`) instead of the boost-distorted\n`score`, so **boost-demoted-but-strong matches survive the LIMIT** into\nthe ranking/rerank stage (A50) rather than being evicted by the boost\nstack.\n\nResolution: agent profile → tenant `default_search_profile` → global\nconstant (0). Validator caps it to 0–200.\n\n## Why\n\nLongMemEval 500-case failure analysis: **64%** of the gold memories\nproduction dropped from its top-20 rank **≤20 by pure cosine** — i.e.\nthe ranking demoted strong semantic matches, it didn't fail to find\nthem. A cross-encoder reranker (A50) only re-scores the candidate pool\nit's handed, so those demoted matches must first be *in* the pool.\nOffline ceiling: a cosine-selected pool of **50 recovers 95%** of the\ndropped gold; >70 adds nothing.\n\n## Scope / behavior\n\n- **Off by default → zero behavior change.** A49 alone\nwidens/relevance-selects the candidate pool; the outer query still\norders by `score` and `PostFilterResults` still trims to the caller's\n`top_k`, so the **final reorder is A50's job**. This is dark-launch\ninfrastructure for A50.\n- Enable per tenant via `default_search_profile.candidate_pool_size` for\nthe A49+A50 A/B.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **core-api**: `CANDIDATE_POOL_SIZE` constant, `_SEARCH_PROFILE_RULES`\nentry (int 0–200), thread `candidate_pool_size` into `search_params`.\n- **core-storage-api**: order the LIMIT pool by `similarity` when\n`candidate_pool_size > 0` (else unchanged `score` order).\n\n## Tests\n\n- core-api plumbing unit tests (6, passing): default-off,\nvalidate/clamp, resolve threading.\n- storage integration test (real pgvector, passing): a boost-demoted\nhigh-similarity row is dropped by score-order but retained by the cosine\npool; `candidate_pool_size=0` is byte-identical to default.\n- Existing `/scored-search` tests: no regression (4/4).\n\n## Not yet validated\n\nEnd-to-end accuracy — that requires the **A49+A50 A/B** (re-seed +\nfull-500), since A49 alone is pool infrastructure. Merging is safe\nbecause the flag is off.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"86f9a674220bae8f1aea40de501d661482410bc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/86f9a674220bae8f1aea40de501d661482410bc2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/1ce740ab97aa292c37cf935f3010bc47edd2fd0f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXNv2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAfcQAKgGdmYy8pTDs9W5dIxpM+tC\no5OLx4FG+GX3Bi5cB4Y4ZtXbSnJYLglCcam/jKhxDtqSrrQ7ti+mlvd0jQdm8rHf\nfY8wxO/V/V/4bI9eSS02VyxiAKVF5RZsOpW4X0meHXHcCvHqthGWZEEDOvRz0WrQ\n7ljStFEfdmMeFODGOHzbfFDcfIZVLzbxL8M214jUI/FqAPWuxeeNZh6ll2OnJEYL\nXf8WQTC8qbvO0mPMNbRUKN+OKEcm+KI1xAV/eT9Djd+71ysqUzKQxOu++h3apzm+\nvDkYTHPETofSTjgVKchRYNShkdTzcyEWEuBVvF/NxWP4Jpy2ME+9LizI6/ecgDbs\n2qZBpWfrtgbbYs/KV67J/8H0FcXZUQtmMVsUUJSikGESPSkLFjPj4O9sFvwO9HrM\nPwOURj4aWD5wrK9X/WHtKPVuAGLtMeyhwA2axzj9P4YlsdJcpdAIYPaM0z2B71AE\niKYcs9QCmFqDHJkRLlt6AgIObA5F2EBLT5FIKBBpGTEs9ftGJw5it0NL9uVezUvX\ny5ZGuJGtX0PoUl3LVmyJrN3qCYVb9seoGjebOFJylDnb/Bzcw1cm/P9KjAvCWZlj\n7DZt3NorIBPzcyfplY0HQaBxoddZUu9bwNlQU0Z2BLfGxNjo1HLBppY+Zc2U/aw8\nQOvSg0qeOg5J1pOK0i6r\n=ro3z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 86f9a674220bae8f1aea40de501d661482410bc2\nparent 0ecc2748149c106d5a95d74e74b4eba956adb4f2\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1784470518 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784470518 +0300\n\nfeat(search): cosine-dominant candidate pool selection (A49), off by default (#579)\n\n## What\n\nAdds an opt-in **per-tenant** knob `candidate_pool_size` (default **0 =\noff**). When `>0`, the first-stage candidate pool is selected by\nsemantic relevance (`similarity`) instead of the boost-distorted\n`score`, so **boost-demoted-but-strong matches survive the LIMIT** into\nthe ranking/rerank stage (A50) rather than being evicted by the boost\nstack.\n\nResolution: agent profile → tenant `default_search_profile` → global\nconstant (0). Validator caps it to 0–200.\n\n## Why\n\nLongMemEval 500-case failure analysis: **64%** of the gold memories\nproduction dropped from its top-20 rank **≤20 by pure cosine** — i.e.\nthe ranking demoted strong semantic matches, it didn't fail to find\nthem. A cross-encoder reranker (A50) only re-scores the candidate pool\nit's handed, so those demoted matches must first be *in* the pool.\nOffline ceiling: a cosine-selected pool of **50 recovers 95%** of the\ndropped gold; >70 adds nothing.\n\n## Scope / behavior\n\n- **Off by default → zero behavior change.** A49 alone\nwidens/relevance-selects the candidate pool; the outer query still\norders by `score` and `PostFilterResults` still trims to the caller's\n`top_k`, so the **final reorder is A50's job**. This is dark-launch\ninfrastructure for A50.\n- Enable per tenant via `default_search_profile.candidate_pool_size` for\nthe A49+A50 A/B.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **core-api**: `CANDIDATE_POOL_SIZE` constant, `_SEARCH_PROFILE_RULES`\nentry (int 0–200), thread `candidate_pool_size` into `search_params`.\n- **core-storage-api**: order the LIMIT pool by `similarity` when\n`candidate_pool_size > 0` (else unchanged `score` order).\n\n## Tests\n\n- core-api plumbing unit tests (6, passing): default-off,\nvalidate/clamp, resolve threading.\n- storage integration test (real pgvector, passing): a boost-demoted\nhigh-similarity row is dropped by score-order but retained by the cosine\npool; `candidate_pool_size=0` is byte-identical to default.\n- Existing `/scored-search` tests: no regression (4/4).\n\n## Not yet validated\n\nEnd-to-end accuracy — that requires the **A49+A50 A/B** (re-seed +\nfull-500), since A49 alone is pool infrastructure. Merging is safe\nbecause the flag is off.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-19T14:15:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1ce740ab97aa292c37cf935f3010bc47edd2fd0f","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1ce740ab97aa292c37cf935f3010bc47edd2fd0f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1ce740ab97aa292c37cf935f3010bc47edd2fd0f/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0ecc2748149c106d5a95d74e74b4eba956adb4f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0ecc2748149c106d5a95d74e74b4eba956adb4f2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0ecc2748149c106d5a95d74e74b4eba956adb4f2"}]},{"sha":"0ecc2748149c106d5a95d74e74b4eba956adb4f2","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDBlY2MyNzQ4MTQ5YzEwNmQ1YTk1ZDc0ZTc0YjRlYmE5NTZhZGI0ZjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-19T12:16:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-19T12:16:47Z"},"message":"fix(core-api): map unhandled upstream 5xx/429 to a retryable 503 (#575)\n\n## Why (finding #3 from the 2026-07-19 prod error review — option a)\nThe one prod 500 in 3 days was `POST /fleet/heartbeat` → `upsert_node()`\n→ core-storage-writer returned a transient **503**, and the storage\nclient's `raise_for_status()` let it bubble as an **unhandled**\nexception → the catch-all returned 500 (`INTERNAL_ERROR`) and opened an\nError-Tracking issue. A transient dependency blip on an idempotent,\nfrequently-retried endpoint shouldn't read as a hard server bug — the\nplugin should just retry next tick.\n\n## What\nApp-level `@app.exception_handler(httpx.HTTPStatusError)` that maps an\n**upstream 5xx/429** to a retryable **503** (canonical `UNAVAILABLE`\nenvelope) instead of the 500 catch-all. Fixing it at the exception\nmechanism covers every endpoint uniformly rather than bolting a\ntry/except onto the heartbeat handler (the \"fix the mechanism, not the\nsymptom\" altitude).\n\nA **4xx** from an upstream means *our* request was malformed — a genuine\nbug, not a blip — so it still flows to the 500 catch-all unchanged.\n\n## Tests (`tests/test_upstream_error_handler.py`)\n- 500/502/503/504/429 → 503 `UNAVAILABLE`;\n- 400/404/409/422 → 500 `INTERNAL_ERROR`;\n- handler is registered for `httpx.HTTPStatusError`.\n`ruff`/`mypy` clean.\n\nCompanion to #574 (which dedups the heartbeat's outdated-plugin log).\nTogether they close the fleet-heartbeat findings from the error review.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f231409da64c97999a60061c6fa3ad7db087540b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f231409da64c97999a60061c6fa3ad7db087540b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/0ecc2748149c106d5a95d74e74b4eba956adb4f2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXMAvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVqUQAJn6wM/cJC+3umUctnZ0riSq\nWkEZ31S0SvxGaEyYVGxfi+7ABPbiaBC8aDsZ2OY7dXrz737UHkZMOVFO5BmPDM88\n3bDleNEQW+QU0QqDd+CPmJd2X59sJVZkx2ZA6ZkilbmQD8e/d/iZPvUkNbwu+ELm\nYt4AE68xfwX4jqNhXf41Kly3cBpWc25tUSBS50ASDzq5epWuPWenaIB7FDELwrR0\nQfViR7A3cxRiLViBdOcAy+Ptnvl2kLvT97Ay7DZruAq9WnIRdS1VCXQuN9jmZ0pP\n1hcAJWaIs3g62Wjjhxcn+fQKY+s2YXqDknBWij7G+RBEN1R6Acz4zHDmf7HvAQIR\nTAO/Wo8fXQuuGoGqZRDfv4lWVBaIo4kQU+lPnuAB5Wy33hrV9xbK4d4mCIABN+zP\nocVVLW/utT4M3il2ilg7CPf0AqPZHKaYLQd/6/8jDFTebx9Dlwfr5M/ecp1yPhQ3\ncSt6gxLmQU1UW1JOzgs3sNFgSy4s/9vFEKSaHdZeun4Dy5SqpNUrSMxeULTprUSn\nhERYYIZFEdanmtM5KnbpOlE00r1IoYY7+KCssQE+7pdvLtJu9+ZkN9MNjGNpn3I3\nu1nMFVBIXDlZ64BxMwqTNMa8IFqbhSAwSyZeE3UmX6iskBSdlXSbd525y2+zjT3e\ndqJQDGmBfnYzZfDYpLh+\n=yX59\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f231409da64c97999a60061c6fa3ad7db087540b\nparent b912f71c1f3872c295e00356194ced769cc8c8d0\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1784463407 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784463407 +0300\n\nfix(core-api): map unhandled upstream 5xx/429 to a retryable 503 (#575)\n\n## Why (finding #3 from the 2026-07-19 prod error review — option a)\nThe one prod 500 in 3 days was `POST /fleet/heartbeat` → `upsert_node()`\n→ core-storage-writer returned a transient **503**, and the storage\nclient's `raise_for_status()` let it bubble as an **unhandled**\nexception → the catch-all returned 500 (`INTERNAL_ERROR`) and opened an\nError-Tracking issue. A transient dependency blip on an idempotent,\nfrequently-retried endpoint shouldn't read as a hard server bug — the\nplugin should just retry next tick.\n\n## What\nApp-level `@app.exception_handler(httpx.HTTPStatusError)` that maps an\n**upstream 5xx/429** to a retryable **503** (canonical `UNAVAILABLE`\nenvelope) instead of the 500 catch-all. Fixing it at the exception\nmechanism covers every endpoint uniformly rather than bolting a\ntry/except onto the heartbeat handler (the \"fix the mechanism, not the\nsymptom\" altitude).\n\nA **4xx** from an upstream means *our* request was malformed — a genuine\nbug, not a blip — so it still flows to the 500 catch-all unchanged.\n\n## Tests (`tests/test_upstream_error_handler.py`)\n- 500/502/503/504/429 → 503 `UNAVAILABLE`;\n- 400/404/409/422 → 500 `INTERNAL_ERROR`;\n- handler is registered for `httpx.HTTPStatusError`.\n`ruff`/`mypy` clean.\n\nCompanion to #574 (which dedups the heartbeat's outdated-plugin log).\nTogether they close the fleet-heartbeat findings from the error review.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-19T12:16:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0ecc2748149c106d5a95d74e74b4eba956adb4f2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0ecc2748149c106d5a95d74e74b4eba956adb4f2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0ecc2748149c106d5a95d74e74b4eba956adb4f2/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b912f71c1f3872c295e00356194ced769cc8c8d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b912f71c1f3872c295e00356194ced769cc8c8d0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b912f71c1f3872c295e00356194ced769cc8c8d0"}]},{"sha":"b912f71c1f3872c295e00356194ced769cc8c8d0","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGI5MTJmNzFjMWYzODcyYzI5NWUwMDM1NjE5NGNlZDc2OWNjOGM4ZDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-19T10:57:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-19T10:57:02Z"},"message":"fix(fleet): dedup the outdated-plugin heartbeat warning (#574)\n\n## Why (finding #2 from the 2026-07-19 prod error review)\n`POST /fleet/heartbeat` logs a WARNING every tick a plugin is below\n`MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION`. A node stuck on an old plugin\nheartbeats ~every 20–60s forever, so it floods: prod produced **6,301\nlines/day** from just **3 internal nodes** — `eyal-open-claw-1` on\nplugin `1.0.1` (~every 20s), a container on `2.8.0`, and\n`shushants-MacBook-Air` on `2.5.0`. That volume drowns real warnings now\nthat log severity classifies correctly (#561).\n\n## What\nGate the warning through a per-`(node, version)` dedup with a 1h window\n— a module-level TTL cache, bounded (5000) + oldest-evicted, mirroring\nthe auth-api cache idiom. The fleet-health signal still surfaces\n(once/hour/stuck node) without the per-tick spam. Keyed on `(node,\nversion)` so a version change re-logs promptly. Per-instance (not shared\nacross Cloud Run instances), so worst case is one line per instance per\nnode per hour — still orders of magnitude below one per tick.\n\n**Behaviour otherwise unchanged** — the auto-upgrade queueing path is\nuntouched; only the log is throttled.\n\n## Tests\n5 new unit tests (appended to `test_fleet_heartbeat_auto_upgrade.py`):\ndedup, version-change re-log, per-node isolation, window expiry, size\ncap. Full file 61 pass; `ruff`/`mypy` clean.\n\n## Ops follow-up (not code)\nThe 3 stuck nodes are all internal (a teammate's box, a container, a\nlaptop) — worth nudging them to upgrade or decommissioning, but not a\ncustomer-fleet problem.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3c190c27c2cd92ce921bd2d4e8bbcb59f8c713b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/3c190c27c2cd92ce921bd2d4e8bbcb59f8c713b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/b912f71c1f3872c295e00356194ced769cc8c8d0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXK1+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMCoQAAxnD2dZwKj0xD1P2B9yO/Wt\nEq3L5tB4cTB8TrcZsdADmpgzeQ4PRrlfDoUflos4XT1+pD4/55KH2oBTQL/CPp8S\ndWT68VQRvl3BGQ5As618XVdXKuS3afM+BeX8Qlwl/niF+pxCNfgJXiZDs6q2M/9Z\nLieQhyWLfCc+59aSmymVpLX1sLJshaxcwjW3W17QlUX+YBC38eY9Nm6yDEvfPEUt\nERHrWuFPFbWiCEzp+SNfrya88tN4HJT3Q/68giydOA8RlhuxvwnnALG2WovFXkt4\n8jfD2ZtPA0lUQYL//jldkFNKLI9KxUODEH7v3eKdMRqP2Sfi6XxKEHVID1c3TFey\n8Ul7RsQAYFZC0GCOD2d2y9sjl9wai5/6wUgjVqt7BFGux06T29EdLslZKkAJtHTm\nSzhIlRDW7HIZzYZ3JQuYkxDWoYoDyrruBvgRLwlX+xyE9k3AlWORJuIkYW4laGcr\nfHRYGKjgxEW+FaWq7Hdkmr6HKd/op1E53XrqTTRzklH9+fwr2W8dPYaqbI6iqTMV\nxkCGsBf9R5ARGRyYbOzSA6h+aeJgm2xHN+4wT/9SCrcNG6ZoUWWH1G1mUSl8hG7s\nAiXo9mz8EYaYLD1GUtzsOtOCgnJMJ0HFl1xFhicGOZ/LlZmVNlC5bizi5Mbf1Gp1\nmQPxCu8dAfskGHRHjIxB\n=Tua1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3c190c27c2cd92ce921bd2d4e8bbcb59f8c713b5\nparent 5f35603ea86904abbb268ff815d14424104743ee\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1784458622 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784458622 +0300\n\nfix(fleet): dedup the outdated-plugin heartbeat warning (#574)\n\n## Why (finding #2 from the 2026-07-19 prod error review)\n`POST /fleet/heartbeat` logs a WARNING every tick a plugin is below\n`MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION`. A node stuck on an old plugin\nheartbeats ~every 20–60s forever, so it floods: prod produced **6,301\nlines/day** from just **3 internal nodes** — `eyal-open-claw-1` on\nplugin `1.0.1` (~every 20s), a container on `2.8.0`, and\n`shushants-MacBook-Air` on `2.5.0`. That volume drowns real warnings now\nthat log severity classifies correctly (#561).\n\n## What\nGate the warning through a per-`(node, version)` dedup with a 1h window\n— a module-level TTL cache, bounded (5000) + oldest-evicted, mirroring\nthe auth-api cache idiom. The fleet-health signal still surfaces\n(once/hour/stuck node) without the per-tick spam. Keyed on `(node,\nversion)` so a version change re-logs promptly. Per-instance (not shared\nacross Cloud Run instances), so worst case is one line per instance per\nnode per hour — still orders of magnitude below one per tick.\n\n**Behaviour otherwise unchanged** — the auto-upgrade queueing path is\nuntouched; only the log is throttled.\n\n## Tests\n5 new unit tests (appended to `test_fleet_heartbeat_auto_upgrade.py`):\ndedup, version-change re-log, per-node isolation, window expiry, size\ncap. Full file 61 pass; `ruff`/`mypy` clean.\n\n## Ops follow-up (not code)\nThe 3 stuck nodes are all internal (a teammate's box, a container, a\nlaptop) — worth nudging them to upgrade or decommissioning, but not a\ncustomer-fleet problem.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-19T10:57:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b912f71c1f3872c295e00356194ced769cc8c8d0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b912f71c1f3872c295e00356194ced769cc8c8d0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b912f71c1f3872c295e00356194ced769cc8c8d0/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","follow