,"events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9c39fd0295380d08846b2e1578009980f267eae2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9c39fd0295380d08846b2e1578009980f267eae2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9c39fd0295380d08846b2e1578009980f267eae2"}]},{"sha":"9c39fd0295380d08846b2e1578009980f267eae2","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDljMzlmZDAyOTUzODBkMDg4NDZiMmUxNTc4MDA5OTgwZjI2N2VhZTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-16T08:43:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-16T08:43:26Z"},"message":"fix(agent-digest): drop placeholder rows + stop 'thin memories' narratives (#557)\n\nContent fixes to the agent-activity digest generator, from reviewing the\nlive eToro output (where 2/3 of a run's rows were dead\n`error`/placeholder rows and the one real summary complained the\nmemories were \"extremely thin\").\n\n## 1. No more generic placeholder rows\nWhen the LLM is unavailable (fallback tier) or returns no narrative, the\nagent is now **skipped** — logged, but **no row written**. Previously it\npersisted a generic `\"<agent> recorded N durable memories this period\"`\nplaceholder, which is noise in the report. Only rows with a real LLM\nnarrative are stored.\n- `generate_for_org` run summary: `fallback` → `skipped`;\n`run_agent_digest` rolls up `agent_skipped`.\n\n## 2. Prompt no longer complains about sparse memories\nThe prompt explicitly forbids meta-commentary on the amount/quality of\nmemories (\"thin\", \"sparse\", \"untitled\", \"what's missing\"). When there's\nno substantive work, the model returns exactly:\n> No significant work by \\<name\\> has been recorded during this period.\nwith empty sections — a clean statement instead of a critique.\n\n## Tests\nUpdated the LLM-unavailable and empty-narrative unit tests to assert\n**no row + `skipped`**. 15/15 generator tests green; ruff + format +\nmypy clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0c73872288eab27467f1c3a830bb33aa2e286bd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/0c73872288eab27467f1c3a830bb33aa2e286bd2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/9c39fd0295380d08846b2e1578009980f267eae2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWJmuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdIMQAGiwoucVLP/o2WNCI11PzVIY\npDjEzEL22/IbozilV8EisYGVTZjCRyCRbzTuPcPB7/J7aKfVKpoYsML55+L74oeW\nBzXaInY2F4BV4nRQINWdAToKpJuuNYsXEuBzr9SsVQpuGtmBnP2mq2y7AZY6wYyN\n+CshZdvuq+NpOQ3js9jx7Tmg5niG1GRLyCDeH/naF803J31scjlSYMIriYyTZksx\nX7t3i4UCM6smF2uo/zlO0BlCBcKm9BOdd8WxIHgdHYTZWQhEp+jqUAJMT6n3Mi7y\nwL1mGoHuJqqSI3n0Rci7DSsejEHsypcCTmRUUEOwpbROC+XGJsqxlKtxTb+N5oit\nJFmfJexiDaa/H9zakCbpUjrOmn6VRVF+57JIbh1mm6qeZD+b4Vpw54y3+SznHVEQ\n4C2dgwsx6bD9dV2Lxu0i6by7zMea6tHW7ykVJF+yNC45T+td/U04C0sdsFvHqJq7\nI+d+YBsVY7f6fcfx0Q1+V1J6LNKhGDkU/s7Bs6wlkpZWlvdowcRFfVGKfqB7EtYF\neOrZAtop7lBAcUdwEhAzsrNhTWC1wmj1k2EckCTZzfNKHfHQmXsE+ngtDbUTKgmq\nCDhZcBdSxhYFSzxLMuRxHBxD8HH8kgBm5jlSt6H9ep2PjxbKa+5XQqIy0ZqId662\n3tLS6P/5nYfEm6ASTyCp\n=pmtP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0c73872288eab27467f1c3a830bb33aa2e286bd2\nparent 42c76f9d7778b4cbe2e62dcde3d88fe6a9845862\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1784191406 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784191406 +0300\n\nfix(agent-digest): drop placeholder rows + stop 'thin memories' narratives (#557)\n\nContent fixes to the agent-activity digest generator, from reviewing the\nlive eToro output (where 2/3 of a run's rows were dead\n`error`/placeholder rows and the one real summary complained the\nmemories were \"extremely thin\").\n\n## 1. No more generic placeholder rows\nWhen the LLM is unavailable (fallback tier) or returns no narrative, the\nagent is now **skipped** — logged, but **no row written**. Previously it\npersisted a generic `\"<agent> recorded N durable memories this period\"`\nplaceholder, which is noise in the report. Only rows with a real LLM\nnarrative are stored.\n- `generate_for_org` run summary: `fallback` → `skipped`;\n`run_agent_digest` rolls up `agent_skipped`.\n\n## 2. Prompt no longer complains about sparse memories\nThe prompt explicitly forbids meta-commentary on the amount/quality of\nmemories (\"thin\", \"sparse\", \"untitled\", \"what's missing\"). When there's\nno substantive work, the model returns exactly:\n> No significant work by \\<name\\> has been recorded during this period.\nwith empty sections — a clean statement instead of a critique.\n\n## Tests\nUpdated the LLM-unavailable and empty-narrative unit tests to assert\n**no row + `skipped`**. 15/15 generator tests green; ruff + format +\nmypy clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-16T08:43:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9c39fd0295380d08846b2e1578009980f267eae2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9c39fd0295380d08846b2e1578009980f267eae2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9c39fd0295380d08846b2e1578009980f267eae2/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"42c76f9d7778b4cbe2e62dcde3d88fe6a9845862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/42c76f9d7778b4cbe2e62dcde3d88fe6a9845862","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/42c76f9d7778b4cbe2e62dcde3d88fe6a9845862"}]},{"sha":"42c76f9d7778b4cbe2e62dcde3d88fe6a9845862","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDQyYzc2ZjlkNzc3OGI0Y2JlMmU2MmRjZGUzZDg4ZmU2YTk4NDU4NjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-15T13:32:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-15T13:32:29Z"},"message":"feat(memories): attribute broker bulk writes to the originating agent (#556)\n\n## What\n\nA broker (install-credential) bulk write carries no request-level\n`agent_id`, so the cloud attributed every such write to a synthetic\n`broker:<install_uuid>` identity — the memory view (Prism) shows\n`broker-<id>`, with no way to tell **which agent** produced a memory\n(feedback from the broker walkthrough).\n\n## How\n\nmemclawd **Layer 1** (already merged, `caura-ai/memclawd#82`) now stamps\neach capture's `metadata.agent_id` with the capturing agent. **Layer 2**\n(this PR): when a broker batch's per-item metadata **unanimously** names\none agent, attribute the write to that agent — so the memory view names\nit. A **mixed batch**, or a **pre-Layer-1 broker** (v0.8.3, no per-item\n`agent_id`), falls back to `broker:<install_uuid>` — the exact prior\nbehavior, so a write is **never mis-attributed**.\n\nNew pure helper `_broker_write_agent_id(items, install_uuid)` in\n`routes/memories.py`, wired into the install-credential branch of the\nbulk-write handler.\n\n## Scope\n\nAttribution stays **request-level** (one `agent_id` per batch —\n`get_or_create_agent` / fleet-enforcement / quota / idempotency all\nassume this). Per-item attribution (each memory to its own agent) would\nrequire re-scoping all of those and is a larger multi-layer change, out\nof scope for this cut. In practice memclawd flushes one agent's captures\nper batch, so the unanimous case is the common one; mixed batches simply\ndegrade to today's behavior.\n\n## Tests\n\n`core-api/tests/test_broker_write_attribution.py` — unit tests for the\nhelper: unanimous → agent, mixed → install, no-metadata → install,\nempty-id ignored, single-named-among-unnamed → agent, missing install →\n`broker:unknown`. ruff + mypy clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0fca0af1a05776e1eb40ea39a40dd292b53927b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/0fca0af1a05776e1eb40ea39a40dd292b53927b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/42c76f9d7778b4cbe2e62dcde3d88fe6a9845862","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV4vtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvowQAClSd88dtiDzKgkvhFzAyAtB\ntK3WIhCd1YOTsRqBLADmjOANBpD+UG5hEPLxFTZBTm5bZ889BVsx1+aIrdVyZ8qD\nkMaPzj5MQ3cQ+HlbvhQ1aQ2sRRnwgoX3eXM38oKlQzuOJ+IFqxz+V0Yv+4uUaL2Z\nAAWjQsyRYGDXM6YoGcSCpLp5nM/CT0VwnsMyeF5v2SABcqJBktCfRFx9IIdvEfxU\nKDXu4RHQw5Bu48B2aN/RL9FuIHi1GpsuJebaWjqBQpm/nzhxDWn08lvEv9ctmym8\n+iQDir+lWmfgplJw7UehFzB4VgERjdPxVDAEtr+RBHvIPj/3ilpPZKOca+EhKayc\nScShYNUpmF5zdT5Sh4XdeuNuop703YTMh3iPcs5pqE6gXhskYomAo9C0Ufdipg5A\nMqO5MgmZtrDqph/U7zX8wq9w05MBH6KbKoM8d7Prm4LfH0jcdIvvnDpL8qn/C66x\nsWjTi6Mr0vK0XJHRIgPCa+bezF5zPchtbbzhvi15NrClI2DkcS4Fr4kUJKs5lLBN\nORwyrCay1QEaSPCULxqvXVTYF0MLMNWAfoevxlmrK0/aKbiqwjfh/CrjpYnsrVzg\nMHYT0LUHAppYd6SOoKxAYShDey/DvS7B+DOTz9JRd8XFoL8oaEYbbn6RTBbg/SDR\nQiUI0gqcVKuPSrGjR0JX\n=KVqc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0fca0af1a05776e1eb40ea39a40dd292b53927b5\nparent c2ea3df2ccb85a523ada427041ecdaceb05ad112\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1784122349 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784122349 +0300\n\nfeat(memories): attribute broker bulk writes to the originating agent (#556)\n\n## What\n\nA broker (install-credential) bulk write carries no request-level\n`agent_id`, so the cloud attributed every such write to a synthetic\n`broker:<install_uuid>` identity — the memory view (Prism) shows\n`broker-<id>`, with no way to tell **which agent** produced a memory\n(feedback from the broker walkthrough).\n\n## How\n\nmemclawd **Layer 1** (already merged, `caura-ai/memclawd#82`) now stamps\neach capture's `metadata.agent_id` with the capturing agent. **Layer 2**\n(this PR): when a broker batch's per-item metadata **unanimously** names\none agent, attribute the write to that agent — so the memory view names\nit. A **mixed batch**, or a **pre-Layer-1 broker** (v0.8.3, no per-item\n`agent_id`), falls back to `broker:<install_uuid>` — the exact prior\nbehavior, so a write is **never mis-attributed**.\n\nNew pure helper `_broker_write_agent_id(items, install_uuid)` in\n`routes/memories.py`, wired into the install-credential branch of the\nbulk-write handler.\n\n## Scope\n\nAttribution stays **request-level** (one `agent_id` per batch —\n`get_or_create_agent` / fleet-enforcement / quota / idempotency all\nassume this). Per-item attribution (each memory to its own agent) would\nrequire re-scoping all of those and is a larger multi-layer change, out\nof scope for this cut. In practice memclawd flushes one agent's captures\nper batch, so the unanimous case is the common one; mixed batches simply\ndegrade to today's behavior.\n\n## Tests\n\n`core-api/tests/test_broker_write_attribution.py` — unit tests for the\nhelper: unanimous → agent, mixed → install, no-metadata → install,\nempty-id ignored, single-named-among-unnamed → agent, missing install →\n`broker:unknown`. ruff + mypy clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-15T13:32:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/42c76f9d7778b4cbe2e62dcde3d88fe6a9845862","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/42c76f9d7778b4cbe2e62dcde3d88fe6a9845862","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/42c76f9d7778b4cbe2e62dcde3d88fe6a9845862/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c2ea3df2ccb85a523ada427041ecdaceb05ad112","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c2ea3df2ccb85a523ada427041ecdaceb05ad112","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/c2ea3df2ccb85a523ada427041ecdaceb05ad112"}]},{"sha":"c2ea3df2ccb85a523ada427041ecdaceb05ad112","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGMyZWEzZGYyY2NiODVhNTIzYWRhNDI3MDQxZWNkYWNlYjA1YWQxMTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-13T12:04:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T12:04:18Z"},"message":"fix(recall): don't inflate recall_count on agentless recalls (A26) (#549)\n\n## Problem\n\n`recall_count` is a per-memory *\"an agent found this useful\"* signal,\nand it feeds `recall_boost` in scoring. `TrackRecalls` bumps it for\n**every** `/search` return — including **agentless** traffic:\nliveness/health probes, monitoring pollers, and dashboard/admin queries\nthat hit `/search` with no agent identity.\n\nNone of those are an agent using memory, yet they:\n- inflate `recall_count` (and the `recall_boost` that rides on it) with\nnon-agent noise, and\n- let a repeating automated caller **pin a single memory's counter** —\ne.g. a health check calling `/search` thousands of times a day at\n`top_k=1` hammers one memory's `recall_count`, which then gets boosted\nfor everyone.\n\n## Fix\n\nSkip the `recall_count` bump when there's no caller agent identity:\n\n```python\nif not ctx.data.get(\"caller_agent_id\"):\n    return None\n```\n\n`caller_agent_id` is the authenticated identity (`filter_agent_id` or\n`auth.agent_id`), so **genuine agent recalls still count** — including\ncross-agent recalls that omit `filter_agent_id` and fall back to\n`auth.agent_id`. Search **results are returned unchanged**; only the\ncounter increment is skipped.\n\n## Why it generalizes\n\nThis isn't specific to one deployment — any environment with automated\n`/search` callers (health checks, monitoring, pipelines, dashboards)\ncurrently skews the usefulness signal and the `recall_boost` derived\nfrom it. Restricting the counter to identified-agent recalls makes\n`recall_count` mean what it's supposed to mean everywhere. (Addresses\ngap **A26** — self-reinforcing `recall_boost` with no usefulness\nsignal.)\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_track_recalls_agentless.py` — bump fires for a real agent,\nis skipped for `None`/empty caller identity, and is a no-op when there\nare no rows. Guard logic also verified standalone against the real\n`TrackRecalls.execute`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"f03fe43e9dd2309d6b712964bf3c1fecb411b229","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f03fe43e9dd2309d6b712964bf3c1fecb411b229"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/c2ea3df2ccb85a523ada427041ecdaceb05ad112","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVNRCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvmcQAIgmn2D9jWlXJoEFTcdGXU4F\nBWR6yo8gZnvjpS1YYqpYlY+69wDVPJlKJI/lnMb0MnWU4ifa5KxAyY4VKQ+m28QN\nPH30Bo3aMJ1hJO0g/ag9eandvaKllhd0tDIy0ZFK3gBD2TooPY0Pc1VX/6KyTjxw\n5XRp8HiQL7VMUzst9Jsbn5eXpwVj5tXQKmNT4SX3ZzNdT1H02e5DNochdmRarUBG\n/GVtO42aEGw2B75RC/dAqzF9DPV7ec95pb+4T7coBL7ujDbLUVJbCw6lXVyxx2AI\nxmFCrSiH/F9SMRJv6jZOQiHhf1meAt1oxMZR6elTnu+eV9nStMGcGWTm1i8de0R8\n4zDRoyf0Unl2UIRyGDsI6Z6zQIU7nrQPILAo7wdJfXbaRGEWHNee8MKNviCfh1To\n6x3SA9Eh2r4VD5E1qL8Nsj8YMwEqQnJZ303StSMBpdH1Vq0PKqCTRi6htDwxwhF1\nXa94aVcqCt+UIDACQwPuxJBhyOOE433RZqMVimPTvkCOpAKAXtPvtVpG3sNF+K2J\nHdchrVlloT0oyyOR/M9t28Fd4OHjcC7J2kc4G4s08n83aS3TyPcjZTL1gzapHkYK\nuz3rVfV2HEyZ5zsXbZtwgzLoSssba//TQqtk7l7Iv1SaMHEFW5fMi2mNGDKftfeP\n2sSwcnRkuR1YcjRu7IU5\n=FyQD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f03fe43e9dd2309d6b712964bf3c1fecb411b229\nparent 84459e90a33805a02a1074abe47d35689bb43a89\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1783944258 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783944258 +0300\n\nfix(recall): don't inflate recall_count on agentless recalls (A26) (#549)\n\n## Problem\n\n`recall_count` is a per-memory *\"an agent found this useful\"* signal,\nand it feeds `recall_boost` in scoring. `TrackRecalls` bumps it for\n**every** `/search` return — including **agentless** traffic:\nliveness/health probes, monitoring pollers, and dashboard/admin queries\nthat hit `/search` with no agent identity.\n\nNone of those are an agent using memory, yet they:\n- inflate `recall_count` (and the `recall_boost` that rides on it) with\nnon-agent noise, and\n- let a repeating automated caller **pin a single memory's counter** —\ne.g. a health check calling `/search` thousands of times a day at\n`top_k=1` hammers one memory's `recall_count`, which then gets boosted\nfor everyone.\n\n## Fix\n\nSkip the `recall_count` bump when there's no caller agent identity:\n\n```python\nif not ctx.data.get(\"caller_agent_id\"):\n    return None\n```\n\n`caller_agent_id` is the authenticated identity (`filter_agent_id` or\n`auth.agent_id`), so **genuine agent recalls still count** — including\ncross-agent recalls that omit `filter_agent_id` and fall back to\n`auth.agent_id`. Search **results are returned unchanged**; only the\ncounter increment is skipped.\n\n## Why it generalizes\n\nThis isn't specific to one deployment — any environment with automated\n`/search` callers (health checks, monitoring, pipelines, dashboards)\ncurrently skews the usefulness signal and the `recall_boost` derived\nfrom it. Restricting the counter to identified-agent recalls makes\n`recall_count` mean what it's supposed to mean everywhere. (Addresses\ngap **A26** — self-reinforcing `recall_boost` with no usefulness\nsignal.)\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_track_recalls_agentless.py` — bump fires for a real agent,\nis skipped for `None`/empty caller identity, and is a no-op when there\nare no rows. Guard logic also verified standalone against the real\n`TrackRecalls.execute`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-13T12:04:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c2ea3df2ccb85a523ada427041ecdaceb05ad112","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/c2ea3df2ccb85a523ada427041ecdaceb05ad112","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c2ea3df2ccb85a523ada427041ecdaceb05ad112/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"84459e90a33805a02a1074abe47d35689bb43a89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/84459e90a33805a02a1074abe47d35689bb43a89","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/84459e90a33805a02a1074abe47d35689bb43a89"}]},{"sha":"84459e90a33805a02a1074abe47d35689bb43a89","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDg0NDU5ZTkwYTMzODA1YTAyYTEwNzRhYmU0N2QzNTY4OWJiNDNhODk","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-13T08:41:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-13T08:41:05Z"},"message":"fix(reports): salvage empty-narrative digests + period-scaled activity floor (#545)\n\n## Why\nProd review of the merged daily agent-activity digest (both eToro\nfleets) showed near-empty output. The latest daily run produced **3 rows\nacross two 300+-agent tenants**, and **2 of 3 were dead `error` rows**\n(`memclaw-insighter`, `\"LLM returned no narrative\"`) that render blank\nin the UI.\n\nGrounded findings (read-only prod queries):\n- **Sparse daily activity is the real bottleneck**, not the corpus: only\n~3 distinct agents/tenant write durable memories per *day* (vs 8–13 per\n*week*). `episode` (32k/7d — the raw firehose) is the only excluded type\nand correctly so; the shared noise-title filter drops genuine\nheartbeat/health noise (34% of `action`, 61% of `outcome`). **Corpus\nleft untouched** — loosening it mostly re-admits noise and is shared\nwith the live report.\n- `min_activity_threshold=3` over a 1-day window then trims the ~3 daily\nagents down to ~1.\n- Empty-narrative responses became blank `error` rows (worse than a\nplaceholder).\n\n## What\n1. **Salvage empty narratives** → `fallback` (not `error`). If a real\nresponse omits the narrative, synthesize a terse one from the structured\n`sections` (`\"Agent: 2 decisions, 1 shipped item across N durable\nmemories.\"`); `error_detail` records why. Actual exceptions still →\n`error`.\n2. **Period-scaled activity floor**: daily floors to `1` (surface every\nactive agent); weekly keeps the configurable `min_activity_threshold`.\n\nNot included (separate, by design): making **weekly the primary UI\nsurface** (data is 4–5× richer weekly) and verifying the weekly cron is\nlive on-prem for Monday — tracked separately.\n\n## Tests\n`test_daily_threshold_is_one` (day floor 1 vs week floor 3), rewrote the\nempty-narrative test to assert `fallback` + synthesized narrative,\nupdated the threshold test to `week`. ruff + format + mypy clean (186\nfiles); 16 generator unit tests green.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d9057d2c515fd7c05a26009a310c6e5967bc4e85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/d9057d2c515fd7c05a26009a310c6e5967bc4e85"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/84459e90a33805a02a1074abe47d35689bb43a89","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVKShCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxlQQAHKHeJPR34d+NSTd6elZloia\nnEhe+uCIRO+d02KHGL4dCx487i+x8ONGh5wBHmVgae/AGma09XdvR39jiHtdJeN6\nAe6sTrMMVv1Ms744L6k0mvi2wRpMTsSDYFBGPHdjJadakYIiAFe4n8lKBPP4454W\nmeAPNZ6mB2f/0XbWqbp6qqcpNBP7NnWprL1lmdMYg4QETGvPdTBxhS7HKA0BRypO\noshM26x7Ha8VD7BuY1f4LSLIDvhmV+SvfmG8BSFlgIoypYcSDPXD4Ua5g6NFBOgB\nGLbqO1svlm1qMqU+EnNe9wt/PPDMxLPfyvk02Cz/DJhERvzny9KtgUopFl4oA6fM\nYgcm5mdaUeSfHIOfMyFrB0uYBl38bIiNxfedIAuXd/7QaztI9JUXDe0CLZLQBSMw\njpXC5vwBFMHkKVOxbl86BcKcOaAtIYFjIuw6D9tGQivPT6LfSa0p4NhXJ4/JxD9Y\nVfmENiz852Ula9HiBkbbOnkiTCA1WarU+sYp4YMeRBuUKn0qPmEy2wTjM/X0MRUN\nCaiWkCth5ld7+emXFfWSaUcjzxc1gmzUhZL0IVohC0eErvvmkIG4R06CeIUWYOCk\nWydLrlfrxC4b2S55gK7X/oheA++4Uaf620WFzn3Xfs3t5hU5HY+eVKDA78iydDxn\nlntUCamrvhaDQ5ANb3qS\n=g/By\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d9057d2c515fd7c05a26009a310c6e5967bc4e85\nparent 00a9f85e53fbb0d1fb0d9daecc5dd1fb18cf1904\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1783932065 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783932065 +0300\n\nfix(reports): salvage empty-narrative digests + period-scaled activity floor (#545)\n\n## Why\nProd review of the merged daily agent-activity digest (both eToro\nfleets) showed near-empty output. The latest daily run produced **3 rows\nacross two 300+-agent tenants**, and **2 of 3 were dead `error` rows**\n(`memclaw-insighter`, `\"LLM returned no narrative\"`) that render blank\nin the UI.\n\nGrounded findings (read-only prod queries):\n- **Sparse daily activity is the real bottleneck**, not the corpus: only\n~3 distinct agents/tenant write durable memories per *day* (vs 8–13 per\n*week*). `episode` (32k/7d — the raw firehose) is the only excluded type\nand correctly so; the shared noise-title filter drops genuine\nheartbeat/health noise (34% of `action`, 61% of `outcome`). **Corpus\nleft untouched** — loosening it mostly re-admits noise and is shared\nwith the live report.\n- `min_activity_threshold=3` over a 1-day window then trims the ~3 daily\nagents down to ~1.\n- Empty-narrative responses became blank `error` rows (worse than a\nplaceholder).\n\n## What\n1. **Salvage empty narratives** → `fallback` (not `error`). If a real\nresponse omits the narrative, synthesize a terse one from the structured\n`sections` (`\"Agent: 2 decisions, 1 shipped item across N durable\nmemories.\"`); `error_detail` records why. Actual exceptions still →\n`error`.\n2. **Period-scaled activity floor**: daily floors to `1` (surface every\nactive agent); weekly keeps the configurable `min_activity_threshold`.\n\nNot included (separate, by design): making **weekly the primary UI\nsurface** (data is 4–5× richer weekly) and verifying the weekly cron is\nlive on-prem for Monday — tracked separately.\n\n## Tests\n`test_daily_threshold_is_one` (day floor 1 vs week floor 3), rewrote the\nempty-narrative test to assert `fallback` + synthesized narrative,\nupdated the threshold test to `week`. ruff + format + mypy clean (186\nfiles); 16 generator unit tests green.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-13T08:41:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/84459e90a33805a02a1074abe47d35689bb43a89","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/84459e90a33805a02a1074abe47d35689bb43a89","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/84459e90a33805a02a1074abe47d35689bb43a89/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"00a9f85e53fbb0d1fb0d9daecc5dd1fb18cf1904","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/00a9f85e53fbb0d1fb0d9daecc5dd1fb18cf1904","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/00a9f85e53fbb0d1fb0d9daecc5dd1fb18cf1904"}]},{"sha":"00a9f85e53fbb0d1fb0d9daecc5dd1fb18cf1904","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDAwYTlmODVlNTNmYmIwZDFmYjBkOWRhZWNjNWRkMWZiMThjZjE5MDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","e