n\nSigned-off-by: release-please[bot] <release-please[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: caura-deploy-bot[bot] <265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-12T11:29:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/00a9f85e53fbb0d1fb0d9daecc5dd1fb18cf1904","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/00a9f85e53fbb0d1fb0d9daecc5dd1fb18cf1904","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/00a9f85e53fbb0d1fb0d9daecc5dd1fb18cf1904/comments","author":{"login":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","id":265395343,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOD9Gcjw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229147182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/caura-deploy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2adad51b4c5ad0699da84058a3f969ff927e540a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2adad51b4c5ad0699da84058a3f969ff927e540a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2adad51b4c5ad0699da84058a3f969ff927e540a"}]},{"sha":"2adad51b4c5ad0699da84058a3f969ff927e540a","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDJhZGFkNTFiNGM1YWQwNjk5ZGE4NDA1OGEzZjk2OWZmOTI3ZTU0MGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-09T11:17:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T11:17:10Z"},"message":"feat(reports): weekly agent-digest cron tick [CAURA-222] (#543)\n\n## Weekly agent-digest generation\n\nPhase 2c registered a nightly tick that only generates `period=day`, so\nthe reports UI's **\"week\" toggle shows nothing**. This adds a weekly\nwall-clock-aligned tick that fires `period=week`.\n\n- **scheduler**: `seconds_until_next_utc_weekday_hour(weekday, hour)` —\nMon..Sun alignment with the same strict-future / no-hot-loop guarantee\nas the existing daily helper.\n- **config**: `AGENT_DIGEST_WEEKLY_RUN_AT_WEEKDAY` (0=Mon, default) +\n`AGENT_DIGEST_WEEKLY_RUN_AT_HOUR` (default 03:00 UTC, just after\nMonday's daily tick so the just-closed Mon–Mon window is covered), both\nvalidated.\n- **tasks**: `run_agent_digest_weekly_tick` → `POST\n/admin/reports/agent-digest/run?period=week`.\n- **app**: registers `agent-digest-weekly` (7-day interval, weekly\n`delay_provider`).\n\n### Also fixes a stale test\n`test_app._EXPECTED_JOBS` never included the daily `agent-digest` job\nadded in Phase 2c (core-operations tests aren't in the CI gate, so it\nslipped through). This adds both jobs and gives the weekly job a 7-day\ndelay bound in the alignment assertion.\n\n### Testing\nFull core-operations suite green (41 tests), incl. 5 new scheduler cases\nfor the weekday helper + the weekly-tick test. ruff + format + mypy\nclean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2ab6a851d7d4c7e68cdf837495165fae12eb47a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/2ab6a851d7d4c7e68cdf837495165fae12eb47a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/2adad51b4c5ad0699da84058a3f969ff927e540a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT4M2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOmkQAIHCgJvSw3Zxm2URII+jY3QN\ncWqt3up5dfGG24pmeWP2BNo13ggUn082uwGUtdZrawI7j6BzRZqn3/xKkezefv7u\nV/OtRp0ur5Ez4Gv9go2p/U9KBQIAty755l7sDRHvvH83Rd2mO+r5l86Gq4iUAA3q\nfzdQmjmloOGsH8hi/pnDahFBq5wsZPG8c6F9zrsHmIjPh7z0hTekX6OYDRsKBx4j\nFumClodl86/g0Os+jcEHG0nrfbn0S71OlXU0blKZpS1wALSfZBnQYdEqSUQjoZgI\ne5qwrMChAKCdBRbywlHJ38OSwJPAVsgOmqFow7GqhcXSdGETczMHN3mYC1pGgrBl\nPTvP5giRPYN5AULeieTYJqOWj0hUekJWAkWNZfD/CDM3lBc+bg4sWW8gL8QCeD4i\n655EwzQznR7FYhPcIswkNpnN6DZl/DGH1AW2/ruowvHC9isfPaiEUWtve4exVD9g\ntofIX5mB6tZ5lU6YSJaXfXmuq/XIkMwKi2ia5nDGT7tSJ0wJ+V6E3jIcC5pQe9ML\n8DKcfQAEt4adWagHUlb5YHegRlodvfz3LNOwyjroVc1Hmn2PQz7dqBpJQejyVk7H\nMjboDhZOl0yEiAi/LlazqkG0/qAAqf7od+4pk0DFMDAdzochVOynxhgtKaV3KLwR\nHjMRbhoaMGExwH5bA31y\n=bMsz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2ab6a851d7d4c7e68cdf837495165fae12eb47a1\nparent e74413d22e98fd838a6899af9b2989c2952ae06a\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1783595830 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783595830 +0300\n\nfeat(reports): weekly agent-digest cron tick [CAURA-222] (#543)\n\n## Weekly agent-digest generation\n\nPhase 2c registered a nightly tick that only generates `period=day`, so\nthe reports UI's **\"week\" toggle shows nothing**. This adds a weekly\nwall-clock-aligned tick that fires `period=week`.\n\n- **scheduler**: `seconds_until_next_utc_weekday_hour(weekday, hour)` —\nMon..Sun alignment with the same strict-future / no-hot-loop guarantee\nas the existing daily helper.\n- **config**: `AGENT_DIGEST_WEEKLY_RUN_AT_WEEKDAY` (0=Mon, default) +\n`AGENT_DIGEST_WEEKLY_RUN_AT_HOUR` (default 03:00 UTC, just after\nMonday's daily tick so the just-closed Mon–Mon window is covered), both\nvalidated.\n- **tasks**: `run_agent_digest_weekly_tick` → `POST\n/admin/reports/agent-digest/run?period=week`.\n- **app**: registers `agent-digest-weekly` (7-day interval, weekly\n`delay_provider`).\n\n### Also fixes a stale test\n`test_app._EXPECTED_JOBS` never included the daily `agent-digest` job\nadded in Phase 2c (core-operations tests aren't in the CI gate, so it\nslipped through). This adds both jobs and gives the weekly job a 7-day\ndelay bound in the alignment assertion.\n\n### Testing\nFull core-operations suite green (41 tests), incl. 5 new scheduler cases\nfor the weekday helper + the weekly-tick test. ruff + format + mypy\nclean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-09T11:17:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2adad51b4c5ad0699da84058a3f969ff927e540a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2adad51b4c5ad0699da84058a3f969ff927e540a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2adad51b4c5ad0699da84058a3f969ff927e540a/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e74413d22e98fd838a6899af9b2989c2952ae06a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e74413d22e98fd838a6899af9b2989c2952ae06a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e74413d22e98fd838a6899af9b2989c2952ae06a"}]},{"sha":"e74413d22e98fd838a6899af9b2989c2952ae06a","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGU3NDQxM2QyMmU5OGZkODM4YTY4OTlhZjliMjk4OWMyOTUyYWUwNmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-08T17:14:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-08T17:14:55Z"},"message":"feat(insights): give the nightly insights run a dedicated registered identity (#540)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe scheduled nightly insights pass had **no caller identity**, so it\nfell through to the generic `DEFAULT_AGENT_ID = \"mcp-agent\"` — an\n*unregistered*, anonymous id that also catches any caller who specifies\nnothing. Consequences:\n\n- Its writes never surfaced in **Prism** or the **per-agent report** —\nthere's no matching `agents` row to join against.\n- It was conflated with unrelated anonymous traffic under one shared\n`mcp-agent` bucket.\n\n(On prod, `mcp-agent` was the top \"agent\" on etoro0/etoro-core purely\nbecause of this — 100% of those writes were\n`client_request_id='insights:%'`.)\n\n## Change\n\nGive the automated run its own registerable identity,\n`memclaw-insighter`:\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `agent_ids.py` | Add `INSIGHTER_AGENT_ID = \"memclaw-insighter\"` +\n`INSIGHTER_TRUST_LEVEL = 3`, distinct from the generic `mcp-agent`\nfallback |\n| `services/lifecycle_audit.py` | `insights()` attributes\n`generate_insights(agent_id=INSIGHTER_AGENT_ID)` and **self-registers**\nthe agent (idempotent `create_or_update_agent`, `ON CONFLICT DO\nNOTHING`) as `belonging_type='service'`, trust 3, before persisting |\n| `migrations/030` | Backfill the same registration for tenants that\nalready hold `memclaw-insighter` memories, so Prism/reports show it\nimmediately |\n\n**Registration timing** = lazy, on first run: the first nightly insights\nrun for any tenant (new or existing) registers the agent; a tenant with\n`auto_insights_enabled` off registers nothing (no phantom agent). No\ncross-repo tenant-provisioning hook needed.\n\n**Privileges:** `service`/trust 3 grants cross-fleet read (≥2, needed\nfor `scope='all'`) and write (≥3, it persists `scope_org`). The\nautomated path calls the service directly and bypasses the route trust\ngate, so this is future-proofing for any gated re-route.\n\n**Scope guard:** interactive MCP/REST callers are unaffected — they pass\ntheir real `agent_id` via `resolve_caller_and_gate`. Only the\nidentity-less automated path changes. The generic `mcp-agent` fallback\nis intentionally left in place.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `test_lifecycle_audit.py`: automated run attributes to\n`memclaw-insighter` + registers the service agent (trust 3); opt-out\nshort-circuits with no registration. 5/5 + 14 handler tests pass\nlocally.\n- Migration 030 validated against the live ORM schema: upgrade registers\nonly tenants with insighter memories, re-run is a no-op, downgrade\nremoves them.\n\n> Note: this is the persistence follow-up to the manual prod DB rename\nof `mcp-agent → memclaw-insighter` on etoro0/etoro-core.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f5f8e47a5b0120063fc488ed80a52dba2048a310","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f5f8e47a5b0120063fc488ed80a52dba2048a310"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/e74413d22e98fd838a6899af9b2989c2952ae06a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqToWPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKPkQAEIT2KPI0c4EedEuDgPfTSGH\nPGOoZcE9+4EF5VfeO3citG92Wa4kkWbalddA6I+kQYJQt0fGZX5vXRRK2vaZ4W5Y\nnSQCJDatIsf6hnSCaJFPfi2923MShS8iFlOita2a2KHNrEb/lQY4lnotN8coWV2J\nL52IwQfLQF+Jq1DCq7rbrT141HMwa1NnovORqMmAAoORFA2zedVa+XGaY3bPRLKB\nclwR+D53j4ElGc43i8rr5bDvTWyq0lK6KwUqe9wlGVSungzSxtXPH7mNxvZEP/19\n70NtDpMzosUSMYxHakR0NN+Z+3FY9sTfkgZUAkuHpJKYFXGVSDICRvG3SnIHjqNF\nlnxFh7YIWa4lShnbYBRHoUyFWsNz4Sb+oalUkzV4wrevFHrH5OBDgoADDHLfa/w2\n04BcZH0lw+79C/KkKwAUcFHJy32LH2+2sSoKNhEgz3d2SZHlF/mJynVx2Pg2DR+q\n2MtbyVZaZBzFUcYgJxdvT85aakZkB3aBIWCUgmNy8tOz1+AGgrJ20U0VA2xOpPAv\nEj3CfuQ4SSSky6fv+W373AEazx0Nxz4Wwt9h3JIVgHx+/Mo2xYr8+jS8c3kS4Qeb\nEgNboEqShMtcJ9Z3bCXgdYWUHoEaHnKWM8d/2vS5lpjNMSBfawM2bQhdycIq2+sP\noti3jmCDO4EcGxPfJvHf\n=AprC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f5f8e47a5b0120063fc488ed80a52dba2048a310\nparent 1d06fde7918deafbff41c5d06438c16fec82f24c\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1783530895 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783530895 +0300\n\nfeat(insights): give the nightly insights run a dedicated registered identity (#540)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe scheduled nightly insights pass had **no caller identity**, so it\nfell through to the generic `DEFAULT_AGENT_ID = \"mcp-agent\"` — an\n*unregistered*, anonymous id that also catches any caller who specifies\nnothing. Consequences:\n\n- Its writes never surfaced in **Prism** or the **per-agent report** —\nthere's no matching `agents` row to join against.\n- It was conflated with unrelated anonymous traffic under one shared\n`mcp-agent` bucket.\n\n(On prod, `mcp-agent` was the top \"agent\" on etoro0/etoro-core purely\nbecause of this — 100% of those writes were\n`client_request_id='insights:%'`.)\n\n## Change\n\nGive the automated run its own registerable identity,\n`memclaw-insighter`:\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `agent_ids.py` | Add `INSIGHTER_AGENT_ID = \"memclaw-insighter\"` +\n`INSIGHTER_TRUST_LEVEL = 3`, distinct from the generic `mcp-agent`\nfallback |\n| `services/lifecycle_audit.py` | `insights()` attributes\n`generate_insights(agent_id=INSIGHTER_AGENT_ID)` and **self-registers**\nthe agent (idempotent `create_or_update_agent`, `ON CONFLICT DO\nNOTHING`) as `belonging_type='service'`, trust 3, before persisting |\n| `migrations/030` | Backfill the same registration for tenants that\nalready hold `memclaw-insighter` memories, so Prism/reports show it\nimmediately |\n\n**Registration timing** = lazy, on first run: the first nightly insights\nrun for any tenant (new or existing) registers the agent; a tenant with\n`auto_insights_enabled` off registers nothing (no phantom agent). No\ncross-repo tenant-provisioning hook needed.\n\n**Privileges:** `service`/trust 3 grants cross-fleet read (≥2, needed\nfor `scope='all'`) and write (≥3, it persists `scope_org`). The\nautomated path calls the service directly and bypasses the route trust\ngate, so this is future-proofing for any gated re-route.\n\n**Scope guard:** interactive MCP/REST callers are unaffected — they pass\ntheir real `agent_id` via `resolve_caller_and_gate`. Only the\nidentity-less automated path changes. The generic `mcp-agent` fallback\nis intentionally left in place.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `test_lifecycle_audit.py`: automated run attributes to\n`memclaw-insighter` + registers the service agent (trust 3); opt-out\nshort-circuits with no registration. 5/5 + 14 handler tests pass\nlocally.\n- Migration 030 validated against the live ORM schema: upgrade registers\nonly tenants with insighter memories, re-run is a no-op, downgrade\nremoves them.\n\n> Note: this is the persistence follow-up to the manual prod DB rename\nof `mcp-agent → memclaw-insighter` on etoro0/etoro-core.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-08T17:14:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e74413d22e98fd838a6899af9b2989c2952ae06a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e74413d22e98fd838a6899af9b2989c2952ae06a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e74413d22e98fd838a6899af9b2989c2952ae06a/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1d06fde7918deafbff41c5d06438c16fec82f24c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1d06fde7918deafbff41c5d06438c16fec82f24c","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1d06fde7918deafbff41c5d06438c16fec82f24c"}]},{"sha":"1d06fde7918deafbff41c5d06438c16fec82f24c","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDFkMDZmZGU3OTE4ZGVhZmJmZjQxYzVkMDY0MzhjMTZmZWM4MmYyNGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-08T08:32:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-08T08:32:38Z"},"message":"chore(fleet): bump plugin auto-upgrade floor to 2.14.0 (#538)\n\n## What\nBump `MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION` **2.13.0 → 2.14.0** in\n`core_api/version_compat.py`, so eligible fleet nodes auto-upgrade to\nplugin 2.14.0.\n\n## Why\nIntended part of the v2.20.0 / onprem-v2.11.6 delivery: get plugin\n2.14.0 onto the fleet.\n\n**2.14.0 is a superset of 2.13.0** — verified\n`plugin-v2.13.0..plugin-v2.14.0` is only #530 + the version bump:\n- **Preserves** the reserved-`main` write self-identification (#507\nfirehose de-collapse) — `main-${getInstallId()}` write default still\npresent.\n- **Adds** opt-in recall-gating + cross-agent recall (#530), both\n**flag-gated OFF by default** (`MEMCLAW_RECALL_GATE`=`off`,\n`MEMCLAW_RECALL_CROSS_AGENT`=`false`).\n\nSo the auto-upgrade **changes no recall behavior** until those env flags\nare deliberately set on a node — it just moves the fleet from 2.13.0 to\n2.14.0.\n\n## Scope / safety\n- One constant. `MIN_AUTO_DEPLOY_PLUGIN_VERSION` unchanged (2.6.0);\nfloor invariant (`recommended >= auto-deploy`) holds —\n`tests/test_plugin_floor_invariant.py` is value-agnostic.\n- De-collapse behavior from 2.13.0 is carried forward unchanged.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4452e3cceed1cfbd1ff39e91354ff9fb0d78bcdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/4452e3cceed1cfbd1ff39e91354ff9fb0d78bcdd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/1d06fde7918deafbff41c5d06438c16fec82f24c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTgsmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAauoQAKXxRpz2v5vmKkw994+XWY8R\n+Vz5/NQ3hShAzN3JoiNHIxiPgm6Lj0m1ZlH1IdEJNiy22BfdqwseOc2GtvevnEOr\n+cQiHQjLXpdOL+cLLcRlD0560ATTw6WlCnp/D8Iik61o2f/Smw0cyxrCGl1NbK4R\n2sW0aZopDdHzAEVEcU45mO4lnE/MkOXj215uTU0mzbrNpnTCGIL6Ue1CorqMmgA7\nFaOcPMojFqwcSzqV2qvqK8hWCluZjId5SdR9j5pSw1lZVahZxj4taPNH6rOd5ynr\nDvs0fAG8VL5/4Y4frSYnJYnxWgMp+oW+3aFsw4AVbM8FFSsTPEYFg4CFGw6kv16a\n4oY3jL39ORBp/8wZqX8o9UNL9/IM73KxBz3PjNw+7glnlZSVLvPLA2RKUegZIFST\nTyhPhwQSGYNqRLgcsYzdXtRQR/syMWNdVao1UF/FPcSECd83YEG4nUULX9J0XaZh\nq3zabfX932J5n/AbwjHvx3Ak0n7PDGlOJLq6oq0G1Tpd916PbV8Wr5j0F4tsSFaA\nJ4x45Vrks7jTcW7IxPACqZG4+E8KAD5OjlYRk93RU7nyr4OgC9Co5MImON/rJ9jb\nFjTeiu0b1mRCUbSxqaJnrofJZ3daA4ymS8bMT87Myb3/XKsGVlLZMVbxMcpvRjsf\n4vqCoCMWvzF7QRl9V2BU\n=M69X\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4452e3cceed1cfbd1ff39e91354ff9fb0d78bcdd\nparent 9aa4b82c9a1da44a148182cd2413c9bb3b8ce5b8\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1783499558 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783499558 +0300\n\nchore(fleet): bump plugin auto-upgrade floor to 2.14.0 (#538)\n\n## What\nBump `MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION` **2.13.0 → 2.14.0** in\n`core_api/version_compat.py`, so eligible fleet nodes auto-upgrade to\nplugin 2.14.0.\n\n## Why\nIntended part of the v2.20.0 / onprem-v2.11.6 delivery: get plugin\n2.14.0 onto the fleet.\n\n**2.14.0 is a superset of 2.13.0** — verified\n`plugin-v2.13.0..plugin-v2.14.0` is only #530 + the version bump:\n- **Preserves** the reserved-`main` write self-identification (#507\nfirehose de-collapse) — `main-${getInstallId()}` write default still\npresent.\n- **Adds** opt-in recall-gating + cross-agent recall (#530), both\n**flag-gated OFF by default** (`MEMCLAW_RECALL_GATE`=`off`,\n`MEMCLAW_RECALL_CROSS_AGENT`=`false`).\n\nSo the auto-upgrade **changes no recall behavior** until those env flags\nare deliberately set on a node — it just moves the fleet from 2.13.0 to\n2.14.0.\n\n## Scope / safety\n- One constant. `MIN_AUTO_DEPLOY_PLUGIN_VERSION` unchanged (2.6.0);\nfloor invariant (`recommended >= auto-deploy`) holds —\n`tests/test_plugin_floor_invariant.py` is value-agnostic.\n- De-collapse behavior from 2.13.0 is carried forward unchanged.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-08T08:32:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1d06fde7918deafbff41c5d06438c16fec82f24c","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/1d06fde7918deafbff41c5d06438c16fec82f24c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/1d06fde7918deafbff41c5d06438c16fec82f24c/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9aa4b82c9a1da44a148182cd2413c9bb3b8ce5b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9aa4b82c9a1da44a148182cd2413c9bb3b8ce5b8","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9aa4b82c9a1da44a148182cd2413c9bb3b8ce5b8"}]},{"sha":"9aa4b82c9a1da44a148182cd2413c9bb3b8ce5b8","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDlhYTRiODJjOWExZGE0NGExNDgxODJjZDI0MTNjOWJiM2I4Y2U1Yjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","email":"265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-08T07:32:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-08T07:32:16Z"},"message":"chore: release main (#531)\n\n:robot: I have created a release *beep* *boop*\n---\n\n\n<details><summary>backend: 2.20.0</summary>\n\n##\n[2.20.0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/backend-v2.19.0...backend-v2.20.0)\n(2026-07-08)\n\n\n### Features\n\n* **plugin:** opt-in recall-gating + cross-agent recall (F2/A44)\n([#530](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/530))\n([a68b3d0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/a68b3d0d4d141bd15bc185afb2c4922847d449ec))\n* **reports:** agent-activity digest — Phase 1 (inert read slice)\n[CAURA-222]\n([#533](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/533))\n([d0d458f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/d0d458f33d60e11397dc1613000fbdb163f825e9))\n* **reports:** agent-activity digest generation — Phase 2 [CAURA-222]\n([#537](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/537))\n([4595284](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/45952841639e454e020d09371e43778beecd1565))\n* **search:** tenant-wide default search profile (agent &gt; tenant &gt;\nconstant) ([#534](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/534))\n([09faf6a](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/09faf6a1c669736ea9d1607e3dc92dbd418fd47e))\n\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* **reports:** count agent-private durable writes in report aggregates\n([#535](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/535))\n([f8c7914](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/f8c7914b34043d37df5f5a72810521d34ecd6d13))\n* **scoring:** cap freshness at 1.0 for future ts_valid_start (A43)\n([#529](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/529))\n([b128553](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/b128553c1e4a3159744bdb542ad49c6332d33fe4))\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>plugin: 2.14.0</summary>\n\n##\n[2.14.0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/plugin-v2.13.0...plugin-v2.14.0)\n(2026-07-08)\n\n\n### Features\n\n* **plugin:** opt-in recall-gating + cross-agent recall (F2/A44)\n([#530](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/530))\n([a68b3d0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/a68b3d0d4d141bd15bc185afb2c4922847d449ec))\n</details>\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with [Release\nPlease](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please). See\n[documentation](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please#release-please).\n\n[CAURA-222]:\nhttps://caura-ai.atlassian.net/browse/CAURA-222?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ\n[CAURA-222]:\nhttps://caura-ai.atlassian.net/browse/CAURA-222?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5Y