ttps://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/530))\n([a68b3d0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/a68b3d0d4d141bd15bc185afb2c4922847d449ec))\n* **reports:** agent-activity digest — Phase 1 (inert read slice)\n[CAURA-222]\n([#533](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/533))\n([d0d458f](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/d0d458f33d60e11397dc1613000fbdb163f825e9))\n* **reports:** agent-activity digest generation — Phase 2 [CAURA-222]\n([#537](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/537))\n([4595284](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/45952841639e454e020d09371e43778beecd1565))\n* **search:** tenant-wide default search profile (agent &gt; tenant &gt;\nconstant) ([#534](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/534))\n([09faf6a](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/09faf6a1c669736ea9d1607e3dc92dbd418fd47e))\n\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* **reports:** count agent-private durable writes in report aggregates\n([#535](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/535))\n([f8c7914](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/f8c7914b34043d37df5f5a72810521d34ecd6d13))\n* **scoring:** cap freshness at 1.0 for future ts_valid_start (A43)\n([#529](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/529))\n([b128553](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/b128553c1e4a3159744bdb542ad49c6332d33fe4))\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>plugin: 2.14.0</summary>\n\n##\n[2.14.0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/plugin-v2.13.0...plugin-v2.14.0)\n(2026-07-08)\n\n\n### Features\n\n* **plugin:** opt-in recall-gating + cross-agent recall (F2/A44)\n([#530](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/530))\n([a68b3d0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/a68b3d0d4d141bd15bc185afb2c4922847d449ec))\n</details>\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with [Release\nPlease](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please). See\n[documentation](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please#release-please).\n\n[CAURA-222]:\nhttps://caura-ai.atlassian.net/browse/CAURA-222?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ\n[CAURA-222]:\nhttps://caura-ai.atlassian.net/browse/CAURA-222?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ\n\nSigned-off-by: release-please[bot] <release-please[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: caura-deploy-bot[bot] <265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-08T07:32:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9aa4b82c9a1da44a148182cd2413c9bb3b8ce5b8","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9aa4b82c9a1da44a148182cd2413c9bb3b8ce5b8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9aa4b82c9a1da44a148182cd2413c9bb3b8ce5b8/comments","author":{"login":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","id":265395343,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOD9Gcjw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229147182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/caura-deploy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"45952841639e454e020d09371e43778beecd1565","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/45952841639e454e020d09371e43778beecd1565","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/45952841639e454e020d09371e43778beecd1565"}]},{"sha":"45952841639e454e020d09371e43778beecd1565","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDQ1OTUyODQxNjM5ZTQ1NGUwMjBkMDkzNzFlNDM3NzhiZWVjZDE1NjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-08T07:23:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-08T07:23:37Z"},"message":"feat(reports): agent-activity digest generation — Phase 2 [CAURA-222] (#537)\n\n## Phase 2 — nightly per-agent activity digest generation\n\nBuilds on Phase 1 (#533, the inert read slice). Generates the cached,\nLLM-written \"what did this agent do this day/week\" prose that `GET\n/api/v1/reports/agent-activity` already serves. Generation runs **off\nthe request path** (an LLM pass per agent is too slow/costly on demand).\n\n### Architecture\ncore-operations nightly cron → POST core-api admin endpoint → enumerate\nopted-in orgs → **inline bounded-concurrency** generation → upsert\ndigest rows. core-operations stays a dumb trigger (no LLM/DB);\ngeneration lives in core-api (LLM + config + storage access).\n\n**Fanout choice:** inline bounded-concurrency (v1), not per-tenant\nPub/Sub. Far less shared-infra surface, adequate at on-prem/eToro tenant\ncounts; a per-tenant Pub/Sub fanout is the documented scale path if org\ncounts grow. (Approved fallback from the design.)\n\n### Sub-phases (one commit each)\n- **2a — storage write path:** `agent_activity_digest_upsert`\n(idempotent; branches on `fleet_id` to hit the correct partial unique\nindex), `POST /reports/agent-activity`, storage client. Integration\ntests.\n- **2b — generation:** `services/agent_digest.py` — fetch each agent's\ncohesive durable memories, rank by volume, LLM-summarize the top-N above\nthe activity threshold (`call_with_fallback` + `complete_json`, JSON\nschema), upsert per-agent rows with `ok`/`truncated`/`error` status; USD\ncost cap trims the call budget. `run_agent_digest` enumerates opted-in\norgs, fans out inline (one org's failure never sinks the rest). Shared\ncorpus rules extracted to `services/report_corpus.py` (one source of\ntruth with the live report). `POST /admin/reports/agent-digest/run`\n(admin-gated). Opt-in `agent_digest` config in `DEFAULT_SETTINGS` (model\n`gpt-5.4-mini`). Unit tests (mocked storage + LLM).\n- **2c — cron:** wall-clock-aligned daily tick in core-operations\n(`agent_digest_run_at_hour`, default 02:00 UTC) → the admin endpoint,\ngenerous timeout. Test.\n- **2d — retention:** per-run prune of rows older than `retention_days`\n(default 90). Unit + storage integration tests.\n\n### Config (org settings, opt-in — disabled by default)\n`agent_digest`: `enabled`, `cadence`, `provider`/`model`, `top_n`,\n`max_memories_per_agent`, `min_activity_threshold`,\n`max_cost_per_run_usd`, `retention_days`.\n\n### Testing\n- core-api unit (generator, mocked storage+LLM): 9 tests — threshold,\ncohesive/episode filtering, top-N, cost cap, truncation, fleet\npassthrough, window, enumerate→generate, retention.\n- core-storage integration (upsert + prune): 11 tests — idempotency on\nboth partial indexes, fleet/no-fleet distinctness, latest-run ordering,\nprune.\n- core-operations: cron tick test.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4212cb96cf8de1df2caa3c3a83098fd040f113e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/4212cb96cf8de1df2caa3c3a83098fd040f113e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/45952841639e454e020d09371e43778beecd1565","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTfr5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOR4QAGMImUm0KlW8W4bOTewnKTe0\nYGegHecmVwmgDRlWXxnB78qzDQMI6IF4QbHkCIG4f1fl4yGgAoihVu0I7aDWDKYE\nvKubsJqfxyBcYVGIOc3JkD6ZGTWnxyOrp6GU/+8JYdqheV7MQcT3UOeiOWH/0jSs\nV4giqvP18ZBgcXqR7TissaoOcmDoOo4gYRrrjJC6t+/vStQSmi7EtBBAI3mzUKrR\nxmeD01Jdo+i+NRR6vo4/nIQg8k2H5e1w/lK+p+VAdCdBXaUEXBPjAI+/wR+usxD5\neH6WxZkw5RuCmsMfcY1Va9u4pf9oSZnz/Uo0eG4hctxZI7xYm7BX9S0h67A67P9C\nkZH7vtMgxNHcIMApeTKuf++i8bJ1C4xrOWLCHOH7l/KpXwhxiuWeZcQtCG0s/5dR\nW+nqBxcv2AZ9xcgAHPN8B/ambx2fK+a0O9BBPhL0qFQ6zAyzMKNshyGFK97xdBnM\nowlc3IDvyAwRf9bloV+flAEMfgcWZdTxlBSMMuuHfa0hhbKA777wi3Oe4WdOU9PM\nFCjKI3hSnvMtYYqovX4q1kcLJuqgN87wyOSLs9GngPMdvLtcUF3TlMT96mBEWB+e\nNgxe81F0w2HlotO7VQCkcorUFRw9JxQwzvw36vVjlNKh0eSkLUF2krwg75v2lvAM\nXkltKUQJAgOhNxHqwlwv\n=ueIW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4212cb96cf8de1df2caa3c3a83098fd040f113e8\nparent d0d458f33d60e11397dc1613000fbdb163f825e9\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1783495417 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783495417 +0300\n\nfeat(reports): agent-activity digest generation — Phase 2 [CAURA-222] (#537)\n\n## Phase 2 — nightly per-agent activity digest generation\n\nBuilds on Phase 1 (#533, the inert read slice). Generates the cached,\nLLM-written \"what did this agent do this day/week\" prose that `GET\n/api/v1/reports/agent-activity` already serves. Generation runs **off\nthe request path** (an LLM pass per agent is too slow/costly on demand).\n\n### Architecture\ncore-operations nightly cron → POST core-api admin endpoint → enumerate\nopted-in orgs → **inline bounded-concurrency** generation → upsert\ndigest rows. core-operations stays a dumb trigger (no LLM/DB);\ngeneration lives in core-api (LLM + config + storage access).\n\n**Fanout choice:** inline bounded-concurrency (v1), not per-tenant\nPub/Sub. Far less shared-infra surface, adequate at on-prem/eToro tenant\ncounts; a per-tenant Pub/Sub fanout is the documented scale path if org\ncounts grow. (Approved fallback from the design.)\n\n### Sub-phases (one commit each)\n- **2a — storage write path:** `agent_activity_digest_upsert`\n(idempotent; branches on `fleet_id` to hit the correct partial unique\nindex), `POST /reports/agent-activity`, storage client. Integration\ntests.\n- **2b — generation:** `services/agent_digest.py` — fetch each agent's\ncohesive durable memories, rank by volume, LLM-summarize the top-N above\nthe activity threshold (`call_with_fallback` + `complete_json`, JSON\nschema), upsert per-agent rows with `ok`/`truncated`/`error` status; USD\ncost cap trims the call budget. `run_agent_digest` enumerates opted-in\norgs, fans out inline (one org's failure never sinks the rest). Shared\ncorpus rules extracted to `services/report_corpus.py` (one source of\ntruth with the live report). `POST /admin/reports/agent-digest/run`\n(admin-gated). Opt-in `agent_digest` config in `DEFAULT_SETTINGS` (model\n`gpt-5.4-mini`). Unit tests (mocked storage + LLM).\n- **2c — cron:** wall-clock-aligned daily tick in core-operations\n(`agent_digest_run_at_hour`, default 02:00 UTC) → the admin endpoint,\ngenerous timeout. Test.\n- **2d — retention:** per-run prune of rows older than `retention_days`\n(default 90). Unit + storage integration tests.\n\n### Config (org settings, opt-in — disabled by default)\n`agent_digest`: `enabled`, `cadence`, `provider`/`model`, `top_n`,\n`max_memories_per_agent`, `min_activity_threshold`,\n`max_cost_per_run_usd`, `retention_days`.\n\n### Testing\n- core-api unit (generator, mocked storage+LLM): 9 tests — threshold,\ncohesive/episode filtering, top-N, cost cap, truncation, fleet\npassthrough, window, enumerate→generate, retention.\n- core-storage integration (upsert + prune): 11 tests — idempotency on\nboth partial indexes, fleet/no-fleet distinctness, latest-run ordering,\nprune.\n- core-operations: cron tick test.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-08T07:23:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/45952841639e454e020d09371e43778beecd1565","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/45952841639e454e020d09371e43778beecd1565","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/45952841639e454e020d09371e43778beecd1565/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d0d458f33d60e11397dc1613000fbdb163f825e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d0d458f33d60e11397dc1613000fbdb163f825e9","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/d0d458f33d60e11397dc1613000fbdb163f825e9"}]},{"sha":"d0d458f33d60e11397dc1613000fbdb163f825e9","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGQwZDQ1OGYzM2Q2MGUxMTM5N2RjMTYxMzAwMGZiZGIxNjNmODI1ZTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-07T13:20:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-07T13:20:19Z"},"message":"feat(reports): agent-activity digest — Phase 1 (inert read slice) [CAURA-222] (#533)\n\n## What\n\nPhase 1 of the **cached per-agent activity digest** — an LLM-generated\n\"what did this agent do this day/week\" report, distinct from the live\n`GET /api/v1/reports` (quantitative, computed per request). This phase\nis the **inert read scaffold**: schema + a read endpoint that returns\nempty until the generation worker lands. **No worker, no LLM, no UI —\nsafe to merge.**\n\n## Changes\n- **Migration 029 + `AgentActivityDigest` model** — one queryable row\nper agent per run (`run_id` groups a scheduled pass). `UNIQUE(tenant,\nfleet, agent, period, window_start)` makes re-runs idempotent; `(tenant,\nperiod, window_start DESC)` index serves the \"latest run\" read.\nDeliberately separate from `analysis_reports` (the single-blob\ncrystallization report) so the UI can deep-link a per-agent narrative.\n- **core-storage** — `agent_activity_digest_get_latest` + `GET\n/reports/agent-activity` (latest run's rows, optional\n`agent_id`/`as_of`; `[]` when none).\n- **core-api** — `GET /api/v1/reports/agent-activity`, gated by the new\n`AuthContext.enforce_cross_tenant_read()` (**strict**: `is_admin or\nis_cross_tenant_read`) + per-tenant `enforce_readable_tenant`. Returns\n`{meta, digests: []}` with `meta.generated_at: null` until generated\n(never a 404).\n- **tests** — gate (403 single-tenant), empty-until-generated, admin\nbypass, 422 period. `conftest` registers the new model + cleanup.\n\n## Verification\n- `ruff format`/`check` + `mypy` clean on both packages.\n- Migration `029` applies with the exact 16 columns + all\nindexes/constraints; `alembic history` linear, single head.\n- 8/8 report tests pass (4 new + 4 regression) against the pgvector test\nDB.\n\n## Design / next phases\nGate = **cross-tenant read privileges** (single-tenant orgs consume via\nthe org-admin-gated proxy). Cadence = **nightly daily digest** primary +\nweekly add-on, scheduled in **core-operations**, generated with\n**gpt-5.4-mini**.\n- **Phase 2** — generation worker (LLM pass per agent, reusing the live\nreport's corpus filters), config surface, upsert writer.\n- **Phase 3** — UI tab on the Reports page + deep-link from the\nleaderboard; org-report proxy passes a dedicated cross-tenant read key.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1f3f83f47c11a8f4ff8f9ac4bd9735b2bcf28b33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/1f3f83f47c11a8f4ff8f9ac4bd9735b2bcf28b33"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/d0d458f33d60e11397dc1613000fbdb163f825e9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTP0TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAADkQABIcEcgIutuLdgmEo1oloSsl\ngqE5pBt3IR0jcS/O960NrNpXz+CIgfKCd35nqIt7SuiWQACJg2Y8yDRI5n9zg1G9\nhGz9f3PeJey7avSW2x2us+Z6bG6o4p9QnrGPlt3083kcu7XtPjTV3ia7ZvWYL210\n0iFJtCuXYGwQjTJmTCK+7u2SR/7AldQmM9nBn1noAZ//BpUYbYBZGMJ+gIZqiecV\nCdUfk+ML0ERSTeRvmrs315snvANor3e6wSgpKo3sGzCWRdjq0SnjhtLdOY35Gc8r\nqLFF8RQLLw4lsYp2ENZ7Bop+Z3g0wTbb9CUWnqitj6nwwWp8cea4NAaRy+o0Uf0G\nmz/gp0KwyXNqfVy5LqenH/6k7b8Czh2g2ZCqq8TyFOTmRt1w7GcI0jKMzCzz8wyd\noDY6w+KZz4hjYEz3EvsfdGm1iMSpwk+dG5EWTUhXoUf2D0Yx4dieECRNn1y5vr6c\nDOzrEXSiGfRiMdFsYpK9dlq/2p7hBQZdiDBg5EuPlZ9FWvlevWStp6b8L0axA7U6\nSoi8mRWjOteDBtTreMvawVS7pAA/v4ALXH1da4MD2d75yFH1469EmqOYTj3b2uSO\nbCi67onTDiLDaUCATDS7fCQJzNET+YBgzrcEfo/FBNNOhuvs5YAJW/OytKY+9EUj\nCM8mqkvMm2xFv844IVTM\n=0XZp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1f3f83f47c11a8f4ff8f9ac4bd9735b2bcf28b33\nparent f8c7914b34043d37df5f5a72810521d34ecd6d13\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1783430419 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783430419 +0300\n\nfeat(reports): agent-activity digest — Phase 1 (inert read slice) [CAURA-222] (#533)\n\n## What\n\nPhase 1 of the **cached per-agent activity digest** — an LLM-generated\n\"what did this agent do this day/week\" report, distinct from the live\n`GET /api/v1/reports` (quantitative, computed per request). This phase\nis the **inert read scaffold**: schema + a read endpoint that returns\nempty until the generation worker lands. **No worker, no LLM, no UI —\nsafe to merge.**\n\n## Changes\n- **Migration 029 + `AgentActivityDigest` model** — one queryable row\nper agent per run (`run_id` groups a scheduled pass). `UNIQUE(tenant,\nfleet, agent, period, window_start)` makes re-runs idempotent; `(tenant,\nperiod, window_start DESC)` index serves the \"latest run\" read.\nDeliberately separate from `analysis_reports` (the single-blob\ncrystallization report) so the UI can deep-link a per-agent narrative.\n- **core-storage** — `agent_activity_digest_get_latest` + `GET\n/reports/agent-activity` (latest run's rows, optional\n`agent_id`/`as_of`; `[]` when none).\n- **core-api** — `GET /api/v1/reports/agent-activity`, gated by the new\n`AuthContext.enforce_cross_tenant_read()` (**strict**: `is_admin or\nis_cross_tenant_read`) + per-tenant `enforce_readable_tenant`. Returns\n`{meta, digests: []}` with `meta.generated_at: null` until generated\n(never a 404).\n- **tests** — gate (403 single-tenant), empty-until-generated, admin\nbypass, 422 period. `conftest` registers the new model + cleanup.\n\n## Verification\n- `ruff format`/`check` + `mypy` clean on both packages.\n- Migration `029` applies with the exact 16 columns + all\nindexes/constraints; `alembic history` linear, single head.\n- 8/8 report tests pass (4 new + 4 regression) against the pgvector test\nDB.\n\n## Design / next phases\nGate = **cross-tenant read privileges** (single-tenant orgs consume via\nthe org-admin-gated proxy). Cadence = **nightly daily digest** primary +\nweekly add-on, scheduled in **core-operations**, generated with\n**gpt-5.4-mini**.\n- **Phase 2** — generation worker (LLM pass per agent, reusing the live\nreport's corpus filters), config surface, upsert writer.\n- **Phase 3** — UI tab on the Reports page + deep-link from the\nleaderboard; org-report proxy passes a dedicated cross-tenant read key.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-07T13:20:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d0d458f33d60e11397dc1613000fbdb163f825e9","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/d0d458f33d60e11397dc1613000fbdb163f825e9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d0d458f33d60e11397dc1613000fbdb163f825e9/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f8c7914b34043d37df5f5a72810521d34ecd6d13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f8c7914b34043d37df5f5a72810521d34ecd6d13","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f8c7914b34043d37df5f5a72810521d34ecd6d13"}]},{"sha":"f8c7914b34043d37df5f5a72810521d34ecd6d13","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGY4Yzc5MTRiMzQwNDNkMzdkZjVmNWE3MjgxMDUyMWQzNGVjZDZkMTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-06T15:22:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T15:22:02Z"},"message":"fix(reports): count agent-private durable writes in report aggregates (#535)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe report's `durable_memories_written` (and `by_type` / `per_agent` /\n`trend` / `quality`) excluded `scope_agent` (agent-private) rows. So the\ntop-line metric silently measured **team-visible** durable writes, not\nwhat was actually **written**.\n\nVisibility is an *audience* attribute — an agent keeping a decision/fact\nprivate doesn't make it less durable or less decision-bearing. The\nexclusion also disproportionately undercounts privacy-heavy tenants.\nVerified against prod:\n\n| tenant | current report | with private counted | delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| etoro0 (noisy/private-heavy) | 98 | **161** | +63 (+64%) |\n| etoro-core (lean) | 254 | **275** | +21 (+8%) |\n\nThe recovered rows are real knowledge (rule/outcome/fact), not noise —\nthe cohesive/episode/`main` filters already ran. The correction is\nself-targeting: it fixes the undercount where it was wrong and barely\nmoves the already-clean tenant.\n\n## Change\n\n- Add an opt-in **`include_scope_agent`** flag (default `False`, so MCP\n`memclaw_stats` behavior is unchanged) to `memory_stats_breakdown`,\n`memory_daily_durable_counts`, and `memory_quality_metrics`.\n- The report sets it `True` on its count/trend/quality queries; it rides\n`scope_keys` too, so the funnel's `written` and the insight-freshness\ncorpus stay consistent (`written >= durable` holds).\n\nThis is a **pure count** change — no memory content is exposed. The\ncontent-bearing sections (`value_highlights` / `learning` / `spotlight`\n/ `working_on`) still exclude `scope_agent`, so no agent's private\nmemory is surfaced to the group.\n\n## Test\n\n`test_report_group_counts_private_writes_but_hides_content`: a\nprivate-scope durable write is counted in `durable_memories_written` /\n`by_type` / `per_agent` / `trend`, but never appears in\n`value_highlights`. Full `tests/test_reports.py` green locally (12\npassed); the 11 pre-existing tests are unchanged (they seed only\n`scope_team`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"26a332888cef44c06d3fc457e8f0302835301162","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/26a332888cef44c06d3fc457e8f0302835301162"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/f8c7914b34043d37df5f5a72810521d34ecd6d13","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS8gaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVSUQABEHHMcthTRJ83vN4HsIrbha\nsOhJsbe+UAb4JC1IN9gTNeanh3LKoBY10bcn5O6VXJLCKGQfhZ9B8h7jHmBMq2TI\nRAjGd8ZZahLe19f7yszvid+0anrTN52BKrSUfcpHGQrdwvjO4BWbOClC+4vJ05iF\nbQdcYkqZYC1M1k8xoC6gBdGxBh1hQA5u7LBHlCl1aoeJ9gqT/PwGaArBvOjeXThB\nr5hb4tS7w/LjhV9wmXZtfiyQ81OYQYsuvC4OHTQKo4pmCG8TXulEvTMx+sCwpI4D\nJu6Sfi5UliBqJsOhupL2GAiviVP5nY00mHcWUV45wYKdDrTbrblfUna5EugQxsVP\nmbUHGHxPhaYMATe91w8HzO0/isjBEVS8eBQWugFqQgFEutNI5St3noPWsy0Bc+X0\nd18WbtCLZvFpo70neA0qdzj15uBcBC11Ig0qb+0U9Wkd+imBIk9cvvvZz8aefsyo\n6G+WkU3mcuyC9qrfGoQFp76aBLDB3qdBne2OBmbyYxTPvrM7XE2EFiB9u66GtkKc\nivZt9nhBaHP9YpTwZiCcbNPVm0b+OFBaUjNHEGixLqMdBedX+eUTg4ir0l1t5r0V\n10wlEI04LkvZVgsm87VYiwI4g6Z/ws0c5I3vhzlYG0ifkkHDFyiHvbEVk+VlebPO\nEQqBp66PeRFgKM/jw4RL\n=HADY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 26a332888cef44c06d3fc457e8f0302835301162\nparent 09faf6a1c669736ea9d1607e3dc92dbd418fd47e\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1783351322 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783351322 +0300\n\nfix(reports): count agent-private durable writes in report aggregates (#535)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe report's `durable_memories_written` (and `by_type` / `per_agent` /\n`trend` / `quality`) excluded `scope_agent` (agent-private) rows. So the\ntop-line metric silently measured **team-visible** durable writes, not\nwhat was actually **written**.\n\nVisibility is an *audience* attribute — an agent keeping a decision/fact\nprivate doesn't make it less durable or less decision-bearing. The\nexclusion also disproportionately undercounts privacy-heavy tenants.\nVerified against prod:\n\n| tenant | current report | with private counted | delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| etoro0 (noisy/private-heavy) | 98 | **161** | +63 (+64%) |\n| etoro-core (lean) | 254 | **275** | +21 (+8%) |\n\nThe recovered rows are real knowledge (rule/outcome/fact), not noise —\nthe cohesive/episode/`main` filters already ran. The correction is\nself-targeting: it fixes the undercount where it was wrong and barely\nmoves the already-clean tenant.\n\n## Change\n\n- Add an opt-in **`include_scope_agent`** flag (default `False`, so MCP\n`memclaw_stats` behavior is unchanged) to `memory_stats_breakdown`,\n`memory_daily_durable_counts`, and `memory_quality_metrics`.\n- The report sets it `True` on its count/trend/quality queries; it rides\n`scope_keys` too, so the funnel's `written` and the insight-freshness\ncorpus stay consistent (`written >= durable` holds).\n\nThis is a **pure count** change — no memory content is exposed. The\ncontent-bearing sections (`value_highlights` / `learning` / `spotlight`\n/ `working_on`) still exclude `scope_agent`, so no agent's private\nmemory is surfaced to the group.\n\n## Test\n\n`test_report_group_counts_private_writes_but_hides_content`: a\nprivate-scope durable write is counted in `durable_memories_written` /\n`by_type` / `per_agent` / `trend`, but never appears in\n`value_highlights`. Full `tests/test_reports.py` green locally (12\npassed); the 11 pre-existing tests are unchanged (they seed only\n`scope_team`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T15:22:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f8c7914b34043d37df5f5a72810521d34ecd6d13","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f8c7914b34043d37df5f5a72810521d34ecd6d13","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f8c7914b34043d37df5f5a72810521d34ecd6d13/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"09faf6a1c669736ea9d1607e3dc92dbd418fd47e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/09faf6a1c669736ea9d1607e3dc92dbd418fd47e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/09faf6a1c669736ea9d1607e3dc92dbd418fd47e"}]},{"sha":"09faf6a1c669736ea9d1607e3dc92dbd418fd47e","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDA5ZmFmNmExYzY2OTczNmVhOWQxNjA3ZTNkYzkyZGJkNDE4ZmQ0N2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-06T12:50:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T12:50:52Z"},"message":"feat(search): tenant-wide default search profile (agent > tenant > constant) (#534)\n\n## What\n\nAdds a **tenant/org-level default search profile** so a single setting\nsets the similarity floor (and any other search knob) for **every\nagent** in a tenant. Resolution order in `resolve_search_profile` is\nnow:\n\n```\nper-agent search_profile  →  tenant default_profile  →  global constant\n```\n\n## Why\n\nToday only a per-agent `search_profile` can override the global\n`MIN_SEARCH_SIMILARITY = 0.3` — there's no tenant layer. Setting a\nper-customer floor (e.g. for eToro) meant tuning every agent\nindividually: drift-prone, and new agents fall back to the global\ndefault. This is the groundwork for a **per-tenant, data-calibrated\nsimilarity floor (A47)** — after this, it's one setting per tenant.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`organization_settings.py`**\n- `DEFAULT_SETTINGS.search.default_profile` — empty by default → neutral\n(global constants unchanged)\n- `ResolvedConfig.default_search_profile` — read accessor, sanitised via\n`validate_search_profile` on read (clamps out-of-range; can never crash\nthe search path)\n- `_validate_default_search_profile` — strict **write** validator:\nraises → **422** on unknown key / wrong type / out-of-range, reusing\n`_SEARCH_PROFILE_RULES`; wired into `update_settings`\n- **`resolve_search_profile.py`** — merge `{**tenant_default,\n**agent_profile}` (agent wins, tenant default fills gaps, constant\nlast). Guarded on a missing `tenant_config` so behaviour is unchanged\nwhen absent.\n\nDefault-off / neutral: with no `default_profile` set, every knob\nresolves exactly as before.\n\n## Usage (once merged)\n\n```\nPUT /api/v1/settings   {\"search\": {\"default_profile\": {\"min_similarity\": 0.40}}}\n```\n\n## Tests\n\n- Unit (`tests/test_search_default_profile.py`, 15 cases): accessor read\n+ sanitise-on-read, write-validator rejects\nunknown-key/wrong-type/out-of-range/bool, and the **real\n`ResolveSearchProfile` step** precedence (agent > tenant > constant).\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean; `cd core-api && mypy src/`\n→ no issues.\n- **Wet-tested on the local enterprise stack**: `PUT /settings` valid\nmulti-key → 200 + GET round-trip; invalid → 422; and the real\n`resolve_config` (fresh DB read) → `ResolveSearchProfile` produced\n`min_similarity=0.42`/`top_k=9` from the tenant default (overriding\nglobal 0.3 / the request), with an agent profile correctly overriding to\n0.55.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"6c0aa906c27be2845922ce1a4eabc1a7ad466fb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/6c0aa906c27be2845922ce1a4eabc1a7ad466fb5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/09faf6a1c669736ea9d1607e3dc92dbd418fd47e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS6SsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAx5EQADwHR7a7OY32tFyym7BYp+H4\nxfs1aGhq1vWAcSmo2AD9vVySp/FFW0Ymx157JBPTzVFyHiyoAM5C0zHlD3GnTzBX\n4OBr/vJBHyHW82ikEbtvDsx2aXkL9/wdc4inggW5Rk0pF7stf0ZCkUwysegu1W8h\niM7CRnGB/N+H3UCnK6zpMmuW0bjRUtmdEcyflXWLqH7bJdPOk/SewSeeWOT73+HA\np/74vQ8B21xymGHDtsVEG2oPXVhf+y0gsGPQymFWMCU+G7+Xfh5vO2Ww4rjYJ5gI\nYHk9+vGrhTopcXey8ZibAqcZAmHVIn90nBVfV9Ss4nkEKedsrZrsA0bJqslp7epw\neGX60fUh9ijXKiVXE8xElu9dvtczDjMvnEF/lnSf2DcrjwlVvn54JlwymWoBeiu/\nxbXge/R2TOVDz4zkL/3u0VIan89u+ZJz1qnEnLl3ewWgp15fZkICceoNncwm+XOE\nv340Ib/IaEJ1F49duNozA3/zn2Pf/GzxjUqqnwfFK38ALNwlaDY6CRdsduynaQml\nVEz5o5VS4zFwij1Mk1Jmd78JewOGVB7n0SJxIKzEl6933kZk8sFXrbrMwHoAZ7Na\n333zEv7SUI7w/QD06yr9T7m1NbBVlYkZP7EOebpEU5xzGYURPBk41NoutK5HSfXa\ntxddMlTBM3ORGg9bET+P\n=en0m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6c0aa906c27be2845922ce1a4eabc1a7ad466fb5\nparent 34813cd06bc75968da080601d6de383ffaae0af2\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1783342252 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783342252 +0300\n\nfeat(search): tenant-wide default search profile (agent > tenant > constant) (#534)\n\n## What\n\nAdds a **tenant/org-level default search profile** so a single setting\nsets the similarity floor (and any other search knob) for **every\nagent** in a tenant. Resolution order in `resolve_search_profile` is\nnow:\n\n```\nper-agent search_profile  →  tenant default_profile  →  global constant\n```\n\n## Why\n\nToday only a per-agent `search_profile` can override the global\n`MIN_SEARCH_SIMILARITY = 0.3` — there's no tenant layer. Setting a\nper-customer floor (e.g. for eToro) meant tuning every agent\nindividually: drift-prone, and new agents fall back to the global\ndefault. This is the groundwork for a **per-tenant, data-calibrated\nsimilarity floor (A47)** — after this, it's one setting per tenant.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`organization_settings.py`**\n- `DEFAULT_SETTINGS.search.default_profile` — empty by default → neutral\n(global constants unchanged)\n- `ResolvedConfig.default_search_profile` — read accessor, sanitised via\n`validate_search_profile` on read (clamps out-of-range; can never crash\nthe search path)\n- `_validate_default_search_profile` — strict **write** validator:\nraises → **422** on unknown key / wrong type / out-of-range, reusing\n`_SEARCH_PROFILE_RULES`; wired into `update_settings`\n- **`resolve_search_profile.py`** — merge `{**tenant_default,\n**agent_profile}` (agent wins, tenant default fills gaps, constant\nlast). Guarded on a missing `tenant_config` so behaviour is unchanged\nwhen absent.\n\nDefault-off / neutral: with no `default_profile` set, every knob\nresolves exactly as before.\n\n## Usage (once merged)\n\n```\nPUT /api/v1/settings   {\"search\": {\"default_profile\": {\"min_similarity\": 0.40}}}\n```\n\n## Tests\n\n- Unit (`tests/test_search_default_profile.py`, 15 cases): accessor read\n+ sanitise-on-read, write-validator rejects\nunknown-key/wrong-type/out-of-range/bool, and the **real\n`ResolveSearchProfile` step** precedence (agent > tenant > constant).\n- `ruff check` + `ruff format --check` clean; `cd core-api && mypy src/`\n→ no issues.\n- **Wet-tested on the local enterprise stack**: `PUT /settings` valid\nmulti-key → 200 + GET round-trip; invalid → 422; and the real\n`resolve_config` (fresh DB read) → `ResolveSearchProfile` produced\n`min_similarity=0.42`/`top_k=9` from the tenant default (overriding\nglobal 0.3 / the request), with an agent profile correctly overriding to\n0.55.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T12:50:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/09faf6a1c669736ea9d1607e3dc92dbd418fd47e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/09faf6a1c669736ea9d1607e3dc92dbd418fd47e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/09faf6a1c669736ea9d1607e3dc92dbd418fd47e/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"34813cd06bc75968da080601d6de383ffaae0af2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/34813cd06bc75968da080601d6de383ffaae0af2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/34813cd06bc75968da080601d6de383ffaae0af2"}]},{"sha":"34813cd06bc75968da080601d6de383ffaae0af2","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDM0ODEzY2QwNmJjNzU5NjhkYTA4MDYwMWQ2ZGUzODNmZmFhZTBhZjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"eyal-bl","email":"eyal.b@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-06T11:20:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T11:20:19Z"},"message":"CAURA-701 feat(enrichment): V2.1 memory-type taxonomy — merge semanti… (#532)\n\n…c into fact, sharpen action/episode/fact boundary\n\nRefines the ENRICHMENT_PROMPT memory-type section based on a 400-row\neToro diagnostic run (dev + non-overlapping held-out set) comparing\ngpt-5.4-nano's writes to independently-classified Opus 4.8 verdicts.\n\nChanges to the classifier surface (prompt-only; no DB schema change):\n\n1. `semantic` folded into `fact`. At N=200, only 2% of prod-semantic\nrows survived Opus review as `semantic`; 84% remapped to `fact`, with\nthe remaining cases flagged as interchangeable in every plausible set.\n`MemoryType.SEMANTIC` is retained in the enum + CHECK constraint for\nread-compat with historical rows (~1,800 in eToro), but a new\n`CLASSIFIER_DEPRECATED_MEMORY_TYPES` set hides it from the prompt and\n`_validate_enrichment` demotes any residual LLM-emitted `semantic` to\n`fact` at the write boundary.\n\n2. `episode` gains three negative rules — NOT first-person self-reports\n(use `action`), NOT durable technical reference (use `fact`), NOT\nstyle/aesthetic guidance (use `preference`). Prod's `episode` bucket was\nthe catchall for 48% of the pool with 38% agreement rate; the negative\nrules directly counter the observed misclassifications.\n\n3. `action` rewritten to lead with the semantic rule (\"a DEED the actor\ncompleted\") + explicit verb list (\"deployed / merged / created / sent /\nfiled / completed\"). Dropped an earlier draft's `[From agent: X]`\nsurface cue — held-out validation showed only 20% of `[From agent:]`\ncontent is actually action; a broader semantic rule generalizes without\nthe overfit shortcut.\n\n4. `fact` description expanded to explicitly cover reference material,\nAPI/schema documentation, and agent-authored technical analyses —\nsurfaces prod was under-picking (94% accurate but only 8% of pool).\n\n5. Replaced the 2-way \"Action vs episode\" contrastive block with a 3-way\naction/episode/fact block plus 10 generic examples (V1 prod-prompt\noriginals + fully synthetic — no lifts from the eval sample).\n\n6. `task` description clarifies \"NOT YET DONE\" to address the\ntask-vs-action boundary that surfaced at N=200.\n\nValidation results (dev N=200 / held-out N=200, non-overlapping):\n\n- nano↔opus exact agreement: 37% (V1) → 73.5% dev / 75.5% held-out\n- rows fitting ≥2 types per Opus probe: 89% (V1) → 70% dev / 62%\nheld-out\n- Opus self-consistency (primary in own plausibles): 93% → 98%/99%\n\nHeld-out matches or beats dev on every core metric — the taxonomy\nrevision generalizes, not memorizes.\n\nNo schema, migration, or storage-layer changes. `MemoryType.SEMANTIC`,\nmigration 013's CHECK constraint, and all historical rows are untouched.\nDownstream code that inspects `memory_type='semantic'` (reports.py\ndisplay map, per-type dedup weights in common/constants.py) continues to\nwork against existing rows; new writes go to `fact`. Historical-row\nbackfill is a separate follow-up (deliberately out of scope).\n\nFull write-up: /Users/eyal/code/memclaw_memtype_classifier_findings.md\n\n<!-- Thanks for the contribution! Please fill in this template so we can\nreview quickly. -->\n\n## Summary\n\n<!-- What does this PR do? One or two sentences. -->\n\n## Related Issue\n\n<!-- Link the issue this PR addresses, e.g. `Closes #123`. Delete if\nN/A. -->\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change that fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change that adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that changes existing behavior)\n- [ ] Documentation update\n- [ ] Refactor / internal cleanup\n- [ ] Other:\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n\n<!-- Describe the tests you ran. Include commands if possible. -->\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [ ] I have added tests that cover my changes (or explained why none\nare needed)\n- [ ] `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass\n- [ ] `mypy` passes\n- [ ] `pytest` passes locally\n- [ ] I have updated relevant documentation (README,\nARCHITECTURE_REVIEW, etc.)\n- [ ] I have updated `CHANGELOG.md` under the `Unreleased` section (if\nuser-facing)\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n<!-- Anything reviewers should know — tradeoffs, follow-up work, open\nquestions. -->\n\nSigned-off-by: Eyal Blyachman <eyal.b@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0df1ffeb3e225c81a573b12de0aab9a5e815db32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/0df1ffeb3e225c81a573b12de0aab9a5e815db32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/34813cd06bc75968da080601d6de383ffaae0af2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS49zCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKfQQALF+getzXwiDL6V0QqOOmpOI\n3v/1VLxpEyv/IPEsBPw4GtwX7T7ozxi8hvDvMtwAaYCZhwPx+F06z+saCmR+fGJ5\nmmSo6Rz4sQbpiN9G3X05unJ9tUcEOzAc3xSGWJFIFLXyuODW5eQWv55aUUVslrXZ\nqhSOKvcJ5ELhQiZjxy00KfUaL4bRBYEEG2xzdIcP944BmcP9VRfeg104QsdBctf6\nz0FDiOqZDAVH1njMCAWnmjoCmacf2WtY8qjnZ8t28l/bN2m8GJI/mJb5leP6fUT+\ntxXWMR6xiAje+qvrfKgI02hGApBzHk9dbpnCh+qw7GoHm49jfBR005FmiPCAA/iK\nwF/yUTu8WzLMtCgkbrCFEpVrTmFI2znzXo266g9bJMWoXVkzNWlaYbVFiYjrvWzQ\nj0vLDqIQVQ44eAR/cnQPx9GXDChvQ4pZxn3u1YY8AAt8PWmd44/8Xxxl6EBuP684\nvLKiuIdEd6SnA4pIM6a1omT+gGBB+u6bC4ySZumLRLU/fBXn99BseeM8DilJHleZ\nVSFvhRBgQaZgLoaykrzmIkcVxCd/TXCk9p73xHGoDQ7A9SqPoC5RNwT4VaoIuP7z\nLvvS/Ml8MC7d1WKSe4a/k+zDzEIjuubbznCYHg5GQ0/4/FYxU0LIe/3d4XQO+4EL\nNP/i6FNuowy27AHP2Ypi\n=2X1m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0df1ffeb3e225c81a573b12de0aab9a5e815db32\nparent a68b3d0d4d141bd15bc185afb2c4922847d449ec\nauthor eyal-bl <eyal.b@caura.ai> 1783336819 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783336819 +0300\n\nCAURA-701 feat(enrichment): V2.1 memory-type taxonomy — merge semanti… (#532)\n\n…c into fact, sharpen action/episode/fact boundary\n\nRefines the ENRICHMENT_PROMPT memory-type section based on a 400-row\neToro diagnostic run (dev + non-overlapping held-out set) comparing\ngpt-5.4-nano's writes to independently-classified Opus 4.8 verdicts.\n\nChanges to the classifier surface (prompt-only; no DB schema change):\n\n1. `semantic` folded into `fact`. At N=200, only 2% of prod-semantic\nrows survived Opus review as `semantic`; 84% remapped to `fact`, with\nthe remaining cases flagged as interchangeable in every plausible set.\n`MemoryType.SEMANTIC` is retained in the enum + CHECK constraint for\nread-compat with historical rows (~1,800 in eToro), but a new\n`CLASSIFIER_DEPRECATED_MEMORY_TYPES` set hides it from the prompt and\n`_validate_enrichment` demotes any residual LLM-emitted `semantic` to\n`fact` at the write boundary.\n\n2. `episode` gains three negative rules — NOT first-person self-reports\n(use `action`), NOT durable technical reference (use `fact`), NOT\nstyle/aesthetic guidance (use `preference`). Prod's `episode` bucket was\nthe catchall for 48% of the pool with 38% agreement rate; the negative\nrules directly counter the observed misclassifications.\n\n3. `action` rewritten to lead with the semantic rule (\"a DEED the actor\ncompleted\") + explicit verb list (\"deployed / merged / created / sent /\nfiled / completed\"). Dropped an earlier draft's `[From agent: X]`\nsurface cue — held-out validation showed only 20% of `[From agent:]`\ncontent is actually action; a broader semantic rule generalizes without\nthe overfit shortcut.\n\n4. `fact` description expanded to explicitly cover reference material,\nAPI/schema documentation, and agent-authored technical analyses —\nsurfaces prod was under-picking (94% accurate but only 8% of pool).\n\n5. Replaced the 2-way \"Action vs episode\" contrastive block with a 3-way\naction/episode/fact block plus 10 generic examples (V1 prod-prompt\noriginals + fully synthetic — no lifts from the eval sample).\n\n6. `task` description clarifies \"NOT YET DONE\" to address the\ntask-vs-action boundary that surfaced at N=200.\n\nValidation results (dev N=200 / held-out N=200, non-overlapping):\n\n- nano↔opus exact agreement: 37% (V1) → 73.5% dev / 75.5% held-out\n- rows fitting ≥2 types per Opus probe: 89% (V1) → 70% dev / 62%\nheld-out\n- Opus self-consistency (primary in own plausibles): 93% → 98%/99%\n\nHeld-out matches or beats dev on every core metric — the taxonomy\nrevision generalizes, not memorizes.\n\nNo schema, migration, or storage-layer changes. `MemoryType.SEMANTIC`,\nmigration 013's CHECK constraint, and all historical rows are untouched.\nDownstream code that inspects `memory_type='semantic'` (reports.py\ndisplay map, per-type dedup weights in common/constants.py) continues to\nwork against existing rows; new writes go to `fact`. Historical-row\nbackfill is a separate follow-up (deliberately out of scope).\n\nFull write-up: /Users/eyal/code/memclaw_memtype_classifier_findings.md\n\n<!-- Thanks for the contribution! Please fill in this template so we can\nreview quickly. -->\n\n## Summary\n\n<!-- What does this PR do? One or two sentences. -->\n\n## Related Issue\n\n<!-- Link the issue this PR addresses, e.g. `Closes #123`. Delete if\nN/A. -->\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change that fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change that adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that changes existing behavior)\n- [ ] Documentation update\n- [ ] Refactor / internal cleanup\n- [ ] Other:\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n\n<!-- Describe the tests you ran. Include commands if possible. -->\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [ ] I have added tests that cover my changes (or explained why none\nare needed)\n- [ ] `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass\n- [ ] `mypy` passes\n- [ ] `pytest` passes locally\n- [ ] I have updated relevant documentation (README,\nARCHITECTURE_REVIEW, etc.)\n- [ ] I have updated `CHANGELOG.md` under the `Unreleased` section (if\nuser-facing)\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n<!-- Anything reviewers should know — tradeoffs, follow-up work, open\nquestions. -->\n\nSigned-off-by: Eyal Blyachman <eyal.b@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T11:20:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/34813cd06bc75968da080601d6de383ffaae0af2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/34813cd06bc75968da080601d6de383ffaae0af2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/34813cd06bc75968da080601d6de383ffaae0af2/comments","author":{"login":"eyal-bl","id":262085605,"node_id":"U_kgDOD58b5Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262085605?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl","html_url":"https://github.com/eyal-bl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a68b3d0d4d141bd15bc185afb2c4922847d449ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a68b3d0d4d141bd15bc185afb2c4922847d449ec","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a68b3d0d4d141bd15bc185afb2c4922847d449ec"}]},{"sha":"a68b3d0d4d141bd15bc185afb2c4922847d449ec","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGE2OGIzZDBkNGQxNDFiZDE1YmMxODVhZmIyYzQ5MjI4NDdkNDQ5ZWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-06T07:54:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T07:54:23Z"},"message":"feat(plugin): opt-in recall-gating + cross-agent recall (F2/A44) (#530)\n\n## What\nTwo **plugin-side**, **flag-gated (default off)** recall changes.\nMerging is behavior-neutral until opted in.\n\n### F2 — recall-gating (`shouldRecall`)\nStops auto `/search` from firing on non-question turns. 5 new noise-skip\nreasons: machine/automation patterns, agent-name self-match,\n`@mention`/number-only, `[Subagent Context]` blobs,\ninstruction-to-3rd-party.\n- **`MEMCLAW_RECALL_GATE`** = `off` (default) · `shadow` (log\nwould-skip, don't enforce) · `on`.\n- **`MEMCLAW_RECALL_MACHINE_PATTERNS`** — machine regex list is\nper-deployment configurable (a term that's noise here may be real\ncontent elsewhere, e.g. \"health check\"), seeded from observed eToro\nautomation traffic.\n- Explicit recall keywords still win.\n\n### A44 — cross-agent recall (silo removal)\n- **`MEMCLAW_RECALL_CROSS_AGENT`** (default `false`): auto-recall omits\n`filter_agent_id` so an agent can retrieve **sibling agents'\nknowledge**, still bounded by the server-side fleet/trust scope. The\nsilo was the plugin sending `filter_agent_id: agentId` on every recall.\n- **Enable alongside the A43 freshness cap (#529)** — otherwise a\nfuture-dated hub memory dominates cross-agent results.\n\n## Evidence\nHeld-out on `etoro-core` (rules built on `etoro0`): the noise gate skips\n**~76% of recall calls with 0/29 genuine questions lost**. Only 5–35% of\n`/search` calls are genuine questions; the rest are\nmachine/probe/chatter.\n\n## Tests\n8 new unit tests for the noise-skip rules — **38/38 context-engine tests\npass**, typecheck clean.\n\n## Rollout\nDefault off → recommended path: `shadow` first (measure), then `on`;\nenable cross-agent only after #529 merges.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"aad2525d7affb7354b6f6b579d45f7d24b3867d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/aad2525d7affb7354b6f6b579d45f7d24b3867d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/a68b3d0d4d141bd15bc185afb2c4922847d449ec","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS18vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAu8cQAEbdrx4zpdSM+4ZasXWEkZNA\nDzvFPG+t0lWICbeufjZHB61i7+mSheTdIxbuGRVgR5+Ixab5gh3sY8XguTPvv09C\ndf4j9SVJlwJCWKcESlMJRhn5wfOAwdny+46gY7+BYn+AjA8DlYUC0RchDv6Irpiu\n/JAbSObVaBNH+IFYcx7+iqehA4rCbUahoT1xSDHU4/mtttL4qWUQWBhvWufxgJWD\nsyV97hyZEWsKnCsBparA5G8jVkSMwb9Npdb4HJsk9AwT3qMUdvMgW7CqEzn/cN7j\nFUTfYnSRed0XsyfjZBxP98Qx8VFXGFLbY5grQ2Dn68AwWneC62CnypM59kP2Q9uJ\nylLQSSsNeNsBeA9L+2ZBPd2fM4DadEfwhp7rUwoxlyB43OSW3tJ1JK7kgPFckX+D\nnypaOauLZH5DOH3D0uPecarWfWIAS01dxDYcu+If0bCJXESOKylJhYBopECByjJS\nprsZzWy5K2PPIGpS6RTjNiKiJ8OdDzI6d8Py+nJIUIlzoLb3D8mxyWi1mvBEAWHB\nVk0OLumeGhOaZM5s4KHff170ZdewPQBnm0tdHGgLLsTg7Xb6D+Tj6M+x2/Zx4cpc\nsrTEXF5AOnTFZ485RXlPDlJKB0HmoQ5zMLRb/npdBHn2IuwKxr1KzkrtPvWFoojn\n4ZIkCiSSmp8h0SIo9qkO\n=2jV3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree aad2525d7affb7354b6f6b579d45f7d24b3867d6\nparent b128553c1e4a3159744bdb542ad49c6332d33fe4\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1783324463 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783324463 +0300\n\nfeat(plugin): opt-in recall-gating + cross-agent recall (F2/A44) (#530)\n\n## What\nTwo **plugin-side**, **flag-gated (default off)** recall changes.\nMerging is behavior-neutral until opted in.\n\n### F2 — recall-gating (`shouldRecall`)\nStops auto `/search` from firing on non-question turns. 5 new noise-skip\nreasons: machine/automation patterns, agent-name self-match,\n`@mention`/number-only, `[Subagent Context]` blobs,\ninstruction-to-3rd-party.\n- **`MEMCLAW_RECALL_GATE`** = `off` (default) · `shadow` (log\nwould-skip, don't enforce) · `on`.\n- **`MEMCLAW_RECALL_MACHINE_PATTERNS`** — machine regex list is\nper-deployment configurable (a term that's noise here may be real\ncontent elsewhere, e.g. \"health check\"), seeded from observed eToro\nautomation traffic.\n- Explicit recall keywords still win.\n\n### A44 — cross-agent recall (silo removal)\n- **`MEMCLAW_RECALL_CROSS_AGENT`** (default `false`): auto-recall omits\n`filter_agent_id` so an agent can retrieve **sibling agents'\nknowledge**, still bounded by the server-side fleet/trust scope. The\nsilo was the plugin sending `filter_agent_id: agentId` on every recall.\n- **Enable alongside the A43 freshness cap (#529)** — otherwise a\nfuture-dated hub memory dominates cross-agent results.\n\n## Evidence\nHeld-out on `etoro-core` (rules built on `etoro0`): the noise gate skips\n**~76% of recall calls with 0/29 genuine questions lost**. Only 5–35% of\n`/search` calls are genuine questions; the rest are\nmachine/probe/chatter.\n\n## Tests\n8 new unit tests for the noise-skip rules — **38/38 context-engine tests\npass**, typecheck clean.\n\n## Rollout\nDefault off → recommended path: `shadow` first (measure), then `on`;\nenable cross-agent only after #529 merges.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T07:54:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a68b3d0d4d141bd15bc185afb2c4922847d449ec","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a68b3d0d4d141bd15bc185afb2c4922847d449ec","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a68b3d0d4d141bd15bc185afb2c4922847d449ec/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b128553c1e4a3159744bdb542ad49c6332d33fe4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b128553c1e4a3159744bdb542ad49c6332d33fe4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b128553c1e4a3159744bdb542ad49c6332d33fe4"}]},{"sha":"b128553c1e4a3159744bdb542ad49c6332d33fe4","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGIxMjg1NTNjMWU0YTMxNTk3NDRiZGI1NDJhZDQ5YzYzMzJkMzNmZTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-06T07:48:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T07:48:00Z"},"message":"fix(scoring): cap freshness at 1.0 for future ts_valid_start (A43) (#529)\n\n## What\nCap the freshness factor at 1.0 in `memory_scored_search` so a **future\n`ts_valid_start`** (with `ts_valid_end` NULL) can't inflate freshness\nabove 1.0.\n\n## Why\nFreshness anchors on `greatest(created_at, coalesce(ts_valid_start,\ncreated_at))`; the age branch `1 - (age/type_decay)*(1-floor)` had no\nlower bound on age. A future anchor drives `age_days` negative →\nfreshness climbs to several× → final `score` exceeds 1.0 → a\nlow-similarity memory dominates ranking for any query.\n\n**Evidence (eToro `etoro0`):** 28 memories had a future `ts_valid_start`\n+ NULL `ts_valid_end`. The AI-Act memory (`ts_valid_start = 2027-08-02`,\nextracted from its own text) reached `recall_count` 3,773 and ranked\n**#1 for 159 unrelated queries** at cosine ~0.33 — this was the true\ncause of that memory's day-0 explosion.\n\n## Fix\nClamp age to ≥ 0 via `greatest(0.0, age_days)` — a memory can never be\n\"fresher than now\"; freshness stays in `[floor, 1.0]`. One-line change\nin the scoring CASE.\n\n## Test\nAdds `test_scored_search_future_valid_start_does_not_inflate_freshness`:\na future-dated memory must not outscore an otherwise-identical\npresent-dated one (same embedding/weight/type).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"1187d146f7700f4dc00c035b869a67497a85ef8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/1187d146f7700f4dc00c035b869a67497a85ef8e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/b128553c1e4a3159744bdb542ad49c6332d33fe4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS12wCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAp78QACjUVqgtuVC2E0s5FhGGS502\ncXMRam8xBkpoXy0CzBRsWvSl4CX2S85d1QDHtXCxhOO4yfa414NhBBoeO/PUhR40\nGHSaF+aR77r3/nS71g6zDQYJlT+3xn0W9DeESNdvHdEgFCXkFTuNI49FuSfdCxFg\n7uothrIR8zEec1XIXMpai4Mlo22BYjKrhfCVq3HBKt5y4kOoOpTiywbaK18PiKYg\nNT5Yz94Nq4xOAYIBEuqLagNeIcmkE8HquKDNXEnHPq5o20U4zLExz3EuZqp/Excz\n3pmepIIu6DdPSDWveFtvFgChb5g5ty+dGKRkfYfWb4oEaXjm4/sNmCkwaXHas+cP\nT9gpgqPKOhZEPLIkykEhBo3Hp8sNgl6W2lC5SZcXVm5u+2IcXUWRN5f2XYyBh1/M\nHRBrzAIL/RkjzZfxEsaTKXRiBPY9cGSB4tsWH+h8gqOSvlQuN3BYSiJGc7XCle81\n3vQks8D8gghJzvKeO/5Xya0bRNACjtjOdDuPb1C+bZ2YrSTPupUexRE4UdROVkaA\n0OMMaM3/KrJ7Pnk9ymmIT9LXYIhmxewm9fmGdlmMuwu3tzDsMUhMEW+Asq3Cw3f8\noxo6DKaWCFCZYgFQuLiB5twZs5ttYTgiR8/PFapXX3eyLZ+iiZdcq1qz+3hBHR+a\nhh95quojYHNwAj6cdqSZ\n=nFyK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1187d146f7700f4dc00c035b869a67497a85ef8e\nparent c4a4fa040ef411d3966dfa7d7f33d0ef4681cabb\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1783324080 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783324080 +0300\n\nfix(scoring): cap freshness at 1.0 for future ts_valid_start (A43) (#529)\n\n## What\nCap the freshness factor at 1.0 in `memory_scored_search` so a **future\n`ts_valid_start`** (with `ts_valid_end` NULL) can't inflate freshness\nabove 1.0.\n\n## Why\nFreshness anchors on `greatest(created_at, coalesce(ts_valid_start,\ncreated_at))`; the age branch `1 - (age/type_decay)*(1-floor)` had no\nlower bound on age. A future anchor drives `age_days` negative →\nfreshness climbs to several× → final `score` exceeds 1.0 → a\nlow-similarity memory dominates ranking for any query.\n\n**Evidence (eToro `etoro0`):** 28 memories had a future `ts_valid_start`\n+ NULL `ts_valid_end`. The AI-Act memory (`ts_valid_start = 2027-08-02`,\nextracted from its own text) reached `recall_count` 3,773 and ranked\n**#1 for 159 unrelated queries** at cosine ~0.33 — this was the true\ncause of that memory's day-0 explosion.\n\n## Fix\nClamp age to ≥ 0 via `greatest(0.0, age_days)` — a memory can never be\n\"fresher than now\"; freshness stays in `[floor, 1.0]`. One-line change\nin the scoring CASE.\n\n## Test\nAdds `test_scored_search_future_valid_start_does_not_inflate_freshness`:\na future-dated memory must not outscore an otherwise-identical\npresent-dated one (same embedding/weight/type).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T07:48:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b128553c1e4a3159744bdb542ad49c6332d33fe4","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b128553c1e4a3159744bdb542ad49c6332d33fe4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b128553c1e4a3159744bdb542ad49c6332d33fe4/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c4a4fa040ef411d3966dfa7d7f33d0ef4681cabb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c4a4fa040ef411d3966dfa7d7f33d0ef4681cabb","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/c4a4fa040ef411d3966dfa7d7f33d0ef4681cabb"}]},{"sha":"c4a4fa040ef411d3966dfa7d7f33d0ef4681cabb","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGM0YTRmYTA0MGVmNDExZDM5NjZkZmE3ZDdmMzNkMGVmNDY4MWNhYmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-06T06:10:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T06:10:49Z"},"message":"chore(fleet): bump plugin auto-upgrade floor to 2.13.0 (firehose de-collapse) (#528)\n\n## What\nBump `MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION` **2.12.0 → 2.13.0** in\n`core_api/version_compat.py`.\n\n## Why\nPlugin **2.13.0** carries the plugin half of #507 — reserved-`main`\nwrite self-identification: when `MEMCLAW_AGENT_ID` is unset,\n`memclaw_write` now sends `agent_id = main-<install_id>` instead of an\nempty id that collapses onto the shared reserved `\"main\"` identity (the\neToro \"firehose\").\n\nThe **server** half (`effective_write_agent_id`, honor body id when the\nverified id is reserved `main`) already shipped in v2.11.4, but it is\n**inert** while the fleet runs 2.12.0 — the old plugin supplies no body\nid, so writes keep collapsing onto `main`. Raising the floor to 2.13.0\nmakes eligible nodes (≥ `MIN_AUTO_DEPLOY` 2.6.0, auto-upgrade enabled)\nauto-upgrade on their next heartbeat, at which point the firehose\n**de-collapses**: new writes land under distinct `main-<install_id>`\nidentities.\n\nDeliberate: this is the intended firehose solution for the v2.19.0 /\nonprem-v2.11.5 delivery.\n\n## Scope / safety\n- One constant. `MIN_AUTO_DEPLOY_PLUGIN_VERSION` unchanged (2.6.0).\n- Floor invariant (`recommended >= auto-deploy`) still holds —\n`tests/test_plugin_floor_invariant.py` is value-agnostic and passes.\n- Forward-going only: affects **new** writes; does not retro-split\nexisting `\"main\"` rows.\n- `reserved_agent_id_policy` stays `warn` (observe-only) and\n`bind_write_identity_to_auth` stays `false` on eToro — the\n`reserved_agent_write` warn-log rate is the success counter (should drop\ntoward 0 as nodes upgrade).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f288437f792c12b032ff06d69a4aa057519c36fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f288437f792c12b032ff06d69a4aa057519c36fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/c4a4fa040ef411d3966dfa7d7f33d0ef4681cabb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS0bpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHosQAH5PFxOW1Fi2yU/c6CJ/QE02\nRwB+Hazilxn8LL/Np+/j0bi3Pi5K0hULEA3S1GL7lZ89rl5CVUDT2Kzpse1lzdjq\nYSTHLGgg9XuAlQaQEHlYHnxs1B0PysNx/cy72pLsqR1CVbBaSneIINbMokiO/Yom\nRbx0/068rUXU3LGF59nvaneTx0o58z4IndnZXODC23eB795J3ssrFn+kqUw6m2Xa\nJ7MEr0iSAj9cHcgDAIvZS2p6A6e29Rf4LrEvfS+BtNDF4knIjPY4WnXls/mPUus+\nEuGSaos1peaWxF3hKGv3fbJnYMemIv8BAD9BnNTsawL+3BERdSax04h9Qfc20fL6\nYzSZYV93NlZR2DoOxv6dxjNRO29qILXiwCPqydu98TGw8z92c5PGdyrsUmd5OqSP\nEV8Tl0dw25c2vqQgg+KMra88l2qbshMrOnVZOKl7yfcpqQnlNragSehUCdW2KbRE\nK/q8BlDYMHN9D8yH3cKzL982Pkvc1BGaPQUX7ErFESAGkxO0fQvHQwVrRE21RohR\nTRdgQWoPQMyso7UWmqvAfZVl22EpsJhj67n6njdiQ9T1grtEF33heDC8ehgvjME+\nYcEerXRijOBS7bwtov57oRTS/bdDlnsaOnOuZV458wh49GMcBZVoANWrJ4j+dtFF\ndp8SIxWn8UdPIo8Q7k6e\n=oJue\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f288437f792c12b032ff06d69a4aa057519c36fa\nparent 9e222a1dba31b33b0e95560ee3ee09620809b119\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1783318249 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783318249 +0300\n\nchore(fleet): bump plugin auto-upgrade floor to 2.13.0 (firehose de-collapse) (#528)\n\n## What\nBump `MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION` **2.12.0 → 2.13.0** in\n`core_api/version_compat.py`.\n\n## Why\nPlugin **2.13.0** carries the plugin half of #507 — reserved-`main`\nwrite self-identification: when `MEMCLAW_AGENT_ID` is unset,\n`memclaw_write` now sends `agent_id = main-<install_id>` instead of an\nempty id that collapses onto the shared reserved `\"main\"` identity (the\neToro \"firehose\").\n\nThe **server** half (`effective_write_agent_id`, honor body id when the\nverified id is reserved `main`) already shipped in v2.11.4, but it is\n**inert** while the fleet runs 2.12.0 — the old plugin supplies no body\nid, so writes keep collapsing onto `main`. Raising the floor to 2.13.0\nmakes eligible nodes (≥ `MIN_AUTO_DEPLOY` 2.6.0, auto-upgrade enabled)\nauto-upgrade on their next heartbeat, at which point the firehose\n**de-collapses**: new writes land under distinct `main-<install_id>`\nidentities.\n\nDeliberate: this is the intended firehose solution for the v2.19.0 /\nonprem-v2.11.5 delivery.\n\n## Scope / safety\n- One constant. `MIN_AUTO_DEPLOY_PLUGIN_VERSION` unchanged (2.6.0).\n- Floor invariant (`recommended >= auto-deploy`) still holds —\n`tests/test_plugin_floor_invariant.py` is value-agnostic and passes.\n- Forward-going only: affects **new** writes; does not retro-split\nexisting `\"main\"` rows.\n- `reserved_agent_id_policy` stays `warn` (observe-only) and\n`bind_write_identity_to_auth` stays `false` on eToro — the\n`reserved_agent_write` warn-log rate is the success counter (should drop\ntoward 0 as nodes upgrade).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T06:10:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c4a4fa040ef411d3966dfa7d7f33d0ef4681cabb","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/c4a4fa040ef411d3966dfa7d7f33d0ef4681cabb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/c4a4fa040ef411d3966dfa7d7f33d0ef4681cabb/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9e222a1dba31b33b0e95560ee3ee09620809b119","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9e222a1dba31b33b0e95560ee3ee09620809b119","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9e222a1dba31b33b0e95560ee3ee09620809b119"}]},{"sha":"9e222a1dba31b33b0e95560ee3ee09620809b119","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDllMjIyYTFkYmEzMWIzM2IwZTk1NTYwZWUzZWUwOTYyMDgwOWIxMTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","email":"265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-05T21:18:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-05T21:18:51Z"},"message":"chore: release main (#496)\n\n:robot: I have created a release *beep* *boop*\n---\n\n\n<details><summary>backend: 2.19.0</summary>\n\n##\n[2.19.0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/backend-v2.18.0...backend-v2.19.0)\n(2026-07-05)\n\n\n### Features\n\n* **core-api,plugin:** self-identify MCP writes when the verified id is\nreserved \"main\"\n([#507](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/507))\n([1bc00c1](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/1bc00c14e2de653f006ab5226e1c22626b5f829d))\n* **core-api:** governed daily/weekly agent activity report (GET\n/api/v1/reports)\n([#514](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/514))\n([d6c569d](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/d6c569d72eaba687e3538743b9293b30760f9ca7))\n* **core-api:** reserve agent_id \"main\" on the write path (Phase 1)\n([#505](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/505))\n([1d313f9](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/1d313f94d3df953d83f37f37e068cdd2e3c6514b))\n* **observability:** log auto /search recalls behind a separate flag\n([#503](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/503))\n([f411db2](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/f411db29ee3f5821303128fb52936b8b6a889d3c))\n* **observability:** sample below-floor near-misses on the /search\nrecall log\n([#506](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/506))\n([9b18bd9](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/9b18bd91a6a816b6fab907c644a2e86eb3a9fa77))\n\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* **core-api:** don't 422 the whole heartbeat on an oversized\nobservability blob\n([#497](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/497))\n([77bfcbe](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/77bfcbe266f804a808b75e895f56c00895a71fd8))\n* **core-api:** stop passing removed positional db to log_action on\nwrite path\n([#495](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/495))\n([3f89218](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/3f892189cf6caa98cab1a838ae5b3dfaa18293a3))\n* **core-operations:** configure logging at import so uvicorn startup\nlines aren't tagged ERROR\n([#523](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/523))\n([ff88064](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/ff88064e3d7eae1aa15ab7302e6c5e405a43b5c0))\n* **logging:** floor ddtrace trace/LLMObs writer loggers at CRITICAL\n([#522](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/522))\n([a878d84](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/a878d84d17235d884cfe5da07502660bcf02bb78))\n\n\n### Performance\n\n* **recall:** cap summary max_tokens and fail fast on slow provider\n([#515](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/515))\n([5fd98b1](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/5fd98b1e991dcd48fa3203317f8daa2397bc480a))\n\n\n### Documentation\n\n* **readme:** add Skill Factory overview [slice 1]\n([#504](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/504))\n([cf8bfe9](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/cf8bfe9115fef1d04c3c1868caaf3fd86e4657a2))\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>plugin: 2.13.0</summary>\n\n##\n[2.13.0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/plugin-v2.12.0...plugin-v2.13.0)\n(2026-07-05)\n\n\n### Features\n\n* **core-api,plugin:** self-identify MCP writes when the verified id is\nreserved \"main\"\n([#507](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/507))\n([1bc00c1](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/1bc00c14e2de653f006ab5226e1c22626b5f829d))\n</details>\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with [Release\nPlease](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please). See\n[documentation](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please#release-please).\n\nSigned-off-by: release-please[bot] <release-please[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: caura-deploy-bot[bot] <265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ad46c229d33d7dc54562f90c4329e53d792c7ce8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/ad46c229d33d7dc54562f90c4329e53d792c7ce8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/9e222a1dba31b33b0e95560ee3ee09620809b119","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSso8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiBMQAARoTZH7lbQpmWz/RVVJ4W/i\nhThrlMTjP21YjIWE46Ed85WC/MmreVwQabUIBOYxfFGID+h19RwxVkd3rZdo5OCC\nPM9ETmm1VKQZ1FFXSYf1oytOPluUT52qAYIy2hxN/ZxV3LXVQWF/BULE1ndVwKHL\ns3oFbKIc/zvJyz2IrXqUlZjOZvt6WKPzVxM5FKJ8J0mITETVwMTYHvU50Oho7sKd\ncuNvumcjOvWqEylkJCW/KAa+7FykohRzB2G8vsCLuvJr2Txh/ed137WPyddQm7SG\nyenu7RyJHaIWHLEUP8jUAVDrJSpHjvm+J/jQfhgN306Bnn/lGoOB8dpRXbcrHRAE\nmm5rWcNsxV3YLKYfmkm8XwOaxnXsN7X9SkuhAFJYaHvSI+ElaeIjs0nhxMic9JEY\nQG7FgcQtvl28QgT8BjPmHT5KYcva2dlHvtE6Rs4ySuuYsvitbhouPOl7E0z8zqPZ\nQskITKUsb3mPjYK3tlnTh+1+r4GuRjUPTWkvbQRuKMmo+xoOnJ0lF+uxV6P7eelh\nIHN2xdpGNlGYvHEHK+D6THF2iroRkARiMN67f2t3j5FqfXkeYoSalIFvs+k39Jgz\nSYsxEnKKDClWx4p1SqAEa2w3wobwCgQyAziDEp+pStrrsKEfTyXCwCCXq6