#release-please).\n\nSigned-off-by: release-please[bot] <release-please[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: caura-deploy-bot[bot] <265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-05T21:18:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9e222a1dba31b33b0e95560ee3ee09620809b119","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/9e222a1dba31b33b0e95560ee3ee09620809b119","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/9e222a1dba31b33b0e95560ee3ee09620809b119/comments","author":{"login":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","id":265395343,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOD9Gcjw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229147182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/caura-deploy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d6c569d72eaba687e3538743b9293b30760f9ca7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d6c569d72eaba687e3538743b9293b30760f9ca7","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/d6c569d72eaba687e3538743b9293b30760f9ca7"}]},{"sha":"d6c569d72eaba687e3538743b9293b30760f9ca7","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGQ2YzU2OWQ3MmVhYmE2ODdlMzUzODc0M2I5MjkzYjMwNzYwZjljYTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-05T18:16:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-05T18:16:44Z"},"message":"feat(core-api): governed daily/weekly agent activity report (GET /api/v1/reports) (#514)\n\n## What\nAdds `GET /api/v1/reports` — a governed, audience-scoped daily/weekly\nagent activity report: per-agent durable-write counts, a by-type\nbreakdown, and recent distilled insights.\n\n## Changes\n- **Agent belonging model** — `belonging_type` + `owner_ref` on `agents`\n(migration `028`) to resolve report delivery audience; surfaced via\n`AGENT_FIELDS` so `get_agent`/`list_agents` return them.\n- **Windowed + durable breakdown** — `memory_stats_breakdown` gains\n`created_after`/`created_before` +\n`exclude_memory_types`/`exclude_agent_ids`, flowing through both the\nlive and `include_deleted` paths. Fixes the compile→`text()` POSTCOMPILE\nexpansion so `NOT IN` filters bind.\n- **Two-check governed read** — tenant authorization (`enforce_tenant`)\n+ a **narrow-only** `destination` down-filter (`owner_1to1` /\n`internal_group` / `private_session` / `external`; unknown or absent\nfails closed). The trust gate applies to agent callers only; a tenant\nmember gets the group view.\n- Corpus = durable, decision-bearing memories (excludes episodic logs +\nthe unattributed default identity).\n\n## Tests\n`tests/test_reports.py` — 5 DB-backed cases (durable filter, destination\nnarrowing, fail-closed, period validation, no-agent group view). All\ngreen locally against pgvector.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"99f287d27006263a5dec6b2b8bc7d452e039369a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/99f287d27006263a5dec6b2b8bc7d452e039369a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/d6c569d72eaba687e3538743b9293b30760f9ca7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSp+MCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjDUQAJWPJRJm5zHuLMm4lDbTqTO3\nrpKja0sVEOfhOQxJRBDx6RZ7Td3Bd4IHVkN4O2r9nu87TSOk0rcRtGVY+OtkCxXA\nvNWNjB1XA3MghmKJrPoRGMFRFmTabDaHSklcRZbLmZtYZ8h6eQvZ3QsTPkat9jAe\nUZ4Y2+9rbUI8xdj8fC7tG66TL3b3ma0wi5rTVoyWzKzV8bmOga5CiOGPxw7rekpO\nJOWngt8X3AUKGvXs7xKiPImIVBNpspNp5hpzO1XuCBiRQJCbdodLADoS/c7SvRD1\nX8RHSsheyhNItlTQI0bom3V0+n9gFi+ZPUn7qX7Lw8MHTCqzF4vF/D90cRgp1P7J\nSpYCRHdE3qSKtPf5W0BP7UxhqDjBhMuSM7qpYKHKb9DZOFgqAJ2fEFAo64ycYK+2\nv4VY0kPpcH8UzbjIvs8T6IUVNi2/UX1vW4PFR/DEkeag8RRAhI+t+UtHSUI05Heg\nx80e5QN2Aq60Np7qdCnkMizwK6m5+ytr84l4t6syTFaY9BxYRbmmbTzcL6zXp8cw\nN3C/BytGFeoxEcbG64JzSk3tpBLLwps9/jsDE8hZzA5jOm71TZguh9MhoWDbLD3W\n4no8XSXGANj2+mKlM2mdgwymBJToMGrWeMQkGkFbnCZkX0KUtsb/CDZrWGIuAW8G\nCiyBdls/8VdjbUTPLs/6\n=A/p1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 99f287d27006263a5dec6b2b8bc7d452e039369a\nparent ff88064e3d7eae1aa15ab7302e6c5e405a43b5c0\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1783275404 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783275404 +0300\n\nfeat(core-api): governed daily/weekly agent activity report (GET /api/v1/reports) (#514)\n\n## What\nAdds `GET /api/v1/reports` — a governed, audience-scoped daily/weekly\nagent activity report: per-agent durable-write counts, a by-type\nbreakdown, and recent distilled insights.\n\n## Changes\n- **Agent belonging model** — `belonging_type` + `owner_ref` on `agents`\n(migration `028`) to resolve report delivery audience; surfaced via\n`AGENT_FIELDS` so `get_agent`/`list_agents` return them.\n- **Windowed + durable breakdown** — `memory_stats_breakdown` gains\n`created_after`/`created_before` +\n`exclude_memory_types`/`exclude_agent_ids`, flowing through both the\nlive and `include_deleted` paths. Fixes the compile→`text()` POSTCOMPILE\nexpansion so `NOT IN` filters bind.\n- **Two-check governed read** — tenant authorization (`enforce_tenant`)\n+ a **narrow-only** `destination` down-filter (`owner_1to1` /\n`internal_group` / `private_session` / `external`; unknown or absent\nfails closed). The trust gate applies to agent callers only; a tenant\nmember gets the group view.\n- Corpus = durable, decision-bearing memories (excludes episodic logs +\nthe unattributed default identity).\n\n## Tests\n`tests/test_reports.py` — 5 DB-backed cases (durable filter, destination\nnarrowing, fail-closed, period validation, no-agent group view). All\ngreen locally against pgvector.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-07-05T18:16:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d6c569d72eaba687e3538743b9293b30760f9ca7","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/d6c569d72eaba687e3538743b9293b30760f9ca7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/d6c569d72eaba687e3538743b9293b30760f9ca7/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ff88064e3d7eae1aa15ab7302e6c5e405a43b5c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ff88064e3d7eae1aa15ab7302e6c5e405a43b5c0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ff88064e3d7eae1aa15ab7302e6c5e405a43b5c0"}]},{"sha":"ff88064e3d7eae1aa15ab7302e6c5e405a43b5c0","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGZmODgwNjRlM2Q3ZWFlMWFhMTVhYjczMDJlNmM1ZTQwNWE0M2I1YzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-04T23:19:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-04T23:19:44Z"},"message":"fix(core-operations): configure logging at import so uvicorn startup lines aren't tagged ERROR (#523)\n\n## What\nMove `configure_logging()` from the lifespan startup hook to **module\nimport** in `core-operations/app.py`, and call\n`reroute_third_party_loggers()` in the lifespan — mirroring core-api.\n\n## Why\nThe 36h error sweep flagged `core-operations` (and\n`platform-operations`) emitting `status:error` logs that are actually\nuvicorn **INFO** startup lines:\n\n```\nINFO:     Started server process [8]\nINFO:     Waiting for application startup.\n```\n\nuvicorn logs these via `uvicorn.error` **before** the ASGI lifespan\nruns. core-operations configured logging *inside* the lifespan, so at\nthat moment the logger reroute wasn't active yet — the two lines fell\nthrough uvicorn's default plain-text stderr handler, and Cloud Logging\ntagged them `ERROR`. They're benign INFO (and pre-caura-ops#192 could\neven page).\n\ncore-api doesn't have this because it calls `configure_logging()` at\nimport (uvicorn imports the app module during config load, so the\nreroute is in effect before the startup lines) and only\n`reroute_third_party_loggers()` in the lifespan. This change brings\ncore-operations in line.\n\n## Test\nFull `core-operations` suite green (**34 passed**), including\n`test_app.py` (imports the module) and `test_scheduler.py` (uses caplog)\n— the deferral was originally to protect pytest caplog, and this proves\nimport-time config doesn't break it (the repo's per-test reset handles\nit, same as core-api). ruff clean.\n\n## Note\n`platform-operations` (enterprise repo) has the same lifespan-deferred\npattern and needs the identical one-line move — happy to follow up with\nthat PR.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"519ada3ac5e73bdaad71079280a87c86f69ed0dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/519ada3ac5e73bdaad71079280a87c86f69ed0dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/ff88064e3d7eae1aa15ab7302e6c5e405a43b5c0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSZUQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUGwQAHOKImpMRrysePK/DtliSUb+\nPv+11TZnypL+GrBrCc6BSwaXGAoLKk3urijnswNj8MBVhogGmT/BYo58k/SUXSFl\nKaYZDq4KLyeCoqmLeXUrsEox+AL80+/rAaS/wMcugYIoCf+GHtVrHeJGyHOf//Yq\nY219kafUyURWul1Opg9q2LbetTdv3Qgwf+UIiACo4uBZLClRLQxsrfT6EXJUatHI\nyx3h+7+voaWHe0mqjVkp33t2aZqEcivagqwPBfp3rU7lAJjfEAjmQevEVAWMuYBF\nrieFhIpBUzC5B8HMk1ThMAL+3sC2/Kq+tBQNVJBtiBM3pdOEnv3fxyxiepPNrg5l\n7FyoFdbI2hE62aoojuyUJFnPpbp6OEpxWdqSiMFKybQHln6X6vbTBJhvzZzKx6nW\nyHGoIB8m1NvS+yJZTayg5FeyRQb3UjejS9gRrU8B9w32Y5ZvZSqUBO8kY+LW5Yiq\nhIP2Lz0B9M4STdgTN/DfFhALbcfy0nUz7eWgsXrw+TVATuZ/szllki1UTeN0+NH1\nI6hQxDso89dRDTXL7GA5bpfRvg2BXYIWhfX7quw+dfthJ3Y1LDJis7cfgeAglA6x\nReaQw8PtcR9Z5Pq1rAG6PdzaO20H/MwsT3Kfcz2jz9ig2Nz/YMya5US+iJoIrZIE\ne+dYaIHOZvlSBnKqEmJg\n=kjYK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 519ada3ac5e73bdaad71079280a87c86f69ed0dc\nparent a878d84d17235d884cfe5da07502660bcf02bb78\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1783207184 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783207184 +0300\n\nfix(core-operations): configure logging at import so uvicorn startup lines aren't tagged ERROR (#523)\n\n## What\nMove `configure_logging()` from the lifespan startup hook to **module\nimport** in `core-operations/app.py`, and call\n`reroute_third_party_loggers()` in the lifespan — mirroring core-api.\n\n## Why\nThe 36h error sweep flagged `core-operations` (and\n`platform-operations`) emitting `status:error` logs that are actually\nuvicorn **INFO** startup lines:\n\n```\nINFO:     Started server process [8]\nINFO:     Waiting for application startup.\n```\n\nuvicorn logs these via `uvicorn.error` **before** the ASGI lifespan\nruns. core-operations configured logging *inside* the lifespan, so at\nthat moment the logger reroute wasn't active yet — the two lines fell\nthrough uvicorn's default plain-text stderr handler, and Cloud Logging\ntagged them `ERROR`. They're benign INFO (and pre-caura-ops#192 could\neven page).\n\ncore-api doesn't have this because it calls `configure_logging()` at\nimport (uvicorn imports the app module during config load, so the\nreroute is in effect before the startup lines) and only\n`reroute_third_party_loggers()` in the lifespan. This change brings\ncore-operations in line.\n\n## Test\nFull `core-operations` suite green (**34 passed**), including\n`test_app.py` (imports the module) and `test_scheduler.py` (uses caplog)\n— the deferral was originally to protect pytest caplog, and this proves\nimport-time config doesn't break it (the repo's per-test reset handles\nit, same as core-api). ruff clean.\n\n## Note\n`platform-operations` (enterprise repo) has the same lifespan-deferred\npattern and needs the identical one-line move — happy to follow up with\nthat PR.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-04T23:19:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ff88064e3d7eae1aa15ab7302e6c5e405a43b5c0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ff88064e3d7eae1aa15ab7302e6c5e405a43b5c0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ff88064e3d7eae1aa15ab7302e6c5e405a43b5c0/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a878d84d17235d884cfe5da07502660bcf02bb78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a878d84d17235d884cfe5da07502660bcf02bb78","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a878d84d17235d884cfe5da07502660bcf02bb78"}]},{"sha":"a878d84d17235d884cfe5da07502660bcf02bb78","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGE4NzhkODRkMTcyMzVkODg0Y2ZlNWRhMDc1MDI2NjBiY2YwMmJiNzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-04T22:49:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-04T22:49:38Z"},"message":"fix(logging): floor ddtrace trace/LLMObs writer loggers at CRITICAL (#522)\n\n## What\nFloor the `ddtrace.internal.writer.writer` and `ddtrace.llmobs._writer`\nloggers at CRITICAL in the shared `configure_logging` (when the root\nlevel is INFO/WARNING; skipped at DEBUG). `_reset_for_testing` clears\nthe floor back to NOTSET.\n\n## Why\nOver the last 36h these two loggers produced **~95% of all\n`status:error` log volume** across prod+staging — every failed flush to\nthe in-container agent at `localhost:8126` logs at ERROR:\n\n```\nfailed to send, dropping N traces to intake at http://localhost:8126/v0.5/traces: timed out\nfailed to send N LLMObs span events to http://localhost:8126 … TimeoutError / 502 / 429 / ConnectionReset\n```\n\nThese are **dropped-telemetry events** (`send_to_telemetry:false`), not\napplication errors — the app is unaffected. But because they emit at\nERROR they surface as errors in Datadog Logs, GCP Logging, and the\n**caura-ops error alerter**, where they drive alert flapping in both\nenvs. CPU-throttling fixes (ent#701/#717) reduce the CPU-starvation\ntimeouts but the agent-side variants (502/429/RemoteDisconnected)\npersist, so silencing at the source is the durable fix.\n\nFlooring at CRITICAL drops the ERROR/WARNING noise while still surfacing\na genuine writer CRITICAL. Lives in the shared structlog config, so it\napplies to every service (core-api, core-worker, core-operations,\nplatform-*) at once.\n\n## Test\nAdded `tests/test_logging.py` coverage: floored at CRITICAL at INFO\n**and** WARNING, not floored at DEBUG, and reset restores NOTSET. `uv\nrun pytest tests/test_logging.py` green; ruff clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"53138d568fb4de7263a0bfaf9bf8b61f9a99a4a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/53138d568fb4de7263a0bfaf9bf8b61f9a99a4a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/a878d84d17235d884cfe5da07502660bcf02bb78","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSY4CCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzZYQAGxX0JY4Fk5jdX4cUMorRlyH\nUNgZ24AMMo2zBMG07dyqY1NNWEzGFhK7Llm+tCgfCvg2dY9Vf1c2D2X0ZB/nKaL3\nf7m72X7UmxQPilWlW7o+pzr7tA1DFtXcllBkpQLJLQsw7Xl//jvc9zcPh7NZTguI\neRNHG9j7373mk3SsO9cakCNUL6Z+2CE8PaMvY3ea+A6PbL874TzPlI8UZEAYzARO\ncuQRKnvcqkccctSPxFDpP9PfmdXeuFpblhRCEhl3xN12CnMc5ld+9+scC+q60VyH\n0+11KFPVjFLA/axoQAg6+gIv4FQCUeFW7tekpgy5bm6IRY1pOpdYOsTZmB+9U5GL\ng3uFvRTKn4uXRpmpCfBipBjIFNd4gSxNjQLmGRgEFTL8a2M84SHFjCVJ13w9aq6V\n0l3Eo4IY8ZfigB1c1gtbwHY8pzfqMxVaHQHnW1g6Lhya77EAyL+KCCk0P3TMcjqv\n10Zrw9BUbIKyOkic6t54ZyMISPJxwMr2MQzHjigH9mu+3pY01qehWy0ne6MzgLAJ\ng2Hi2xD5QTONkB1OI9y+wLOta9Dtb/wMKBFbgjgsI9wOWujD//IFkA7E5Fl9EVR8\ncTA5fXVqoD+Q2vOqbWPIKog8T3CtZHWFWfAfo5NaUTOQ5sz86FDhzVpCUkUuDrei\nPvSDtuJZC6SAkUj9cMIU\n=Jzt0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 53138d568fb4de7263a0bfaf9bf8b61f9a99a4a1\nparent ce3f31beefc5b302b5188368e3beb4d83dd66fdc\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1783205378 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783205378 +0300\n\nfix(logging): floor ddtrace trace/LLMObs writer loggers at CRITICAL (#522)\n\n## What\nFloor the `ddtrace.internal.writer.writer` and `ddtrace.llmobs._writer`\nloggers at CRITICAL in the shared `configure_logging` (when the root\nlevel is INFO/WARNING; skipped at DEBUG). `_reset_for_testing` clears\nthe floor back to NOTSET.\n\n## Why\nOver the last 36h these two loggers produced **~95% of all\n`status:error` log volume** across prod+staging — every failed flush to\nthe in-container agent at `localhost:8126` logs at ERROR:\n\n```\nfailed to send, dropping N traces to intake at http://localhost:8126/v0.5/traces: timed out\nfailed to send N LLMObs span events to http://localhost:8126 … TimeoutError / 502 / 429 / ConnectionReset\n```\n\nThese are **dropped-telemetry events** (`send_to_telemetry:false`), not\napplication errors — the app is unaffected. But because they emit at\nERROR they surface as errors in Datadog Logs, GCP Logging, and the\n**caura-ops error alerter**, where they drive alert flapping in both\nenvs. CPU-throttling fixes (ent#701/#717) reduce the CPU-starvation\ntimeouts but the agent-side variants (502/429/RemoteDisconnected)\npersist, so silencing at the source is the durable fix.\n\nFlooring at CRITICAL drops the ERROR/WARNING noise while still surfacing\na genuine writer CRITICAL. Lives in the shared structlog config, so it\napplies to every service (core-api, core-worker, core-operations,\nplatform-*) at once.\n\n## Test\nAdded `tests/test_logging.py` coverage: floored at CRITICAL at INFO\n**and** WARNING, not floored at DEBUG, and reset restores NOTSET. `uv\nrun pytest tests/test_logging.py` green; ruff clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-04T22:49:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a878d84d17235d884cfe5da07502660bcf02bb78","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/a878d84d17235d884cfe5da07502660bcf02bb78","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/a878d84d17235d884cfe5da07502660bcf02bb78/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ce3f31beefc5b302b5188368e3beb4d83dd66fdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ce3f31beefc5b302b5188368e3beb4d83dd66fdc","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ce3f31beefc5b302b5188368e3beb4d83dd66fdc"}]},{"sha":"ce3f31beefc5b302b5188368e3beb4d83dd66fdc","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGNlM2YzMWJlZWZjNWIzMDJiNTE4ODM2OGUzYmViNGQ4M2RkNjZmZGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-02T22:16:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-02T22:16:43Z"},"message":"chore(search): log temporal_hint at DEBUG, not INFO (#519)\n\n## What\n`extract_temporal_hint` logged the raw search query at `INFO` on every\nsearch:\n```\ntemporal_hint: query='<the query>' ref=… window=… date_range=…\n```\nDropped to `DEBUG`.\n\n## Why\n1. **PII / noise:** it emits verbatim customer query content to prod\nlogs, once per search.\n2. **The \"phantom error\" echo:** caura-ops's error-investigator\nsemantically searches memclaw using each error-alert **signature** as\nthe query. So an error string like `failed to send, dropping 1 traces to\nintake at http://localhost:8126/v0.5/traces` comes back through *this*\nlog as `temporal_hint: query='failed to send, dropping 1 traces…'` —\nwhich looks like a recurring tracer error in prod logs but is just the\nsearch echo. Dropping to DEBUG removes the echo (and the PII) from prod\nregardless of what triggers the search.\n\n`extract_temporal_hint` is the only search step that logs the raw query\nat INFO (the others log classifications). `temporal_window` /\n`date_range_filter` remain on `ctx.data` for downstream logging. Tests\ngreen (41), ruff clean.\n\n## Note\nOSS repo — auto-review skips for non-public-member authors; `@claude`\nfor a review pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ad1eefb07a51e3fed8a8e1a5e874e2211da881af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/ad1eefb07a51e3fed8a8e1a5e874e2211da881af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/ce3f31beefc5b302b5188368e3beb4d83dd66fdc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRuNLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9AsQAHrMySYb9TYKWaO/QI6vvW7m\ncJWpYE/mMCFJ2AG0E4AXy6GM/pdLSnpjh3OrEdpdjkmmL4bAYY5fcvHlnbPEl1fw\n/Hzl/8AGEHeiXIzeFIt1xALFZTiZZFc7dhwGngv8FHcMpx0osGeqkNjjbCEens1k\nmM1ECW39IJphqaq7ChMuaTv+mDjP2RUG9t5CdwDSve1R4i2MNT3lKQfwPmAdYga2\nOl1DGhVpP9M/yIdEXI1R4gxY4IEmcUpfkqMscBjpAO57tP+4WYcN4bLzbSxue77b\nuOBu4Za07t/xcioPKNuTFyIe2qMDhXQMYVZRIda1KfGLXU4fHdK3MRHXJhAQsapU\nzt1i70GLbeoQtlfMPipwoVuZVkysfrsAp2DU7QaijXkeYmw+Vt3t28gu3MYiz1C2\nn21icBSkdUSNxVDwyBuL9ijTbis+uuW4ThoGuitJAFwueAVvpjq3fWbDTUGqoZsS\nb6ukSX2yqnh19RJWSOIThlDpzsxJFozKwVLSXRh+3oXTURj2A20Uox7cGEP1j+lX\nESpkefiafghd6FdGvjrXWkK9vomj0sl2DqAN9uLXs3Guv8a4WChpyAbBJNoXmS3G\nIKnZgkd4N8+SrI8SqjIr1XjtZJbJeS1PeCcyEtlqZ2CCq+KzGWH1qfcsnisXICvu\n73RvcjLfpmIX2TYK0DVv\n=1HjY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ad1eefb07a51e3fed8a8e1a5e874e2211da881af\nparent e78f4f8bdc1c5a307deecf3bae6b5db30adcfe21\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1783030603 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783030603 +0300\n\nchore(search): log temporal_hint at DEBUG, not INFO (#519)\n\n## What\n`extract_temporal_hint` logged the raw search query at `INFO` on every\nsearch:\n```\ntemporal_hint: query='<the query>' ref=… window=… date_range=…\n```\nDropped to `DEBUG`.\n\n## Why\n1. **PII / noise:** it emits verbatim customer query content to prod\nlogs, once per search.\n2. **The \"phantom error\" echo:** caura-ops's error-investigator\nsemantically searches memclaw using each error-alert **signature** as\nthe query. So an error string like `failed to send, dropping 1 traces to\nintake at http://localhost:8126/v0.5/traces` comes back through *this*\nlog as `temporal_hint: query='failed to send, dropping 1 traces…'` —\nwhich looks like a recurring tracer error in prod logs but is just the\nsearch echo. Dropping to DEBUG removes the echo (and the PII) from prod\nregardless of what triggers the search.\n\n`extract_temporal_hint` is the only search step that logs the raw query\nat INFO (the others log classifications). `temporal_window` /\n`date_range_filter` remain on `ctx.data` for downstream logging. Tests\ngreen (41), ruff clean.\n\n## Note\nOSS repo — auto-review skips for non-public-member authors; `@claude`\nfor a review pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-02T22:16:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ce3f31beefc5b302b5188368e3beb4d83dd66fdc","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ce3f31beefc5b302b5188368e3beb4d83dd66fdc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ce3f31beefc5b302b5188368e3beb4d83dd66fdc/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e78f4f8bdc1c5a307deecf3bae6b5db30adcfe21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e78f4f8bdc1c5a307deecf3bae6b5db30adcfe21","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e78f4f8bdc1c5a307deecf3bae6b5db30adcfe21"}]},{"sha":"e78f4f8bdc1c5a307deecf3bae6b5db30adcfe21","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGU3OGY0ZjhiZGMxYzVhMzA3ZGVlY2YzYmFlNmI1ZGIzMGFkY2ZlMjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-02T17:31:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-02T17:31:59Z"},"message":"fix(lifecycle): correct run_crystallization args in crystallize adapter (#518)\n\n## What\nOne-line fix at `core-api/src/core_api/services/lifecycle_audit.py` —\nthe lifecycle `crystallize` adapter called `run_crystallization` with a\nstray leading `None` and a colliding `trigger`:\n\n```python\n# before\nrun_crystallization(None, org_id, fleet_id, trigger=\"lifecycle\")\n# after\nrun_crystallization(tenant_id=org_id, fleet_id=fleet_id, trigger=\"lifecycle\")\n```\n\n## Why\n`run_crystallization(tenant_id, fleet_id=None, trigger=\"manual\",\nauto_crystallize=True)`. The stray `None` shifted every positional —\n`tenant_id=None`, `fleet_id=org_id`, `trigger=fleet_id` — and then\n`trigger=\"lifecycle\"` was *also* passed by keyword, so **every**\nlifecycle-triggered crystallization raised:\n\n```\nTypeError: run_crystallization() got multiple values for argument 'trigger'\n```\n\nThe pubsub lifecycle handler (`common/events/lifecycle_handlers.py` →\n`crystallize_op` → `adapter.crystallize`) then nacked + redelivered —\n**~20 occurrences/day on prod core-api**, and lifecycle-driven\ncrystallization never actually ran.\n\n`org_id` is the tenant scope at this boundary — the adapter's own\ndocstring says *\"the storage client's primitives still call the column\n`tenant_id`; translate at the boundary\"*, and `resolve_config(org_id)`\nhere is the same call the HTTP routes make as\n`resolve_config(tenant_id)` before `run_crystallization(tenant_id, …)`.\nSo `tenant_id=org_id`. Keyword args are used so this positional class of\nbug can't recur.\n\n## Tests\nAdds `tests/test_lifecycle_audit.py` (3 tests): the happy path asserts\nthe exact call `run_crystallization(tenant_id=\"t1\", fleet_id=\"f1\",\ntrigger=\"lifecycle\")` via an **`autospec`'d** mock (which enforces the\nreal signature — the old buggy call would raise `TypeError` in the\ntest), plus the two skip gates (auto-crystallize disabled, below\nactive-memory threshold). The existing `test_lifecycle_handlers.py`\nfully fakes the adapter, which is why this call site was uncovered. Full\nrun green; ruff clean.\n\n## Note\nAuto-review will skip on open (public OSS repo, non-public-member\nauthor) — `@claude` if you want a review pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"df0fb3890ec635a99f40408b81bcc9b871ff12b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/df0fb3890ec635a99f40408b81bcc9b871ff12b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/e78f4f8bdc1c5a307deecf3bae6b5db30adcfe21","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRqCPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAH3sQAARPW8yLKrennohepC3r0rfH\n7lI3lHy96aeY8XpdxyJbQdhWms7Nm1fJhfIsEkBI4jC0rH3z3oSSBrC5NTMKK+uO\nZiP/9uzFDZ2Kfme0smLU06tnFt94UnG+P53XYJRegIaRJT9zzKawAQNw1iVLXFKD\nnaP7YmeBBPhT6746MXjEnPKHYIoKqhX5RUWtHtZNOUVj/iMfQie3Cgp4gJ7GY5OU\nKZHOqNz7yxPXGA23LFs8eApk9otEKDXtlVcvwtLGUS66bgONVPSixhtbgIRUITdI\nlohzNkDIThnayPC3KUmk1Y8a5934exDfYatPdBcIq5HVezd6FPyHrnZKt2hTiR8o\nnjusuGlcREAdEUdRZ9sGW2krxELg9OkePgK+u9BumOOXg0ePSWazmMqodw/VzFSU\nwCfa/tWHERDXkHQaQ9Pwhqvms2ozblR7wQ+VqF6Zp/NANQv70QW131hkWlMUrAi1\nBk2vaVmgi8HfCMWF45a4nc5aleTjmrBU0odswIVghjCylxbn4B9HV5voS3AruuEC\nlTrS/8Bq4xDYVdqgBwYx5kxw5v/HBp5wGPHIA8W2qrh4E9VEGRLX99yMReecOvue\nDoRd9IJjvlOiR34advRCcTkiIFygFReJa6Weyl1W8aZjCTMlVxwmiVQrrgubmXr9\nMt/P8etL7GUJ9soYSHnC\n=d2pq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree df0fb3890ec635a99f40408b81bcc9b871ff12b2\nparent 5fd98b1e991dcd48fa3203317f8daa2397bc480a\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1783013519 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783013519 +0300\n\nfix(lifecycle): correct run_crystallization args in crystallize adapter (#518)\n\n## What\nOne-line fix at `core-api/src/core_api/services/lifecycle_audit.py` —\nthe lifecycle `crystallize` adapter called `run_crystallization` with a\nstray leading `None` and a colliding `trigger`:\n\n```python\n# before\nrun_crystallization(None, org_id, fleet_id, trigger=\"lifecycle\")\n# after\nrun_crystallization(tenant_id=org_id, fleet_id=fleet_id, trigger=\"lifecycle\")\n```\n\n## Why\n`run_crystallization(tenant_id, fleet_id=None, trigger=\"manual\",\nauto_crystallize=True)`. The stray `None` shifted every positional —\n`tenant_id=None`, `fleet_id=org_id`, `trigger=fleet_id` — and then\n`trigger=\"lifecycle\"` was *also* passed by keyword, so **every**\nlifecycle-triggered crystallization raised:\n\n```\nTypeError: run_crystallization() got multiple values for argument 'trigger'\n```\n\nThe pubsub lifecycle handler (`common/events/lifecycle_handlers.py` →\n`crystallize_op` → `adapter.crystallize`) then nacked + redelivered —\n**~20 occurrences/day on prod core-api**, and lifecycle-driven\ncrystallization never actually ran.\n\n`org_id` is the tenant scope at this boundary — the adapter's own\ndocstring says *\"the storage client's primitives still call the column\n`tenant_id`; translate at the boundary\"*, and `resolve_config(org_id)`\nhere is the same call the HTTP routes make as\n`resolve_config(tenant_id)` before `run_crystallization(tenant_id, …)`.\nSo `tenant_id=org_id`. Keyword args are used so this positional class of\nbug can't recur.\n\n## Tests\nAdds `tests/test_lifecycle_audit.py` (3 tests): the happy path asserts\nthe exact call `run_crystallization(tenant_id=\"t1\", fleet_id=\"f1\",\ntrigger=\"lifecycle\")` via an **`autospec`'d** mock (which enforces the\nreal signature — the old buggy call would raise `TypeError` in the\ntest), plus the two skip gates (auto-crystallize disabled, below\nactive-memory threshold). The existing `test_lifecycle_handlers.py`\nfully fakes the adapter, which is why this call site was uncovered. Full\nrun green; ruff clean.\n\n## Note\nAuto-review will skip on open (public OSS repo, non-public-member\nauthor) — `@claude` if you want a review pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-02T17:32:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e78f4f8bdc1c5a307deecf3bae6b5db30adcfe21","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/e78f4f8bdc1c5a307deecf3bae6b5db30adcfe21","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/e78f4f8bdc1c5a307deecf3bae6b5db30adcfe21/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5fd98b1e991dcd48fa3203317f8daa2397bc480a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5fd98b1e991dcd48fa3203317f8daa2397bc480a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5fd98b1e991dcd48fa3203317f8daa2397bc480a"}]},{"sha":"5fd98b1e991dcd48fa3203317f8daa2397bc480a","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDVmZDk4YjFlOTkxZGNkNDhmYTMyMDMzMTdmOGRhYTIzOTdiYzQ4MGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-02T08:02:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-02T08:02:58Z"},"message":"perf(recall): cap summary max_tokens and fail fast on slow provider (#515)\n\n## What\n\nTwo latency levers on the `POST /api/v1/recall` hot path, from the\ninvestigation into the prod recall tail (and its link to the Cloud Run\n503 alert).\n\n1. **Cap `MEMORY_RECALL_SUMMARY_MAX_TOKENS` 1000 → 500**\n(`core-api/constants.py`). The recall summary is generated\nnon-streaming, so the full generation time is exposed to the caller and\nlong completions dominate the tail. 500 halves the worst-case\noutput-bound generation.\n2. **Recall calls `call_with_fallback(timeout=15.0, max_attempts=1)`**\n(`recall_service.py`). Adds a backward-compatible `max_attempts` kwarg\nto `call_with_fallback` (default `LLM_RETRY_ATTEMPTS`, threaded to both\nthe primary and fallback `call_with_retry` — no change for any other\ncaller).\n\n## Why\n\nProd `POST /api/v1/recall` p95+ was routinely **5–15s** — all HTTP 200,\njust slow. Traced to the LLM summarization step (`summarize_memories` →\n`llm.complete_text`, non-streaming); search/embed is not the bottleneck\n(`DEFAULT_SEARCH_TOP_K=5`, small input).\n\nThe retry path is also a **503 amplifier**: `call_with_fallback` ran\n`LLM_RETRY_ATTEMPTS=2` per-attempt-timeout retries across **both**\nprimary and fallback at a **30s** per-attempt timeout — worst case\n~122s, capped only by the 45s request-timeout middleware / 60s Cloud\nRun, at which point it becomes one of the *\"malformed response /\nconnection to the instance had an error\"* 503s. Capping the timeout\n**and** dropping to a single attempt per provider bounds recall at ~30s\nworst case (15s primary → 15s fallback → `_fake_recall`) and fails fast\ninstead of hanging.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\n- **max_tokens=500, not lower:** `RECALL_PROMPT` still emits\nstep-by-step chain-of-thought *before* the answer, so a tighter cap\nrisks truncating the answer. If we later trim the CoT from the prompt\n(the separate prompt lever), this can drop toward ~400.\n- **max_attempts=1 for recall only:** removes *same-provider* retries on\nthis read path. Cross-provider resilience (primary → fallback → fake) is\nunchanged; a same-provider retry after a timeout rarely succeeds and\ndoubles user-facing latency. Write-path enrichment/extraction keep the\ndefault 2 attempts.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_p4_1_llm_fallback.py`: added\n`TestCallWithFallbackMaxAttempts` — `max_attempts=1` invokes the primary\nonce (no retry) then falls through; default still retries\n`LLM_RETRY_ATTEMPTS` times. Full fallback suite (40) + recall suites\n(43) green; ruff clean.\n\n## Follow-up / verification\n\nNow that DD APM + LLMObs are live in prod, the `POST /api/v1/recall` APM\nspan waterfall + `ml_obs.span.llm.duration` for the recall model will\nshow the before/after split directly (these are the traces the\n`--no-cpu-throttling` fix stopped dropping).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b451bd28256bdce8dc4df37b62d7ee2547fd8695","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/b451bd28256bdce8dc4df37b62d7ee2547fd8695"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/5fd98b1e991dcd48fa3203317f8daa2397bc480a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRhsyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3aMQALGLhn0ucJvdup0JhqiUDY59\nXKpFfirPrE5cv1wbKh+9PdhpEmWTuRkbYJb6CW6sXNSInEXoVBO9npc2paRfKc47\nCvEheURruHUBl/hFuse2kYk6RI6lbfifaMSTetMoJCXdE9BGhKnH0OIFDhFwbB2C\nl7trzEq4RF4h8rwNvUBX2Xw9xRZ4W9lt5DQ9MGsOFHW3+Zaqe/J0do+CXiwLlW6k\nnV6SSdT8/PGQhIoKN8HofZLhvfaPDQtaWz6Cdpkd2MF5W2vj7FR0b2gTo1H6PIxD\nwUGg2icq2S1ilK6k5nWVlRMzSiaSSbptxnHDr3nF7atjkY3Cl9Kuqej4FfDePmM7\nlLjykPwvgpa+jSYxEsEUQ+b8AFdk57PwlLmbcYnme5AIiG17Y/wNkY8XH1V02h8T\nP51dM6i8KNuc4AWJhX3y/4I5oQx6fHTKVx4q5b//V3tlFhEgvNyI55imqnP1k7FE\nvDnkUV/vATZ2Ha5uw8w4+l7Uep+IAzhs9yFo4aNWEo6dK2704dQpTSrmhf4Gjgil\nkzxG0N5SGZpP3MxsJtBoaMF2K2g4oDSrGfdTwatWdQrQthKy/zvzD1aH/uSmHI7q\niYjX801y+hvhN2AN7I1etVO23wDfHnm9J8ltoodAcGm7YpDOKpImMaV/jd4/J1dw\njPbhqmlQ15qVhq90YeTL\n=Sbyj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b451bd28256bdce8dc4df37b62d7ee2547fd8695\nparent 3e2bb6640f532209b4a01f964374b36a6eab0741\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782979378 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782979378 +0300\n\nperf(recall): cap summary max_tokens and fail fast on slow provider (#515)\n\n## What\n\nTwo latency levers on the `POST /api/v1/recall` hot path, from the\ninvestigation into the prod recall tail (and its link to the Cloud Run\n503 alert).\n\n1. **Cap `MEMORY_RECALL_SUMMARY_MAX_TOKENS` 1000 → 500**\n(`core-api/constants.py`). The recall summary is generated\nnon-streaming, so the full generation time is exposed to the caller and\nlong completions dominate the tail. 500 halves the worst-case\noutput-bound generation.\n2. **Recall calls `call_with_fallback(timeout=15.0, max_attempts=1)`**\n(`recall_service.py`). Adds a backward-compatible `max_attempts` kwarg\nto `call_with_fallback` (default `LLM_RETRY_ATTEMPTS`, threaded to both\nthe primary and fallback `call_with_retry` — no change for any other\ncaller).\n\n## Why\n\nProd `POST /api/v1/recall` p95+ was routinely **5–15s** — all HTTP 200,\njust slow. Traced to the LLM summarization step (`summarize_memories` →\n`llm.complete_text`, non-streaming); search/embed is not the bottleneck\n(`DEFAULT_SEARCH_TOP_K=5`, small input).\n\nThe retry path is also a **503 amplifier**: `call_with_fallback` ran\n`LLM_RETRY_ATTEMPTS=2` per-attempt-timeout retries across **both**\nprimary and fallback at a **30s** per-attempt timeout — worst case\n~122s, capped only by the 45s request-timeout middleware / 60s Cloud\nRun, at which point it becomes one of the *\"malformed response /\nconnection to the instance had an error\"* 503s. Capping the timeout\n**and** dropping to a single attempt per provider bounds recall at ~30s\nworst case (15s primary → 15s fallback → `_fake_recall`) and fails fast\ninstead of hanging.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\n- **max_tokens=500, not lower:** `RECALL_PROMPT` still emits\nstep-by-step chain-of-thought *before* the answer, so a tighter cap\nrisks truncating the answer. If we later trim the CoT from the prompt\n(the separate prompt lever), this can drop toward ~400.\n- **max_attempts=1 for recall only:** removes *same-provider* retries on\nthis read path. Cross-provider resilience (primary → fallback → fake) is\nunchanged; a same-provider retry after a timeout rarely succeeds and\ndoubles user-facing latency. Write-path enrichment/extraction keep the\ndefault 2 attempts.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_p4_1_llm_fallback.py`: added\n`TestCallWithFallbackMaxAttempts` — `max_attempts=1` invokes the primary\nonce (no retry) then falls through; default still retries\n`LLM_RETRY_ATTEMPTS` times. Full fallback suite (40) + recall suites\n(43) green; ruff clean.\n\n## Follow-up / verification\n\nNow that DD APM + LLMObs are live in prod, the `POST /api/v1/recall` APM\nspan waterfall + `ml_obs.span.llm.duration` for the recall model will\nshow the before/after split directly (these are the traces the\n`--no-cpu-throttling` fix stopped dropping).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-02T08:02:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5fd98b1e991dcd48fa3203317f8daa2397bc480a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5fd98b1e991dcd48fa3203317f8daa2397bc480a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5fd98b1e991dcd48fa3203317f8daa2397bc480a/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3e2bb6640f532209b4a01f964374b36a6eab0741","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3e2bb6640f532209b4a01f964374b36a6eab0741","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3e2bb6640f532209b4a01f964374b36a6eab0741"}]},{"sha":"3e2bb6640f532209b4a01f964374b36a6eab0741","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDNlMmJiNjY0MGY1MzIyMDliNGEwMWY5NjQzNzRiMzZhNmVhYjA3NDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-01T09:17:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-01T09:17:17Z"},"message":"core-{storage-api,worker,operations}: add opt-in Datadog APM (#509)\n\nRollout Phase 1 (OSS images). Replicates the merged [core-api APM\npattern](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/508) across the\nthree remaining OSS Cloud Run services.\n\n## Per service\n- `ddtrace` → optional `datadog` extra, installed only when built with\n`--build-arg DD_APM_ENABLED=true` (`--extra datadog`).\n- Top-of-Dockerfile stage conditionally pulls Datadog's\n`serverless-init` (pinned by digest) behind the same build-arg — **OSS /\non-prem / local images carry no Datadog code or binary**.\n- New `docker-entrypoint.sh` runs the app under serverless-init +\nddtrace-run **only when `DD_API_KEY` is set** (else plain uvicorn;\n`DD_TRACE_ENABLED` falsy kill-switch honored).\n- `uv.lock` regenerated.\n\n## Verified (local builds, both variants)\n| | OSS build | `DD_APM_ENABLED=true` build |\n|---|---|---|\n| ddtrace | absent (ModuleNotFoundError) | 4.10.6 present |\n| /app/dd | empty | serverless-init binary |\n| runtime, no key | plain uvicorn, 0 spans | plain uvicorn, 0 spans |\n| runtime, key set | plain uvicorn | serverless-init + ddtrace active |\n\nConfirmed core-operations' `sh -c` CMD wraps correctly under the shim.\nDeploy-side wiring (build-args + DD_* env + `datadog-api-key` secret +\nlabel per service, staging) follows in a paired caura-memclaw-enterprise\nPR.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"6216494d710a9a5039311fe5f2c370bb80286d62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/6216494d710a9a5039311fe5f2c370bb80286d62"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/3e2bb6640f532209b4a01f964374b36a6eab0741","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRNsdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnusQAJZb3kKG14emMNd1fJvNGsrG\nJ89krZvBiTT1sitTC7O/GWBW9kLHTH9o/3MO7Mhf0kuqmaWRsTetCoBwA10j6jzW\nM7VWnfbMJV9fmvr17kWFUQD48DcSfx1L/5pvHdCM+P0+A9kbAQpVdhehJzq9aGMX\nSbnTb/Xy/2R5IeSld7+UlzXOai1CRYicBhx+vBSDLmnOdWU//Hv+xOr7PO1SvW5j\nMZttNSM2cHY1DuyXEjy8+UI9hgy3uRRaQCyBB2h/dC4FA1SzM+QrgfWm+dp+4xvq\nfqpDx3/cM8jFTj9wVVgsrH1ZzFDndsLWFzzRkbnVAhvd2V1qToecB275fsoEWBao\naX332KgcKZxrPD3AA7C0uYu8JvD7s7xpBVM0barlj7V8SsazXzyjER19xC5JKtYC\nLrqhem/bTcahIdbQG/N37GnXeLfkaKpR/ZqfcHZmQvHVmJ7A9Pt9b5kV2W6VbTi3\nH6Q/TAztdXIG7L/0cJ3p4b1BwmsRi84eMDXFq8nOdCkFEFey3L0fI4EfG46PN5YJ\nIYhznZD8D4TFpn+Yfv7zjiVFOS6Y/KBHTFn2qQNnFJoJCyA12wGIwDu+uuw2tzd4\n0zM9hXkfAG1I/+QeigMJSx3wz5SElJ53buh9kyJ8y75yPf+Zm2t0yax0K0WxuY3x\nR4JaPu01tKZzbixUFEBB\n=G9h5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6216494d710a9a5039311fe5f2c370bb80286d62\nparent 5713d5cf5187674e016948568f17a19d9ba046a7\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1782897437 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782897437 +0300\n\ncore-{storage-api,worker,operations}: add opt-in Datadog APM (#509)\n\nRollout Phase 1 (OSS images). Replicates the merged [core-api APM\npattern](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/pull/508) across the\nthree remaining OSS Cloud Run services.\n\n## Per service\n- `ddtrace` → optional `datadog` extra, installed only when built with\n`--build-arg DD_APM_ENABLED=true` (`--extra datadog`).\n- Top-of-Dockerfile stage conditionally pulls Datadog's\n`serverless-init` (pinned by digest) behind the same build-arg — **OSS /\non-prem / local images carry no Datadog code or binary**.\n- New `docker-entrypoint.sh` runs the app under serverless-init +\nddtrace-run **only when `DD_API_KEY` is set** (else plain uvicorn;\n`DD_TRACE_ENABLED` falsy kill-switch honored).\n- `uv.lock` regenerated.\n\n## Verified (local builds, both variants)\n| | OSS build | `DD_APM_ENABLED=true` build |\n|---|---|---|\n| ddtrace | absent (ModuleNotFoundError) | 4.10.6 present |\n| /app/dd | empty | serverless-init binary |\n| runtime, no key | plain uvicorn, 0 spans | plain uvicorn, 0 spans |\n| runtime, key set | plain uvicorn | serverless-init + ddtrace active |\n\nConfirmed core-operations' `sh -c` CMD wraps correctly under the shim.\nDeploy-side wiring (build-args + DD_* env + `datadog-api-key` secret +\nlabel per service, staging) follows in a paired caura-memclaw-enterprise\nPR.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-07-01T09:17:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3e2bb6640f532209b4a01f964374b36a6eab0741","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/3e2bb6640f532209b4a01f964374b36a6eab0741","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/3e2bb6640f532209b4a01f964374b36a6eab0741/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/foll